ision/strategy page)
Official webpage text reading copy | Retrieved 12 November 2026
Commitment to ethical AI and innovation
Guided by our core values of Integrity, Respect, Courage, Excellence, and Impact, we encourage the
ethical use of AI throughout our university.
From enriching teaching and learning experiences to driving innovative research, Curtin is using AI
as a transformative force. Our aim is to use AI to elevate academic excellence and enhance your
student journey, through our core values and our reputation for technological innovation.
AI as a complementary tool
We recognise the challenges posed by AI, particularly in maintaining academic integrity and
ensuring our technology use enriches rather than detracts from your student experience. We view
AI not as a replacement for traditional teaching methods but as a complementary tool that
enhances our ability to provide you with personalised, effective education.
Workplaces of the future
By integrating AI into our curriculum, student experience and research, we can give you the skills
and knowledge you need for a career in AI-driven workplaces of the future, and to lead and
innovate in a world where AI is a cornerstone of progress and innovation.
Driving research and innovation at Curtin
Artificial intelligence is revolutionising research methodologies globally, and empowering
researchers to tackle contemporary challenges in novel and sophisticated ways. At Curtin, we aspire
to apply AI across diverse research domains – from the sciences to the humanities – promoting
collaboration and driving impactful research and innovation.
AI units and courses
Master of Artificial Intelligence
The course focuses on machine learning and emphasises the skills sought by the industry, such as
neural networks design and implementation, while continually reinforcing the fundamental
knowledge that underpins AI.
View details
Artificial Intelligence Major (M Comp)
This major provides coverage of the key concepts and challenges in artificial intelligence with a
focus on machine learning. The aim is to provide a broad coverage of the different approaches to
machine learning with an emphasis on the latest methods as well as explainable Artificial
Intelligence.
View details
Artificial Intelligence Specialisation
This specialisation is a quick but deep dive into artificial intelligence. Make the best use of
programming and analytic skills by learning techniques to have the computer carry out a range of
problem-solving activities.
View details
Resources for staff
Find out about the potential of artificial intelligence to accelerate research, enrich learning and
teaching, and innovate work within the University.
AI – Staff Portal (login required)
Guidelines for students
Learn to use Gen-AI technology ethically and responsibly, and prepare for future professional
environments.
Find out more
