 Study
 Gen-AI
 Declare and Reference
Declaring and
referencing Gen-AI
If you use a Generative AI (Gen-AI) tool, such as ChatGPT, Claude,
or Copilot, when completing an assessment, it is recommended to
declare your use. Additionally, if you have used Gen-AI to create
content that you include in your work, you must reference this use
as a source of information.
Referencing is a standardised way of acknowledging sources
such as books, articles, and websites to show that your work is
based on credible evidence. Gen-AI must be cited if used as an
information source. This is required in the same way as any other
information you include in your work that comes from an external
source.
It is important to understand that AI-generated content is
considered a non-recoverable source. This means that the
content produced is usually not accessible to anyone other than
the person who generated it. Unless the Gen-AI tool provides a
shareable link to the chat, other people cannot be directed to the
