Bundle page 24 | A006 | source page 3 | line numbers at left","Gen-AI at Curtin in a safe and responsible way.
You can use Gen-AI as a student at
Curtin…
… (1) for study-related purposes.
Study-related purposes include all parts of your learning that
will not be graded. Examples are:
Making a study schedule
Generating extra practice questions for an exam or test
Helping to write or edit emails to classmates or academics
Troubleshooting programs
Gen-AI can also help you look at topics from different angles,
break down complex ideas into simpler explanations, or
suggest links between concepts you are learning. Think of it
as a study helper that can support brainstorming, clarify your
thinking, or help you practise explaining ideas in your own
words.
… (2) for assessment tasks if given
written permission by a unit
coordinator.
You must get clear permission from your unit
coordinator before using Gen-AI for assessment tasks.
Copyright considerations
