Recording Further Assessment 
2.15 Once Further Assessment is offered by the Board of Examiners, an interim grade of X is 
recorded, and the original Mark remains. For example, an F-47 will become X-47. 
2.16 If the student passes the Further Assessment Task, the original Mark will remain the same; 
however, the Grade will be changed to PX (pass after Further Assessment). For example: X-
47 to PX-47. 
2.17 If the student attempts but does not pass the Further Assessment Task, the original Mark will 
remain the same; however, the Grade will be changed to FX (fail after Further Assessment). 
For example: X-47 to FX-47. 
2.18 If a student declines an offer of the Further Assessment Task, the interim grade will revert to 
