2.6 
A student who fails a unit two or more times will be subject to additional approval requirements 
for re-enrolment by the relevant Owning Areas, and such approval, if forthcoming, may include 
conditions (e.g., a reduced study load, specified sequencing of units, or other similar conditions 
designed to improve the student’s prospects of success): 
2.6.1 
For a third enrolment, approval will be obtained from the Head of School (or authorised 
officer) or via the Board of Examiners and is not subject to referral to the Academic 
Registrar. 
2.6.2 
For a fourth enrolment or greater, approval is at the discretion of the Academic 
Registrar in consultation with the relevant School or Owning Area. A student statement 
is mandatory.  
2.7 
A student with an Academic Status of Conditional will be returned to Good Standing in the 
subsequent study period if they meet all of the following criteria:  
2.7.1 
If they pass any previously failed core units that resulted in their status remaining 
Conditional; 
2.7.2 
If they meet all conditions that may have been set down in relation to Conditional 
status; or 
2.7.3 
If they no longer meet the criteria for Conditional or Terminated status. 
2.8 
A Student Support Notification instructing students to complete a Student Success Plan will 
be provided to all students who are defined as at risk in accordance with Clause 2.2.2 or 2.2.3 
of the Support for Students Procedure. 
2.9 
Students will be responsible for seeking advice and support to develop and engage with the 
Student Success Plan. 
2.10 All Consecutive Conditional international students will be notified of their requirement to 
complete a documented intervention strategy plan. 
2.11 Individual Faculties and Schools may implement their own intervention strategies, in addition 
to the minimum requirements at 2.8, to assist students to achieve satisfactory course progress.  
2.12 A student whose Academic Status is either Conditional or Terminated will receive Official 
Communication of this decision via the Official Communication Channel. The Official 
Communication will be sent by the Progression, Assessment and Awards Office.  
2.13 If a student does not take action in relation to the recommendations provided as part of the 
documented intervention strategy plan, this may result in their place in the Course being 
Terminated. 
Student Agreement Regarding Conditions 
2.14 The University may place condition(s) associated with course progression upon a student and 
specify these condition(s) (e.g., through a Student Progression Agreement or documented 
intervention strategy plan).  
2.14.1 A student whose place in the Course has been re-instated as a result of a review or 
appeal and who fails to agree and adhere to any condition(s) of the review or appeal 
will have their place in the Course terminated. 
Student Continuation in their Course 
2.15 The entitlement to continue in a Course and to re-enrol will be, in all cases, subject to any 
other restrictions or prohibitions imposed on the student (e.g., a prohibition on enrolment due 
