Official webpage text reading copy | Retrieved 12 November 2026
Academic Integrity Program (AIP)
If you’re a coursework student, you’re required to complete Curtin’s Academic Integrity Program
(AIP) within 14 days of the start of your first study period at Curtin.
The AIP will help you learn about the concept of academic integrity, Curtin’s Values, and what Curtin
expects of you as a member of this academic community. The program will provide you with tools
to successfully navigate tricky situations that challenge your academic integrity throughout your
studies.
The AIP will take about two hours to complete and you must receive a mark of 80 per cent to pass.
You can retake the test as many times as you need to pass the program.
The course is available with your other enrolled units in the Learning Management System (LMS).
Button block
Log into OASIS to complete the AIP
Topics
Topics include:
Ethics
Curtin’s values and expectations for students
Referencing
Plagiarism
Cheating (including contract cheating and appropriate use of Gen-AI tools)
Warning and misconduct processes and possible outcomes.
Where do I find the AIP?
Curtin is replacing its learning management system (LMS), Blackboard, with Canvas. The rollout is
happening across all Australian and global campuses, and some units have already started in
Canvas as they continue into 2027.
The AIP will be available to you in Blackboard until 14 December 2026.
Important: If you do not complete the AIP in Blackboard by 14 December 2026, you will lose your
progress in the module content. You will then be moved to a new AIP in Canvas and will need to
start again from the beginning.
How to access the AIP in Blackboard
Your AIP will appear in Blackboard, which you can access via OASIS.
To open the program content, select the ‘Content Modules’ tab in the navigation bar on the left side
of the screen.
This document (544kb .pdf) includes screenshots of each step.
For students commencing from 30 November 2026
If you are starting your Curtin course in OUA Study Period 4 (30 November 2026 or later), you
should complete the AIP in Canvas rather than Blackboard.
How to access the AIP in Canvas
Your AIP will appear in Canvas, which you can access via OASIS.
To open the program content, select the ‘Modules’ tab in the navigation bar on the left side of the
screen.
This document (469kb .pdf) includes screenshots of each step.
What happens if I don’t complete the program?
If you do not pass the program within 14 days after the start of your first study period of enrolment
at Curtin, a sanction withholding your results will be applied to your account until you pass the
