SUMMARISING, SYNTHESISING AND PARAPHRASING 
Summarising means picking out the main ideas from a resource (like a book, article, website, or 
video) and restating them in your own words. It involves simplifying and condensing complex 
information, demonstrating that you can clearly and concisely explain key concepts.  
 
Steps for summarising information 
1. Read and understand the text's main ideas and key points 
2. Note the most important information 
3. Remove any unnecessary details, examples, or repetitions 
