YOU BE THE JUDGE 
IS THIS PLAGIARISM? 
Two second-year students, Amy and Carin, submitted nearly identical assignments worth 30%. The 
tutor discovered that Amy had completed her assignment early and shared it with Carin to help her 
start. However, Carin copied most of it and submitted it as her own without Amy's knowledge. 
 
AND THE VERDICT IS… 
This is a clear case of plagiarism. Carin knowingly copied Amy's assignment and submitted it as her 
own. As a second-year student, Carin will likely lose all marks for the assignment. Amy might receive 
a Warning for unintentionally assisting Carin. Although Amy didn't intend for Carin to copy her work, 
sharing her assignment indirectly facilitated the plagiarism. 
 
