Bundle page 228 | N010 | source page 3 | line numbers at left","Data acts as the building blocks for information and knowledge. 
This definition includes Research Data, Confidential Data and Sensitive Data as defined in the 
Research Data and Primary Materials Policy. 
 
Information 
Any communication or representation of knowledge such as facts, data or opinions in any medium 
or form. This definition includes, but is not limited to, documents, emails, webpages, images, 
audio visual files, social media posts, chat messages, building plans and other types of 
knowledge captured in digital or hard copy format.   
 
Information Lifecycle 
The stages through which information passes, from creation or collection through to destruction, 
deletion or Archival preservation.  Stages include Creation, collection and capture; Classification; 
Storage; Use and sharing; Reusing and maintaining; Archiving and preserving; Deleting and 
destroying. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
