     Information Management Procedures 
1. COMPLIANCE OBLIGATION SUPPORTED 
Information Management Policy 
2. PROCEDURAL DETAILS 
This document outlines the procedures for managing data and information created, collected or used 
for undertaking research, teaching and learning activities, as well as engagement, administrative and 
commercial activities.  It applies to data and information regardless of format. 
2.1 
The Information Lifecycle 
Data and information requires effective management throughout the information lifecycle to ensure its 
authenticity, integrity, reliability, accessibility, useability and security is maintained and that it is used 
for the purposes intended.  
Information must be protected from loss, theft, unauthorised access or destruction, while being 
available to those who are authorised to access it, by ensuring it is appropriately created, stored, 
classified, protected, disposed of or retained. 
 
3. RESPONSIBILITIES 
The following responsibilities apply to all individuals, and where specified, Areas, regardless of 
location or role: 
3.1 
 Individuals are to comply with any restrictions or obligations with regards to the management of 
data and information as required by: 
a) any legislative requirements to release information (including to regulators) 
b) any compliance and contractual requirements related to the data and information 
c) the Information Security Classification category assigned to the information 
d) relevant Policies and Procedures including, but not limited to the: 
• Accessible Information Procedures 
• Disclosure of Personal Information Procedures  
• Diversity, Inclusion and Belonging Policy 
• Cyber Security & Information & Communication (ICT) Appropriate Use Policy 
• Information and Communication Technology Appropriate Use Procedures  
• Privacy Policy and the Privacy Procedures 
3.2 
CREATE, COLLECT AND CAPTURE 
a) Individuals will create data and information in the course of undertaking teaching, learning, 
research, engagement, administrative and commercial activities that supports those 
activities.  
