3.6 
RE-USE and MAINTAIN 
a) Any real or suspected loss, theft or unauthorised access of personal data or information 
will be reported in accordance with the Information Breach Policy.  Global campuses will 
abide by any local requirements in their country for management and reporting of data 
breaches. 
b) Processes will be put in place, and followed, so that data and information, along with its 
associated metadata, remains discoverable, accessible and useable by those authorised 
to access it, over its lifecycle regardless of the repository or system within which it is 
stored. 
c) The data and information managed by Individual Areas will be included in their business 
continuity and disaster recovery planning. 
d) Data and information will be retained and maintained for the appropriate minimum time as 
determined by the relevant Retention and Disposal Authority regardless of when it was 
last used and regardless of format. 
