November 2026 (Admin) 
Director, Data and Information Governance will: 
 
Ensure that data and information governance strategies and policies support the Procedure.  
 
Develop and maintain a data and information governance framework. 
 
Develop risk management capability across the University in relation to data and privacy. 
 
Develop and monitor the University’s approach to the management of all data and 
information. 
 
Associate Director, Curtin Information Management and Archives will: 
a) Ensure the development and implementation of policies and frameworks within which the 
Procedures are to operate.  
b) Ensure the development and implementation of best practice guides, tools, education and 
training on information management to support the University Community in meeting these 
Procedures. 
c) Provide advice to the University Community on matters related to the management of 
information. 
d) Monitor compliance with information management policies and procedures. 
e) Advise senior management of risks associated with non-compliance or poor data and 
information management 
University Archivist will: 
a) Determine what data and information, whether digital or physical, is suitable for the University 
Archives. 
b) Mediate donations and transfers of material to and from the University. 
c) Manage changes to Information Security Classifications of Restricted Access Archives to 
enable public access after certain periods in accordance with the Western Australian 
University Sector Disposal Authority (WAUSDA) (Introduction Item 2.3 Restricted Access 
Archives). 
d) Enable appropriate access to the University Archives. 
e) Undertake active preservation of both physical and digital Archives.  
Privacy Officer will: 
a) Prepare, review, and provide guidance and training on the University’s Privacy Policy and 
Privacy Procedures 
b) Prepare, review, and provide guidance and training on the University’s Information Breach 
Policy and Information Breach Procedures 
c) Oversee processes for undertaking Privacy Impact Assessments (PIA) and conduct PIAs in 
consultation with project leads and business units 
d) Manage and coordinate privacy complaints and reports made under the Information Breach 
Procedures 
Business Information System Owners (e.g. Manager, Student Systems) will: 
 
Ensure the system processes and controls are in place such that individuals are provided 
with the required level of access to data and information in order to effectively carry out their 
activities. 
 
Ensure effective controls are in place to support appropriate information handling in line with 
the Information Handling Guideline. 
 
Ensure the system is captured in Curtin’s Information Asset Register. 
 
Ensure the systems hold sufficient metadata to describe the content, structure and context of 
the data and information held in the system throughout the lifecycle of the Information.  (See 
Metadata Guide) 
 
Contact CIMA prior to decommissioning Business Information Systems.  
 
Work with CIMA with regards to the preservation of data and information where it is deemed 
that the Business Information System contains Archival data and information. 
