November 2026 (Admin) 
Metadata  
Structured information that describes and/or allows users to find, manage, control, understand or 
preserve other information over time. Examples of metadata include author, date created, title, 
date last modified and by whom, etc. 
 
Preservation 
Preservation encompasses the activities which prolong the usable life of Archival material. 
Preservation activities are designed to minimize the physical and chemical deterioration of 
material and to prevent the loss of informational content and metadata. Hard copy archives 
activities include providing a stable environment for material of all media types. Activities for 
digital material include active ongoing management of digital data, such as migrating data to 
newer formats, creating multiple copies, backup systems and fixity checking. 
