APPENDIX A 
 
INFORMATION SECURITY CLASSIFICATIONS#  
 
CLASSIFICATIONS 
DESCRIPTION  
EXAMPLES 
PUBLIC 
 
Official University data and 
information that has been 
authorised for public access and 
circulation or deemed public by 
legislation or routine disclosure.    
No access restrictions or special 
handling are required.   
Examples include:   
• 
University public facing web pages  
• 
Published course information (Curtin 
Handbook)  
• 
Information for prospective students  
• 
Released media statements  
• 
Academic calendar  
• 
University Annual Reports and published 
Strategic Plan  
• 
University Policies and Procedures 
published on the Find a Policy webpage  
• 
Campus maps  
• 
Brochures and other promotional materials 
or information  
• 
Researcher summary profiles published for 
the purposes of supervision or expertise  
• 
Research related information (including 
data) that has been published openly which 
may be downgraded to this classification 
such as:  
• Appropriately de-identified 
aggregated research data  
• Non-sensitive data from sensors and 
cameras with containing no personal 
information 
• Non-sensitive data from instruments 
and imaging systems  
 
INTERNAL 
This classification is appropriate 
for much of the information 
created, used or handled by the 
University. This includes routine 
business operations and services 
where the information is not for 
general public release.  It is for 
internal Curtin use (and limited 
authorised external audiences).     
 
 
Some access restrictions and 
special handling are required.  
This is the default classification for all University 
information except:   
• 
research data  
• 
information related to research projects  
• 
personal information    
 
Examples include:   
• Intranet sites and other internal facing web 
pages   
• Operational plans for Schools and Areas    
• Teaching materials    
• Operational meeting agendas and minutes 
which do not contain or relate to sensitive 
information    
• Employee directories (where information is 
not publicly available)    
• Research-related information which does 
not contain sensitive information which may 
be downgraded to this classification. 
Examples might include:   
• Appropriately de-identified 
aggregated research data    
• Non-sensitive data from sensors and 
cameras containing no personal 
information  
• Non-sensitive data from instruments 
and imaging systems    
• Drafts of research publications    
