CLASSIFICATIONS 
DESCRIPTION  
EXAMPLES 
SENSITIVE  
This classification is for 
information that commonly 
includes ‘sensitive’ or confidential 
material created, used or handled 
by the University. Such 
information is for limited 
audiences within Curtin (and 
limited authorised external 
audiences – e.g., research 
collaborators).  
 
Several sub-categories can be 
applied to indicate the nature of 
the data and information and that 
access restrictions and special 
handling is required: 
• 
SENSITIVE – Legal  
• 
SENSITIVE – Personal  
  
This is the default classification for research data 
and information related to research projects, as 
well as Personal Information (PI) as defined under 
the Privacy and Responsible Information Sharing 
Act 2024 (including Sensitive Personal 
Information). 
 
 
Examples of SENSITIVE information include:   
• Information related to research projects, 
including ethics approvals, management of 
the project, and foreign risk reviews.   
• All research data created by Curtin staff or 
Higher Degree by Research (HDR) 
students held by, or in, University systems 
(unless the classification is changed to a 
higher or lower classification).   
• Secretariat-supported committee agendas 
and minutes and non-Secretariat-supported 
committees or groups containing or relating 
to sensitive information of individuals or 
sensitive research (e.g., Promotions 
assessment panels).  
• Exam papers – both master sets and 
student completed exam scripts.   
• Exam results and grades.  
• Password and cryptographic key 
information.  
• Organisational financial data.  
• Intellectual property containing trade 
secrets or other commercially sensitive 
Intellectual Property.   
• Information provided to the University as 
commercial-in-confidence or under a Non-
Disclosure Agreement.  
