2.7 
Emergency or a serious threat to University community 
2.7.1 
The University may disclose personal information under the following conditions: 
(a) if it is unreasonable or impracticable for the University to obtain the individual's 
consent to the use or disclosure and the University reasonably believes that the 
use or disclosure is necessary to lessen or prevent a serious threat to the life, 
health or safety of any individual, or to public health or safety; 
(b) if the University has reason to suspect that unlawful activity, or misconduct of a 
serious nature, that relates to the University's functions or activities has been, is 
being or may be engaged in and the University reasonably believes that the use 
or disclosure is necessary in order for the University to take appropriate action 
in relation to the matter; or 
(c) if the University reasonably believes that the use or disclosure is reasonably 
necessary to assist any agency, organisation, body or person to locate a person 
who has been reported as missing and the use or disclosure is necessary in 
order for the University to take appropriate action in relation to the matter. 
