3.7. 
Anonymous complaints 
3.7.1. An anonymous complaint will be addressed in accordance with these procedures, with 
the exception that there is no requirement to identify or notify the complainant. 
3.7.2. Action taken in relation to anonymous complaints may be limited where further 
information from the complainant is required to sufficiently investigate and determine 
an appropriate resolution.  
3.8. 
Public Interest Disclosures 
3.8.1. Where a person expresses a desire to lodge a complaint as a protected disclosure 
under the Public Interest disclosure (PID) Act, the person must first seek advice from 
the University’s PID Officer who will, on request, provide information on how to make 
such a disclosure. 
3.8.2. Public Interest Disclosures (PIDs) are lodged and managed outside of these 
procedures (refer to the following ISU webpage - Public Interest Disclosures (PIDs). 
