3.3 
Scholarly work and artistic work 
The University does not assert ownership over the IP in scholarly work or artistic work. 
3.4 
Indigenous cultural and intellectual property 
3.4.1 The University acknowledges that Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander communities 
are the custodians of their ICIP and have an interest in protecting their ICIP from 
exploitation that is contrary to their customary laws. 
3.4.2 The University aims to give appropriate recognition, protection and respect to ICIP and 
its owners by ensuring that: 
(a) 
ICIP is used for a purpose permitted by the owners of the ICIP with informed 
consent and, if required, continued consent of its owners; 
(b) 
the ownership of ICIP made available for use in research and University 
