2.2.2. 
Permitted purchasing payment methods: 
Permitted methods - in order or preference - include 
1. Automated payment through the Ci-Anywhere purchase order process, allowing 
for confirmation of delivery, automatic invoice matching and linking of purchases 
to Curtin contracts. This includes using the Online Catalogues in Ci-Anywhere 
(FinanceOne) 
2. University issued corporate credit card 
3. Ci-Anywhere payment without purchase order process where a CI-Anywhere 
purchase order is not possible, with the specific approval of a Financial Services 
Director or CFO  
4. Reimbursement through Concur for a University business expense that has been 
personally incurred.  
Direct Debit or standing orders from Curtin bank account are not permitted as each 
individual payment transaction must be specifically approved. Exceptions to this 
requirement need the specific approval of the Director of Finance & Disruption, 
Financial Services. Cash advances are discouraged due to the risk and operational 
problems in correctly accounting and recording (see Section 2.3.11). 
