2.3. 
Overarching purchasing requirements and guidelines 
2.3.1. 
Documentation Requirements 
Regardless of the ordering and payment method used, documentation of all expense 
transactions must be retained for accounting and regulatory purposes by the Finance 
teams responsible. Where purchasing is done via Ci-Anywhere (be it through 
contracts, catalogues or ad-hoc purchase orders) all relevant information is captured 
and no further detail is required for documentation purposes. 
For all other transactions, documentation must specifically include the following: 
i) 
transaction date; 
ii) 
transaction value; 
iii) 
a full description of the Item(s) purchased; 
iv) the name and address of the supplier; 
v) 
the supplier's Australian Business Number (ABN) (if an Australian supplier) or 
equivalent from International suppliers;  
vi) the GST component (if an Australian supply); and 
vii) Name of staff or area that ordered the goods or services. 
viii) Where a contract exists, the Ci-Anywhere contract number 
