9A. 
Term of office of members  
 
(1) 
Subject to section 10 —  
 
(a) 
a member appointed under section 9(1)(a) or (h) holds 
office for a period of 3 years, commencing on the day of 
their appointment, unless a shorter term of office is 
specified under subsection (4); 
 
(b) 
a member elected under section 9(1)(c), (e) or (f) holds 
office for a period of 3 years, commencing on the day 
their election takes effect, unless a shorter term of office 
is specified under subsection (5); 
 
(c) 
a member elected under section 9(1)(d) holds office for 
a period of one year commencing on the day their 
election takes effect, unless a shorter term of office is 
specified under subsection (5). 
 
(2) 
An appointed (which includes co-opted) or elected member, on 
the expiry of their term of office —  
 
(a) 
may be again appointed or elected, if they continue to be 
qualified under section 9; but  
 
(b) 
on the expiry of a third successive term of office (of 
whatever duration), they are not eligible to hold office as 
a member until 12 months have elapsed after that expiry. 
