21. 
Powers of Council  
 
 
Subject to this Act and the Statutes, the Council —  
 
(a) 
may provide such courses of education as it thinks fit 
and may in accordance with this Act award appropriate 
degrees, diplomas and certificates or honorary awards; 
and 
 
(b) 
may from time to time appoint persons to the staff of the 
University and other officers and engage employees for 
the University; and 
 
(c) 
has the entire control and management of the affairs, 
concerns and property of the University; and 
 
[(d) 
deleted] 
 
(e) 
may act in all matters concerning the University in such 
manner as appears to it best calculated to promote the 
objects and interests of the University. 
 
[Section 21 amended: No. 57 of 1970 s. 5; No. 96 of 1986 
s. 9 and 11; No. 48 of 1989 s. 13; No. 32 of 2016 s. 25.]  
21AA. Relief of members from liability 
 
 
If, in any civil proceeding against a person who is or was a 
member for negligence, default, breach of trust or breach of 
duty in the person’s capacity as a member, it appears to the 
court that the person —  
 
(a) 
is, or may be, liable in respect of the negligence, default 
or breach; and 
 
(b) 
has acted honestly; and 
 
(c) 
ought fairly to be excused for the negligence, default or 
breach having regard to all the circumstances of the 
case, including those connected with the person’s 
appointment,  
 
 
the court may relieve the person either wholly or partly from 
liability on such terms as the court thinks fit. 
 
[Section 21AA inserted: No. 8 of 2005 s. 11.] 
