21I.  
Kalgoorlie Campus  
 
(1) 
The Council is to maintain the educational facility at Kalgoorlie 
established as part of the University and known as the Curtin 
University — Kalgoorlie Campus. 
 
(2) 
The Kalgoorlie Campus —  
 
(a) 
must include a School of Mines known as the Western 
Australian School of Mines; and 
 
(b) 
may include any other facilities that are for the purposes 
of the University or a purpose that is incidental to the 
purposes of the University. 
 
(3) 
It is not necessary for all of the facilities or operations of the 
Western Australian School of Mines to be located on the 
Kalgoorlie Campus. 
 
[Section 21I inserted: No. 32 of 2016 s. 28.]  
