35. 
Approval, publication, disallowance and proof of Statutes 
 
(1) 
A Statute made by the Council —  
 
(a) 
must be sealed with the common seal of the University; 
and 
 
(b) 
must be submitted to the Governor for approval; and 
 
(c) 
if approved by the Governor, must be published in the 
Gazette; and 
 
(d) 
takes effect on the later of —  
 
(i) 
the day after publication in the Gazette; or 
 
(ii) 
if a later day is specified for that purpose in the 
Statute, that day. 
 
(2) 
The Interpretation Act 1984 section 42 applies to a Statute 
approved and published under subsection (1) as if the Statute 
were a regulation. 
