ance processes will be used to inform"", ""L043"": ""actions to improve course quality."", ""L044"": ""3.23 Academic Board will approve, each year, a five-year schedule of CCRs."", ""L045"": ""3.23.1 The Deputy Vice-Chancellor, Academic may, upon recommendation from Courses Committee,"", ""L046"": ""grant extensions or variations to the CCR schedule provided that each course will be reviewed"", ""L047"": ""within a seven year window."", ""L048"": ""3.23.2 The Vice-Chancellor, the Deputy Vice-Chancellor, Academic, the Provost or the Academic Board"", ""L049"": ""may initiate a CCR at any time."", ""L050"": ""3.24 Course review processes should use an evidence-led, risk-based approach informed by:"", ""L051"": ""Course Quality Assurance Manual – Consolidated Policies and Procedures Page 5 of 83"", ""L052"": ""G50-746-426"", ""L053"": ""Published April 2026""}","Course Quality Assurance Manual – Consolidated Policies and Procedures 
