Collaborating authors will agree on authorship of a publication at an early stage in the 
research project and review their decision periodically.  
2.1.6. 
All those who contributed to the research but do not meet the criteria for authorship as 
described in section 2.1.1 will be properly acknowledged. To be properly 
acknowledged, researchers will consider the provisions set out in Authorship: A guide 
to supporting The Code. Where individuals are to be named, authors will make a 
reasonable attempt to obtain their written consent. 
2.2. 
Record of authorship acknowledgement 
2.2.1. 
A person who qualifies as an author will not be included or excluded as an author 
