intellectual property in the Intellectual Property Policy and Intellectual Property 
Procedures.  
2.9.2. 
Where ethical approval was required for the research to proceed, researchers will 
ensure any ethical approvals, as well as the approving committee, will be recorded 
within the publication arising from that research. 
2.9.3. 
Where regulatory permits or other discipline specific approvals are required to conduct 
the research, researchers will ensure these permits are maintained and will be 
recorded within the publication arising from that research in the manner generally 
accepted for that discipline. 
2.9.4. 
Researchers will obtain the permission of the original publisher before republishing 
research outputs, and the original publication will be acknowledged. 
2.9.5. 
Researchers will retain the rights to their authored research outputs through the Open 
Scholarship Policy, which maximises the rights retained by the author and/or the 
University.  
2.9.6. 
Researchers will ensure research outputs arising from grant funded projects comply 
with the rules of the funding body. E.g. National Health and Medical Research Council 
Dissemination and Communication, Australian Research Council Open Access Policy.  
2.9.7. 
Researchers understand Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools cannot meet the requirements 
for authorship as they cannot take responsibility for the submitted work. Researchers 
will ensure they keep up to date with each organisations publishing policies around 
Intellectual Property of AI generated content to avoid breaking any laws. 
2.10. Acknowledgements in research outputs 
2.10.1. Researchers will: 
(a) cite the work of others appropriately and accurately. 
(b) list Curtin University as their affiliated organisation 
(c) acknowledge all sources of financial support for the research  
(d) acknowledge any conflicts of interest in their research outputs. 
2.11. Publishing metadata and digital publishing 
2.11.1. Researchers will 
(a) publish research data and metadata in accordance with the Research Data and 
Primary Materials Policy to support research outputs where appropriate. 
(b) ensure digital publication of research outputs are consistent with the Digital 
Publishing Procedures. 
2.12. Communicating research outputs to the media 
2.12.1. Researchers will comply with the Media and Public Comment Procedures when 
communicating research outputs. 
2.12.2. Corporate Communications (Strategic)  team will support researchers in 
communicating research outputs through the media where allowed under any relevant 
contractual arrangement. 
2.13. Compliance and breaches 
2.13.1. Breaches of these procedures or The Code will be managed in accordance with the 
misconduct or serious misconduct provisions of the Curtin University Academic, 
Professional and General Staff Enterprise Agreement 2022-2025 for staff or Statute 
No. 10 – Student Disciplinary Statute for students. Potential research misconduct will 
be reported and dealt with in accordance with the Responsible Conduct of Research 
Policy and Responsible Conduct of Research Procedures. 
 
3. 
SCOPE OF PROCEDURES 
 
These procedures apply to all employees, adjuncts, University Associates and students in any 
location or campus, whether in or outside of Australia. 
 
