Curtin,N211,Copyright Procedures,551,551,"L001, L002, L003, L004, L005, L006, L007, L008, L009, L010, L011, L012, L013, L014, L015, L016, L017, L018, L019, L020, L021, L022, L023, L024, L025, L026, L027, L028, L029, L030, L031, L032, L033, L034, L035, L036, L037, L038, L039, L040, L041, L042, L043, L044, L045, L046","{""L001"": ""Copyright Procedures"", ""L002"": ""1. STRATEGIC PLAN THEME AND COMPLIANCE OBLIGATION SUPPORTED"", ""L003"": ""Strategic Plan Theme: Learning and Student Experience"", ""L004"": ""Copyright Act 1968 (Commonwealth)"", ""L005"": ""Copyright Regulations 2017"", ""L006"": ""2. PROCEDURAL DETAILS"", ""L007"": ""This procedure outlines the ways that Curtin staff and students comply with the Copyright Act 1968"", ""L008"": ""(the Act) and will be read in conjunction with the Intellectual Property Policy and Procedure and the"", ""L009"": ""Authorship, Peer Review and Publication of Research Outputs Policy and Procedure."", ""L010"": ""Use of Copyright Materials for Learning and Teaching (within Australia)"", ""L011"": ""2.1. Staff will arrange access to unit readings via the Curtin Library’s Reading Lists Service."", ""L012"": ""2.2. Where staff incorporate third party copyright material into teaching materials (e.g. handouts,"", ""L013"": ""slides etc.), they will:"", ""L014"": ""(a) attribute the source of the content clearly on the materials;"", ""L015"": ""(b) insert the Statutory Licence electronic warning notice;"", ""L016"": ""(c) not exceed the copying limits of 10% of the words/one chapter per book, or one article"", ""L017"": ""per journal issue."", ""L018"": ""2.3. Staff delivering programs to individuals or groups who are not Curtin enrolled students will only"", ""L019"": ""use:"", ""L020"": ""(a) copies of openly licensed materials (such as Creative Commons licensed content);"", ""L021"": ""(b) links to freely available content;"", ""L022"": ""(c) content copied with permission of the copyright holder;"", ""L023"": ""(d) content copied in reliance on the fair dealing exceptions in the Act. Use of these"", ""L024"": ""exceptions will require a risk assessment of the activity and the use must genuinely be for"", ""L025"": ""one of the fair dealing purposes as set out in the Act."", ""L026"": ""Use of Copyright Materials for Learning and Teaching (outside Australia)"", ""L027"": ""2.4. Staff will use third party copyright material that is made available from an Australian location"", ""L028"": ""only (e.g. content in Blackboard and Reading Lists) or through the Curtin Library (e.g."", ""L029"": ""subscribed database content)."", ""L030"": ""2.5. Staff will abide by the copyright legislation in their local jurisdiction if making available third party"", ""L031"": ""copyright material from the overseas location."", ""L032"": ""Takedown requests to remove third party copyright material from University platforms and"", ""L033"": ""websites"", ""L034"": ""In order to comply with the requirements set out in Part V Division 2AA of the Act:"", ""L035"": ""2.6 Curtin websites and webpages will prominently and publicly display a link to the process to"", ""L036"": ""submit a takedown notice."", ""L037"": ""2.7 Requests to takedown third party copyright material from University platforms and websites:"", ""L038"": ""(a) must be forwarded to the Copyright Compliance Officer (the ‘Designated Officer’ for"", ""L039"": ""takedown requests) who will investigate the take down request and report the outcome to"", ""L040"": ""all parties involved;"", ""L041"": ""(b) Schools and Areas will respond to requests for information relating to takedown requests"", ""L042"": ""by the Copyright Compliance Officer within two business days;"", ""L043"": ""(c) Where appropriate matters of conduct will be referred to the Office of the Academic"", ""L044"": ""Registrar, or Heads of School or Area as appropriate for further investigation."", ""L045"": ""G50-746-421 1"", ""L046"": ""September 2022 (Admin)""}","G50-746-421 
