This includes evidence of: 
a) the nature of the imputed disability including observed functional impacts that 
are persistent and ongoing; 
b) functional impacts which are not better accounted for by other factors; 
c) adjustments that have been recommended and trialled and have had limited 
effectiveness/ impact, and 
d) consultation and collaboration with student, staff, and relevant external 
professionals. 
2.5.2 
Where AccessAbility Services have identified that there is clear evidence of impact 
on function in the education environment and in the absence of a formal diagnosis, 
a student may be considered to have imputed disability in accordance with section 
2.5.1 and can be provided with a CAP. 
2.5.3 
Once formal diagnosis of disability has been determined, section 2.3 shall apply 
thereafter. 
 
