Use with Library database material does not breach licensing terms.
For more detailed guidance, see the Researchers section below.
Curtin staff
Staff may use portions of copyrighted material with Gen AI for teaching purposes as part of the
Statutory Education License. Limits to the amount of material used apply regardless of the
Gen-AI tool used (see the text and images page for more information on material limits). Curtin
staff may upload educational materials (unit outlines, PowerPoint slides) to Curtin’s secure
version of Microsoft Copilot. Review the Artificial Intelligence guidance on the Staff Portal for
more information on approved tools, in addition to the GenAI in Learning and Teaching
guidance. Ensure that:
The use is only for educational purposes
The amount used is limited to 10% or one chapter of the work
Gen-AI tools used are secure (e.g. they do not train on or share content)
Outputs are not shared publicly (e.g. posted on the open internet)
Use with Library database material does not breach licensing terms.
Please contact the Copyright Officer via Library Help with questions about using copyrighted
material with Gen-AI for teaching.
