Privacy policy
ECU's Privacy Policy and related procedures cover the following:
Collection of personal and sensitive information
Use and disclosure of personal and sensitive information
Overseas disclosure
Information breach management and cyber security incident response
Direct marketing
Access and correction of personal information
Access to personal information for research purposes
Contact details for ECU’s privacy officers
Privacy Impact Assessments
To support the responsible handling of personal information, the University has established a
process to ensure privacy risks are consistently identified and managed whenever new or
significant changed practices are introduced.
The University will undertake Privacy Impact Assessment (PIA) for all high privacy impact initiatives.
The PIA Procedure outlines how this obligation is met.
Further information and how to contact us
For further information or if you have any concerns regarding the handling of your personal
information or seek access to that information, you may contact the Privacy Officer, Privacy@ECU.
If you believe there has been a information breach involving personal information, please lodge this
using Information breach notification form.
If you have reason to believe there has been a cybersecurity incident, please report it via the ECU IT
Service Desk.
If you are seeking information on how make a Freedom of Information Act 1992 (WA) application,
please refer to the Freedom of Information page.
If you would like to make a formal privacy complaint, you can lodge this via the ECU’s Complaints
Resolution process.
If you are a student and wish to request access to, or to correct personal information held by ECU
about you AND you were unable to do this as via Student Hub or other administration services.
If you are a staff member and wish to request access to, or correct, personal information held by
ECU about you AND were unable to via Staff Kiosk.
ECU may, from time to time, update its Privacy Policy, Collection Statements and various
information handling tools to ensure they remain appropriate to changing laws, technology and the
