From this perspective, telling students that they can or cannot use AI in a task is insufficient; it does not role-model
the variety of responsible ways students may leverage AI tools either during their studies or future workplaces.
Such rules-based approaches are also difficult to enforce, arguably introducing more problems than they solve
(Corbin, Dawson, & Liu, 2025; Dawson et al., 2024). Instead, curriculum needs to reform to create space for
students to experience how AI can be used responsibly to meet a learning goal, in contexts where its value is
