Using Generative AI Tools in Learning
Generative AI in Learning
Developing skills in using artificial intelligence (gen AI) tools appropriately is an increasingly
important part of being a successful university student. This page outlines all the support
that’s available for ECU students to learn how to use gen AI responsibly.
Self-access resourcesECU students can access a range of resources on Canvas that offer
guidance on using these tools. In alignment with ECU’s Ethical Framework, these resources
include:
advice on how to use gen AI for learning and demonstrating academic integrity
practical prompt strategies for obtaining meaningful feedback
guides for correctly attributing AI-assisted work
Drop-insFor additional support with gen AI tools, students can access the Academic Skills
Drop-Ins page for information about our gen AI drop-in sessions. The face-to-face and online
sessions do not need to be booked. For more details on how to join the online session, please
visit “How to Join Online”.
WorkshopsECU also offers workshops on Understanding MS Copilot and Generative AI Tools.
Make sure you check the dates and register; if you miss a workshop, recordings are available
on the ECU Library website.
Have a question?Still need help? Contact the learning advisers via email at
learningadviser@ecu.edu.au.
