Education Quality and Standards Committee
The Education Quality and Standards Committee (EQSC) reviews, monitors and makes
recommendations on student related matters, academic standards, including academic policy
and international compliance, and educational partnership arrangements. It is a subcommittee
of ECU's Academic Board, and was formed after the disestablishment of the Education
Committee and Internationalisation Committee in March 2025.
Research and Higher Degrees Committee
The Research and Higher Degree Committee (RHDC) makes recommendations to Academic
Board on policies and procedures relating to research and development (including commercial
research and development and research consultancies); internal and external research
funding; contract research; research institutions and centres; procedures and quality of
research training for graduate students and staff; the legal requirements for ethical conduct in
research involving human and animal subjects; work health and safety; and bio-safety,
hazardous substances and the use of radioactive materials. The RHDC develops and reviews
the University Research and Research Training Functional Plan.
