th the principles of academic integrity in their learning and research"", ""L044"": ""including making ethical decisions about the ways in which they represent their knowledge"", ""L045"": ""and Capabilities;"", ""L046"": ""complete relevant academic or research integrity modules as set out in the Admission,"", ""L047"": ""Enrolment and Academic Progress Rules;"", ""L048"": ""actively engage with the University’s expectations for assessment, including Assessment and"", ""L049"": ""submission requirements, acknowledgement and referencing practices, marking criteria and"", ""L050"": ""any other relevant standards;""}","From these values flow principles of behaviour that are foundational to the work of the whole
