d security of their account has been"", ""L019"": ""compromised must immediately report their concern to the CIO or their nominee."", ""L020"": ""A University identity card must always be carried when using on-campus computing facilities."", ""L021"": ""Authorised Users unable to show a current and valid University identity card to security officers"", ""L022"": ""and/or other University staff on request may be required to leave the facility immediately."", ""L023"": ""Persons seeking entry to a computing facility where use of an access card is required to gain"", ""L024"": ""entry must use their own access card. Accessing a facility using a card other than the"", ""L025"": ""Authorised User’s own access card is considered unauthorised access."", ""L026"": ""Authorised Users who access the University’s ICT environment remotely must avoid accessing"", ""L027"": ""or creating sensitive University Information Assets from shared devices or publicly accessible"", ""L028"": ""systems."", ""L029"": ""Authorised Users who access/store University information using a personal device must do so"", ""L030"": ""in accordance with the Information Security and Information Technology policy."", ""L031"": ""Digital Communication Channels:"", ""L032"": ""Members of the University Community communicating from a University provided account"", ""L033"": ""must ensure the way they communicate reflects positively on the University and upholds the"", ""L034"": ""University’s values."", ""L035"": ""All communications are regarded as University records. Users of the University’s ICT"", ""L036"": ""environment accept that there are legislative requirements which may oblige the University to"", ""L037"": ""disclose information contained in any such communications."", ""L038"": ""Users of the University’s ICT environment must take all reasonable steps to ensure information"", ""L039"": ""reasonably believed to be confidential, sensitive, or to present a risk to the University should it"", ""L040"": ""be accessed by entities other than the intended recipient, is only conveyed using Information"", ""L041"": ""Systems that are protected and secure."", ""L042"": ""Staff must be aware agreements made in digital communications channels, for example,"", ""L043"": ""email, can be considered legally binding on the University and must only make offers and"", ""L044"": ""agree to undertake actions reflective of the level of authority and decision-making powers"", ""L045"": ""vested in them by the University."", ""L046"": ""Staff must seek approval from the relevant senior executive prior to sending a global staff"", ""L047"": ""email."", ""L048"": ""Breaches and exceptions:"", ""L049"": ""Non-compliance with this policy by an Authorised User will be investigated and, subject to the"", ""L050"": ""applicable provisions of relevant legislation, statutes, rules, policies and industrial agreements,""}","As far as reasonable and practicable, and in accordance with the Information Security and
Information Technology policy, University sanctioned, and protected Information Systems must
be used for the storage of University-related data and information.
Access to Information Systems:
The University reserves the right to decide who will and will not be provided access to
University Information Systems and to remove access should the University deem access to no
longer be required or to no longer be in the University’s best interests.
Authorised Users provided with accounts enabling access to University Information Systems
accept accounts on the understanding they are for the exclusive use of the Authorised User
and must not be shared or used by anyone other than the Authorised User.
Passwords, accounts and documented processes required for the access of University
information must be protected and secured in accordance with the conditions under which
access has been provided.
Authorised Users must not deliberately avoid or attempt to avoid authentication or conceal or
attempt to conceal their identity whilst using University information Systems.
Authorised Users must not acquire, possess, trade, or use hardware or software tools that
could be employed to evaluate or compromise Information Security.
Authorised Users who reasonably suspect the privacy and security of their account has been
compromised must immediately report their concern to the CIO or their nominee.
A University identity card must always be carried when using on-campus computing facilities.
Authorised Users unable to show a current and valid University identity card to security officers
and/or other University staff on request may be required to leave the facility immediately.
Persons seeking entry to a computing facility where use of an access card is required to gain
entry must use their own access card. Accessing a facility using a card other than the
Authorised User’s own access card is considered unauthorised access.
Authorised Users who access the University’s ICT environment remotely must avoid accessing
or creating sensitive University Information Assets from shared devices or publicly accessible
systems.
Authorised Users who access/store University information using a personal device must do so
in accordance with the Information Security and Information Technology policy.
Digital Communication Channels:
Members of the University Community communicating from a University provided account
must ensure the way they communicate reflects positively on the University and upholds the
University’s values.
All communications are regarded as University records. Users of the University’s ICT
environment accept that there are legislative requirements which may oblige the University to
disclose information contained in any such communications.
Users of the University’s ICT environment must take all reasonable steps to ensure information
reasonably believed to be confidential, sensitive, or to present a risk to the University should it
be accessed by entities other than the intended recipient, is only conveyed using Information
Systems that are protected and secure.
Staff must be aware agreements made in digital communications channels, for example,
email, can be considered legally binding on the University and must only make offers and
agree to undertake actions reflective of the level of authority and decision-making powers
vested in them by the University.
Staff must seek approval from the relevant senior executive prior to sending a global staff
email.
Breaches and exceptions:
Non-compliance with this policy by an Authorised User will be investigated and, subject to the
applicable provisions of relevant legislation, statutes, rules, policies and industrial agreements,
