INTENT
The purpose of this policy is to govern the collection, use, disclosure, storage and destruction
of Personal Information and Health Information by the University, including access, sharing,
amendment and loss of Personal Information.
ORGANISATIONAL SCOPE
This policy applies to all University Staff, Students, and the broader University community.
DEFINITIONS
The University Glossary and the following definitions apply to this policy:
Term:
Definition:
Australian Privacy Principles
The privacy principles set out in Schedule 1 to the Privacy Act, to the extent applicable to the
University.
Contracted Service Provider
As defined in the PRIS Act.
Cyber Security Incident
One or more acts, events or circumstances involving any of the following:
unauthorised access to (i) computer data or (ii) a computer program;
unauthorised modification of (i) computer data or (ii) a computer program;
unauthorised impairment of electronic communication to or from a computer; or
unauthorised impairment of the availability, reliability, security or operation of (i) a computer,
(ii) computer data or (iii) a computer program.
Data Subject
As defined in Article 4 [Definitions] of the General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679,
which at the date of this document is “an identified or identifiable natural person.”
De-identified Information
As defined in the PRIS Act.
FOI Act
