POLICY CONTENT
General Principles
The University must comply with the PRIS Act as its primary privacy framework and must not
engage in any act or practice that is inconsistent with its Information Privacy Principles.
In handling Personal Information, the University will collect, use and disclose that information
in accordance with this policy and applicable privacy laws.
Where not otherwise required by law, the University will adopt privacy practices broadly
consistent with recognised Australian and international standards, including the Australian
Privacy Principles, to the extent applicable to its activities and subject to the limitations set out
in paragraph 4.4.
The University’s obligations under the Privacy Act are primarily limited to:
the collection, use and disclosure of information obtained for the purposes prescribed by the
