44"": ""including:"", ""L045"": ""assessing whether a proposed information sharing activity is for a Permitted Purpose;"", ""L046"": ""ensuring responsible sharing principles are applied;"", ""L047"": ""determining whether an information sharing agreement is required; and"", ""L048"": ""authorising or refusing information sharing requests.""}","Higher Education Support Act 2003 (Cth);
the collection, use and management of tax file number information of individuals, which must
also be consistent with the Privacy (Tax File Number) Rule 2015 (Cth); and
where it has agreed to be contractually bound to it.
The University is committed to the responsible management of Personal Information and
Health Information in undertaking its core functions of teaching, research and activities to
support these functions.
The University will maintain transparent privacy practices, including making this policy and
related privacy information publicly available, and clearly communicating how Personal
Information is handled. In doing so, the University will balance transparency, responsible
information sharing, and the protection of individual privacy, having regard to the public
interest in access to information.
In applying this policy, the University will have regard to proportionality, necessity, and risk to
individuals’ privacy.
A Privacy Impact Assessment will be undertaken for any high privacy impact function or
activity, where the handling of Personal Information is likely to have a significant impact on the
privacy of individuals.
Accountable Roles
Privacy Officer
For the purposes of Part 2 of the PRIS Act, the University designates the Director, Strategic and
Governance Services as its Privacy Officer.
The Privacy Officer is the senior officer responsible for strategic oversight of the University’s
compliance with this policy and applicable privacy legislation together with the development,
maintenance and oversight of the University’s privacy management approach, including:
the University’s privacy management practices;
privacy complaints or concerns in line with the Complaints Policy;
identification, assessment and articulation of privacy risks in line with the ECU Risk
Management Framework to enable ECU to make informed risk-based decisions;
Privacy Impact Assessments with University stakeholders and wider University community as
necessary; and
investigation and response to Information Breach Incident reports (in line with Critical Incident
and Business Continuity Management Policy and supporting procedures and other operational
documents).
The Privacy Officer’s role is one of governance, accountability and oversight, and does not
require the Privacy Officer to personally undertake day-to-day operational activities, which
may be performed by officers within the Strategic and Governance Services portfolio in
accordance with internal delegations.
Information Sharing Officer
For the purposes of Part 3 of the PRIS Act, the University designates the Associate Director,
Legal and Integrity, Strategic and Governance Services as its Information Sharing Officer.
The Information Sharing Officer is a senior officer responsible for receiving, assessing and
authorising information sharing requests and activities in accordance with the PRIS Act,
applicable information sharing agreements, and responsible information sharing principles
including:
assessing whether a proposed information sharing activity is for a Permitted Purpose;
ensuring responsible sharing principles are applied;
determining whether an information sharing agreement is required; and
authorising or refusing information sharing requests.
