y risks and impact;"", ""L021"": ""aligning accountabilities and responsibilities of Relevant Data Owners in line with the Data"", ""L022"": ""Governance Framework; and"", ""L023"": ""ensuring storage and retention protocols under the Records Management Policy."", ""L024"": ""The University will take reasonable steps to de-identify or destroy Personal Information about"", ""L025"": ""an individual where the:"", ""L026"": ""University no longer needs the information for any purpose for which the information may be"", ""L027"": ""used or disclosed by the entity under this policy;"", ""L028"": ""information is not contained in a Commonwealth record; and"", ""L029"": ""University is not required by or under an Australian law, a court or tribunal order, to retain the"", ""L030"": ""information."", ""L031"": ""Access, Quality and Correction6"", ""L032"": ""The University will take steps to reasonably ensure that the Personal Information it collects,"", ""L033"": ""uses, or discloses is accurate, up-to-date and complete."", ""L034"": ""The University recognises that, under the PRIS Act, the Information Privacy Principle relating to"", ""L035"": ""access and correction does not apply to agencies subject to the FOI Act, and that requests for"", ""L036"": ""access to, and correction of, Personal Information for the University are primarily governed"", ""L037"": ""under the FOI Act mechanisms."", ""L038"": ""The University may, at its discretion, provide access to Personal Information outside of the FOI"", ""L039"": ""Act where it is reasonable and practicable to do so. The University may decline informal"", ""L040"": ""requests where it considers it appropriate to require a formal application under the FOI Act."", ""L041"": ""Individuals may apply or request access to their own Personal Information or correction of this"", ""L042"": ""Personal Information by contacting the relevant University area, or by application to the"", ""L043"": ""Privacy Officer."", ""L044"": ""The University will aim to respond to informal access or correction requests within 45 days,"", ""L045"": ""noting that statutory timeframes apply where requests are made under the FOI Act. If the"", ""L046"": ""University determines that it is not reasonable to allow access or amend an individual’s"", ""L047"": ""Personal Information, it will inform the individual of the reasons for denial of access or"", ""L048"": ""correction."", ""L049"": ""Individuals may also apply under the FOI Act for an amendment of Personal Information.""}","The University may be bound by extra-territorial privacy legislation and standards in some
circumstances either because of the nature of work being undertaken or because of its
contractual obligations.
Privacy advice from the Privacy Officer must be sought where Personal and Health Information
is to be transferred outside of Australia. Where applicable, a Privacy Impact Assessment may
be required.
The University will comply with extra-territorial privacy legislation, including the European
Union / United Kingdom General Data Protection Regulation, to the extent it applies to the
handling of specific Personal Data by the University.
Security 4 and De-identification 5
The University will take a proactive approach to manage Personal Information and Sensitive
Personal Information (including Health Information) by ensuring appropriate safeguards and
protocols are in place, including by:
only collecting and retaining Personal Information that is necessary for its functions and not
retaining information longer than required;
protecting against Information Breach Incidents, including from misuse, interference, loss and
from unauthorised access, modification, and disclosure;
following a ‘privacy by design’ approach for processes and system change initiatives;
where relevant, undertaking a Privacy Impact Assessment to appropriately consider and
manage privacy risks and impact;
aligning accountabilities and responsibilities of Relevant Data Owners in line with the Data
Governance Framework; and
ensuring storage and retention protocols under the Records Management Policy.
The University will take reasonable steps to de-identify or destroy Personal Information about
an individual where the:
University no longer needs the information for any purpose for which the information may be
used or disclosed by the entity under this policy;
information is not contained in a Commonwealth record; and
University is not required by or under an Australian law, a court or tribunal order, to retain the
information.
Access, Quality and Correction6
The University will take steps to reasonably ensure that the Personal Information it collects,
uses, or discloses is accurate, up-to-date and complete.
The University recognises that, under the PRIS Act, the Information Privacy Principle relating to
access and correction does not apply to agencies subject to the FOI Act, and that requests for
access to, and correction of, Personal Information for the University are primarily governed
under the FOI Act mechanisms.
The University may, at its discretion, provide access to Personal Information outside of the FOI
Act where it is reasonable and practicable to do so. The University may decline informal
requests where it considers it appropriate to require a formal application under the FOI Act.
Individuals may apply or request access to their own Personal Information or correction of this
Personal Information by contacting the relevant University area, or by application to the
Privacy Officer.
The University will aim to respond to informal access or correction requests within 45 days,
noting that statutory timeframes apply where requests are made under the FOI Act. If the
University determines that it is not reasonable to allow access or amend an individual’s
Personal Information, it will inform the individual of the reasons for denial of access or
correction.
Individuals may also apply under the FOI Act for an amendment of Personal Information.
