individual.
Overseas Disclosure
The University may disclose Personal Information or De-identified Information outside Australia
where disclosure is permitted under this policy, including where it is reasonably necessary for
its functions, services or activities.3
Overseas disclosure may occur where:
a Student studies or undertakes work-integrated learning activities abroad;
a Student or Staff member undertakes official University travel or business abroad; or
the University has contractual or data transfer arrangements with third parties.
Where overseas disclosure is required, the University will take reasonable steps to ensure
compliance with appropriate collection, usage and handling safeguards and security detailed
within this policy and the Australian Privacy Principles.
