any other legislative or regulatory reporting obligations.
evaluate, treat the cause of the incident to protect Personal Information held by the University;
and
review and remediate to prevent or reduce the risk of future Information Breach Incidents.
Where the University determines that serious harm is likely, the University will, as soon as
reasonably practicable:
notify affected individuals; and
provide information to assist individuals to mitigate potential harm.
Such notification will, to the extent practicable, include:
a description of the breach;
the kinds of information involved;
recommended steps individuals should take in response; and
contact details for further information and support.
The University may delay or withhold notification to individuals where:
