Establish key compliance control points to prompt University stakeholders to consider privacy
and PIA obligations when developing new initiatives:
University Executive Sponsors – initiative or project sponsors should assess whether a PIA is
required as part of business case or proof of concept proposal;
University Project Management Office (UPMO) – when developing or supporting new business
cases or project proposals, ensure privacy and PIA requirements are considered;
Digital Services (DS), Business Partnerships team – when engaged by University areas for new
Information and Communication Technology (ICT) solutions or supplier/vendor engagements,
include PIA requirement in existing due diligence / compliance checklists, similar to
International Compliance Review or Security Risk Due Diligence requirements;
Enterprise Risk – upon engagement for project risk engagement and support, refer as
appropriate to Privacy team for consideration of PIA requirements;
The Privacy Officer or delegate will maintain a PIA Register as a centralised record of all PIA
performed to monitor progress, status and trends in privacy risk across initiatives in the
University.
Regular privacy reporting:
Quarterly to Risk, Incident Management Committee (RIMC).
Bi-annually to Quality, Audit and Risk Committee (QARC).
ACCOUNTABILITIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
The Procedures Owner is the Director, Strategic and Governance Services and has overall
responsibility for the content of these procedures and their operation.
The Privacy Officer or delegate is responsible for currency of information and provision of
advice relating to these procedures.
Project Sponsor, Project Manager and/or Officer are accountable for ensuring the PIA is
performed in accordance with the procedure for initiatives or projects which meet the
threshold.
UPMO is responsible for the governance and oversight of the PIA integration into project
lifecycle.
DS Business Partners will support Project Manager and/or Officer and ensure early awareness
of the required risk and compliance due diligence, such as PIA and Information Technology
Security Due Diligence.
