-quality, trusted and credible. The University will ensure"", ""L044"": ""these Staff have appropriate skills, qualifications, support, and resources to perform the role"", ""L045"": ""with a high level of quality and in alignment with this policy."", ""L046"": ""The University’s Statement on Academic Freedom and Freedom of Speech applies to all of the"", ""L047"": ""University’s Research activities."", ""L048"": ""The University is committed to the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion, and will ensure"", ""L049"": ""this is reflected in University Research activities.""}","Research Ethics Management System
The Research Ethics Management System is the University’s online ethics system. It supports
the governance of research at ECU.
Research Misconduct
A serious Breach of the Code which is also intentional or reckless or negligent, which may
amount to misconduct or serious misconduct under the Enterprise Agreement.
Strategic and School-Based Research Entities
This definition is to be understood as including:
ECU Strategic Research Institute
A group of researchers of sufficient scale centred around a cohesive research topic of strategic
significance to the University. The Institute produces well above world-standard research and
is a national and/or international academic leader in its field.
ECU Strategic Research Centre
A group of researchers of sufficient scale centred around a cohesive research topic of strategic
significance to the University. The Centre produces above world-standard research with strong
national and/or international academic recognition in its field. School-Based Research Centre
A School-RC is a cohesive group of Researchers within a School which is collectively furthering
the strategic Research directions of that School by focussing on a Research topic. Collectively,
the group represents the very best Research within a School that is already, or on a very clear
trajectory towards, delivering on world-class Research outcomes.
POLICY CONTENT:
Responsible conduct of Research
As far as reasonable and practicable, the University will align its principles and processes with
those outlined in the Australian Code for the Responsible Conduct of Research (the Code),
whilst remaining compliant with relevant Industrial Instruments, and any applicable legislation.
The University will develop and maintain processes and procedures to inform the way this
policy will be made operational. Compliance with these processes and procedures is required
by the University. Changes and updates to these documents will, to the extent reasonable and
required, be undertaken in consultation with impacted stakeholders, including the Research
and Higher Degrees Committee, and will be approved by the Deputy Vice-Chancellor
(Research) or their nominee.
The University commits to ensuring all Researchers, regardless of their level of development,
experience, role, or seniority, are:
informed of the minimum standard of quality and responsibility expected of an ECU
Researcher;
provided with training as required and appropriate; and
are made aware of how and where to access Research related information should they require
clarity or additional guidance.
The University requires all Researchers to adopt methods and methodology appropriate to the
aims of the Research to ensure confidence in Research processes and outcomes.
The University acknowledges the critical role Staff who provide guidance, mentorship and
supervision, play in establishing and maintaining Research conduct and a Research culture
that is honest, conscientious, high-quality, trusted and credible. The University will ensure
these Staff have appropriate skills, qualifications, support, and resources to perform the role
with a high level of quality and in alignment with this policy.
The University’s Statement on Academic Freedom and Freedom of Speech applies to all of the
University’s Research activities.
The University is committed to the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion, and will ensure
this is reflected in University Research activities.
