s must not proceed until all necessary"", ""L044"": ""approvals and permissions have been formally provided."", ""L045"": ""All people involved with or exposed to Research and teaching activities that involve animals"", ""L046"": ""must at all times comply with the Western Australian Animal Welfare Act (2002) (WA) and the"", ""L047"": ""Australian Code for the Care and Use of Animals for Scientific Research Purposes"", ""L048"": ""Research involving University Staff or Student participants"", ""L049"": ""Requests for access to information relating to Staff or Students for Research purposes must be""}","The University will comply with its requirements under the Defence Security Industry Program
(DISP) and, to the extent relevant and required, will ensure DISP advice is available to
Researchers through the University’s DISP Security Officer.
Research related intellectual property
Research related Intellectual Property will be managed in accordance with the University’s
Intellectual Property policy.
Publication, authorship, and peer review
Researchers will ensure appropriate and fair authorship attribution in accordance with the
University’s Authorship, Publication and Peer Review Guidelines, formalising authorship
arrangements, where possible.
Researchers will disseminate Research findings responsibly, accurately, and broadly, and
openly acknowledge those who have contributed to it.
Notwithstanding the above, Researchers must be aware of, and comply with, the University’s
Intellectual Property policy and any legislative or contractual requirements or restrictions
relating to the confidentiality or the publication of Research or related Data. Researchers must
also be aware of their responsibility to complete International Compliance Reviews and the
related Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade (DFAT) Consolidated List Review with respect
to the supply and dissemination of research to foreign individuals and entities.
The University has an expectation that peer review will be used throughout the Research
lifecycle, including during the development of Research proposals, as a mechanism for
providing expert scrutiny, maintaining high standards in Research, and ensuring accepted
disciplinary standards are met.
Researchers will participate in peer review in a way that is fair, rigorous and timely and
maintains the confidentiality of the content.
The University encourages Open Access to Research where possible and appropriate,
especially where the Research was publicly funded.
Research involving human participants
Research involving Human Participants must be conducted in alignment with the University’s
Conduct of Ethical Human Research guideline and must not proceed until the University has
confirmed:
the Research complies with the latest available version of the National Statement on Ethical
Conduct in Human Research;
compliance with the latest available version of the Ethical Guidelines for Research with
Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Peoples if required; and
compliance with any additional specific statutory regulation, both Commonwealth and State if
applicable.
Research and teaching involving animals
Research involving animals must be conducted in alignment with the University’s Animal
Ethics guideline. Research and teaching involving animals will only be approved by the
University where it can be demonstrated there is robust evidence or scientific merit for their
use, and when it can be demonstrated there is no other viable way of achieving a critical
outcome without the use of animals.
Research and teaching activities involving animals must not proceed until all necessary
approvals and permissions have been formally provided.
All people involved with or exposed to Research and teaching activities that involve animals
must at all times comply with the Western Australian Animal Welfare Act (2002) (WA) and the
Australian Code for the Care and Use of Animals for Scientific Research Purposes
Research involving University Staff or Student participants
Requests for access to information relating to Staff or Students for Research purposes must be
