The University shall not enter into Research Collaborations in breach of applicable sanctions
laws, including the Autonomous Sanctions Act 2011 (Cth). The University shall not engage in a
Research Collaboration with a foreign individual or entity until relevant International
Compliance Reviews and a DFAT Consolidated List Review have been completed, and the
results of those reviews are deemed acceptable by the University.
The Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research) has authority to direct that a Research Collaboration is
not entered into, or is not to be continued, if it is reasonably suspected that:
the collaboration may compromise the reputation of the University;
the collaboration may negatively impact the University’s ability to conduct Research in
accordance with the Code;
