December 2021:
A comprehensive review of the suite of policies owned by the Deputy-Vice-Chancellor
(Research) was undertaken. The review included the identification of operational content to be
removed from policies, opportunities to increase alignment with the Australian Code for the
Responsible Conduct of Research, the need for redrafting to ensure the policy position was
principle-based, and the need to streamline the suite of policies to reduce complexity and
unnecessary regulatory burden.
The content of this policy has been completely re-drafted, and it now contains all policy related
to the Australian Code for the Responsible Conduct of Research. The redevelopment of this
policy has allowed for the following policies to be rescinded:
Responsible Research Conduct
Research Data Management
Authorship, Publication of Research, and Peer Review
Open Access to Research
Conduct of Ethical Human Research
Conduct of Ethical Research and Teaching Involving Animals
