rn will be through the LMS, except for work completed in class."", ""L021"": ""Course/Unit Coordinators are responsible for storing and de-identifying samples of completed"", ""L022"": ""Assessments across a range of grades for moderation and quality assurance purposes."", ""L023"": ""Examinations"", ""L024"": ""Examinations may occur as a form of Assessment in an Assessment Unit. Examinations are"", ""L025"": ""conducted by the Student Administration Directorate on behalf of Schools during specified"", ""L026"": ""Assessment Periods."", ""L027"": ""Use of Examinations must take a whole-of-Course approach, recognising both their utility for"", ""L028"": ""assessing knowledge and their limitations for assessing a full range of CLOs and Capabilities."", ""L029"": ""An Examination cannot be used to assess all CLOs at a Course Stage."", ""L030"": ""An Examination must be based on the CLOs and content described in the approved Unit"", ""L031"": ""Outline, which is contained in CAPS."", ""L032"": ""The Unit Coordinator must advise Students in writing, where practicable, using a template in"", ""L033"": ""the LMS, of the Examination structure, conditions and requirements, including permitted"", ""L034"": ""materials. The Unit Coordinator may provide Students with sample questions and answers."", ""L035"": ""Where the Examination is “open-book”, the Unit Coordinator will ensure all required resources"", ""L036"": ""are freely accessible to Students."", ""L037"": ""All Examination papers must differ from any Examination paper previously used in that Course."", ""L038"": ""All Examination papers must be securely prepared, approved, and submitted using OESS to the"", ""L039"": ""Student Administration Directorate by the date published by the Director Student"", ""L040"": ""Administration."", ""L041"": ""All Examination papers (including for Deferred Examinations) must be submitted at the same"", ""L042"": ""time. An alternate Deferred Examination and an Examination paper that could be used for a"", ""L043"": ""Supplementary Assessment must be submitted at the same time. The alternate Deferred"", ""L044"": ""Examination and the Supplementary Assessment Examination paper may be the same as each"", ""L045"": ""other, with different title pages."", ""L046"": ""All Examination papers must be reviewed by a co-examiner recorded in the OESS. Where a"", ""L047"": ""co-examiner is not available in a particular discipline or field, an appropriate co-examiner will"", ""L048"": ""be nominated by the Associate Dean (Teaching and Learning) to review the paper, including"", ""L049"": ""for suitability, readability and clarity.""}","Assessment must:
be developmentally appropriate to the Course Level;
be in an appropriate format and genre for Students to demonstrate achievement in relation to
the CLOs being assessed;
be capable of generating relevant and timely feedback that offers insights into the Students’
performance and areas of improvement in relation to the specific CLOs; and
mitigate foreseeable risks to academic integrity.
Each Course must have a range of relevant and increasingly authentic Assessment types
appropriate to the discipline to evaluate different aspects of the CLOs and provide a
comprehensive understanding of the Student’s Capabilities.
Assessment Units must culminate in one summative Assessment being undertaken. With
approval of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Education), an Assessment Unit can have more than
one summative Assessment, which may occur outside of the Assessment Period.
For Assessment purposes, CLOs in an Assessment Unit must be equally weighted.
Electronic submission and return of Assessments
Assessments must be submitted in accordance with the relevant Unit Outline, unless
authorised by the relevant Associate Dean (Teaching and Learning).
Marked Assessments must be returned to the Student in a manner that protects the
confidentiality of the mark and the Student’s work. The default mode of Assessment
submission and return will be through the LMS, except for work completed in class.
Course/Unit Coordinators are responsible for storing and de-identifying samples of completed
Assessments across a range of grades for moderation and quality assurance purposes.
Examinations
Examinations may occur as a form of Assessment in an Assessment Unit. Examinations are
conducted by the Student Administration Directorate on behalf of Schools during specified
Assessment Periods.
Use of Examinations must take a whole-of-Course approach, recognising both their utility for
assessing knowledge and their limitations for assessing a full range of CLOs and Capabilities.
An Examination cannot be used to assess all CLOs at a Course Stage.
An Examination must be based on the CLOs and content described in the approved Unit
Outline, which is contained in CAPS.
The Unit Coordinator must advise Students in writing, where practicable, using a template in
the LMS, of the Examination structure, conditions and requirements, including permitted
materials. The Unit Coordinator may provide Students with sample questions and answers.
Where the Examination is “open-book”, the Unit Coordinator will ensure all required resources
are freely accessible to Students.
All Examination papers must differ from any Examination paper previously used in that Course.
All Examination papers must be securely prepared, approved, and submitted using OESS to the
Student Administration Directorate by the date published by the Director Student
Administration.
All Examination papers (including for Deferred Examinations) must be submitted at the same
time. An alternate Deferred Examination and an Examination paper that could be used for a
Supplementary Assessment must be submitted at the same time. The alternate Deferred
Examination and the Supplementary Assessment Examination paper may be the same as each
other, with different title pages.
All Examination papers must be reviewed by a co-examiner recorded in the OESS. Where a
co-examiner is not available in a particular discipline or field, an appropriate co-examiner will
be nominated by the Associate Dean (Teaching and Learning) to review the paper, including
for suitability, readability and clarity.
