uch that it can be confidently used to inform"", ""L020"": ""effective decision making."", ""L021"": ""The University will ensure that Data design and structure is informed by the way Critical Data"", ""L022"": ""must be used across the entire Data value chain including giving consideration to any potential"", ""L023"": ""downstream impacts and implications for strategic decision making, and compliance."", ""L024"": ""To ensure consistency, University Critical Data values and design principles will align with"", ""L025"": ""available government standards."", ""L026"": ""Uncontrolled Data"", ""L027"": ""Reports that use or are informed by Critical Data and do not conform with the University’s"", ""L028"": ""approved Data values and design parameters will be considered uncontrolled and will not be"", ""L029"": ""relied on for strategic purposes or use by any machine-driven data consumption."", ""L030"": ""ACCOUNTABILITIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES"", ""L031"": ""The Chief Information Officer is the Policy Owner and has overall responsibility for the content"", ""L032"": ""of this policy and its operation."", ""L033"": ""The Chief Data Officer is responsible for currency of information and provision of advice"", ""L034"": ""relating to operationalising this policy."", ""L035"": ""RELATED DOCUMENTS"", ""L036"": ""Policies"", ""L037"": ""Information Security and Information Technology"", ""L038"": ""Privacy"", ""L039"": ""Records Management"", ""L040"": ""Operational documents and resources"", ""L041"": ""Data Principles"", ""L042"": ""ECU Information Management Principles"", ""L043"": ""Risk appetite statement"", ""L044"": ""CONTACT INFORMATION"", ""L045"": ""For queries relating to this document please contact:"", ""L046"": ""Policy Owner"", ""L047"": ""Chief Information Officer""}","When considering exception requests, the primary focus will be the integrity of the University’s
Critical Data. This may mean requests, such as those relating to modifications to system
schemas and platforms, changes to Data values, or changes to design parameters, may not be
endorsed.
Data Creation
All reasonable steps will be taken to prevent or minimise data duplication, and to ensure
consistent, uniform, and streamlined processes are undertaken for Data modelling and Data
creation. Unnecessary duplication or deviations from standard processes arising from the
preferences of individual business areas will not be supported.
To the extent reasonable and practicable, creation of Master Data for entities must be limited
to one system or otherwise minimised to prevent unnecessary duplication.
Consistency of Master Data must be maintained across systems, and there must be only one
source of truth for each Critical Data Element. Where this isn’t reasonable and practicable, a
collaborative consultation led by the Chief Data Officer, or their delegate, will be undertaken to
agree on a practicable way forward.
Data Governance Approach
The University will adopt a collaborative, cohesive, and pragmatic approach to discussions and
actions required to ensure the University’s Critical Data are continually monitored, reviewed,
and improved, and the quality of Critical Data is such that it can be confidently used to inform
effective decision making.
The University will ensure that Data design and structure is informed by the way Critical Data
must be used across the entire Data value chain including giving consideration to any potential
downstream impacts and implications for strategic decision making, and compliance.
To ensure consistency, University Critical Data values and design principles will align with
available government standards.
Uncontrolled Data
Reports that use or are informed by Critical Data and do not conform with the University’s
approved Data values and design parameters will be considered uncontrolled and will not be
relied on for strategic purposes or use by any machine-driven data consumption.
ACCOUNTABILITIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
The Chief Information Officer is the Policy Owner and has overall responsibility for the content
of this policy and its operation.
The Chief Data Officer is responsible for currency of information and provision of advice
relating to operationalising this policy.
