m potential improvements."", ""L020"": ""De-identified Complaint data will be analysed at least every six months to identify trends, risks"", ""L021"": ""and underlying causes. A report will be provided to Council to support its assurance that those"", ""L022"": ""matters are appropriately identified and addressed."", ""L023"": ""Discontinuation of Complaints"", ""L024"": ""The University may discontinue dealing with a Complaint, in whole or in part, where:"", ""L025"": ""the Complainant withdraws the Complaint;"", ""L026"": ""the subject matter of the Complaint has previously been considered;"", ""L027"": ""the Complaint is frivolous or vexatious;"", ""L028"": ""the Complainant engages in unreasonable conduct, including behaviour that is abusive,"", ""L029"": ""threatening or harassing, and the University has taken reasonable steps to manage that"", ""L030"": ""conduct;"", ""L031"": ""the subject matter has been, is required to be, or is more appropriately addressed under"", ""L032"": ""another applicable framework; or"", ""L033"": ""the Complaint has been resolved through an agreed resolution or another process and no"", ""L034"": ""further action is reasonably required under this Policy."", ""L035"": ""Where appropriate, the Complainant will be informed of the basis for the proposed"", ""L036"": ""discontinuation and given a reasonable opportunity to respond or, where the issue concerns"", ""L037"": ""unreasonable conduct, to modify their behaviour before a decision is finalised."", ""L038"": ""The Complainant will be given reasons for the decision to discontinue the Complaint unless"", ""L039"": ""those reasons have already been provided."", ""L040"": ""Withdrawal or discontinuation does not prevent the University from taking action where the"", ""L041"": ""matter raises an ongoing safety, legal, regulatory, disciplinary or systemic issue."", ""L042"": ""Public Reporting"", ""L043"": ""The University will publish an annual report of de-identified Complaints data, including the"", ""L044"": ""number and types of Complaints, resolution timeframes, unresolved cases, and key"", ""L045"": ""performance indicators for managing complex Complaints. Public reporting will be subject to"", ""L046"": ""applicable privacy, confidentiality, legal professional privilege and statistical-disclosure"", ""L047"": ""requirements."", ""L048"": ""Mandatory Reporting and Record Keeping""}","A confidentiality direction ceases upon completion of the Complaint process, unless the
direction is withdrawn earlier or ongoing confidentiality is required under an applicable law.
Personal information will be handled in accordance with applicable privacy legislation and the
Privacy Policy.
Monitoring and Continuous Improvement
The University will monitor, review, and consider lessons learned throughout the Complaints
management lifecycle, from receipt through to resolution, and will identify and act on
opportunities for improving services, systems, and processes.
The University will identify, monitor and take reasonable steps to remove barriers to making
Complaints, including barriers experienced by specific student cohorts or arising from
accessibility, cultural, linguistic or systemic factors.
The University will undertake periodic review and benchmarking of Complaint policies,
procedures, processes and Staff training.
Students and Staff, including persons with relevant lived experience of, or directly affected by,
discrimination, harassment, victimisation or violence, will be consulted on the design, review
and improvement of complaints processes. Their feedback will be genuinely considered and
the University will provide a summary of its response to those who participated in the
consultation process.
Complainants will be invited to provide feedback to inform potential improvements.
De-identified Complaint data will be analysed at least every six months to identify trends, risks
and underlying causes. A report will be provided to Council to support its assurance that those
matters are appropriately identified and addressed.
Discontinuation of Complaints
The University may discontinue dealing with a Complaint, in whole or in part, where:
the Complainant withdraws the Complaint;
the subject matter of the Complaint has previously been considered;
the Complaint is frivolous or vexatious;
the Complainant engages in unreasonable conduct, including behaviour that is abusive,
threatening or harassing, and the University has taken reasonable steps to manage that
conduct;
the subject matter has been, is required to be, or is more appropriately addressed under
another applicable framework; or
the Complaint has been resolved through an agreed resolution or another process and no
further action is reasonably required under this Policy.
Where appropriate, the Complainant will be informed of the basis for the proposed
discontinuation and given a reasonable opportunity to respond or, where the issue concerns
unreasonable conduct, to modify their behaviour before a decision is finalised.
The Complainant will be given reasons for the decision to discontinue the Complaint unless
those reasons have already been provided.
Withdrawal or discontinuation does not prevent the University from taking action where the
matter raises an ongoing safety, legal, regulatory, disciplinary or systemic issue.
Public Reporting
The University will publish an annual report of de-identified Complaints data, including the
number and types of Complaints, resolution timeframes, unresolved cases, and key
performance indicators for managing complex Complaints. Public reporting will be subject to
applicable privacy, confidentiality, legal professional privilege and statistical-disclosure
requirements.
Mandatory Reporting and Record Keeping
