May 2022: revised (major). A review of the University’s Complaints policies was undertaken to
ensure the policy position was contemporary and fit-for-purpose. The review identified an
opportunity to consolidate the Student Complaints and Public Complaints policies into a single
overarching Complaints policy. Re-drafting was undertaken to ensure the policy was
principle-based and to remove operational content from the policy. The review made it
possible to rescind P Public Complaints and the former Student Complaints policy. The PL
code (P) for the former Student Complaints policy was retained for the amalgamated
policy.
2 September 2026: Vice-Chancellor approval of policy amendments (GDA26-051).
Amendments include: (i) expansion of scope and definitions; (ii) enhanced requirements for
complaint handling and outcomes; and (iii) introduction of new provisions on procedural
fairness, non-retaliation, confidentiality, and trauma informed practice.
