Purpose and Scope 
This policy outlines the principles underpinning the University’s student academic 
integrity standards and its response to student academic misconduct. 
Academic integrity is the commitment to and demonstration of honest and fair 
behaviour in all forms of academic work and practice. It is an indispensable foundation 
of university learning, teaching and research. A commitment to academic integrity is 
fundamental to the reputation of the University and to the value of the degrees it 
awards to students.  
This policy applies to students enrolled in non-award, undergraduate and 
postgraduate coursework units and courses. Academic misconduct by Higher Degree 
Students is dealt with under the Research Integrity Policy and Research Integrity 
Procedure.  
This policy applies to all staff and students. 
Objectives 
• 
Align the University’s student academic integrity policy with:  
o 
The Higher Education Standards Framework (Threshold Standards) 2021  
o 
The Education Services for Overseas Students Act 2000 and the related 
National Code of Practice for Registration Authorities and Providers of 
Education and Training to Overseas Students 2018  
o 
The Tertiary Education Quality and Standards Agency Act 2011  
o 
The Tertiary Education Quality and Standards Agency Amendment 
(Prohibiting Academic Cheating Services) Act 2020.  
• 
Create and maintain a culture of academic integrity  
• 
Identify behaviours that constitute student academic misconduct.  
 Student Academic Integrity Policy  
Murdoch University | N087 | Source page 1
Bundle page 11 | N087 | source page 1 | line numbers at left",,"Page 2 of 4 
Overarching Regulations 
Student Integrity Regulations  
Policy 
1. 
The University aims to create and maintain a culture of academic integrity that: 
1.1 makes explicit to students the norms, structures and practices of the wider 
academic culture of which student academic integrity forms a part 
1.2 promotes academic integrity by supporting students to use, generate and 
communicate information and ideas in an honest and responsible manner 
1.3 ensures that student academic integrity is supported through curriculum 
and assessment design and their periodic review  
1.4 undertakes that all academic staff are trained in educating students about 
academic integrity 
1.5 provides students with timely opportunities to learn and practise the 
principles and techniques needed to maintain academic integrity. 
2. 
