4.1.4. outcomes imposed for student Misconduct will be appropriate and 
proportionate 
4.1.5. privacy will be treated in accordance with the university’s Privacy 
Policy 
4.1.6. the requisite standard of proof is the balance of probabilities.  
5. 
Managing Allegations of Student Misconduct  
5.1. Allegations of student Misconduct will be made in accordance with 
university policies and procedures.  
5.2. The relevant decision-makers will review allegations of Misconduct, 
except those related to Gender-based Violence, and: 
5.2.1. dismiss the allegation if it does not constitute Misconduct 
5.2.2. determine that it be resolved through an educative process 
5.2.3. impose an outcome if there is clear evidence that Misconduct has 
occurred 
5.2.4. refer the matter for formal investigation.  
6. 
Outcomes  
6.1. Where a decision-maker determines that Misconduct has occurred, or an 
allegation of Gender-based Violence is substantiated, the following 
Outcomes may be applied: 
6.1.1. the requirement to access support or undertake training 
6.1.2. a reprimand, caution or requirement to undertake service 
6.1.3. variation to assessment activity or results 
6.1.4. variation to results, enrolment or award of degree 
6.1.5. the requirement to make financial/material restitution 
6.1.6. the requirement to make a retraction or apology 
6.1.7. Suspension 
6.1.8. Exclusion or Expulsion. 
6.2. In the event of Exclusion or Expulsion the relevant decision-maker is the 
Vice Chancellor. 
6.3. Details of Outcomes are included in Schedule 1 of these Regulations.  
7. 
Appeal  
7.1. A student can appeal a decision in accordance with the Student Appeals 
Procedure.  
 
 
 
