SCHEDULE 1 
Outcomes for Failure to Meet Student Integrity Standards 
 
1. 
The relevant decision-maker may impose outcomes including:  
1.1 The requirement to access support or undertake training; 
1.1.1 
require the student to take part in specified support activities. 
1.1.2 
require the student to take a course of corrective action or specified 
training. 
1.2 A reprimand, caution or requirement to undertake service  
1.2.1 
issue a reprimand, caution, behavioural reminder or formal 
warning. 
1.2.2 
require the student to undertake service. 
1.3 Variation to learning, assessment activity or results 
1.3.1 
require the student to resubmit, or revise and resubmit, the whole 
or part of the assessment, examination or research. 
1.3.2 
disallow or amend a mark or grade (including zero marks) for the 
whole or part of the assessment task, examination, final grade or 
unit. 
1.3.3 
determine that any learning activity be attempted again. 
1.4 Variation to results, enrolment or award of degree 
1.4.1 
place condition/s on the student’s enrolment or academic 
performance. 
1.4.2 
require the student to transfer to another course if the student 
wishes to remain enrolled at the University. 
1.4.3 
determine that the degree cannot be awarded. 
1.4.4 
recommend to Academic Council to rescind the student’s award. 
1.5 The requirement to make financial/material restitution 
1.5.1 
require the student to pay for repair or replacement of damaged or 
lost property or facilities. 
1.5.2 
require restitution of data. 
1.6 Require a retraction or apology 
1.6.1 
require a verbal, written or published apology. 
1.6.2 
require a retraction of a publication/s or amendment of material on 
the public record. 
 
 
