the date upon which the Regulations are made."", ""L028"": ""Revision History"", ""L029"": ""Published 25/06/2010, Government Gazette No. 112 p2887"", ""L030"": ""Note: All enquiries relating to Legislation should be referred to the University"", ""L031"": ""Secretary’s Office."", ""L032"": ""Page 1 of 1"", ""L033"": ""[OFFICIAL]""}","Page 1 of 1 
[OFFICIAL]
 
 
 
 
 
This Statute should be read in conjunction with the Student Integrity Regulations 
1. 
This Statute comes into operation on the day it is published in the Government 
Gazette. 
Regulations 
2. 
Regulations will be made under this Statute for the discipline of students 
of the University. The Regulations will specify: 
(a) 
the misconduct for which a student may be disciplined by the University; 
(b) 
the procedure for dealing with allegations of misconduct made against 
a student; 
(c) 
the penalties that may be imposed on a student if any allegation of 
misconduct is upheld; 
(d) 
the capacity for an appeal against any finding of misconduct against a 
student; 
(e) 
any other matters which the Senate considers necessary to give 
effect to this Statute and the Regulations. 
Repeal 
3. 
Statute No 23 - Student Discipline is hereby repealed. 
Transitional Provisions 
4. 
On the date the Regulations are made, any disciplinary action previously 
taken, commenced or implemented under Statute No. 23 – Student 
Discipline shall be completed in accordance with the provisions of Statute 
No. 23. 
5. 
Any allegations of misconduct made against a student after the date the 
Regulations are made, shall be dealt with under the Regulations 
notwithstanding that the matter giving rise to the allegations may have taken 
place prior to the date upon which the Regulations are made. 
Revision History 
Published 25/06/2010, Government Gazette No. 112 p2887 
 
Note: All enquiries relating to Legislation should be referred to the University 
Secretary’s Office.  
Statute No. 26 – Student Misconduct 
