Purpose and Scope 
Murdoch University is committed to protecting the privacy of individuals and 
responsibly managing information in accordance with the Privacy and Responsible 
Information Sharing Act 2024 (WA) (PRIS Act). This policy outlines how the University 
collects, uses, stores, shares, and safeguards personal information to support 
education, research, and community engagement while ensuring compliance with 
Western Australian law and other impacted legislation. 
This policy and the supporting Privacy Procedure  apply to students, employees, other 
members of the University Community and the public and includes information 
collected through teaching, research, administration, and community services and 
information shared with external entities under the Responsible Information Sharing 
Principles (RSPs) and core Information Privacy Principles (IPPs) governing collection, 
use, integrity, storage, security, and access to information as set out in the PRIS Act. 
Policy 
1. 
Murdoch University adheres to the Information Privacy Principles (IPPs) 
and Responsible Information Sharing Principles (RSPs) established under 
the PRIS Act. 
1.1 Lawful and fair collection: Information is collected only for legitimate 
University purposes. 
1.2 Transparency: Individuals are informed about how their information will be 
used. 
1.3 Data minimisation: Only necessary information is collected and retained. 
1.4 Security: Personal information is protected against loss, misuse, and 
unauthorised access. 
1.5 Access and correction: Individuals have the right to access and correct their 
personal information. 
1.6 Responsible sharing: Information is shared only when it serves a clear 
public interest, is authorised under the PRIS Act, and safeguards privacy. 
 
 
 
