Purpose and Scope 
Murdoch University is committed to protecting the privacy of individuals and 
responsibly managing information in accordance with the Privacy and Responsible 
Information Sharing Act 2024 (WA) (PRIS Act). This procedure outlines how the 
University collects, uses, stores, shares, and safeguards personal information to 
support education, research, and community engagement while ensuring compliance 
with Western Australian law and other impacted legislation. 
Supporting the Privacy Policy, this procedure   applies to students, employees, other 
members of the University community and the public and includes information 
collected through teaching, research, administration, and community services and 
information shared with external entities under the Responsible Information Sharing 
Principles (RSPs) and core Information Privacy Principles (IPPs) governing collection, 
use, integrity, storage, security, and access to information as set out in the PRIS Act. 
Overarching Policies 
Privacy Policy 
Procedure 
1.  
Privacy Officer 
1.1 The Vice Chancellor will appoint a Privacy Officer for the University who will 
hold responsibilities under the Privacy and Responsible Information 
Sharing (PRIS) Act 2024 (WA).  
 
2.  
Collection 
2.1 The University will collect personal information only by lawful and fair 
means. 
2.2 So long as it is reasonable and practicable to do so, personal information 
will be collected directly from the individual. 
2.3 If it is necessary to collect personal information from a third party, 
reasonable steps will be taken to inform the individual of the circumstances 
of this collection. 
