8.  
Disclosure to WA government agencies 
8.1 Murdoch University is subject to Western Australia’s responsible 
information sharing framework established under the PRIS Act, 
consequently: 
8.1.1 
Information sharing requests are assessed against the PRIS Act 
criteria. 
8.1.2 
Sharing is permitted only when it improves community outcomes 
(e.g., health, education, research) and aligns with privacy 
protections. 
8.1.3 
Aboriginal data governance principles are respected, ensuring 
culturally appropriate handling of Indigenous information. 
 
9.  
Security of personal information and breach notification 
9.1 Reasonable technical and organisational measures will be taken to protect 
the personal information held by the University from misuse, interference, 
and loss, as well as from unauthorised access, modification, or disclosure. 
9.2 As part of the security measures, the University has developed a range of 
policies and standards, available on the website, which should be read in 
conjunction with this Privacy Policy and Privacy Procedure in the context of 
personal information. These policies relate to: 
9.2.1 
Privacy collection notice of personal information 
9.2.2 
Information security Incident Management Policy 
9.2.3 
IT conditions of use policy 
9.2.4 
Email and electronic messaging policy 
9.2.5 
Information Management Policy 
