9.3 Personal information will be retained in accordance with the Western 
Australian University Sector Disposal Authority established under the State 
Records Act (WA) and disposed of lawfully and securely. 
9.4 In the event of a serious data breach, Murdoch University will notify the 
Western Australian Information Commissioner and affected individuals, as 
required under the PRIS Act. 
 
10.  Unsolicited personal information 
10.1 If the University receives personal information about an individual that was 
not solicited, information will be assessed whether it is a part of a public 
record or could have been lawfully collected. If not, and if lawful and 
reasonable, steps will be taken to destroy or de-identify the information. 
10.2 If any personal information is uploaded to the University’s Facebook page 
or other social media channels, no steps are taken by the University in 
relation to that information. If a specific enquiry or complaint is received, 
steps considered necessary in the circumstances will be taken to 
investigate and address the matter within a reasonable time. 
 
11.   Direct Marketing 
11.1 As a general rule, personal information will not be disclosed (including any 
sensitive information) for direct marketing purposes. 
11.2 Subject to clause 11.5, the University may use personal information 
(excluding sensitive information) collected to send direct marketing material 
that an individual would reasonably expect to receive. A “reasonable 
expectation” includes situations where there is a past or existing 
relationship with the University, or an individual has expressed interest in 
the functions or activities of the University. Such material may include, but 
is not limited to, invitations or information about the University’s events and 
activities. 
11.3 Subject to clause 11.5, the University may also use personal information 
(excluding sensitive information) collected from a third party to send direct 
marketing material to individuals which may or may not be reasonably 
expected, but only where there has been consent or it is impracticable to 
obtain that consent. 
11.4 Sensitive information will only be used for direct marketing purposes with 
prior consent. 
11.5 All direct marketing material will include an opt-out mechanism. If an 
individual decides at any time that they do not wish to receive certain 
promotional material, they may request removal from the mailing list, and 
this will be actioned without charge. 
11.6 Subject to clause 11.5, the University may share personal information 
