in the Australian Code for the Responsible Conduct of Research (the Code), the 
Research Integrity Policy, the Student Code of Conduct and the Student Integrity 
Regulations. 
3.1. A breach of these Regulations, the Code or any other relevant legislation 
and University policies by a candidate or Supervisory Panel member must 
be reported and will be managed in accordance with the Research Integrity 
Procedure. 
3.1.1. A breach by the candidate may result in termination of candidature. 
3.2. Any disciplinary matter will be managed under the Student Integrity 
Regulations. 
