20. A candidate may apply to enrol concurrently for another qualification at this 
University or elsewhere with the Dean's written approval, as outlined in the 
Graduate Research Degrees Procedure.  
21. A candidate must withdraw or suspend enrolment in the concurrent program if 
they do not make satisfactory progress in the graduate research degree at 
Murdoch University. 
22. Subject to exceptional circumstances, an extension or Leave of Absence will not 
be granted due to concurrent enrolment. 
Expected Time Commitment 
23. It is expected that a full-time candidate would commit a minimum of 37.5 hours 
per week to their degree  
Mode of Enrolment 
24. Subject to Regulation 25, candidates who are residents within the Perth 
metropolitan area who are not enrolled in coursework units are normally enrolled 
in the face to face attendance mode.  
25. The Dean may approve the enrolment of existing and new candidates (part-time 
and full-time) in the mixed mode, which is restricted to candidates who: 
25.1. are normally resident outside the Perth metropolitan area;  
25.2. are resident within the Perth metropolitan area who, for reasons of disability 
or infirmity, or other acceptable reasons, are unable to attend the 
University’s facilities on a regular basis;  
25.3. reach an agreement with the Principal Supervisor about the amount of 
candidature time spent at the University and when. Candidatures proposing 
to have no time spent at the University will not normally be approved, and 
25.4. meet any stipulated conditions to ensure adequate supervision and 
resources are available. 
Leave Entitlements 
26. Candidates are entitled to twenty days Annual Leave, and ten days Personal 
Leave each year. Personal Leave may include family caring responsibilities. 
26.1. Leave entitlements are calculated on a pro-rata basis for part-time 
candidates. 
26.2. Leave entitlements may be accrued, but unused leave will be forfeited at 
the end of the enrolment period. 
27. Candidates who have completed at least one year of full-time or equivalent part-
time candidature, subject to Regulation 45.3, may apply to the Dean, in 
accordance with the Graduate Research Degrees Procedure and subject to any 
scholarship conditions, for a period of leave as follows: 
27.1. Parental Leave, for up to a total of one year, which may be granted to the 
primary carer of a newborn infant or adopted child. 
27.1.1. To be eligible for a subsequent period of Parental Leave, the 
candidate must be continuously enrolled for at least another twelve 
months.  
