Supervisor Eligibility Criteria 
36. A Principal Supervisor or Co-Supervisor must be on the Supervisor Register and 
must maintain their registration in order to supervise candidates. 
36.1. To be registered, staff must meet the criteria for supervision as detailed in 
Regulations 36 to 41, and as outlined in the Supervisor Register. 
37. Principal Supervisors must meet the following criteria: 
37.1. possess a degree at least equivalent to that undertaken by the candidate; 
37.2. be a University academic employee based in a School or Institute who can 
be expected to provide supervision for the duration of the candidature;  
37.3. satisfy the University’s definition of research-active. 
38. A proposed Principal Supervisor who meets Regulations 37 must also comply 
with the supervisory registry specifically as it pertains to the requirements for 
additional supervisors and/or the appointment of a mentor supervisor.  
39. Co-Supervisors must be a Murdoch staff member and will normally possess a 
degree at least equivalent to that undertaken by the candidate. 
40. Staff supervising more than the EFTSL caps outlined in Schedule A must seek 
the endorsement of the Head of School, by whatever name known, or relevant 
Pro Vice Chancellor Institute, as well as approval by the Dean for each additional 
candidate supervision. 
41. A Supervisor appointed under Regulation 34 will: 
41.1. meet the eligibility criteria specified in Regulations 36 to 40;  
41.2. be free of conflict of interest, as outlined in the Conflict of Interest Policy; 
and 
41.3. meet the Supervisor responsibilities outlined in Schedule A. 
42. If a Supervisor is unable to continue supervising a candidate for any reason, the 
Head of School, by whatever name known, or relevant Pro Vice Chancellor 
Institute, in consultation with the candidate, is responsible for ensuring that 
adequate and acceptable supervision arrangements, subject to Regulations 36 
to 41, are made prior to the Supervisor ceasing their supervisory commitments. 
43. If a Supervisor plans to take leave for any period of more than three months 
during the candidature, in consultation with the candidate and subject to the 
Head of School, by whatever name known, or relevant Pro Vice Chancellor 
Institute’s endorsement, the Supervisor must obtain approval from the Dean for 
the supervision arrangements for the period of their absence, which remain 
subject to Regulations 36 to 41. 
44. Subject to these Regulations, in exceptional circumstances, the Dean may 
determine any special arrangements required for the candidate’s supervision. 
Confirmation of Candidature  
45. Candidature is deemed to be probationary until confirmed in accordance with the 
Graduate Research Degrees Procedure within the confirmation of candidature 
timeframe set out in the Handbook. 
