58. A candidate may transfer between attendance modes, subject to the Dean’s 
approval on the recommendation of the Principal Supervisor and endorsement 
by the PGRC, any scholarship conditions, and in accordance with Regulations 
24 and 25. 
Withdrawal from Candidature 
59. A candidate may withdraw from candidature up until the date that the thesis is 
submitted by informing the Dean in writing.  
59.1. The candidature is terminated once the candidate withdraws and 
Regulation 65 applies. 
59.2. Withdrawal from candidature is not granted retrospectively. 
59.3. Enrolment load and associated fees or charges stand for withdrawals made 
after the census date. 
60. Where a candidate’s enrolment is terminated following a withdrawal from 
candidature the candidate subsequently enrols in a new graduate research 
degree at the same level: 
60.1. if at least three years have elapsed since the previous enrolment, the 
candidate is entitled to the maximum enrolment period allowed for the 
course, as outlined in Regulation 17, subject to any restrictions placed by 
the relevant professional bodies; or 
60.2. if fewer than three years have elapsed since the previous enrolment, the 
candidate is entitled to the maximum enrolment period allowed for the 
course, as outlined in Regulation 17, subject to Regulation 12, less any 
period of prior entitlement consumed; or 
60.3. if fewer than three years have elapsed since the previous enrolment and 
the full entitlement period has been consumed, re-admission will be subject 
to the Dean’s approval in accordance with Regulations 19. 
61. Where a candidate withdraws from candidature and subsequently enrols in a 
different graduate research degree course at a different level, the candidate is 
entitled to a full enrolment period for the new course, as outlined in Regulation 
17, provided the change in enrolment is not a transfer as set out in Regulations 
63 to 64. 
Withdrawal from a Coursework Unit 
62. Candidates who are completing coursework units in accordance with 
Regulations 48 and 49 may withdraw before the census date without penalty 
from a unit or incurring fees. 
62.1. Unit withdrawals shall be recorded on the candidate’s academic transcript. 
62.2. Candidates can only apply for approved withdrawal or fee remission for a 
unit with the approval of the Dean, in accordance with the Graduate 
Research Degrees Procedure.  
62.2.1. Fees may apply. 
Transfer of Candidature 
63. Subject to Regulation 63.2, candidates enrolled for a Master of Philosophy may 
apply to transfer to a Doctoral Degree (Research) with credit for the work 
