Nomination of Examiners 
73. Following the candidate’s notice of intention to submit, the Principal Supervisor, 
in consultation with the other Supervisors, must nominate examiners in 
accordance with Regulations 74 and 75 and the Graduate Research Degrees 
Procedure. 
73.1. Candidates may contribute a list of potential examiners and exclusion list 
to their Supervisor/s, but otherwise must play no part in determining their 
examiners. 
73.2. Candidates must not communicate with examiners during the course of the 
nomination and examination process, as outlined in Regulations 83 to 83.3.  
74. Subject to Regulation 75, the Dean will normally appoint three (two preferred and 
one reserve) examiners; with at least two from the recommendations of the 
Principal Supervisor. 
