[OFFICIAL]
90. In accordance with open access principles, the candidate’s thesis is available 
through the University Library for consultation, loan and photocopying, subject to 
any restrictions contained in the Copyright Act 1968  (C’th). 
90.1. Subject to Regulation 90.2, an access restriction (embargo) normally not 
exceeding one year may be approved by the Dean in exceptional 
circumstances, if requested by the candidate in accordance with the 
Graduate Research Degrees Procedure. 
90.2. Where, pursuant to the terms of any agreement between the University, the 
candidate and/or any third party, obligations of confidentiality are imposed 
in relation to all or a section/s of a candidate’s thesis, an access restriction 
as specified in the agreement will automatically apply to the thesis or 
section/s of it, consistent with the terms and conditions of those 
confidentiality obligations. 
Section 2: Regulations governing all matters in relation to coursework 
undertaken as a requirement in the graduate research degrees of Murdoch 
University 
91. The Regulations in Section 2 apply to all matters governing courses or units 
undertaken as a requirement in the graduate research degrees of the University 
unless Academic Council has approved otherwise.  
Award of Credit or Advanced Standing 
92. Subject to Regulation 18, candidates may be granted credit on the coursework 
component of their degree on the basis of previous studies undertaken at this or 
another recognised university or tertiary institution, in accordance with the 
Recognition of Prior Learning Procedure. 
92.1. Where credit is granted, the maximum enrolment period, as set out in 
Regulation 17, will be reduced accordingly. 
93. Enrolment in Work Integrated Learning units must be in accordance with the 
Work Integrated Learning Policy  
94. The assessment methods of each coursework unit shall comply with the 
Assessment Procedure. 
Structure of Graduate Research Degree Courses 
95. Unless otherwise approved by Academic Council, in addition to Regulation 2, in 
order to be awarded a graduate research degree at Murdoch University, a 
candidate must successfully complete the number of credit points required for 
that award (subject to reduction as a result of the use of any credit awarded under 
Regulation 92), as outlined in the Handbook. 
Academic Progress 
96. Academic Chairs are responsible for the academic matters and the respective 
enrolled graduate research degree candidates within their relevant School. 
97. The Academic Progress of each candidate enrolled in the coursework 
component of a graduate research degree is reviewed periodically, usually at the 
end of each academic period. 
98. For the purpose of determining satisfactory progress where a unit is taken over 
two or more academic periods, the credit points for the unit will be counted within 
