[OFFICIAL]
3.1. seek professional, psychosocial or medical support  
3.2. obtain legal advice 
3.3. seek external review of the matter by a government body   
3.4. comply with law, including those related to safety. 
4. 
Action will be taken to address the underlying causes of complaints.  
5. 
Barriers to submitting complaints will be identified and reasonable steps 
undertaken to minimise or remove them. 
6. 
Roles responsible for managing or resolving a complaint, will:  
6.1. be at the appropriate level 
6.2. have appropriate knowledge. 
7. 
Appropriate mitigations and supports will be put in place to respond to the 
wellbeing and safety needs of employees handling complaints and action will be 
taken to address underlying risks. 
8. 
Accurate and relevant information will be provided in plain English. 
9. 
Information about complaint processes will be advertised and publicly available. 
Governance 
Approval Authority 
Senior Leadership Team 
Owner 
Vice Chancellor 
