Code: 
1. 
General Conduct 
1.1 Staff of Murdoch University are required to do the following throughout the 
course of their employment: 
1.1.1 
behave honestly and with integrity; 
1.1.2 
act with care and diligence; 
1.1.3 
act with courtesy and respect in all dealings with other staff and 
students; 
1.1.4 
comply with all applicable laws; 
1.1.5 
comply with all lawful and reasonable direction given by someone 
who has authority to give the direction; 
1.1.6 
not make improper use of inside information; or the employee’s 
duties, status, power or authority, in order to gain, or seek to gain, 
a benefit or advantage for the staff member of for any other 
persons; and 
1.1.7 
at all times behave in a way that upholds the Code of Ethics, and 
the integrity and good reputation of Murdoch University, both within 
Australia and overseas. 
 
2. 
Freedom of Speech and Academic Freedom  
2.1 Murdoch University declares its commitment to uphold Freedom of Speech 
and Academic Freedom as fundamental to the process of gaining and 
disseminating knowledge without unreasonable interference or penalty by 
the University. The University recognises and protects the concept and 
practice of Academic Freedom as essential to the proper conduct of 
teaching, research and scholarship within the University.  
2.2 Staff are expected to behave ethically and respectfully in all dealings with 
members of the University and wider community in their capacity as a staff 
of the University. 
2.3 The University recognises the freedom of Academic Staff to participate in 
professional or representative academic bodies. 
 
3. 
Rescinded. 
 
