1 Purpose 
Murdoch University’s vision is to be widely recognised as the university of choice for 
people who care, who value inclusion, curiosity and innovation, and who seek to make 
a positive social impact. We recognise the important role our suppliers play in 
supporting this work through the goods and services they provide.  
The University seeks to partner with suppliers who align with our values. This includes 
our commitment to sustainability, equity, diversity and inclusion, and to be the 
university of first choice for First Nations communities.  
This Supplier Code of Conduct (Code) sets out the standards and behaviours the 
University expects from its suppliers. It applies to all suppliers of goods and services, 
including independent contractors, labour hire providers, and the employees and 
subcontractors of those suppliers.  
This Code supports the University’s Ngala Kwop Biddi Strategy 2023-2030 and 
reflects our commitment to the principles and standards of the United Nations 
Declaration of Human Rights, International Labour Organisation Conventions and the 
UN Sustainable Development Goals.  
The University believes in the power of collaboration to effect meaningful change. The 
University is committed to these standards and expects its suppliers to uphold them in 
their own operations and supply chains.  
2 Application of the Code of Conduct  
Under this Code, suppliers are expected to:  
• Read and understand this Code.  
• Take practical and proportionate steps to comply with its requirements.  
• Communicate this Code to employees and subcontractors involved in 
delivering goods or services to the University.  
• Notify the University in writing if they become aware of any material non-
compliance with this Code.  
• Cooperate with reasonable requests for information, audits, due diligence 
checks or investigations related to this Code.  
Supplier Code of Conduct 
 
