3 Sustainability  
The University seeks to be a leader in education, research and operations that support 
a more sustainable world.  
The University expects suppliers to operate in a way that manages environmental 
impacts linked to the goods and services they provide. At a minimum, suppliers are 
expected to comply with all relevant environmental laws and regulations.  
Suppliers are encouraged to:  
• Integrate sustainability practices into business decisions and operations.  
• Reduce environmental impacts associated with energy use, emissions, water 
use, waste and hazardous substances.  
• Support more sustainable production and supply practices, including reduced 
packaging and increased use of recyclable or recycled materials where 
practicable.  
