[OFFICIAL]
5 First Nations  
The University is committed to advancing opportunities for First Nations peoples and 
supporting meaningful participation in education, employment and economic activity.  
Suppliers are expected to:  
• Respect and uphold First Nations rights, knowledge, cultural heritage and 
cultural protocols.  
• Promote safe, fair and inclusive workplaces for First Nations employees and 
contractors.  
• Seek, where practicable, to engage First Nations businesses within their supply 
chains.  
• Engage with First Nations communities in a respectful and culturally informed 
manner.  
The University recognises that progress requires practical action. Suppliers are 
therefore expected to demonstrate genuine and proportionate efforts to support First 
Nations participation and inclusion.  
6 Modern Slavery  
The University requires suppliers to comply with the intent and purpose of the Modern 
Slavery Act 2018 (Cth).  
Modern slavery includes practices such as human trafficking, forced labour, child 
labour and other forms of exploitation. Suppliers are expected to identify, assess and 
manage modern slavery risks within their operations and supply chains where these 
risks are relevant to the goods and services provided to the University.  
Suppliers should have policies and processes in place to prevent exploitation and to 
respond appropriately where risks or incidents are identified.  
The University maintains a reporting mechanism that allows workers, suppliers and 
other stakeholders to raise concerns confidentially, including concerns relating to 
modern slavery. Suppliers are expected to support the use of such mechanisms and 
not retaliate against individuals who raise concerns in good faith.  
7 Ethical Conduct  
The University expects suppliers to conduct business with integrity and 
professionalism.  
Suppliers are expected to:  
• Act honestly and fairly in all dealings with the University.  
• Disclose any actual or perceived conflicts of interest as soon as practicable.  
• Protect confidential, private and sensitive University information.  
Murdoch University | N089 | Source page 3
Bundle page 117 | N089 | source page 3 | line numbers at left","ed materials where 
practicable.  
The University expects suppliers to demonstrate ongoing improvements in 
sustainability performance where their activities present material environment 
impacts.  
4 Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  
The University aims to foster a safe, inclusive and respectful community where all 
people are treated fairly and with dignity.  
Suppliers are expected to operate ethical workplaces and comply with all relevant 
equal opportunity and anti-discrimination laws.  
Suppliers should:  
• Provide workplaces free from discrimination, harassment and bullying.  
• Support fair and transparent recruitment, development and promotion 
practices.  
• Foster inclusive and respectful working environments.  
• Take reasonable steps to support staff wellbeing and participation.  
• Take reasonable steps to promote the above principles within their own supply 
chains.  
