• Avoid bribery, corruption, or improper influence, including offering gifts, benefits 
or hospitality to gain an unfair advantage.  
• Use fair contract terms and transparent processes when engaging 
subcontractors.  
• Treat their workforce in a fair and respectful manner.  
8 Workplace Health and Safety  
The University is committed to providing a safe and healthy environment for staff, 
students, contractors and visitors.  
Suppliers are expected to:  
• Comply with all applicable workplace health and safety laws.  
• Identify and manage health and safety risks associated with the goods or 
services they provide.  
• Provide appropriate training, supervision, resources and guidance to support 
safe work practices.  
• Ensure workers understand their health and safety responsibilities.  
