[OFFICIAL]
 
 
 
 
Purpose and Scope 
To establish the principles for governing and managing University Legislation and 
Policy Documents. 
This policy applies to all members of the University community. 
Policy 
1. 
In this policy, the following words have the following meanings: 
1.1. An “Act” is a formal law or decision made by a Federal or State legislature. 
1.2. “Authorisation” is explained in the Delegations and Authorisations Policy. 
1.3. A “Code” is statement of mandatory requirements guiding the behaviour of 
the University’s community. 
1.4. A “By-Law” is delegated legislation established under the Murdoch 
University Act 1973 which regulates the University. By-Laws pertain to the 
use of university lands and buildings and provide for penalties for breaches. 
1.5. “Delegation” is defined in the Delegations and Authorisations Policy. 
1.6. A “Policy” is a statement of mandatory principles guiding the University’s 
operations and significant decision making. 
1.7. “Policy Documents” are Codes, charters, Policies, frameworks, terms of 
reference, plans, principles, statements, Procedures, standards, and 
guidelines. 
1.8. A “Procedure” is a statement of the University’s mandatory processes and 
responsibilities which give effect to a Policy. 
1.9. A “Regulation” is a delegated legislation established under the Murdoch 
University Act 1973 and is designed to control or govern procedure or 
conduct. 
1.10. A “Rule” is delegated legislation established under the Murdoch University 
Act 1973 governing a particular matter. 
1.11. A “Statute” is established under the Murdoch University Act 1973. It is a law 
or directive, or mandate intended to be or a permanent or long-lasting that 
Policy Governance and Management Policy 
