Policy. 
13. Each Coursework Award Course has an approved structure that specifies the: 
13.1 Components included in the Course; 
13.2 Units (or equivalent) included in each Component; 
13.3 Total credit point value for the Course and each of its Components; and 
13.4 Completion requirements for the Course and each of its Components. 
14. One credit point reflects an average student workload of 50 hours. 
15. A unit is normally worth three credit points. 
Course Quotas 
16. The design of a course, major, co-major or minor will accommodate any Quotas 
for Units. 
Course Components 
17. All Components of Coursework Award Courses have a title and unique 
identification code. 
18. The Components which may be included in Coursework Award Courses are: 
Discovery Study, Course Core, Major, and Options. 
19. The total credit point value of each Component must be completed. 
20. Discovery Study: 
20.1 Is drawn from a set of Units that meet criteria recommended to Academic 
Council by the Deputy Vice Chancellor Education in collaboration with the 
Senior Leadership Team and the broader academic community;  
20.2 Is a set of Units that are approved by the Deputy Vice Chancellor Education; 
and 
20.3 Is offered as a student-nominated choice. 
