29. All Bachelor Award Courses: 
29.1 Require students to complete Discovery Study; 
29.2 Have transition experiences and research training embedded within their 
Course Core and/or Major/s; 
29.3 Require students to pass a minimum of 12 credit points at 100 Level before 
enrolling in higher level units; 
29.4 Should be structured to accommodate two Majors within the total credit 
point value of the Course, where possible; and 
29.5 Should be structured to enable their inclusion in Combined Award Courses. 
Bachelor Award Courses 
30. A Standard Bachelor Award Course has a total credit point value of 72 or 96 
credit points and includes: 
30.1 Discovery Study with a total credit point value between 3 and 9; 
30.2 A Course Core with a total credit point value between 9 and 15; 
30.3 A Major with a total credit point value of 24; and 
30.4 Options with a total credit point value of at least 24 consisting of: 
30.4.1 Additional Major/s each with total credit point values not exceeding 
that allocated to Options; 
30.4.2 Co-Major/s each with a standard value of 18 credit points and up to 
24 credit points in 96 credit point Bachelor Award Courses; 
30.4.3 Minor/s each with total credit point values of 12; and/or 
30.4.4 General electives with a total credit point value up to the remaining 
value of the Course. 
31. The following variations to Bachelor Award Courses are permitted: 
31.1 A Course Core with a total credit point value between 0 and the total credit 
point value of the Course, less the credit point value of the Discovery Study 
in that course;  
31.2 A Major with total credit point value between 24 and 36, in a Course with a 
total credit point value of 72; and 
31.3 A Major with a total credit point value between 24 and 48, in a Course with 
a total credit point value of 96. 
31.4 Options with a total credit point value up to the remaining value of the 
Course. 
Combined Bachelor Award Courses 
32. A Standard Combined Bachelor Award Course is structured by: 
32.1 Combining two 72 credit point Bachelor Award Courses to form a Combined 
Bachelor Award Course with a total credit point value of 96; or 
32.2 Combining a 72 credit point and a 96 credit point Bachelor Award Course 
to form a Combined Bachelor Award Course with a total credit point value 
of 120; or 
