39. A Standard Graduate Certificate Award Course has a total credit point value of 
12 and includes: 
39.1 A Course Core with a total credit point value of 12. 
40. The following variations to Graduate Certificate Award Courses are permitted: 
40.1 A Course Core with a total credit point value between 0 and 12; 
40.2 A Major with a total credit point value of 12; or 
40.3 Options with a total credit point value not exceeding 12 consisting of a 
Minor. 
Graduate Diploma Award Courses 
41. A Standard Graduate Diploma Award Course has a total credit point value of 24 
and includes: 
41.1 A Course Core with a total credit point value of 24. 
42. The following variations to Graduate Diploma Award Courses are permitted: 
42.1 A Course Core with a total credit point value between 0 and 24;  
42.2 A Major with a total credit point value between 12 and 24; and/or 
42.3 Options with a total credit point value not exceeding 12 consisting of a 
Minor. 
Masters by Coursework Award Courses 
43. A Masters by Coursework Award Course, designed for students who hold an 
AQF level 7 qualification in a non-cognate area of study, has a total credit point 
value of 48. 
44. A Masters by Coursework Award Course, designed for students who hold an 
AQF level 7 qualification in a cognate area of study or an AQF level 8 qualification 
in a non-cognate area of study, has a total credit point value of 36. 
45. A Masters by Coursework Award Course, designed for students who hold an 
AQF level 8 qualification in a cognate area of study, has a total credit point value 
of 24. 
46. An extended Masters by Coursework Award Course, designed for students who 
hold a three year AQF level 7 qualification and who require significant practice-
related learning, has a total credit point value of 72. 
47. A Standard Masters by Coursework Award Course includes: 
47.1 A Course Core equivalent to the total credit point value of the Course. 
48. The following variations to Masters by Coursework Award Courses are permitted: 
48.1 Course Core with a total credit point value between 0 and the total credit 
point value of the Course; 
48.2 Major with a total credit point value between 12 and the total credit point 
value of the Course; and/or 
48.3 Options with a total credit point value not exceeding 12 consisting of: 
48.3.1 A Minor; and/or 
