48.3.2 General Electives. 
Combined Masters by Coursework Award Courses 
49. A Combined Masters by Coursework Course is structured by combining two 
Masters by Coursework Courses as follows: 
49.1 A 48 credit point Course combined with a 48 credit point Course creates a 
Combined Course with a minimum value of 72 credit points. 
49.2 A 48 credit point Course combined with a 36 credit point Course creates a 
Combined Course with a minimum value of 60 credit points. 
49.3 A 48 credit point Course combined with a 24 credit point Course creates a 
Combined Course with a minimum value of 60 credit points. 
49.4 A 36 credit point Course combined with a 36 credit point Course creates a 
Combined Course with a minimum value of 48 credit points. 
49.5 A 36 credit point Course combined with a 24 credit point Course creates a 
Combined Course with a minimum value of 48 credit points. 
49.6 A 24 credit point Course combined with a 24 credit point Course creates a 
Combined Course with a minimum value of 48 credit points. 
50. A Combined Masters by Coursework Course has a minimum of 24 credit points 
from the Course Core and/or Major of each constituent Course. 
51. Variations to a Combined Masters by Coursework Award Course to modify one 
or more of the Course Cores or Majors may be approved provided the Learning 
Outcomes and credit point value of the amended Components are equivalent to 
those of the constituent Course. 
Doctorate (Professional) Award Courses 
52. A Standard Doctorate (Professional) Award Course has a total credit point value 
of 72. 
53. A Standard Doctorate (Professional) Award Courses includes: 
53.1 A Course Core with a total credit point value of 72. 
54. The following variations to Doctorate (Professional) Award Courses are 
permitted: 
54.1 A Course Core, with a total credit point value between 0 and 72; 
54.2 Major/s with a total credit point value up to the total credit point value of the 
Course; and/or 
54.3 Options with a total credit point value not exceeding 12 consisting of: 
54.3.1 A Minor; and/or 
54.3.2 General Electives. 
Nested Award Suite 
55. Graduate Award Courses may be structured as stand-alone Courses or as part 
of a Nested Award Suite. 
56. A Nested Award Suite is group of cognate Graduate Courses that lead to 
qualifications at successively higher levels. 
