57. Within a Nested Award Suite: 
57.1 Accumulated credit is carried forward progressively from Course to Course. 
57.2 Enrolled students may, upon request, be conferred with a constituent Award 
where all completion requirements of the Course specified as leading to 
that single Award are satisfied. 
COMPLETION REQUIREMENTS  
General 
58. To satisfactorily complete a Coursework Award Course students must: 
58.1 Satisfy completion requirements for the Course and all Components as 
specified in the University Handbook; 
58.2 Satisfactorily complete the University’s requirements for assuring academic 
integrity; and 
58.3 Satisfactorily complete the total number of credit points specified for that 
Course and each of its Components. 
59. Where the University approves one or more changes to the structure of a 
Coursework Award Course, and/or its Components, a student must satisfy the 
completion requirements specified for the version of the Course in which they are 
enrolled at the time of completion. 
Recognition of Course Completion Requirements 
60. For Diplomas, students may select from structured Components but are 
restricted to receiving recognition for a maximum of: 
60.1.1 One Major; or 
60.1.2 One Minor. 
61. For Standard Advanced Diplomas and Associate Degrees, students may select 
from structured Components but are restricted to receiving recognition for a 
maximum of: 
61.1 One Major; or 
61.2 One Minor. 
62. For Standard Bachelor Award Courses, students are restricted to receiving 
recognition for a maximum of: 
62.1 Two Majors; and up to 
62.1.1 One Minor. 
62.2 A Single Major; and up to 
62.2.1 One Co-Major; or 
62.2.2 Two Minors. 
63. For Standard Combined Bachelor Award Courses, students may select from 
structured Components but are restricted to receiving recognition for a single 
Major from each constituent Course. 
64. For Graduate Award Courses, students may select from structured Components 
but may receive recognition for a maximum of one Major and one Minor. 
