65. For Integrated Award Courses, students may select from structured Components 
of each constituent Course and receive recognition for Components up to the 
limits articulated for each constituent Award type. 
66. Where units are shared between Components, to be eligible for recognition 
students must fulfil the requirements of each: 
66.1 Major, Co-Major and Minor; and 
66.2 Co-Majors must include 9 credit points distinct from other Components. 
66.3 Minors must include 6 credit points distinct from other Components. 
67. Variations to Standard Award Courses may include provision for recognition of 
Components outside of the limits specified above. 
68. For Courses approved for offering prior to 2018, recognition of two Majors 
requires a minimum of 9 credit points total at 200 and 300 Level, which are 
distinct to and not counted towards the requirements of the other Major. 
69. For Courses approved for offering prior to 2014, recognition of three Minors is 
possible provided the total number of Majors and Minors did not exceed four. 
Time Limits for Completion 
70. Students are required to complete a Coursework Award Course within the 
following maximum completion time periods, except where variations have been 
approved and are specified in the University Handbook for individual Courses. 
