[OFFICIAL]
 
 
 
EFFECTIVE AS OF 01 JANUARY 2026 
1. 
These Regulations apply to the academic Colleges and Schools of the 
University. 
Establishment and Membership 
2. 
Colleges and Schools are established by the University Senate, upon 
recommendation from the Vice Chancellor following consultation with Academic 
Council. 
3. 
The membership of each School consists of: 
3.1 all members of academic staff assigned to that School by the Vice 
Chancellor; 
3.2 all postgraduate research students whose principal supervisor is a 
member of the academic staff of the School; and 
3.3 all undergraduate and postgraduate coursework students enrolled in 
Majors or Courses assigned to that School by Academic Council. 
Heads of College 
4. 
Each College has a Head of College, by whatever name known, who reports to 
the Vice Chancellor. 
5. 
The Head of College is appointed by the Senate on the recommendation of the 
Vice Chancellor. 
5.1 The term of office for a Head of College is normally five years. 
5.2 Appointees are eligible for re-appointment. 
5.3 The total term of office can be no greater than 10 years. 
5.4 In recommending the appointment of a Head of College, the Vice 
Chancellor will ensure that staff of the College are involved in the process. 
6. 
The Head of College provides oversight and support for the constituent Schools 
of the College, and is responsible for ensuring those Schools are managed in 
accordance with University strategy, regulations, policies, and procedures. 
College Executive 
7. 
Each College has a College Executive, comprising: 
7.1 the Head of College; 
7.2 the Heads of School; and 
7.3 other members that the College Executive may agree to appoint. 
College and School Regulations 
