8. 
The membership of the College Executive will reflect the University’s 
commitment to diversity and no more than 60% of the members should identify 
with the same gender. If this is not possible, an explanation must be provided to 
and accepted by the Vice Chancellor. 
9. 
The Head of College will consult regularly with colleagues, keep them informed 
with respect to developments, and adopt a transparent and collegiate approach. 
10. The College Executive must meet at least four times a year. 
11. The College Executive may determine the structure of the College. 
12. The College Executive, on recommendation of the Head of College, may appoint 
Deputy Heads of College, by whatever name known. 
Heads of School 
13. Each School has a Head of School1, by whatever name known, who reports to 
the Head of College. 
14. The Head of School is appointed by the Vice Chancellor on the recommendation 
of the Head of College. 
14.1 The term of office for a Head of School is normally five years. 
14.2 Appointees are eligible for re-appointment. 
14.3 The total term of office can be no greater than 10 years. 
14.4 In recommending a Head of School, the Head of College will involve the 
members of the School and ensure the recommendation has support from 
the majority of School staff. 
15. The Head of School has a key leadership role within the University. They provide 
the School with leadership, direction and management, and represent the 
interests of the School at the College and University level. 
16. The Head of School is responsible for: 
16.1 developing and instilling a collegiate approach among all staff; 
16.2 learning and teaching; 
16.3 research; 
16.4 professional activity (including oversight of professional accreditation 
activities); 
16.5 community engagement; and 
16.6 raising the effectiveness and profile of the School. 
17. With the oversight of the Head of College, the Head of School is responsible for: 
17.1 the strategic planning, budgeting, and financial management of the 
School; 
17.2 managing academic staff including recruitment, annual reviews, 
workloads; and 
17.3 fostering a culture of teamwork. 
 
_______________________________________ 
1 Where a College is a one School College, the Head of College is also Head of School. 
 
