18. In managing the School, the Head of School will consult regularly with 
colleagues, keep them informed with respect to developments, and adopt a 
transparent and collegiate approach. 
19. The Head of College may appoint Deputy Heads of School, by whatever name 
known, on the recommendation of the Head of School. Before recommending a 
Deputy Head, the Head of School will involve the members of the School and 
ensure that the recommendation has the support of the majority of the School 
staff. 
School Executive 
20. Each School may have a School Executive, comprising: 
20.1 the Head of School; 
20.2 any Deputy Heads of School; and 
20.3 other members that the School Executive may agree to appoint. 
21. The membership of the School Executive will reflect the University’s commitment 
to diversity and no more than 60% of the members should identify with the same 
gender. If this is not possible, an explanation must be provided to and accepted 
by the Vice Chancellor. 
22. If the School has a School Executive, it must meet at least four times a year. 
23. The staff members of the School must meet at least twice a year, or at least four 
times a year if there is no School Executive. 
24. Beyond what is specified in these Regulations, the Head of School will determine 
the structure of the School in consultation with the School staff. 
Discipline Lead 
25. Where there is a professional body requirement to have an identified discipline 
lead, such will be appointed with an appropriate title. 
Academic Chairs 
26. Each Award Course, Major, Co-Major and Minor will have an Academic Chair. 
27. Academic Chairs may be responsible for more than one Course, Major, Co-Major 
or Minor. A Course with multiple Majors, Co-Majors or Minors may have more 
than one Academic Chair. 
28. Academic Chairs are appointed by the Academic Council on the 
recommendation of the Head(s) of College of the College(s) teaching into the 
Award Course: 
28.1 The term of appointment is normally three years. 
28.2 Where the Course is contained within a single School, the appointment 
will be made on the recommendation of the Head of School. 
28.3 Appointees are eligible for re-appointment. 
29. An Academic Chair is responsible to the Head(s) of College and Head(s) of 
School for the academic integrity, management of, and progress of students in 
the relevant Course, Major, Co-Major or Minor. 
30. Academic Chairs are responsible for carrying out tasks as specified by University 
legislation, policy or procedure. 
