Murdoch,N175,Work Integrated Learning Policy,214,214,"L001, L002, L003, L004, L005, L006, L007, L008, L009, L010, L011, L012, L013, L014, L015, L016, L017, L018, L019, L020, L021, L022, L023, L024, L025, L026, L027, L028, L029, L030, L031","{""L001"": ""Work Integrated Learning Policy"", ""L002"": ""Purpose and Scope"", ""L003"": ""The purpose of this policy is to promote the inclusion of Work Integrated Learning"", ""L004"": ""(WIL) in all courses offered at Murdoch University and to establish the principles and"", ""L005"": ""procedures for its adoption."", ""L006"": ""This policy, in conjunction with the associated Work Integrated Learning Work"", ""L007"": ""Placements Procedure, provides a comprehensive and integrated approach to WIL,"", ""L008"": ""recognising that there will always be a variety of expressions of WIL across disciplines."", ""L009"": ""Key policy considerations include quality of learning experience, sustainability of"", ""L010"": ""industry partnerships, good operational practices, and risk management."", ""L011"": ""This policy applies to staff, students and public."", ""L012"": ""Policy"", ""L013"": ""1. In this policy, the following words have the following meanings:"", ""L014"": ""1.1. “Course” is defined in the Coursework Regulations."", ""L015"": ""1.2. “Learning Outcomes” is defined in the Coursework Regulations."", ""L016"": ""1.3. “Work Integrated Learning” exists where the Learning Outcomes, the"", ""L017"": ""learning activities, and the assessment:"", ""L018"": ""1.3.1. require students to integrate and appropriately apply previous"", ""L019"": ""learning and knowledge to make and justify decisions in a work-"", ""L020"": ""related context;"", ""L021"": ""1.3.2. require students to reflect upon their personal choices, decisions"", ""L022"": ""and actions in a work-related context to critically appraise their"", ""L023"": ""appropriateness;"", ""L024"": ""1.3.3. engage students with the world of work in one of three broad"", ""L025"": ""categories: Work Placement, Industry or Community Project,"", ""L026"": ""Workplace Simulation."", ""L027"": ""1.4. “Work Placement”: Sometimes referred to as an internship, clinical"", ""L028"": ""placement or practicum, student learning and assessment takes place in"", ""L029"": ""the context of a real workplace, under supervision, where students can"", ""L030"": ""develop professional competencies."", ""L031"": ""Page 1 of 5""}","Page 1 of 5 
 
 
 
 
Purpose and Scope 
The purpose of this policy is to promote the inclusion of Work Integrated Learning 
(WIL) in all courses offered at Murdoch University and to establish the principles and 
procedures for its adoption. 
This policy, in conjunction with the associated Work Integrated Learning Work 
Placements Procedure, provides a comprehensive and integrated approach to WIL, 
recognising that there will always be a variety of expressions of WIL across disciplines. 
Key policy considerations include quality of learning experience, sustainability of 
industry partnerships, good operational practices, and risk management. 
This policy applies to staff, students and public. 
Policy 
1. 
In this policy, the following words have the following meanings: 
1.1. “Course” is defined in the Coursework Regulations. 
1.2. “Learning Outcomes” is defined in the Coursework Regulations. 
1.3. “Work Integrated Learning” exists where the Learning Outcomes, the 
learning activities, and the assessment: 
1.3.1. require students to integrate and appropriately apply previous 
learning and knowledge to make and justify decisions in a work-
related context; 
1.3.2. require students to reflect upon their personal choices, decisions 
and actions in a work-related context to critically appraise their 
appropriateness; 
1.3.3. engage students with the world of work in one of three broad 
categories: Work Placement, Industry or Community Project, 
Workplace Simulation. 
1.4. “Work Placement”: Sometimes referred to as an internship, clinical 
placement or practicum, student learning and assessment takes place in 
the context of a real workplace, under supervision, where students can 
develop professional competencies.  
 Work Integrated Learning Policy  
