5. 
Partnerships 
5.1. The University recognises the value of its business, industry, government 
and community partners and seeks to build sustainable partnerships that 
focus on providing high-quality Learning Outcomes for students involved in 
WIL. 
5.1.1. Work Placements will be sought that provide a high-quality learning 
environment and workplace supervision in the partner organisation, 
regardless of whether the partner is university-sourced or student-
sourced. 
5.1.2. Industry or Community Projects will be sought that provide students 
with high quality projects with a real-world application and 
audience, as well as significant engagement with the partner 
organisation. 
5.1.3. Workplace Simulations will be created that are informed by regular 
consultation with partner organisations to provide learning 
environments that are as realistic to the workplace as possible. 
6. 
Governance and Due Diligence 
6.1. WIL activities are jointly managed by academic staff in the Schools and a 
centralised WIL team.  
6.2. WIL activities must comply with relevant legislation, University policies and 
professional accreditation requirements. 
6.3. WIL activities are consistent with the guidance available from Fair Work 
Australia on work experience and internships. Where undertaken outside 
of Australia, WIL activities must conform with local employment and 
workplace legislation and consider any additional risks to student safety. 
6.4. Formal agreements governing the conditions of placement are negotiated 
between the University and partner organisations, as well as an agreement 
between the student and the University. 
6.5. Due diligence processes are followed with respect to contract approvals, 
ethical requirements, insurance arrangements, occupational safety and 
health, risk assessment, intellectual property, student visa requirements 
and disability rights and access. 
6.6. The University, partner organisations, and students have a shared 
responsibility for matters relating to workplace health and safety. 
7. 
Student Responsibilities 
7.1. Students must comply with all applicable agreements, codes of practice, 
professional behaviours, laws governing privacy or confidentiality in relation 
to all WIL activities, and other conditions as stipulated in relevant student 
agreements. 
 
 
