7.1 Representation 
7.2 Information for Prospective and Current Students 
7.3 Information Management 
8.2.3 
Terms of Reference: 
i. 
Monitor compliance with the Higher Education Standards 
Framework 2021, Australian Qualifications Framework, Higher 
Education Support Act 2003, Education Services for Overseas 
Students Act 2000 and supporting legislative instruments as well 
as any other relevant regulatory requirements. Annually  review 
the outcomes of quality review activities and provide guidance on 
the identification of academic risk and priorities for improvement. 
Report to Academic Council and refer items to other relevant 
committees. 
ii. 
Oversee the development and embedding of an institutional 
framework of continuous improvement.  
iii. 
Report and recommend to Academic Council on any academic 
quality assurance and compliance matter referred from 
governance committees or management. 
iv. 
Consider and recommend actions on compliance matters related 
to delivery with other parties, including transnational delivery, 
collaborative research arrangements, work-integrated learning 
and other partnerships. 
v. 
Assure compliance with HESF in relation to research and research 
training through annual reporting from relevant management and 
governance committees. 
vi. 
Assure compliance with HESF in relation to the staffing 
complement for each course of study and ensure it is sufficient to 
meet the educational, academic support and administrative needs 
of student cohorts undertaking the course. 
vii. 
Ensure University representation through publicly available 
information, agents and other parties is accurate and not 
misleading. 
viii. 
Monitor and advise Academic Council on trends in national and 
international compliance and regulatory developments. 
8.2.4 
