scholarly integrity and professional performance. The responsibility of a board 
is to govern but not to manage. “Noses in, fingers out” remains sound and 
tested advice to board members4.  
2.1.3. The purpose of this Charter is to set out the guiding governance principles and 
practices to be upheld at all times. The Charter is also intended to bring together 
the policies and procedures that the Senate adopts from time to time and which 
form part of best practice governance. 
 
