3 Senate Code of Conduct 
3.1 Rationale for the Code 
3.1.1. The Senate and its Senators represent a prestigious public institution. They 
should always act to promote the interests of the University, its reputation and 
standing. However, uninformed or ill-advised actions may have the contrary 
effect. 
3.1.2. All Senators are responsible and accountable to the Senate. A Senator must 
always act in the best interests of the University. It is essential for the 
University’s well-being that all Senators understand and fully accept the 
responsibilities of their membership. 
