3.3 Senate Buddy: 
Each new Senate member will be paired with an experienced Senate member who 
will act as a buddy. The buddy provides an informal source of support as the new 
member becomes familiar with Senate and its ways of working. The buddy would 
ordinarily: 
• 
arrange an initial informal meeting with the new member; 
• 
make contact with them after their first few Senate meetings to debrief and 
discuss any questions they might have; and 
• 
be available, as appropriate, as an informal point of contact for questions 
about Senate or matters coming before it. 
The buddy arrangement complements the formal induction program and is 
intended to provide a peer perspective on the practical operation of Senate. The 
formal buddy arrangement concludes after 12 months. 
