Official webpage text reading copy. Retrieved 12 November 2026. Browser layout is not preserved.
Accessibility services
Murdoch University is committed to supporting students with disability, physical or mental
health conditions, or those who are carers for people with disability, to enable equal
participation in study.
Welcome to Access and Inclusion
If you have a disability or health condition (including mental health), or you are caring for a
person with disability, we encourage you to reach out to us to discuss the support you may
need whilst undertaking your studies. Even if you feel you don’t need any assistance now, get
in touch with us to find out the ways we can help.
We support students with:
Physical disabilities
Sensory disabilities
Mental health conditions
Medical conditions
Specific learning disorders
Temporary injuries
Carers of people with disability
Pregnant or breast feeding parents
Post cancer treatment cycles
In discussion with an experienced team member an access plan will be tailored to your specific
needs.
Your plan may include support for:
Exams
Assessments (e.g. written assignments. oral presentations, practical assessments)
Communication or participation
Assistive technology or equipment
Audio/Video or text accessibility
Physical access
Library support
Other equipment (e.g. ergonomic chairs)
How to register for support
These short, captioned videos outline how to register for support.
To register for support, please contact us on (08) 9360 6084 or access@murdoch.edu.au to
make an appointment
Before your appointment, you will need to provide your current medical documents or a
completed Health Practitioner Report. These documents are used to indicate suitable
accommodations for your plan and are treated confidentially.
The information you provide helps us create an access plan and won’t be used for any other
purpose. It will not be shared or discussed with anyone unless you provide consent. If you have
any concerns about this please do not hesitate to ask us for more information.
myAccess plan
Our Accessibility Advisors will work with you to develop an access plan that explicitly outlines
