Merged policy sources for human coding
Read the single PDF for this university. Use the bookmarks and contents to open a source. Each
original PDF page is preserved inside a wider page. Webpage content is a reflowed text reading
copy; Word documents have been converted to PDF.
Cite the BUNDLE page printed at the bottom and the L-number in the left margin. Line numbers
restart on every page. A line means a visual text row; cells sharing a table row share its line
number. Example format: Curtin bundle p. 34, -, document N001. This is a format
example, not an evidence claim.
Source collection includes current website copies and distinct earlier/register copies. Alternative
versions are identified in the source register. Public accessibility, approval authority and currency
must be checked before freezing the final analytic corpus. These files do not authenticate a July
2026 baseline.
Security pages, failed downloads, repeated captures, repository-only indexes and the
future-effective 2027 manual are excluded from the reading body. The accompanying register
records exclusions and unresolved access limitations. No earlier empirical scores are reproduced.
