Bundle page 5 | N180 | source page 1 | line numbers at left","Anonymisation and de‑identification: Apply strong de‑identification techniques where possible.
When suitable, use synthetic data for model development or testing to avoid exposing real data.
See the data linkage programs available in Australia for more on synthetic and other data services.
Secure storage and access controls: Encrypt data at rest and in transit. Limit data access to
authorised personnel and routinely monitor access logs.
Privacy by design: Embed privacy considerations throughout the research lifecycle. Conduct Privacy
Impact Assessments (PIAs) to identify and address risks early.
Data retention management: Establish clear retention timelines and securely dispose of data once it
is no longer required.
Further reading
AI and Ethics: Investigating the first policy responses of higher education institutions to the
challenge of generative AI
