emerging strengths progressively over the program of study. 
4.8 
Principle 6: Assessment provides multiple planned opportunities for productive feedback, 
dialogue and advice on performance, to assist students to evaluate their learning and actively 
improve future performance. 
4.8.1 Feedback promotes deep learning that is relevant to disciplinary contexts, practices and 
standards, and builds student capability for independent and lifelong learning.  
4.8.2 Embedding feedback loops into assessment builds student confidence and enables 
scaffolded reflection on performance for growth, reflexivity and development.  
4.8.3 Feedback builds trust and connection and enables staff to proactively identify and 
support students at risk.  
4.9 
Principle 7: Assessment enables valid and reliable evidence of student achievement of course 
and program learning outcomes to assure student learning. 
4.9.1 Accurately and consistently evaluating student achievement through multiple methods 
of assessment secures assurance of learning and assessment security more effectively 
than any single method of assessment.  
4.9.2 Validity and reliability of assessment is demonstrated through moderation, peer review 
and benchmarking.  
4.9.3 Confidence in student achievement of course and program learning outcomes supports 
the conferral of qualifications and assures University awards.  
4.10 Principle 8: Assessment design, standards and practices are reviewed as part of continuous 
improvement and quality assurance practices.  
4.10.1 Effective governance and systematic and cyclical review and improvement of 
assessment provides assurance of quality and standards across the University. 
5 ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES 
5.1 
The following academic committees of have responsibilities in relation to this policy, as 
defined in their charters:  
