7 INTERPRETATION AND DEFINITIONS  
7.1 
The following rules of interpretation apply to this policy. 
7.1.1 The University’s Policy Framework sets out the hierarchy of the University’s policy 
documents. 
7.1.2 Should any provision in this policy be inconsistent with a provision of a document higher 
in the University’s hierarchy of policy documents as stated in the Policy Framework, the 
higher document prevails and overrules this policy to the extent of the inconsistency. 
7.1.3 This policy must be read alongside other closely-related policy documents: 
7.1.3.1 the procedures that support this policy, listed in the Related documents section 
7.1.3.2 the Employee Code of Conduct and Ethical Behaviour and Code of Conduct 
(Students), which include a requirement to comply with policy documents of 
the University, and 
7.1.3.3 any other documents listed in the Related documents section. 
7.1.4 The procedures that support this policy state detailed requirements in relation to the 
principles stated in this policy. 
7.1.4.1 Where a principle stated in this policy implies a service or entitlement to a 
person, to enjoy the service or entitlement, the person must meet any 
requirements and/or conditions that a supporting procedure states in relation 
to the service or entitlement. 
7.1.5 Where this policy uses: 
7.1.5.1 the verbs ‘will’ or ‘must’, it states a requirement 
7.1.5.2 the phrases ‘cannot’, ‘must not’ or ‘only [position title] can’, it states a 
prohibition 
7.1.5.3 the words ‘include’, ‘includes; or ‘including’ followed by a list, the words 
‘without limitation’ are taken to follow immediately  
7.1.5.4 the phrase ‘for example’ or ‘such as’ followed by a single instance or list, the 
instance or list is not exhaustive 
7.1.5.5 the phrases ‘described in’, ‘set out in’, ‘specified in’ or ‘stated in’, it will be read 
as if the words ‘expressly or impliedly’ appeared immediately before them; 
7.1.5.6 the singular, it also means the plural, and vice versa 
7.1.5.7 any gender, it includes the other genders, and 
7.1.5.8 a reference to a statute, ordinance, code or other law, it includes regulations, 
by-laws, rules and other statutory instruments under it for the time being in 
force and consolidations, amendments, re-enactments or replacements of any 
of them. 
7.2 
For the purpose of this Policy, the following definitions apply: 
7.2.1 Academic integrity has the same meaning as in the Policy: Academic Integrity. 
7.2.2 Academic standard mean an agreed specification, such as a defined benchmark or 
indicator, that is used to define a level of academic performance or achievement. 
7.2.3 Assessment is the systematic process for facilitating and evaluating student learning. It 
includes the design, development and implementation of assessment tasks, the 
judgement and reporting of student performance and the provision of feedback to 
students on their performance. 
