7.2.18 Programmatic assessment is a systematic and wholistic approach wherein assessments 
are designed to promote learning and students are provided opportunities to 
demonstrate their learning authentically through a variety of purposefully selected 
assessment tasks. This enables a triangulation of information about a learner's progress 
and a more authentic representation of their development of key competencies, 
domain knowledge, skills and attributes. Assessment is designed across each level of 
study (horizontally) to provide alignment of standards, curriculum, resources and 
assessments through an integrated, relational and balanced approach and through a 
program (vertically /longitudinally) to provide alignment, building from foundational 
learning to graduate capabilities through a sequenced learning journey that also 
promotes future learning in life and work. 
7.2.19 Reliability means the extent to which assessments produce stable and consistent results 
over time, including consistency of grading by markers across a course and program. 
7.2.20 Validity means the extent to which assessment aligns with the learning outcomes and 
the assessment methods are fit for purpose. 
 
