4.3 
Exceptional circumstances do not include: 
4.3.1 
a misreading of or mistake in relation to the time, date or place of an assessment 
4.3.2 
competing workload 
4.3.3 
an expected employment commitment  
4.3.4 
poor academic preparation or planning, or 
4.3.5 
travel or other commitments that the student has scheduled at the time of an 
assessment task or had scheduled at that time before they enrolled in the relevant 
course. 
4.4 
To receive assessment flexibility for exceptional circumstances, a student must: 
4.4.1 
apply by the process and in the timeframe stated in the section on the relevant type 
of assessment flexibility below, and 
4.4.2 
provide supporting evidence of their circumstances as specified in that section. 
5 
REASONABLE ADJUSTMENTS FOR DISABILITY 
5.1 
The University provides reasonable adjustments to enable a student to undertake courses on 
an equal basis with other students where the student: 
5.1.1 
has a disability, injury or medical condition that is episodic, temporary or permanent 
5.1.2 
has a short-term injury or medical condition that requires an adjustment to exam 
conditions, or 
5.1.3 
is a primary carer for someone who has an episodic, temporary or permanent 
disability, medical condition (including a terminal or chronic illness), mental health 
condition, or who is frail and aged. 
5.2 
Where such a student wishes to have reasonable adjustments, they must: 
5.2.1 
register with the University’s access and inclusion advisors, and 
5.2.2 
provide current documentation of their disability or condition from the treating 
health practitioner. 
5.3 
Similarly, where a student who is a primary carer, they must: 
5.3.1 
register with the access and inclusion advisors 
5.3.2 
provide current documentation of the other person’s disability or condition from the 
person’s treating health practitioner and 
5.3.3 
provide satisfactory documentation of the carer relationship. 
5.4 
To register for reasonable adjustments and have a learning access plan to provide the 
adjustments issued, a student must: 
5.4.1 
complete a request for assistance form 
5.4.2 
attend an assessment interview in which the Access and Inclusion Advisor will consult 
the student about the kinds of adjustment to learning activities and assessment 
arrangements they need, and 
5.4.3 
submit all documentation required for assessment of their adjustment needs. 
5.5 
Staff involved in assessing or deciding a student’s request for reasonable adjustments will: 
5.5.1 
ensure the security of the health information provided by the student, and 
5.5.2 
not disclose the student’s circumstances or health information to anyone who is not 
involved in assessing and deciding the student’s request unless the student gives 
