5.6 
The Director, Student Engagement and Success may share the student’s circumstances or 
health information with other staff, or with an external tribunal, as needed to: 
5.6.1 
manage a risk that the student will harm themselves or another person 
5.6.2 
provide information to decide a grievance or appeal by the student in relation to their 
reasonable adjustments 
5.6.3 
where approval of a non-standard adjustment is needed from a head of school, 
executive dean, pro vice-chancellor, executive director or the Academic Registrar, 
and/or 
5.6.4 
where the University is obliged by law to provide the information to a court or other 
external authority. 
5.7 
Students who need reasonable adjustments for in-course learning activities and assessment 
tasks should register and provide supporting documentation before the start of the teaching 
period in which they need the adjustments, or failing that, as early in the teaching period as 
possible. 
5.8 
Where a student needs an adjustment to arrangements for a final exam, they should register 
and provide their supporting documentation by the published due date to register an 
adjustment for the relevant teaching period. 
5.9 
If students do not register in time for the Access and Inclusion Advisors to assess their needs 
and for other areas of the University to arrange the adjustments, the University may not be 
able to provide some or all of the adjustments. In these circumstances, students may apply 
for special consideration in accordance with section 9 of this Procedure. 
5.10 
An access and inclusion advisor or (for an adjustment to exam arrangements) the National 
Manager, Student Services and Graduations may decline to provide an adjustment requested 
by a student where: 
5.10.1 the student has not met the published date to register the adjustment 
5.10.2 the effect of the adjustment would be to give the student an advantage over other 
students in the same course 
5.10.3 the adjustment would have the effect that the student would not have to 
demonstrate achievement of a course learning outcome 
5.10.4 the adjustment would compromise the academic integrity of an assessment task, or 
5.10.5 providing the adjustment would impose an unjustifiable hardship on the University. 
5.10.6 Where a student has not met the published date to register an adjustment, Access 
and Inclusion in consultation with Student Administration may decide to apply 
reasonable adjustments where it is warranted by exceptional circumstances. 
5.11 
After assessing a student, if an access and inclusion advisor considers that the student needs 
reasonable adjustments in learning activities and assessment arrangements, they will prepare 
and issue the student with a learning access plan (LAP). 
5.12 
In preparing the LAP, to establish what adjustments are reasonable, the access and inclusion 
advisor may consult: 
5.12.1 where the student is enrolled in a pathway program, the Director, Pathways 
5.12.2 the head of a school or campus student adviser of a school that manages a program 
or course in which the student is enrolled 
5.12.3 the program coordinator of the student’s program of study 
