5.12.4 the discipline coordinator of the student’s discipline major 
5.12.5 the course coordinator of a course in which the student is enrolled, and/or 
5.12.6 in relation to possible adjustments to exam arrangements, the National Manager, 
Student Services and Graduations. 
5.13 
When consulting other staff to formulate a LAP, an access and inclusion advisor may describe 
the student’s adjustment needs but will not reveal the disability or health condition that the 
student has declared, unless the student has given them written permission to do so. 
5.14 
A student who has been issued with an LAP is expected to approach the course coordinator 
of a course in which they need the LAP adjustments, at least two weeks prior to any 
assessment for provisions to be implemented (unless previously negotiated). 
5.14.1 A school may direct students with an LAP to approach the school’s campus student 
adviser for this purpose instead of individual course coordinators 
5.14.2 A student who feels they need support for the approach to the course coordinator 
may ask an Access and Inclusion Advisor, or other relevant staff to join that 
discussion. 
5.14.3 The course coordinator or campus student adviser will not seek to know the details 
of the student’s disability or condition, although the student may disclose these if 
they choose. 
5.14.4 Course coordinators will provide the adjustments described in the LAP in a timely 
manner. 
5.14.5 A course coordinator or other staff member who has received an LAP from a student 
may contact the access and inclusion advisor who formulated the LAP to seek 
clarification of the adjustments. 
5.15 
Where, however, the student requires an adjustment to arrangements for them to sit a final 
exam, the student must give their permission for the Access and Inclusion advisors to liaise 
with the relevant program or course coordinators and to notify the National Manager, Student 
Services and Graduations of these adjustments. 
5.15.1 The Director, Student Engagement and Success will review any unusual, proposed 
exam adjustment before this is submitted to the National Manager, Student Services 
and Graduations. 
5.15.2 The National Manager, Student Services and Graduations will decide what exam 
adjustments can be provided, in consultation with the Director, Student Engagement 
and Success. 
5.16 
The Director, Student Engagement and Success (or their delegate) may ask a head of school 
to consider providing, for a student with a learning access plan, an alternative assessment task 
in place of a final exam that a student's disability or health condition prevents them from 
undertaking on an equal basis with other students. 
5.16.1 Such an alternative assessment task will assess the same learning outcomes, with the 
same level of challenge, as the exam it replaces. 
5.17 
A student who has not received an adjustment they requested: 
5.17.1 should, where the school that manages the course has declined to provide the 
adjustment, ask the access and inclusion advisors for support to arrange the 
adjustment with the school, and 
5.17.2 may appeal the decision not to provide the adjustment in accordance with the Policy: 
Student Appeals. 
