and Success. 
5.16 
The Director, Student Engagement and Success (or their delegate) may ask a head of school 
to consider providing, for a student with a learning access plan, an alternative assessment task 
in place of a final exam that a student's disability or health condition prevents them from 
undertaking on an equal basis with other students. 
5.16.1 Such an alternative assessment task will assess the same learning outcomes, with the 
same level of challenge, as the exam it replaces. 
5.17 
A student who has not received an adjustment they requested: 
5.17.1 should, where the school that manages the course has declined to provide the 
adjustment, ask the access and inclusion advisors for support to arrange the 
adjustment with the school, and 
5.17.2 may appeal the decision not to provide the adjustment in accordance with the Policy: 
Student Appeals. 
