9 
SPECIAL CONSIDERATION 
9.1 
Special consideration is a way of providing flexibility where exceptional circumstances beyond 
a student’s control adversely affects their performance in assessment. 
9.2 
Staff who hold the following roles may grant a student’s request for special consideration in 
relation to an assessment task for a course managed by the school: a head of school, deputy 
head of school, program coordinator, discipline coordinator, campus student adviser, course 
coordinator and, in the School of Medicine, the National Head of Assessment. 
9.2.1 
The head of each school will decide which staff of the school who hold these roles 
will be the school’s decision-maker(s) on special consideration applications. 
9.3 
Only a head of school or, in the School of Medicine, the National Head of Assessment can 
approve a student’s request for special consideration where: 
9.3.1 
the outcome is permission to resubmit assessment work for which the student has 
received a mark 
9.3.2 
the outcome of the request will delay release of the student’s final grade in the 
course, or 
9.3.3 
the student has applied for special consideration later than (as relevant): 
9.3.3.1 
three working days after the original due date to submit the assessment 
work, or 
9.3.3.2 
three working days after the date on which the assessment task took place. 
Grounds for special consideration 
9.4 
Students who know in advance they will not be able to submit an assessment task by the due 
date due to exceptional circumstances can apply for an extension in accordance with section 
8 of this Procedure. 
9.5 
Special consideration may be granted where exceptional circumstances as defined in section 
4 significantly impair a student’s ability to: 
9.5.1 
perform in an assessment task at their usual standard  
9.5.2 
complete an assessment task scheduled for a specific date (such as a final 
examination, in class test/quiz, in class presentation) 
9.5.3 
attend scheduled classes or learning activities where attendance is required to pass 
the course, or 
9.5.4 
attend part or all of a work integrated learning activity such as a practical placement, 
clinical placement or internship. 
9.6 
Special consideration will not be granted where: 
9.6.1 
the student has completed the assessment task and their mark for it is consistent 
with their performance in assessment tasks in general, or 
9.6.2 
the student would not pass the course were special consideration granted, because 
their results in other assessments tasks have been such that a fail grade is certain. 
Applying for special consideration 
9.7 
Applications for special consideration must be submitted using the University’s online form 
for this purpose, either before or no later than three working days after the deadline for 
submission or scheduled date for completion of the assessment task and include supporting 
evidence of the exceptional circumstances that have caused them to need special 
consideration.   
