10 
DEFERRED EXAMINATIONS 
10.1 
A deferred exam is a final examination that is held after time scheduled for the final exam it 
replaces. 
10.2 
Deferred exams are normally scheduled during the next exam period, as shown on the 
University Academic Calendar. However, the University may schedule deferred exams at other 
times where this required to support student progression. 
10.3 
To be eligible to be considered for a deferred exam, the student must: 
10.3.1 be prevented from sitting the final exam by exceptional circumstances as defined in 
section 4 
10.3.2 be registered with the University as an elite athlete, and have an elite sporting or 
coaching commitment at the time of the exam, or 
10.3.3 be an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander and have a cultural commitment of which 
the timing is outside their control, at the time of the exam. 
10.4 
A student is not eligible for a deferred exam if they have sat the exam at the originally 
scheduled time. 
10.4.1 A student should decide before entering the exam venue whether they are capable 
of sitting the exam. 
10.4.2 A student will be considered to have sat an exam if they enter the exam venue and 
remain there longer than 10 minutes after the exam start time. 
10.5 
A deferred exam will: 
10.5.1 examine the same course learning outcomes as the exam it replaces 
10.5.2 have different questions from the original exam, and 
10.5.3 be scheduled and managed by Student Administration. 
10.6 
To apply for a deferred exam, a student must: 
10.6.1 use the online application form for this purpose and follow the instructions in the 
form 
10.6.2 provide satisfactory supporting documentation, and 
10.6.3 submit the application no later than three working days after the date of the exam. 
10.7 
The supporting documentation the student needs to provide in support of their application is: 
10.7.1 where the student needs the deferred exam because of exceptional circumstances, 
independent documentary evidence, including: 
10.7.1.1 a statutory declaration signed by an independent witness, or 
10.7.1.2 where the circumstances are an injury or physical or mental health 
condition, a certificate from the treating health professional 
10.7.2 where the student needs the deferred exam because of an elite sporting or training 
commitment, evidence that they are registered with the University as an elite 
athlete, and independent supporting documentation of the commitment 
10.7.3 where the student is an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander student and needs the 
deferred exam to meet a cultural commitment, written confirmation of the 
commitment from an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander staff member or the 
relevant community organisation. 
