12.1.3 A student will be granted only one opportunity to undertake a supplementary 
assessment task, unless the head of the school that manages the relevant course 
considers that unusual circumstances warrant granting the student a further 
supplementary assessment task. 
12.2 
Where program requirements allow, a board of examiners may grant on the recommendation 
of a head of school a supplementary assessment to allow a student one further attempt at an 
assessment in a course where the student has: 
12.2.1 achieved a narrow fail: that is, where the student’s overall mark for the course is in 
the range 45–49 percent, or 
12.2.2 received an FN grade because they did not achieve the minimum mark required for 
a hurdle assessment, or 
12.2.3 received an FN grade because their mark meant they did not achieve the minimum 
result across a sub-set of assessment tasks that collectively form a hurdle 
requirement for the course. 
12.3 
A supplementary assessment task will not normally be granted to a student: 
12.3.1 who has failed to maintain satisfactory academic progress in accordance with the 
Procedure: Academic Progress 
12.3.2 who has had their program enrolment terminated or has been suspended from the 
University in accordance with the Procedure: Academic Progress, or 
12.3.3 in a course in which the student is enrolled for a bachelor (honours) degree. 
12.4 
Where a student has been granted a supplementary assessment task: 
12.4.1 If the supplementary assessment task will not be completed in time for approval of 
the student’s final grade in the course, an interim grade will be recorded until the 
assessment process has been completed. 
12.4.2 Once the student has undertaken the supplementary assessment task: 
12.4.2.1 if they achieve a mark in the task sufficient to pass the course, the next 
board of examiners meeting will approve a grade of Pass (P) and an overall 
mark of 50 for the student in the course 
12.4.2.2 if they do not achieve a mark in the task sufficient to pass the course, their 
original overall mark for the course will stand, and either: 
• their current grade of fail (F) will stand or 
• where an interim grade of SP has been recorded for them in the course, 
Student Administration will change this back to a fail (F) grade. 
12.5 
Students who are granted an opportunity to sit a supplementary exam as a supplementary 
assessment will be notified in writing of their exam at least five working days prior to the exam 
date. 
12.6 
Where a student is prevented from sitting a supplementary exam due to exceptional 
circumstances outside their control, they may apply to sit the deferred exam in accordance 
with clause 10.12. 
