14 
RESPONSIBILITIES AND DECISION-MAKING AUTHORITIES 
14.1 
This section summarises the requirements and decision-making authorities stated in this 
procedure that apply to each of the positions, committees or roles listed below. 
14.1.1 Should any decision-making authority stated in this procedure be inconsistent with a 
delegation in the schedule of academic delegations to the Standing Delegations of 
Authority, the Standing Delegations of Authority states the correct delegation of the 
decision-making authority. 
14.2 
Access and inclusion advisors: 
14.2.1 will keep in confidence the circumstances and health information of a student who 
was seeking reasonable adjustments (see clause 5.5 and its subclauses) 
14.2.2 may decline to provide an adjustment requested by a student under certain 
circumstances (see clause 5.7 and its subclauses), and 
14.2.3 will issue learning access plans (see clause 5.8) 
14.3 
Boards of examiners may: 
14.3.1 grant a student a supplementary assessment task, where the student meets certain 
conditions (see section 12), and/or 
14.3.2 grant a student a conceded pass, where the student meets certain condition (see 
section 13). 
14.4 
Campus student advisers, deputy heads of school, discipline coordinators and program 
coordinators: 
14.4.1 may, where their head of school has nominated them to make such decisions, 
approve a student’s request to have an extension of up to seven days on a deadline 
to submit assessment work (see section 8) 
14.4.2 may require a student seeking an extension to provide supporting documentation 
and/or complete the University’s form for requesting such extensions (see clause 8.1 
and its subclauses) 
14.4.3 must accept as sufficient evidence that a student deserves an extension: 
14.4.3.1 the student’s learning access plan if this provides for reasonable 
extensions see clause 8.1.4.3), or 
14.4.3.2 a respect officer’s confirmation that the student has experienced adverse 
circumstances which warrant an extension (see clause 8.2 and its 
subclauses) 
