14.4.4 may, where their head of school has nominated them to decide students’ 
applications for special consideration, grant such a request in relation to an 
assessment task (other than in relation to a final exam or permission to resubmit 
assessment work already marked), if: 
14.4.4.1 this will not delay release of the student’s final grade in the course, and 
14.4.4.2 the student’s application for special consideration is timely (see clause 9.3 
and its subclauses) 
14.4.5 may accept, in lieu of supporting documents for a student’s special consideration 
application, a respect officer’s confirmation that student has experienced adverse 
circumstances that warrant special consideration (see clause 9.9), and 
14.4.6 where they have decided the outcome of a student’s special consideration 
application, will inform the student and Student Administration of the outcome (see 
clause 9.12). 
14.5 
Course coordinators: 
14.5.1 will not seek to know the details of a student's disability or health condition, where 
the student approaches them seeking the reasonable adjustments set out in a 
learning access plan (see clause 5.9.3) 
14.5.2 will provide a student with the reasonable adjustments set out in the student’s 
learning access plan (see clause 5.9.4) 
14.5.3 may contact the access and inclusion advisor who formulated a learning access plan 
to clarify its requirements (see clause 5.9.5) 
14.5.4 will provide a student with adjustments to learning activities and/or assessment 
arrangements to enable them to meet elite sporting commitments, subject to the 
student and the commitments meeting certain conditions (see section 6) 
14.5.5 will provide an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander student with reasonable 
adjustments to enable the student to meet a cultural commitment, subject to the 
student and the commitment meeting certain conditions (see section 7) 
14.5.6 may, where their head of school has nominated them to make such decisions, 
approve a student’s request to have an extension of up to seven days on a deadline 
to submit assessment work (see section 8) 
14.5.7 may require a student seeking a short extension to provide supporting 
documentation and/or complete the University’s form for requesting extensions (see 
clause 8.1 and its subclauses), and 
14.5.8 must accept as sufficient evidence that a student deserves an extension: 
14.5.8.1 the student’s learning access plan if this provides for reasonable 
extensions see clause 8.1.4.3), or 
14.5.8.2 a respect officer’s confirmation that the student has experienced adverse 
circumstances which warrant an extension (see clause 8.2 and its 
subclauses). 
14.6 
The Director, Student Engagement and Success: 
14.6.1 may under certain circumstances share the circumstances or health information of a 
student who is seeking reasonable adjustments with 
14.6.1.1 staff for the purpose of managing a risk in relation to the student 
14.6.1.2 decision-makers in relation to an appeal by the student 
14.6.1.3 senior staff to inform a decision about a non-standard adjustment, or 
14.6.1.4 a court or other external authority where the University is obliged by law 
