14.12 The National Manager, Student Services and Graduations may: 
14.12.1 grant a student a deferred exam (see section 10) or an irregularly scheduled exam 
see section 11). 
14.12.2 accept, in lieu of supporting documents for a student’s deferred exam application, a 
respect officer’s confirmation that the student has experienced adverse 
circumstances that warrant special consideration (see clause 10.8) 
14.12.3 grant a student a further opportunity to sit a deferred exam or a supplementary 
exam, where they are satisfied that the student is experiencing exceptional 
circumstances that warrant compassion (see clause 10.12 and clause 12.6). 
14.13 Program coordinator responsibilities and decision authorities are summarised above under 
‘Campus student advisers, deputy heads of school, discipline coordinators and program 
coordinators’. 
14.14 Student Administration will schedule and manage: 
14.14.1 deferred exams (see section 10) 
14.14.2 irregularly scheduled exams (see section 11), and 
14.14.3 supplementary exams (see section 12). 
14.15 Respect officers may request: 
14.15.1 an extension on behalf of a student (see clause 8.2) 
14.15.2 special consideration on behalf of a student (see clause 9.9), and/or 
14.15.3 a deferred exam on behalf of a student (see clause 10.8). 
14.16 Students: 
14.16.1 if they wish to receive reasonable adjustments for a disability or health condition, or 
as a caregiver for someone without disability or health condition, must register with 
the access and inclusion advisors, provide documentation and attend an interview 
(see section 5) 
14.16.2 if they have been issued with a learning access plan, are expected to approach course 
coordinators to discuss specific adjustments (see clause 5.9 and its subclauses) 
14.16.3 if they wish to receive reasonable adjustments for a disability or health condition in 
relation to a final exam, must give permission for an access and inclusion advisor to 
notify the Academic Registrar of the adjustments (see clause 5.10) 
14.16.4 where the school that manages their course declines to provide a reasonable 
adjustment stated in the student’s learning access plan, may ask for support from the 
access and inclusion advisors (see clauses 5.13) 
14.16.5 if they wish to receive assessment flexibility as an elite athlete, elite coach or elite 
sporting official, must satisfy the elite athlete program administrator that they are 
such (see section 6) 
14.16.6 if they are Aboriginal or a Torres Strait Islander, may (subject to meeting certain 
conditions) receive reasonable adjustments to learning activities and/or assessment 
tasks to enable them to be absent for up to 10 days per year to meet cultural 
