15.2 
Definitions 
15.2.1 The definitions section of the Policy: Programs and Courses defines the terms used 
in this procedure, other than those listed below.  
15.3 
The following additional terms have the meanings stated below. 
15.3.1 Alternative assessment task means a different assessment task that is equivalent to 
the original assessment task and assesses the same learning outcomes. 
15.3.2 Carer means a person who provides personal care, support and assistance to another 
person who has an episodic, temporary or permanent disability, medical condition 
(including a terminal or chronic illness), mental health condition, or who is frail and 
aged. 
15.3.3 Deferred assessment task means the same assessment task, such as a test with 
different questions, at a later date than the originally scheduled task. 
15.3.4 Deferred examination has the meaning stated in the Procedure: Assessment and 
Examinations.  
15.3.5 Examination has the meaning stated in the Procedure: Assessment and 
Examinations.  
15.3.6 Exceptional circumstances has the meaning stated in clauses 4.2 and 4.3. 
15.3.7 Final examination has the meaning stated in the Procedure: Assessment and 
Examinations. 
15.3.8 In writing means by email from/to the student’s student email account or in a hard 
copy letter. 
15.3.9 Irregularly scheduled examination has the meaning stated in the Procedure: 
Assessment and Examinations. 
15.3.10 Major has the meaning stated in the Procedure: Program and Course Design. 
15.3.11 Respect officer has the meaning stated in the Policy: Sexual Assault and Sexual 
Harassment. 
15.3.12 Special consideration has the meaning stated in clause 9.1. 
15.3.13 Supplementary assessment task has the meaning stated in clause 12.1. 
15.3.14 Working day means a day when the University is open for business and excludes 
weekend days or public holidays when the University is closed for business. 
 
