1 
PURPOSE 
1.1 
This procedure supports the Policy: Assessment in Higher Education and Enabling Coursework 
Programs by stating requirements for assessment in: 
1.1.1 higher education coursework and enabling programs and courses, and 
1.1.2 courses with a supervised research component in bachelor (honours) and masters by 
coursework programs. 
1.2 
The Interpretation and definitions section at the end of this procedure: 
1.2.1 states requirements for interpreting this procedure and 
1.2.2 explains its hierarchical relationship with other policy documents in the University’s 
Policy Framework. 
1.3 
Scope 
1.3.1 This procedure applies to: 
1.3.1.1 assessment in all higher education coursework and enabling (tertiary 
preparation or pathway) programs and non-award higher education courses of 
the University of Notre Dame Australia (the University) 
1.3.1.2 supervision and examination of students’ research for a research component 
course in a bachelor (honours) or masters by coursework program of the 
University 
1.3.1.3 staff who design or conduct assessment in coursework courses, or who 
supervise or examine students’ research for a research component course for 
a coursework program, including staff of a third-party organisation that 
delivers a course on behalf of the University, and 
1.3.1.4 students enrolled in coursework programs and/or coursework courses, 
including a program or course delivered by a third-party organisation on behalf 
of the University. 
2 
RELATED POLICIES AND REGULATIONS 
2.1 
This procedure should be read alongside the Policy: Assessment in Higher Education and 
Enabling Coursework Programs, which it supports. 
2.2 
Further related policies and regulations are: 
2.2.1 Procedure: Assessment and Learning Flexibility  
2.2.2 Policy: Programs and Courses 
2.2.3 Procedure: Program and Course Life Cycle  
2.2.4 Procedure: Program and Course Design  
2.2.5 Procedure: Program and Course Quality  
2.2.6 Procedure: Program and Course Information 
2.2.7 Policy: Student Appeals, and 
2.2.8 General Regulations 
3 
PROGRAM LEVEL ASSESSMENT DESIGN 
3.1 
Assessment and feedback are designed and integrated through a team-based, whole-of-
program approach that supports student achievement and maintains the integrity of 
assessment.  
3.2 
Program coordinators (or their equivalent) will lead the design and implementation of 
