7.3.6 exam / test papers are evaluated and modified each teaching period. 
8 
ASSESSMENT OF WORK INTEGRATED LEARNING 
8.1 
Student work integrated learning, including practicums, internships and other work 
placements, will be formally assessed and appropriately weighted to contribute to the overall 
mark and grade for the course. (Refer to Section 6 in the Procedure: Program and Course 
Design.) 
8.2 
Courses that include work-integrated learning must be supported by an assessment plan that 
is informed by contemporary theories, practices, and standards and: 
8.2.1 aligns course learning outcomes and assessment methods to the applicable professional 
and / or industry standards and professional competencies 
8.2.2 incorporate learning schemas that focus student attention on practice processes and 
standards and enable theoretical learning to be integrated with applications in a 
workplace or community 
8.2.3 develops students’ interpersonal skills and capacity for interprofessional collaboration 
8.2.4 provide students opportunity for reflection and reflexivity and evaluative judgement, 
and 
8.2.5 provide opportunities for students to give feedback on the quality of their work 
integrated learning experience.  
8.3 
Section 9 in the Procedure: Program and Course Delivery and Management sets out the 
University’s requirements for managing the delivery of work integrated learning, including for 
assessment of placement providers and placement arrangements, written agreements with 
placement providers, risk management plans, and monitoring the quality of placements and 
student placement experiences. 
9 
STUDENT PARTICIPATION IN ASSESSMENT DESIGN 
9.1 
Where aspects of an assessment task are to be negotiated with students during the teaching 
as part of the learning experience: 
9.1.1 the process for and scope of this negotiation must have been detailed in the information 
on the assessment task in the course outline 
9.1.2 all students in the course must be given an opportunity to participate in the negotiation, 
and  
9.1.3 the negotiated assessment must meet the course learning outcomes with which it is 
aligned. 
