11.2 Late submission penalties 
11.2.1 If a student submits assessment work after the deadline or, where the student has been 
granted an extension of the deadline, after the extended deadline, the course 
coordinator (or, in the School of Medicine, the Head of Assessment) may apply a mark 
reduction penalty. 
11.2.1.1 In calculating the number of days a submission is late, weekend days and 
university holidays are counted. 
11.2.1.2 As far as possible, penalties for late submission will be: 
• consistent across all courses in a school, program or discipline, and 
• applied consistently to all students enrolled in a course who submit work 
late. 
11.2.1.3 A penalty for late submission cannot be greater than the penalties in the 
following table. 
 
Number of days the assessment task is submitted after the deadline or, where 
the student has been granted an extension, after the extended deadline 
Maximum reduction to be 
subtracted from the mark for 
the assessment task 
One day or less 
5 percent 
Two days or less, but more than one day 
10 percent 
