30 percent 
Seven days or less, but more than six days 
35 percent 
Eight days or less, but more than seven days 
40 percent 
Nine days or less, but more than eight days 
50 percent 
Ten days or less, but more than nine days 
60 percent 
Eleven days or less, but more than ten days 
100 percent 
 
12 EXAMS AND TESTS ADMINISTERED BY FACULTIES OR SCHOOLS 
12.1 Where a course requires students to sit an exam or test that is administered by staff of the 
faculty or school that manages the course, the course coordinator will make the following 
arrangements to ensure academic integrity and quality of assessment. 
12.1.1 The exam or test questions will be kept securely until the time when they are to be 
provided to students sitting the exam or test. 
12.1.2 Where the exam or test is held in a physical venue, enough staff will supervise it to 
ensure students: 
12.1.2.1 are identified, so that no one else sits the exam or test in place of a student 
12.1.2.2 follow any relevant instructions 
12.1.2.3 use only materials and resources they are permitted to use, and 
12.1.2.4 collaborate only to the extent permitted. 
12.1.3 Implement reasonable adjustments for any student with an approved and current 
Learning Access Plan (LAP).  
12.1.4 Where a faculty or school administers a final exam, the exam questions and instructions 
will beforehand undergo at least the following two checks by staff other than the staff 
member(s) who set the questions and created the instructions: 
12.1.4.1 a check by an academic staff member (typically the relevant program 
