subclauses. 
12.1.7 Where it is necessary for a student to sit the exam or test at a later time than other 
students, different exam/test questions will be used for that sitting. 
13 FINAL EXAMS ADMINISTERED BY STUDENT ADMINISTRATION 
13.1 Final exams centrally administered by Student Administration are: 
13.1.1 normally scheduled within the standard examination periods set out in the University 
Academic Calendar, and 
13.1.2 included in the examinations timetable provided to students each semester by Student 
Administration. 
13.2 Where a final exam is required to be scheduled for a course outside of a standard examination 
period: 
13.2.1 a request for Student Administration to administer the final exam must be submitted to 
Student Administration for approval by the Director, Student Administration at least six 
months prior to the date the examination is to take place, and 
13.2.2 the exam must be scheduled to ensure there will be sufficient time to meet the 
University’s dates for finalising course results and grades and releasing these to 
students. 
13.3 Where a school manages either a practical final exam to be held in a lab or clinical space and 
supervised by teaching staff or clinical experts, or a final exam is to be held online, with students 
sitting the exam on their own computer, the school will: 
13.3.1 provide details of the exam needed for the examinations timetable, to Student 
Administration, by the deadline for these details specified by Student Administration, 
and 
13.3.2 administer the exam in accordance with the requirements of Section 13 of this 
Procedure. 
13.4 The examinations timetable for each standard examination period is made available to 
students four weeks prior to the commencement of the examination period. 
13.4.1 Students with a Learning Access Plan will be notified of their personal Examination 
Timetable. 
13.4.2 The examinations timetable for standard examination periods is determined to ensure 
that a student will not be required to sit more than two exams in one day, and no more 
than three examinations in consecutive days. 
