13.4.3 Faculties and schools will work with Student Administration when scheduling the exams 
they administer to ensure they do not conflict with the scheduling of final exams 
administered by Student Administrations. 
13.4.4 It is the responsibility of each student to be aware of their scheduled exam times and 
venues, and to notify Student Administration by email (via timetable@nd.edu.au) of any 
examination scheduling clashes. 
13.4.5 For final exams held in a University venue, a student may apply to sit an exam at an 
alternative examination venue on the grounds of exceptional circumstances. 
13.4.5.1 Requests from students for an alternative examination venue must: 
• be made in writing to the Director, Student Administration at least six weeks 
before the commencement of the relevant examination period, and 
• include evidence of the circumstances that will prevent them from sitting 
the exam in a University venue. 
13.4.6 Where a final exam is to be conducted online, at least two weeks before the day the 
exam is scheduled, students who will be sitting the exam must check to confirm their 
computer is suitable for sitting online invigilated exams following the instructions 
published to the University’s website. 
13.4.6.1 Where a student finds their computer unsuitable for sitting online invigilated 
exams, 
they 
must 
contact 
Student 
Administration 
(via 
student.admin@nd.edu.au) within five working days of the release of the exam 
timetable to make alternative exam arrangements. 
13.4.7 The Procedure: Assessment and Learning Flexibility sets out provisions for students to 
apply for a deferred exam or an irregularly scheduled exam where exceptional 
circumstances prevent them from sitting a final exam. 
13.5 Examination papers 
13.5.1 Course coordinators will follow administrative processes and timelines, and use the 
templates and coversheet, which are established and maintained by Student 
Administration, for preparing and submitting final exam papers, and later collecting 
students’ answers (where these are still handwritten). 
13.5.2 Exam papers must be sent to Student Administration: 
13.5.2.1 no later than six weeks prior to the commencement of the standard 
examination period in which they are to be scheduled, or 
13.5.2.2 for exams held outside of the standard examination period, by the due date 
otherwise specified by Student Administration. 
13.5.2.3 Where a final exam is to be held online, the course coordinator will send a print 
version of the online examination to Student Administration. 
13.5.3 The preparation and approval of final exam questions will be in accordance with the 
requirements for design of exams in Section 7 of this Procedure. 
13.5.4 The course coordinator of a course will prepare the questions for final exams, deferred 
exams and supplementary exams, for approval by the program coordinator (or 
equivalent). 
13.5.4.1 Where a program coordinator is also the coordinator of a course, the head of 
school may approve the exam questions. 
13.5.4.2 The course coordinator may nominate another academic staff member to 
prepare the exam questions. 
13.5.5 Where a final exam administered by Student Administration is to be held online, with 
students sitting the exam on their own computer: 
