13.5.5.1 Student Administration will create a shell for the online exam in ExamSoft, and 
13.5.5.2 the course coordinator will import the final exam questions, as approved in 
accordance with clause 13.5.4 above, and set up the exam within the 
timeframe specified by Student Administration. 
13.6 Conduct of final exams administered by Student Administration 
13.6.1 The supervision arrangements for final exams centrally administered by Student 
Administration in University exam venues are coordinated by Student Administration. 
13.6.2 The course coordinator or other academic staff member who prepared the exam paper 
for an exam will: 
13.6.2.1 be available for exam invigilators to contact by telephone during the scheduled 
exam time 
13.6.2.2 attend the exam venue for the first 15 minutes of the exam to 
• advise the exam invigilators on materials students may use in the exam, and 
• answer questions about the exam paper, and 
13.6.2.3 where there are written exam answers, attend the exam venue to collect these 
no later than 10 minutes after the end of the exam. 
13.6.2.4 The staff member who prepared the exam paper may nominate, in their place: 
• another academic staff member to attend the start of the exam and be 
available to answer questions that arise during the exam and/or 
• another academic or general staff member to collect any written exam 
answers. 
13.6.2.5 Where a final exam is held online, the course coordinator or other academic 
staff member who prepared the exam paper must ensure they will be 
contactable by students who are sitting the exam for the first 15 minutes of the 
exam. 
13.6.3 The Director, Student Administration will maintain detailed instructions for exam 
invigilators and students sitting final exams managed by Student Administration, to 
ensure that: 
13.6.3.1 the identity of students sitting an exam is confirmed 
13.6.3.2 students only bring resource materials into an exam that are permitted to be 
used in the exam  
13.6.3.3 exams are conducted in accordance with instructions specific to the exam 
13.6.3.4 orderly conduct and academic integrity of exams, and 
13.6.3.5 a student’s exam answers are identified as the students in the exam marking 
process.  
13.6.4 The duration of a final exam will include time for students to read the exam questions 
before starting to answer them. 
13.6.5 A student may enter a physical exam venue up to half an hour after the scheduled exam 
start time. 
13.6.6 Other than in extraordinary circumstances, a student will not be allowed to leave a 
physical exam venue: 
13.6.6.1 in the first 30 minutes of the exam, or 
13.6.6.2 in the last 20 minutes of the exam. 
13.6.7 A student sitting a final exam must comply with: 
13.6.7.1 the exam instructions provided by Director, Student Administration, and 
13.6.7.2 written or verbal instructions given them by an exam invigilator. 
13.6.8 Where an exam invigilator considers that a student sitting the exam is breaching 
