17 ASSESSMENT RECORDS AND EXAM ANSWERS 
17.1 The course coordinator will ensure that staff teaching in the course record students’ results for 
all assessment tasks in the marking module of the University’s learning management system. 
17.2 Students’ exam answers remain the property of the University. 
17.2.1 A student may request information about marking of their exam answers and what 
marks they received for each by writing to the head of school within 10 working days of 
the date on which final grades in the course are released. 
17.2.2 Where a student requests this information, the school will, within 10 working days of 
receiving the request, provide it either in a written communication or by inviting the 
student to a meeting with the course coordinator or (as relevant) program coordinator. 
17.3 A year after students’ final grades in a course have been released, the school may: 
17.3.1 destroy exam scripts and other assessment work that has not been returned to 
students, and 
17.3.2 delete digital files of students’ exam answers and assessment work. 
18 ACADEMIC GRADES 
18.1 The table below specifies the grades that can be awarded to record a student’s level of 
academic achievement in a higher education course (academic grades). A student may achieve 
at different levels in different assessment tasks for a course, in which case their grade will 
reflect the student’s weighted average level of achievement in the course assessment tasks. 
 
Grade  Description 
Mark range 
Criteria 
HD 
High Distinction 
80–100% 
The student has demonstrated a very high standard of academic 
achievement and produced work of outstanding quality. 
 
To record this grade, there must be evidence that the student has: 
 
• achieved the highest level of attainment in relation to the 
learning outcomes 
• demonstrated a deep and critical understanding of the course 
content through considerable insight, originality, evaluation 
and problem-solving 
• consistently demonstrated advanced application of 
knowledge, competencies, skills and mastery 
D 
Distinction  
70–79% 
The student has demonstrated a high standard of academic 
achievement and produced work of very high quality. 
 
To record this grade, there must be evidence that the student has: 
 
• achieved a high level of attainment in relation to the learning 
outcomes 
• frequently demonstrated insight and understanding, through 
skilled and integrated application of methods, principles, 
concepts and/or theories 
• demonstrated superior application of knowledge, critical 
evaluation, competencies and skills 
