19.3 Where a school manages a double degree of which a component single degree is managed by 
a different school, a representative of the relevant discipline in the other school will attend the 
school board of examiners when it considers the grades of students in that double degree. 
19.4 The Procedure: Academic Progress states the responsibilities of boards of examiners for:  
19.4.1 monitoring students’ academic progress and deciding their current academic status, and 
19.4.2 deciding whether to 
19.4.2.1 terminate a student’s program enrolment for sustained unsatisfactory 
academic progress and/or 
19.4.2.2 suspend or terminate a student’s enrolment at the University for repeated fails 
in required courses. 
19.5 The Procedure: Program and Course Quality states the responsibilities of boards of examiners 
for: 
19.5.1 monitoring grade distributions, and 
19.5.2 checking that moderation of assessment and second marking of narrow fail grades have 
occurred. 
19.6 The Academic Registrar may withhold an approved grade from a student until: 
19.6.1 the outcome of a student misconduct allegation that may lead to a change in the 
student’s grade is known, or 
19.6.2 the student has paid a debt to the University. 
