20.1.1 Where an H grade is recorded: 
20.1.1.1 the head of the school that manages the course will recommend the academic 
grade for the student to the next scheduled meeting of the board of examiners, 
or 
20.1.1.2 if this has not occurred by that next meeting, the H grade will be converted to, 
as relevant, an F (fail) or FN (fail due to non-completion) grade, unless 
20.1.1.3 the head of school recommends, and the relevant executive dean approves, an 
extension to the period before the grade will be converted to the relevant fail 
grade. 
20.1.2 Where an IP grade is recorded: 
20.1.2.1 the head of the school that manages the course will recommend the student’s 
academic grade in the course, as advised by the course coordinator, to the next 
scheduled meeting of the board of examiners, or 
20.1.2.2 if this has not occurred by that next meeting, the IP grade will be replaced with 
an H grade, and the process stated in clause 20.1.1 will apply. 
21 APPROVAL OF AWARD OF MICROCREDENTIALS 
21.1 A school board of examiners may approve the award of a microcredential to a student who 
has passed the assessment for the microcredential. 
21.2 Where a student has passed the assessment for a microcredential, and the school board of 
examiners is not scheduled to meet, the chair of the board of examiners may 
21.2.1 approve the award of the microcredential to the student, provided that they 
21.2.2 report the approval to the next meeting of the board of examiners. 
22 APPEALS AGAINST COURSE MARKS 
22.1 A student may appeal their marks in a course in accordance with the Policy: Student Appeals 
which states the grounds and process for a student to appeal against: 
22.1.1 denial of a request made via special consideration, to resubmit assessment work 
22.1.2 denial of a request to have assessment work remarked, and 
22.1.3 a final overall mark they have been awarded for a course. 
