23.1.1 A GPA will not be calculated for: 
23.1.1.1 a student’s enrolment in a program with a volume of learning of 100 units of 
credit or less 
23.1.1.2 any program (other than the Doctor of Medicine) in which the student has 
received academic grades in fewer than six courses. 
23.1.2 The following grades do not contribute to a student’s GPA calculation: 
23.1.2.1 a grade for a course graded on an NGP (satisfactory performance – no range of 
passing grades)/F (fail basis) 
23.1.2.2 a grade for a research component course in a bachelor (honours) program, and 
23.1.2.3  an E grade to show that credit has been granted for a course on the basis of 
prior learning, unless an E grade is from an internal program transfer where 
original marks must be manually reinstated. 
