will calculate the GPA of a student’s academic grades for courses they have completed as part 
of their enrolment in a program. 
23.1.1 A GPA will not be calculated for: 
23.1.1.1 a student’s enrolment in a program with a volume of learning of 100 units of 
credit or less 
23.1.1.2 any program (other than the Doctor of Medicine) in which the student has 
received academic grades in fewer than six courses. 
23.1.2 The following grades do not contribute to a student’s GPA calculation: 
23.1.2.1 a grade for a course graded on an NGP (satisfactory performance – no range of 
passing grades)/F (fail basis) 
23.1.2.2 a grade for a research component course in a bachelor (honours) program, and 
23.1.2.3  an E grade to show that credit has been granted for a course on the basis of 
prior learning, unless an E grade is from an internal program transfer where 
original marks must be manually reinstated. 
23.2 The GPA calculation is as follows. 
23.2.1 Each course grade is assigned a grade points value in accordance with the following 
table. 
 
Grade 
HD 
D 
C 
P 
CP 
F* 
FN 
WF 
Grade points 
4 
3 
2 
1 
0 
0 
0 
0 
* Only where this grade is recorded for a course that is graded with a range of passing grades (HD, D and 
so on). 
 
23.2.2 The grade point value of each course is multiplied by the number of units of credit at 
which the course is weighted. 
23.2.3 The products of these multiplications for all eligible courses are added to produce total 
A. 
23.2.4 The numbers of units of credit at which the courses are weighted are added to produce 
total B. 
23.2.5 Total A is divided by total B to produce the GPA, which is rounded to two decimal places 
(values less than 0.005 are rounded down; values of 0.005 or more are rounded up). 
23.3 GPAs are used: 
23.3.1 as an indication of a student’s overall academic performance on their formal transcript 
of results, and 
23.3.2 to decide whether to 
23.3.2.1 confer a qualification on the student with distinction or high distinction 
23.3.2.2 award a student a prize or award. 
23.3.2.3 A student’s weighted average mark in a program or part of a program may also 
be used to decide whether to award them a prize or award. 
23.4 A weighted average mark is calculated: 
23.4.1 based on the same courses as are used to calculate a student’s GPA in a program, and 
23.4.2 by the same calculation process as a GPA, except that the student’s overall mark in each 
course is used in the calculation in place of the grade point value of the course. 
