26 RESPONSIBILITIES AND DECISION-MAKING AUTHORITIES  
26.1 This section summarises the requirements and decision-making authorities stated in this 
procedure that apply to each of the positions, committees or roles listed below. 
26.1.1 Should any decision-making authority stated in this procedure be inconsistent with a 
delegation in the schedule of academic delegations to the Standing Delegations of 
Authority, the Standing Delegations of Authority states the correct delegation of the 
decision-making authority. 
26.2 Associate deans, learning and teaching, faculty academic integrity officers and program 
coordinators (or their equivalent) will work with Curriculum and Quality to support effective 
assessment design and review processes faculties and schools in accordance with the 
requirements in Procedure. (see section 3) 
26.3 Boards of examiners 
26.3.1 Boards of examiners will review and confirm student marks and grades, decide students’ 
level of honours, and record an interim grade for a student under various circumstances. 
(see section 19) 
26.3.2 Boards of examiners may approve the award of a microcredential to a student.  
26.3.3 The chair of a board of examiners may approve the award of a microcredential to a 
student when the board of examiners is not scheduled to meet. (see section 21) 
26.4 Course coordinators 
26.4.1 Course coordinators: 
26.4.1.1 will ensure course outlines include an assessment rubric for each assessment 
task (subject to certain exceptions) (see section 3) 
26.4.1.2 will collaborate with other staff who teach in the course to ensure students 
receive feedback on their assessment work in accordance with this Procedure 
(see section 5) 
26.4.1.3 may apply a mark reduction penalty to assessment work that a student submits 
after a deadline or, where the student has been granted an extension on the 
deadline, after the extended deadline (see section 11) 
26.4.1.4 will make arrangements to ensure the academic integrity of an exam or test in 
the course that is administered by staff of the school (see section 12) 
26.4.1.5 will prepare exam papers for exams managed by Student Administration in 
accordance with this Procedure, or nominate another teaching staff member 
to do this (see section 13) 
26.4.1.6 for an exam managed by the Student Administration for which they have 
written the exam paper, will attend the start of the exam, be available for exam 
invigilators to contact by telephone during the exam, and attend the exam 
venue promptly to collect exam papers at the end of the exam (see section 13) 
26.4.1.7 will work collaboratively with other staff teaching and assessing in the course 
to ensure they understand the assessment and feedback requirements for each 
assessment task (see section 14) 
26.4.1.8 may, where their head of school has nominated them to make this decision, 
grant a student’s request for re-marking of their work for an assessment task 
they have failed (see section 15), and 
26.4.1.9 will ensure that staff teaching in the course record students’ results for all 
assessment tasks in the marking module of the learning management system. 
(see section 17) 
