26.4.2 See also the responsibilities of teaching staff below. 
26.5 Curriculum and Quality 
26.5.1 Curriculum and Quality will work with associate deans, learning and teaching, faculty 
academic integrity officers and program coordinators (or their equivalent) to coordinate 
and facilitate assessment design and review processes in faculties and schools in 
accordance with the requirements of this Procedure (see section 3). 
26.6 Deputy heads of school 
26.6.1 A deputy head of school may grant a student’s request for re-marking of their work for 
an assessment task in accordance with this Procedure, where this decision has been 
delegated to them by their head of school. (see section 15) 
26.7 Executive deans 
26.7.1 An executive dean may: 
26.7.1.1 approve an extension to the period before an H (hold) grade will be converted 
to a fail grade (see section 20), or 
26.7.1.2 grant a student permission to resubmit their thesis or dissertation for a 
supervised research component of a bachelor (honours) or masters by 
coursework program. (see section 24) 
26.8 Faculty learning and teaching committees (or equivalent committees)  
26.8.1 Faculty learning and teaching committees (or an equivalent committee) may: 
26.8.1.1 approve an exception to the maximum weighting of any assessment tasks of 
50 percent of the overall course mark (see section 3) 
26.8.1.2 approve an exception to the limit on the weighting of group marks, peer 
marks and/or self-marks in a course set out clause 6.2.2 
26.8.1.3 approve the use of a hurdle assessment task for another reason than those 
listed in clause 10.3.2 and its sub-clauses 
26.8.1.4 as an exception, permit submission of written assessment work in hardcopy 
or by email (see section 11) 
26.8.1.5 exempt an exam or test administered by a faculty or school from having 
arrangements to verify students’ identity and/or monitor students while 
they sit the exam or test, subject to the conditions stated in this Procedure. 
(see section 12) 
26.9 General staff 
26.9.1 General staff who support teaching staff in their assessment work will keep students’ 
marks, grades, assessment feedback and assessment work in confidence. (see section 
16) 
26.10 Head of Assessment (School of Medicine) 
26.10.1 The Head of Assessment in the School of Medicine may apply a mark reduction penalty 
to assessment work that a student submits after a deadline or, where the student has 
been granted an extension on the deadline, after the extended. (see section 11) 
26.11 Head of Clinical and Head of Preclinical (School of Medicine) 
26.11.1 The Head of Clinical and Head of Preclinical in the School of Medicine may, where their 
head of school has nominated them to make such decisions: 
26.11.1.1 grant a student’s request for re-marking of their work for an assessment task 
they have failed, and/or 
26.11.1.2 under certain circumstances, choose a co-marker to collaborate with the 
original marker in re-marking a student’s assessment task, and decide the 
mark that results from the re-marking. (see section 15) 
