26.12 Heads of school 
26.12.1 Heads of school will: 
26.12.1.1 recommend to a board of examiners the academic grade to replace an H 
(hold) grade or IP (in progress) grade (see section 20) 
26.12.1.2 recommend to an executive dean that they approve an extension to the 
period before an H (hold) grade will be converted to a fail grade (see section 
20) 
26.12.1.3 appoint supervisors of students’ research for research components of 
bachelor (honours) and masters by coursework programs (see section 24), 
and 
26.12.1.4 where the marks recommended by the two readers of a student’s thesis or 
dissertation for a supervised research component of a bachelor (honours) 
or masters by coursework program differ by more than 10 percent, will 
appoint a third examiner. (see section 24) 
26.13 Innovation and Design 
26.13.1 Innovation and Design will provide guidance, training and other support for staff in 
schools, faculties, and professional support areas, including for technology enabled 
assessment: application of the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines, providing 
assessment requirements and information in the LMS. (see section 3) 
26.14 Program coordinators (or their equivalent) 
26.14.1 Program coordinators (or their equivalent) will: 
26.14.1.1 lead the design and implementation of assessment across the programs 
they coordinate in accordance with the requirements set out in this section 
3 of this Procedure 
26.14.1.2 ensure the assessment design for the program they coordinate provides 
multiple planned opportunities for meaningful feedback, including feed 
forward and early feedback, to ensure students can effectively apply it to 
future learning and assessment tasks and staff can proactively identify and 
support students at risk (see section 5) 
26.14.1.3 approve final examination questions (see Section 13), and 
26.14.1.4 monitor moderation of marking, in courses in the programs they 
coordinate, including for assessments as part of third-party delivery 
arrangements (see section 14). 
26.15 Student Administration 
26.15.1 Student Administration will administer and manage final exams and deferred exams 
(see section 13) 
26.16 Schools 
26.16.1 Schools: 
26.16.1.1 may administer exams and tests in accordance with section 12 
26.16.1.2 where a student requests information about marking of their exam 
answers and what marks they received for each, will provide this 
information (see section 17) 
26.16.1.3 may destroy exam scripts and other assessment work that has not been 
returned to students after enough time has elapsed (see section 17) 
26.16.1.4 will provide, to examiners of a student’s thesis or dissertation submitted 
for a supervised research component in bachelor (honours) and masters 
by coursework program, the criteria for examination (see section 24), and 
