26.10 Head of Assessment (School of Medicine) 
26.10.1 The Head of Assessment in the School of Medicine may apply a mark reduction penalty 
to assessment work that a student submits after a deadline or, where the student has 
been granted an extension on the deadline, after the extended. (see section 11) 
26.11 Head of Clinical and Head of Preclinical (School of Medicine) 
26.11.1 The Head of Clinical and Head of Preclinical in the School of Medicine may, where their 
head of school has nominated them to make such decisions: 
26.11.1.1 grant a student’s request for re-marking of their work for an assessment task 
they have failed, and/or 
26.11.1.2 under certain circumstances, choose a co-marker to collaborate with the 
original marker in re-marking a student’s assessment task, and decide the 
mark that results from the re-marking. (see section 15) 
