26.17 Students 
26.17.1 Students: 
26.17.1.1 must complete the online academic integrity training modules and comply 
with the University’s expectations for academic integrity as set out in the 
Procedure: Academic Integrity 
26.17.1.2 must, as relevant, submit, perform or sit each assessment task detailed in 
the course outline, to pass the course (see section 10) 
26.17.1.3 when submitting assessment work, will provide a declaration that the work 
is their own (see section 11) 
26.17.1.4 will only use resource materials in an exam that the course coordinator or 
school explicitly permits them to use (see section 12) 
26.17.1.5 will follow the Academic Registrar’s instructions for the conduct of exams 
(see section 13), and 
26.17.1.6 will obey verbal instructions given to them by an exam invigilator (section 
13) 
26.17.1.7 if they are undertaking research for a research component of a bachelor 
(honours) program or masters by coursework program, will 
• conduct their research in accordance with the University’s policies and 
procedures on the responsible conduct of research, and 
• undertake the University’s online training module in research ethics for 
higher degree by research students. (see section 24) 
26.18 Teaching staff 
26.18.1 Teaching staff: 
26.18.1.1 will provide students with feedback on their assessment work in 
accordance with section 5 
26.18.1.2 will keep students’ marks, grades, assessment feedback and assessment 
work in confidence (see section 16) 
26.18.1.3 where they help to administer an exam or test, or write questions for an 
exam or test, will take the required measures to ensure academic integrity 
(see sections 12 and 13) 
26.18.1.4 where they prepare an exam paper for a final exam, deferred exam or 
supplementary exam on behalf of a course coordinator, will follow the 
processes and timelines set by the Student Administration, and use the 
templates provided by the Student Administration (see section 13) 
26.18.1.5 for an exam managed by the Student Administration for which they have 
written the exam paper, will: 
• attend the start of the exam 
• be available for exam invigilators to contact by telephone during the 
exam, and 
• where students write their answers to the exam, attend the exam venue 
promptly at the end of the exam to collect them (see section 13 
26.18.1.6 will participate in moderation of assessment tasks in a course (see section 
14), and 
26.18.1.7 will record students’ results for all assessment tasks in the marking module 
of the learning management system (see section 14) 
