27 INTERPRETATION AND DEFINITIONS 
27.1 The following rules of interpretation apply to this procedure: 
27.1.1 The University’s Policy Framework sets out the hierarchy of the University’s policy 
documents. 
27.1.2 Should any provision in this procedure be inconsistent with a provision of a document 
higher in the University’s hierarchy of policy documents as stated in the Policy 
Framework, the higher document prevails and overrules this procedure to the extent of 
the inconsistency. 
27.1.3 This procedure must be read alongside other closely related policy documents: 
27.1.3.1 the policy that it supports, identified in the Purpose section 
27.1.3.2 closely related policies and regulations listed in the Related policies and 
regulations sections 
27.1.3.3 the Employee Code of Conduct and Ethical Behaviour and Code of Conduct 
(Students), which include a requirement to comply with policy documents of 
the University, and 
27.1.3.4 any other documents listed in the Related documents section. 
27.1.4 Where this procedure uses: 
27.1.4.1 the verbs ‘will’ or ‘must’, it states a requirement 
27.1.4.2 the phrases ‘cannot’, ‘must not’ or ‘only [position title] can’, it states a 
prohibition 
27.1.4.3 the words ‘include’, ‘includes’, or ‘including’ followed by a list, the words 
‘without limitation’ are taken to follow immediately  
27.1.4.4 the phrase ‘for example’ or ‘such as’ followed by a single instance or list, the 
instance or list is not exhaustive 
27.1.4.5 the phrases ‘described in’, ‘set out in’, ‘specified in’ or ‘stated in’, it will be 
read as if the words ‘expressly or impliedly’ appeared immediately before 
them 
27.1.4.6 the singular, it also means the plural, and vice versa 
27.1.4.7 any gender, it includes the other genders, and 
27.1.4.8 a reference to a statute, ordinance, code, or other law, it includes regulation, 
by-laws, rules and other statutory instruments under it for the time being in 
force and consolidations, amendments, re-enactments, or replacements of 
any of them. 
27.2 The definitions section of the Policy: Assessment in Higher Education and Enabling Coursework 
Programs defines terms used in this procedure. The following additional terms have the 
meanings stated below. 
27.2.1 Assessment method means the process(es) involved in accomplishing the assessment 
such as writing, performing, visualising, etc. 
27.2.2 Assessment mode means the manner in which the assessment occurs such as online, 
face to face, off campus. 
27.2.3 Assessment has the meaning stated in the Policy: Assessment in Higher Education and 
