Enabling Coursework Programs. 
27.2.4 Assessment type means the category of assessment such as essay, portfolio, script. 
27.2.5 Board of examiners has the meaning stated in sections 56 and 57 of the Statutes. 
27.2.6 Deferred examination means an examination that is conducted under the same 
invigilated conditions as a centrally administered examination but is held later than the 
original examination.  
27.2.7 Dissertation has the meaning stated in the General Regulations. 
27.2.8 Examination is a formal, invigilated, time limited assessment activity (also expressed as 
exam). 
27.2.9 Feedforward means providing students with meaningful qualitative feedback that 
enables them to answer the questions, where am I now, where am I heading and how 
do I get there? 
27.2.10 Final examination means an examination held after the end of teaching in a teaching 
period and included in the schedule of final examinations provided to students by 
Student Administration.  
27.2.11 Formative assessment means assessment that facilitates learning by helping students 
and teaching staff identify strengths, weaknesses, and ways to improve and enhance 
attainment of intended learning outcomes and monitor progress toward the intended 
learning outcomes. They are no-stakes assessments.  
27.2.12 Grade point average has the same meaning as in clause 23.1 and it is calculated 
following the method set out in clause 23.2. 
27.2.13 Graduate Attributes means the generic qualities, skills and understandings which the 
University aspires to develop in its students.  
27.2.14 Hurdle assessment has the meaning stated in clause 10.3.1. 
27.2.15 Intended learning outcomes means the knowledge and skills a student will acquire 
and be able to demonstrate as a result of learning in a course and a program of study. 
27.2.16 Irregularly scheduled examination means an examination that is conducted under the 
same invigilated conditions as a centrally administered examination but is held at a 
different time, date, and/or place, prior to or during the formal examination period. 
27.2.17 Mandatory requirements are requirements associated with assessment such as a 
vaccination, or a Working with Children Check, that are required to be completed prior 
to students engaging in the associated assessment activity and are generally provided 
by external bodies, associations or practices. They are not assessable. 
27.2.18 Mandatory task is a type of hurdle task and has the meaning stated in clause 10.3.1. 
27.2.19 Mastery path allows students more self-paced progression through a course, or 
section of a course to meet the learning outcomes, with differentiated pathways that 
are designed to deliver targeted learning and assessment to meet students at different 
levels of competence. The mastery path takes students through course material and 
assessments based their successive performances and, in some cases, allows multiple 
attempts at assessments, for example quizzes, or performative tasks until the student 
demonstrates proficiency.   
27.2.20 Microcredential has the meaning stated in the Procedure: Program and Course Design. 
27.2.21 Moderation of assessment means quality assurance processes and activities such as 
peer review that aim to assure the consistency or comparability, appropriateness, 
fairness, and comprehensibility of an assessment task, and the related criteria and 
standards. Moderation applies to many aspects of assessment such as the choice of 
assessment task and its design, assessment instructions, marking guides, rubrics, 
