27.2.22 Offering means, of a course, a delivery of a course, in a teaching period, at a location 
or online. 
27.2.23 Overall course mark means a student’s percentage mark for a course based on their 
mark in each assessment task they have completed, weighted in calculating the overall 
percentage according to the task’s weighting stated in the course outline. 
27.2.24 Performance standards mean the standard of performance for individual assessment 
criteria that correspond with each possible grade. 
27.2.25 Research project has the meaning stated in the General Regulations. 
27.2.26 Summative assessment means an assessment task, that it is primarily focused on 
assessing whether students are achieving or have achieved the course learning 
outcomes and contributes to the overall course mark. 
27.2.27 Triangulation of assessment means instances where two or more assessment 
methods are employed to assess the same learning outcomes through a variety of 
assessment types and forms of production.  
27.2.28 Thesis has the meaning stated in the General Regulations. 
27.2.29 Universal Design for Learning (UDL) is a framework to improve and optimise teaching 
and learning for all people based on scientific insights into how humans learn that aims 
to provide equal learning opportunities for all students by removing barriers to learning. 
27.2.30 Volume of learning has the meaning stated in the Procedure: Program and Course 
Design. 
27.2.31 Work Integrated Learning has the meaning stated in the Procedure: Program and 
Course Design. 
 
