1 
PURPOSE  
1.1 
This procedure supports the Policy: Academic Integrity by stating requirements for: 
1.1.1 supporting staff and students to maintain academic integrity, and 
1.1.2 responding to breaches of academic integrity when they occur. 
2 
RELATED POLICIES AND REGULATIONS 
2.1 
This procedure should be read in conjunction with the following policy documents: 
2.1.1 Policy: Academic Integrity 
2.1.2 General Regulations 
2.1.3 Code of Conduct: Students 
2.1.4 Employee Code of Conduct and Ethical Behaviour 
2.1.5 Policy: Managing Misconduct 
2.1.6 Policy: Programs and Courses and its supporting procedures: 
2.1.6.1 Procedure: Assessment and Examinations, and 
2.1.6.2 Procedure: Program and Course Design. 
3 
EDUCATING STUDENTS ABOUT ACADEMIC INTEGRITY 
3.1 
Coursework programs will be designed so that students have opportunities to develop the 
knowledge and skills needed to maintain academic integrity. 
3.2 
The Procedure: Program and Course Design states requirements for design of programs to 
include early assessment tasks, so that students who need academic support can be identified 
and referred to Student Success. 
3.3 
Students will have access to learning resources and academic support services to help them 
understand and apply principles of academic integrity. These will include: 
3.3.1 online academic integrity training modules 
3.3.2 workshops and a consultation service for students provided by Student Success; and 
3.3.3 Library resources such as referencing guides, guides to using scholarly resources, 
research skills and learning skills guides. 
3.4 
To minimise academic integrity breaches: 
3.4.1 All staff are expected to: 
3.4.1.1 ensure they understand how to comply with the university’s expectations for 
academic integrity 
3.4.1.2 model ethical behaviour, and 
3.4.1.3 communicate the University’s expectations for academic integrity to students. 
3.4.2 Staff involved in teaching, student supervision, training and assessment are expected 
to: 
3.4.2.1 engage with resources for teaching staff on how to maintain academic 
integrity provided by the University 
3.4.2.2 be aware of the signs of contract cheating and monitor student assessment 
work for their occurrence 
3.4.2.3 provide students with feedback that supports an educative approach to 
maintaining academic integrity 
3.4.2.4 refer students who need further academic support to the course coordinator 
or to Student Success, and 
