3.4 
To minimise academic integrity breaches: 
3.4.1 All staff are expected to: 
3.4.1.1 ensure they understand how to comply with the university’s expectations for 
academic integrity 
3.4.1.2 model ethical behaviour, and 
3.4.1.3 communicate the University’s expectations for academic integrity to students. 
3.4.2 Staff involved in teaching, student supervision, training and assessment are expected 
to: 
3.4.2.1 engage with resources for teaching staff on how to maintain academic 
integrity provided by the University 
3.4.2.2 be aware of the signs of contract cheating and monitor student assessment 
work for their occurrence 
3.4.2.3 provide students with feedback that supports an educative approach to 
maintaining academic integrity 
3.4.2.4 refer students who need further academic support to the course coordinator 
or to Student Success, and 
