5.2 
Reporting pathways for academic integrity breaches 
5.2.1 All suspected breaches of academic integrity by students referred to a course 
coordinator for investigation are formally reported. 
5.2.2 The pathways for reporting academic integrity breaches include: 
5.2.2.1 the head of school for courses in coursework programs 
5.2.2.2 the National Director, Pathways for enabling programs  
5.2.2.3 the  Director, Research Services for coursework courses in higher degree by 
research programs, and 
5.2.2.4 the Chief Executive Officer, VET for VET courses. 
5.3 
Academic integrity breaches that are not considered to be student misconduct (level one) 
5.3.1 If the initial investigation identifies a level one breach that is not considered to be 
misconduct, the course coordinator will: 
5.3.1.1 decide on an appropriate response (refer to Appendix 1 of this procedure) 
5.3.1.2 advise the student in writing of the decision, and 
5.3.1.3 copy that communication to the appropriate head of school or director (refer 
to clause 5.2.2 of this procedure) and the National Appeals and Policy 
Coordinator for recording in the University’s academic integrity register (see 
Section 7). 
5.4 
Contract cheating 
5.4.1 All breaches of academic integrity involving contract cheating are considered to be 
student misconduct. 
5.4.2 If the suspected breach of academic integrity involves an allegation of contract 
cheating, the course coordinator will refer it to the Academic Integrity Officer for 
investigation to decide if it can be substantiated. 
5.4.3 If the Academic Integrity Officer decides it is likely that contract cheating has occurred, 
they will notify the course coordinator who will report the matter to the appropriate 
head of school or director. (refer to clause 5.2.2 of this procedure) 
5.4.3.1 If the incident of contract cheating involves multiple students, the Academic 
Integrity Officer will also notify the Pro Vice Chancellor, Education and the 
Deputy Vice-Chancellor, Academic. 
5.4.4 If the Academic Integrity Officer decides that contract cheating cannot be 
substantiated, they will notify the course coordinator and provide the reason for their 
decision. 
5.5 
Other academic integrity breaches that are considered to be student misconduct (level two 
and above) 
5.5.1 If a suspected breach of academic integrity does not involve contract cheating and the 
course coordinator finds the breach to be level two or above, the course coordinator 
will report the matter to the appropriate head of school or director (refer to clause 
5.2.2 of this procedure). 
5.5.2 When reporting the matter, the course coordinator will provide the documentary 
evidence that supports the allegation. 
5.6 
Referral of academic integrity breaches that are considered to be student misconduct 
