5.6.1 On receiving a report of a breach of academic integrity the head of school or director 
will decide whether the allegation against the student should proceed in accordance 
with clause 8.7 of the General Regulations. 
5.6.2 Where, however, the student is also a staff member, the head of school or director will 
decide whether the allegation will proceed and, if so, whether it will be handled as: 
5.6.2.1 a case of student misconduct in accordance with clause 8.7 of the General 
Regulations, or 
5.6.2.2 an allegation of staff misconduct in accordance with the Policy: Managing 
Misconduct. 
6 
SUSPECTED BREACHES OF ACADEMIC INTEGRITY BY STAFF 
6.1 
Suspected breaches of academic integrity by staff, will be treated as an allegation of 
misconduct in accordance with the Policy: Managing Misconduct (staff), except where: 
6.1.1 the breach occurred in a situation where the staff member was a student and clause 
5.6.2.1 of this procedure applies. 
7 
RECORDING ACADEMIC INTEGRITY BREACHES 
7.1 
Student Administration will maintain a central academic integrity register that records the 
following details for all level one breaches of academic integrity and all instances where a 
suspected breach is handled as an allegation of student misconduct. 
7.1.1 The date when the alleged breach occurred 
7.1.2 Student ID 
7.1.3 Student name 
7.1.4 Course code 
7.1.5 Course title 
7.1.6 School administering the course 
7.1.7 Level of breach 
7.1.8 The type of breach (in alignment with the breach-types classified in clause 4.5.2 of the 
Policy: Academic Integrity) 
7.1.9 The type of assessment task in which the breach was detected 
7.1.10 Decision-maker (course coordinator, school discipline committee, University Discipline 
Committee) 
7.1.11 Whether the allegation was upheld or denied (in cases considered to be student 
misconduct) 
7.1.12 The response and any penalty applied. 
7.2 
The National Appeals and Policy Coordinator will manage staff access to the academic integrity 
register and keep a record of approved users. 
7.2.1 The following positions may have access to the register:  
7.2.1.1 Head of school 
7.2.1.2 Academic Integrity Officers 
7.2.1.3 Manager, Academic Integrity and Misconduct 
7.2.1.4 Director, Research Services 
7.2.1.5 Academic Registrar 
7.2.1.6 Pro Vice Chancellor, Education 
7.2.1.7 Any other positions approved to have the access by the Academic Registrar. 
