7.2.2 Users of the register are expected to keep their login details secure and maintain the 
confidentiality of the information in the register in accordance with the Policy: Privacy. 
7.3 
The Chair of the University Disciplinary Committee (in accordance with the student 
misconduct process in the General Regulations) will: 
7.3.1 provide details of alleged level three and level four breaches of academic integrity to 
the National Appeals and Policy Coordinator once the University Disciplinary 
Committee has made a determination, and 
7.4 
Chairs of School Disciplinary Committees (in accordance with the student misconduct process 
in the General Regulations) will: 
7.4.1 provide details of alleged level two breaches of academic integrity to the National 
Appeals and Policy Coordinator when the School Disciplinary Committee had made a 
determination. 
7.5 
Heads of school or directors (for alleged breaches not referred to a disciplinary committee, in 
accordance with the student misconduct process in the General Regulations) will: 
7.5.1 provide details of alleged level two breaches of academic integrity to the National 
Appeals and Policy Coordinator Officer when they have made a determination. 
7.6 
Records of breaches of academic integrity by staff will be maintained in accordance with the 
Policy: Managing Misconduct (staff), except where 
7.6.1 the breach occurred in a situation where the staff member was a student and clause 
5.7.1.1 of this procedure applies. 
8 MONITORING AND IMPROVEMENT 
8.1 
Executive deans, heads of school and other staff in learning and teaching leadership roles will 
have access to student academic integrity breach data to monitor and improve practices for: 
8.1.1 educating students about academic integrity, and 
8.1.2 detecting and responding to alleged breaches of academic integrity. 
8.2 
To maintain student confidentiality in accordance with the Policy: Privacy individual students 
will not be identified in any reports that include student academic integrity breach data. 
8.2.1 Breach data will not be reported for a student cohort if the number of students in the 
cohort is small enough to make it likely that an individual student could be identified. 
8.3 
The Manager, Academic Integrity and Misconduct will use the central academic integrity 
register to report on trends for the occurrence and outcomes of student academic integrity 
breaches to the Academic Standards and Policy Committee for each Study Period. 
8.4 
The Deputy Vice-Chancellor, Academic will report annually on student academic integrity to 
Academic Council. 
8.4.1 Annual student academic integrity reports will include analyses of: 
8.4.1.1 institutional trends for academic integrity breaches (number and types of 
breach, student referrals to academic support and penalties applied) 
8.4.1.2 training and support for students (number of students completing the online 
academic integrity modules, attendance at the Office of Student Success and 
Library workshops, individual consultations) and 
8.4.1.3 training and support for staff (engagement in continuing professional learning 
activities, available support resources). 
8.4.2 Academic Council will use annual academic integrity reports to monitor the 
effectiveness of institutional systems and processes for 
8.4.2.1 controlling or mitigating risks to academic integrity, 
