1 
OBJECTS OF THE UNIVERSITY 
The Objects of The University of Notre Dame Australia (the University) are defined in Section 5 of its 
Act of Parliament: 
 
The Objects are: 
 
(a) the provision of university education, within a context of Catholic faith and values; and 
(b) the provision of an excellent standard of - 
i. 
teaching, scholarship and research; 
ii. 
training for the professions; and 
iii. 
pastoral care for its students. 
2 
PURPOSE 
2.1 
This policy states the University’s expectations of staff and students in relation to academic 
integrity.  
3 
SCOPE 
3.1 
This policy applies to: 
3.1.1 staff of the University, including adjuncts and clinical academics 
3.1.2 students of the University (including former students) 
3.1.3 students enrolled in a program or course of the University delivered by a third party 
3.1.4 academic visitors to the University 
3.1.5 anyone who undertakes research on behalf of the University. 
3.2 
Principles and requirements for maintaining research integrity (responsible research conduct 
and practice) are defined in the Code of Conduct Research.  
3.2.1 Considerations for breaches of research integrity are set out in the Procedure: Managing 
Potential Breaches of the Code of Conduct Research. 
3.3 
Principles and requirements for managing potential conflicts of interest that relate to staff 
obligations for maintaining academic integrity are set out in the Employee Code of Conduct and 
Ethical Behaviour. 
4 
PRINCIPLES 
4.1 
Academic integrity is a shared responsibility that is fundamental to the University achieving its 
objects of an excellent standard of teaching, scholarship, research and training for the 
professions. 
4.1.1 Academic integrity means acting, ‘even in the face of adversity,’ with ‘honesty, trust, 
fairness, respect, responsibility and courage’ in all academic activities. This includes: 
4.1.1.1 Being honest in acknowledging other people’s work 
4.1.1.2 Reporting truthfully on the methods and result of one’s research 
4.1.1.3 Acting in an ethical manner in all academic activities 
4.1.1.4 Ensuring academic judgements or decisions relating to students and staff are 
fair and objectively based on all the information available. 
4.2 
The University will meet the standards of the Higher Education Standards Framework (HESF) 
