5.4 
A minor breach is a failure to meet the principles or responsibilities of the Code of Conduct: 
Research that is not intentional, reckless or negligent, and that has limited impact on research 
participants, communities or the integrity of the research, but requires remedial action to 
prevent recurrence. 
5.5 
A major breach (Research Misconduct) is a serious breach of the Code of Conduct: Research that is 
intentional, reckless or negligent, and that has caused, or has the potential to cause, significant harm 
to research participants or communities, substantially undermines the integrity or trustworthiness of 
research, or seriously damages public confidence in research. 
5.6 
The classification of a breach will inform the level of investigation, and any outcomes or actions, 
consistent with the requirement for proportionality under the Australian Code. 
 
