d) State whether or not, in the view of the Panel, there is sufficient evidence to prove the 
allegation of a breach of the Code of Conduct: Research has occurred and describe the 
extent and seriousness of the breach; 
e) Any mitigating circumstances arising out of the investigation; 
f) 
Any other matter the Panel or Investigating Officer considers necessary to assist the Vice 
Chancellor or PVC, Research in forming a determination; 
g) Include a recommendation on what disciplinary action, if any, may be taken against the 
Respondent. This recommendation will be proportionate to the seriousness of the breach. 
Where the Respondent is a staff member, any recommendation in relation to staff must 
comply with Clause 47 of the University’s Enterprise Agreement 2022-2026. 
Outcomes – Staff members 
8.24 Where it is found that the Respondent has breached the Code of Conduct: Research, the 
University may take appropriate and proportionate disciplinary action up to and including 
termination of employment, as determined by the Vice Chancellor in consideration of the 
recommendation of the report and ERC, and in accordance with the University’s Enterprise 
Agreement 2022-2026 and Policy: Managing Misconduct. 
8.25 The Investigating Officer will advise the Respondent in writing, as part of the Report, that he or 
she has a right to appeal the findings and/or recommendations of the Investigating Officer and 
Panel and that the Respondent must lodge an appeal with the Vice Chancellor, in writing, within 
five (5) working days of the Respondent receiving the Panel’s report. 
8.26 If the Respondent does not lodge an appeal under clause 8.31 below the Vice Chancellor may 
make a decision on the basis of the report as to any disciplinary action to be taken and that 
decision will be the final decision of the University.  
Outcomes - Students 
8.27 Where the Respondent is a student and the Panel determines that a breach of the Code of 
Conduct: Research has occurred the PVC Research will make a determination as to what 
disciplinary action, if any, should be taken against the student, taking into account the Panel’s 
final report and recommendations and the penalties prescribed in Section 8 of the General 
Regulations. 
8.28 Once the PVC Research has made a determination under clause 8.27, the Investigating Officer will 
advise the Respondent of the outcome and the disciplinary action, if any, to be taken. 
8.29 For international students found to have breached the Code of Conduct: Research, the PVC 
Research will consult with the PVC International to identify any potential implications for 
reporting to relevant government departments, including in relation to a student’s visa. 
8.30 If, during its investigation, the Panel has identified systemic issues as a contributing factor to 
any breach, these will be referred to the appropriate committee or staff member to be 
addressed. 
Appeal Process 
8.31 In the event a Respondent who is a staff member lodges an appeal of the findings or 
recommendations as to the disciplinary action of the Panel, the Vice Chancellor will refer the 
matter to an Employee Review Committee who will undertake a review for the Vice Chancellor 
in accordance with clause 47.4 of the University’s Enterprise Agreement 2022-2026. 
