4.4 
University research must be supported by a Research Data Management Plan (RDMP), where 
appropriate that is maintained throughout a research project and documents location and 
management arrangements for research data associated with the research project. 
4.5 
The University requires that researchers adhere to the FAIR and CARE data principles. 
4.6 
The University will provide the necessary infrastructure and services to enable researchers to 
meet their responsibilities for research data throughout the research data lifecycle. 
5 
RESEARCH DATA MANAGEMENT RESPONSIBILITIES 
 
5.1 
All researchers must ensure that research data is managed in accordance with ethical protocols 
and agreements, relevant contractual obligations and the University’s Policy: Information and 
Information Technology and Procedure: Information Management. 
5.2 
Researchers will, in consultation with their supervisors and Executive Deans, follow the norms 
of best practice in their discipline for Data Management, to establish the nature of Data 
management required. 
5.3 
Researchers, where appropriate, must prepare and maintain a Research Data Management Plan 
(RDMP) for all research projects ensuring: 
5.3.1 data creation, collection, storage and management, and the provisions for its access 
from its creation or collection to its preservation are documented early in the research 
process;  
5.3.2 data are accurate, secure, complete, and documented with enough detail to enable 
verification of research results and to reflect what was communicated, decided, or done 
throughout the research process; 
5.3.3 clear roles and responsibilities for the management of research data within their 
research project or group, with principal investigators retaining ultimate responsibility 
for ensuring compliance with this policy; 
5.3.4 legal, ethical, data sovereignty, protective security and commercial constraints relating 
to research data are considered prior to data collection and adhered to throughout the 
research data lifecycle; 
5.3.5 appropriate data governance arrangements are in place to represent the interests of 
rights-holders and other key stakeholders of the research data; 
5.3.6 collaborations with external parties have agreements in place prior to the 
commencement of the research that are executed by the appropriate University 
delegate and specify ownership and custodianship rights and responsibilities for 
research data including compliance with the Foreign Relations Act, ethics and/or other 
relevant clearances; 
5.3.7 clear and accurate records of research methods, research data, primary materials and 
data sources are kept in a durable, organised and accessible manner. 
6 
STORAGE, RETENTION AND DISPOSAL 
 
6.1 
Where possible, data and materials should be digitised, recorded in a durable and retrievable 
form, stored in institutionally sanctioned infrastructure (refer to the Research Data Storage and 
Access guide), appropriately indexed and described by metadata, and backed up. Where 
appropriate, metadata should contain the location of any physical object being digitised. Data 
