to) software, systems, assets, network resources, servers and switches. 
Metadata means data that provides information about other data, such as information about an 
object or resource that describes characteristics of that object, such as its content, quality, format, 
location and/or access rights. 
Primary Materials means objects (physical or virtual) acquired through a process of scholarly 
investigation from which research data may be derived. 
Research means the creation of new knowledge and/or the use of existing knowledge in a new and 
creative way so as to generate new concepts, methodologies, inventions and understandings. This 
could include synthesis and analysis of previous research to the extent that it is new and creative 
(Excellence in Research Australia 2018 Submission Guidelines 2018, ARC). 
Research Data means all data, inclusive of primary materials, created and/or generated by researchers 
throughout and beyond the research lifecycle. Data that are in the form of facts, observations, images, 
computer program results, recordings, measurements, narratives or experiences on which argument, 
theory, test or hypothesis, or another research output is based, and for which the University has a 
custodial responsibility under the relevant Agreements and the relevant archives/record keeping Acts. 
See also Appendix (Section 12) 
RDMP means a document (a Research Data Management Plan) that describes how a researcher will 
collect, organize, manage, store, secure, back up, preserve and share your data during and beyond the 
lifecycle of the research project. It deals with matters such as retention and disposal, archiving, accessing, 
sharing or publishing the data, and conditions or restrictions for data reuse 
Researcher means anyone engaged in research activity by the University as a member of staff, a 
volunteer, an affiliate, an adjunct, visiting scholar or students enrolled in a research higher degree, 
including doctoral degrees and masters by research degrees. 
The Code means The Australian Code for the Responsible Conduct of Research (2018). 
University Resources means resources of the University which include premises, facilities, ICT 
infrastructure, relevant policies and procedures, funds, services, equipment, staff time and support 
staff. 
 
 
 
