4.7.3 relates to the use of an innovative technique for the first time. 
4.8 
Longer retention times are encouraged if sharing or secondary data use is expected. For 
sensitive data, intended retention time should be included in the application to HREC. 
At the end of the retention period, data must be destroyed in a manner which 
permanently prevents its reassembly. Relevant metadata items describing the data 
should be updated to indicate that the data has been destroyed. 
4.9 
Should changes to research data storage affect ethical considerations, then revised 
ethics approvals must be sought. 
