2.3.6 Whether the University is likely to disclose personal information to overseas recipients 
and if so, the countries the recipients are likely to be located. 
 
Privacy – Legal Requirements   
2.4 
The University is committed to protecting the privacy of personal information. The University 
is required to comply with a number of privacy laws including the Australian Privacy 
Principles (APPs) contained in the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) (Privacy Act). The APPs regulate 
the manner in which personal information is handled by the University.  
 
 
