controls to protect information at each classification level will be implemented in 
accordance with relevant Information Security Standards. 
5.3 
The business owner of an enterprise information system will maintain instructions for users of 
the system on how to classify information they create or change in the system. 
5.4 
Employees who operate an enterprise information system (as opposed to merely using it) 
will: 
5.4.1 ensure users of the system follow the instructions on classifying information, and 
5.4.2 correct the classification of any information on the system that has been classified 
incorrectly. 
6 
SECURITY OF UNIVERSITY-PROVIDED DEVICES AND SOFTWARE, AND 
REMOVABLE STORAGE MEDIA 
6.1 
The Chief Information Officer will maintain instructions for staff to ensure: 
6.1.1 the security of university-provided mobile phones and tablet computers (mobile 
devices) 
6.1.2 the security of personal computers in university workplaces 
6.1.3 the security of removable digital storage media 
6.1.4 that staff maintain information security in their use of software provided by the 
University. 
6.2 
A staff member who uses their own mobile device to access a university information system is 
expected to take the security precautions required in the Chief Information Officer’s 
instructions to ensure the security of university-provided mobile devices. 
7 
PHYSICAL SECURITY OF INFORMATION 
7.1 
Where an office or work area contains information classified as internal, sensitive or very 
sensitive, the supervisor of the office or work area will ensure it is not left unattended and 
unlocked. 
8 
DECOMMISSIONING OF DIGITAL STORAGE DEVICES 
8.1 
The Chief Information Officer will maintain instructions for staff to ensure that, before digital 
storage devices that contain licensed software and/or university information pass out of the 
University’s control, the devices are reliably erased or destroyed. 
9 
RETURN OR DELETION OF INFORMATION WHEN STAFF LEAVE THE 
UNIVERSITY 
9.1 
The Chief People Officer will ensure that the process to offboard staff who are leaving the 
University requires that they confirm that they have: 
9.1.1 returned to the University any hard copy or physical information that is classified as 
internal, sensitive or very sensitive, and 
9.1.2 transferred to appropriate storage or deleted any University data or information from 
all their own computers, mobile devices and removable digital storage media in 
