appendices. This statement should detail the contribution of the student to each 
publication and be signed by all co-authors. An example is available on the Research 
Office Website. 
3.2.3    The majority of outputs must be published or accepted for publication at the time of 
submission.  
3.2.4  For thesis by publication, there should be enough outputs to support the important 
research findings. Minimum requirements are: 
a) For a Doctor of Philosophy, a minimum of three (3) high-quality  outputs as defined 
in section 4.10. 
b) For a Professional Doctorate, a minimum of three (3) high-quality outputs as defined 
in section 4.10. 
c) For a Masters by Research, a minimum of two (2) high-quality outputs as defined in 
section 4.10. 
d) For a Masters of Philosophy, a minimum of one (1) high-quality output as defined 
in section 4.10. 
Where it is proposed to include less than the minimum number of outputs, as outlined above, 
approval must be sought from the Faculty Research delegate and Pro Vice-Chancellor Research 
(PVCR) and any such proposal should be planned early in the candidature. Requests to the PVCR 
should include a statement by the HDR student and Principal Supervisor justifying the rationale 
for including fewer outputs and should be sent to the Research Office after endorsement from 
the Faculty Research delegate. 
3.3 
Format 
The following is a recommended format of the thesis, or the dissertation component of a 
practice-based thesis. This recommendation is provided, with the knowledge that there may be 
some variations based on discipline standards. If unsure, the HDR student may contact the 
relevant ADR. 
3.3.1 Format of the thesis submitted for examination should be one-and-a-half spaced, A4- 
sized, with ~2.4cm margins (default settings in Microsoft Word are appropriate). 
Footnotes, block quotes, or table text may be single spaced. 
3.3.2 After examination, should a hard copy of the final version of the thesis be required, the 
margin must be not less than 4cm on the spine side of the page. 
3.3.3 Type-face should be 12 point in Times New Roman or Arial. Only one font should be 
used for the entirety of the thesis. A font size of 10 point may be used in tables, captions, 
graphs, footnotes, and other apparatus. 
3.3.4 The text must be black throughout, including headings. Hyperlinks may be in blue and 
underlined as per convention. 
3.3.5 Text pages must be numbered sequentially. 
3.3.6 If mathematical or other scientific notation is presented using a font other than 
Symbol, the HDR student must embed the notation as an image into the PDF submitted 
to the University. 
3.3.7 Any graphics that are pivotal to the thesis, and which must be viewed in high resolution, 
