4.11 All research data should be stored and archived in compliance with the Policy: Research Data 
Management and documented in the completed and approved Research Data Management 
Plan, which should include exit planning. 
 
5 
THESIS EXAMINATION 
 
This section should be read in conjunction with the Procedure: Higher Degree by Research 
Candidature and Procedure: Nomination of Thesis Examiners for a Higher Degree by Research. 
5.1 
Examination process 
5.1.1 The final PDF version of the thesis, and the two completed forms, Student Statement 
Form and Supervisors' Certificate for Thesis Submission Form, must be submitted by the 
relevant Associate Dean’s Research office to the Research Office. 
5.1.2 Supervisors must provide advice about thesis examiners nominated per the Procedure: 
Nomination of Thesis Examiners for a Higher Degree by Research to the Research Office 
who will then review the documentation to ensure that the nominated examiners are 
suitably qualified, and that there are no conflicts of interest. The Australian Council of 
Graduate Research Conflict of Interest Guidelines can be found here. 
5.1.3 When the thesis is submitted, the electronic thesis is submitted to the examiners for 
thesis examination. At this time, the HDR student’s enrolment status will change from 
‘Enrolled’ to ‘Under Examination’. The HDR student’s University accounts such as library 
access and email will remain available during this time.  
5.1.4 HDR students and supervisors must not contact the examiners during the examination 
process. If they have questions or concerns regarding the examination, they should 
contact the Research Office. 
5.1.5 The Research Office remains in close communication with examiners during this period, 
and follows up with outstanding examination reports as a priority. However, to protect 
the integrity of the process, the Research Office will not provide students or supervisors 
with specific details on examination progress. 
5.1.6 In the case of project-based thesis requiring in person examination the relevant ADR or 
