user account to IT Service Desk. 
3.5 
Where someone such as a consultant, contractor or academic visitor needs temporary access 
to university information and communication systems to carry out their role, the Office of 
Information Technology will provide them with a temporary account only for the period 
during which they need the access. 
3.6 
Where a person or organisation external to the University maintains or supports the 
University’s information technology or software, the Office of Information Technology will 
provide them with access only to the relevant system(s) and to the extent needed for this 
work. 
Conditions of access 
3.7 
The Chief Information Officer will maintain terms and conditions of access to a university 
information technology user access account to ensure that users of university information 
and communication systems: 
3.7.1 maintain their security 
3.7.2 maintain the security and confidentiality of the information the system contains 
3.7.3 use the system only for the uses for which it is intended, and 
3.7.4 are aware that their use of the system must comply with the relevant code of conduct. 
3.8 
A business owner of a university information system may maintain supplementary terms and 
conditions of access to that system. 
Appropriate use of access 
3.9 
A staff user may only access information they need to carry out the functions of their work role. 
Disabling user accounts 
3.10 When someone ceases to be an employee, a student or alumnus of the University, or when 
someone with temporary access to university information and communication systems ceases 
to need the access, the Office of Information Technology will immediately disable their user 
account, either: 
3.10.1 as part of an automated process that will occur when a staff member ceases to be 
employed or after a student ceases to be enrolled (an offboarding process), or 
3.10.2 where the change will not be picked up by an automated offboarding process, on 
notification by the manager responsible for the employment, enrolment or other type 
of relationship with the University. (Such a manager is responsible for notifying the IT 
Service Desk promptly of such changes.) 
3.10.3 In the case of a student becoming a graduate with no current student enrolment, their 
student user account will be replaced with an alumnus user account. 
3.10.4 The Office of Information Technology will collaborate with Student Administration and 
People and Culture to maintain business rules for offboarding (as relevant) students or 
employees. 
3.10.5 Where a user account needs to be disabled immediately for an unexpected reason such 
as a suspected serious breach of a code of conduct, this must have been authorised by 
one of the Vice-Chancellor, Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic or Chief People Officer. 
3.10.6 Where the Vice-Chancellor, Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic or Chief People Officer 
are not available to authorise disabling a user’s account for such a reason, the Chief 
Information Officer may authorise disabling it. 
