4 
MONITORING INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY USE 
4.1 
The University will monitor use of its information systems to ensure users are complying with 
the terms and conditions of access to the relevant systems. 
4.1.1 University information systems generate logs of transactions and usage, which system 
administrators may use to view the content of electronic communications and files sent 
and stored. 
4.1.2 Even where a user has deleted a file, the University may retain and review archived 
and/or backup copies of the file. 
4.1.3 The Office of Information Technology will monitor internet usage via university 
information technology infrastructure, including sites and pages visited, files 
downloaded, video and audio files accessed and data entered, and may access records 
of these 
4.2 
The Vice-Chancellor or Chief Information Officer may authorise an employee to gain access to 
a staff member’s or student’s university information and communication systems user 
account in exceptional circumstances such as: 
4.2.1 where the employee is unexpectedly away, and access to their user account is needed 
to provide continuity of service, or 
4.2.2 to investigate an allegation of misconduct by an employee or student involving misuse 
of university information and communication systems. 
4.3 
For the purposes of the Workplace Surveillance Act 2005 (Cth), this section constitutes written 
notice of the University's computer surveillance of its employees. 
5 
MOBILE DEVICES 
5.1 
The University provides mobile phones and/or tablet computers (mobile devices) to: 
5.1.1 university employees who need these to perform their duties 
5.1.2 members of the University’s Board of Directors, and 
5.1.3 independent contractors who need a mobile device provided by the University to carry 
out the work for which the University has engaged them. 
5.2 
A new mobile phone will normally be provided to each executive employee and manager on 
their appointment to their position. 
5.2.1 Where an employee below manager level needs a mobile device to perform their work 
duties (for example, where these require them to be contactable while away from their 
work area and/or outside working hours), an executive staff member in the employee’s 
line of management reporting may request that they be issued with a device. 
5.2.2 In such a case, the employee will be issued with a device from the pool of available new 
and used devices. 
5.3 
Where an employee who has been issued with a mobile device changes to a different position 
below the level of manager, their eligibility to have the device will be re-assessed. 
5.4 
To request a mobile device, an employee must complete the university form for this purpose, 
and submit it by the process stated on the form. 
5.5 
By accepting the issue of a university-provided mobile phone, an employee is accepting that 
the mobile phone number may be communicated internally and externally to meet the needs 
of the University and the purposes for which the phone was provided: for example, the 
