6.3 
If supporting documents are provided by the Student after the initial appeal is lodged or if 
significant investigation or review is required due to the nature of the appeal, the time within 
which the appeal is to be considered in accordance with this Policy may be extended by the 
person reviewing the appeal (the Reviewer). In such situations, the Student will be advised of 
the expected delay. 
6.4 
A Student who requires assistance with lodging an appeal should contact a Student Appeals 
Officer on the relevant campus to assist with the appeal process. 
6.5 
Notifications of the outcome of an appeal will be provided in writing and emailed to the 
Student’s Notre Dame Student email address. 
6.5.1 The notification will contain the reasons for the decision.  
6.5.2 The notification will be sent within 10 working days of determining the outcome. 
6.5.3 The notification will include further appeals options (if any) and complaints information.  
7 COMPLAINTS  
 
7.1 
Where a Student has a concern about how the appeals process has unfolded, for example that 
the appeals process was not managed in accordance with the principles of procedural fairness 
or that the University has not complied with relevant policies, procedures or legislation, the 
Student can make a complaint with:  
7.1.1 a Student Grievance Officer under the Procedure: Student Grievance;  
7.1.2 an external complaints/review body, such as the National Student Ombudsman (for 
non-VET students) and the Commonwealth Ombudsman (for VET students).  
8 ENROLMENT AND ATTENDANCE UNTIL APPEAL OUTCOME 
 
8.1 
A Student who has lodged an internal appeal in accordance with clause 6 above and is awaiting 
the outcome of their appeal is permitted to enrol in once the Semester has commenced and until 
they are notified of the outcome of their appeal. 
8.2 
A Student who has lodged an appeal with an external agency or person is permitted to enrol in 
Courses until the University has been notified of the outcome of their appeal. In this 
circumstance: 
8.2.1 a Student must, upon request by the University, provide appropriate evidence that an 
appeal has been lodged or is under consideration; and 
8.2.2 must inform the University in writing immediately when he or she is aware of the 
outcome of the appeal. 
8.3 
Exceptions to clauses 8.1 and 8.2 will apply where: 
8.3.1 a Student has either failed, or has not yet received a final grade for any Course that is a 
prerequisite for a Course they wish to enrol in, or 
8.3.2 a Student wishes to enrol in a Placement Course and they have either failed or not yet 
received a final grade for a Course that the National Head of School considers they must 
successfully complete to be adequately prepared to undertake the placement (see 
clause 10.1 in the Procedure: Program and Course Delivery and Management).  
8.3.3 Where clauses 8.3.1 or 8.3.2 apply, the National Head of School has discretion whether 
or not to allow the Student  to enrol in the relevant Course. 
8.4 
A Student who chooses to enrol in one or more Courses while an appeal is under review will 
