9 CONFIDENTIALITY, ACCESSIBILITY AND RETENTION OF RECORDS 
 
9.1 
The University will keep records of appeals, appeal documents and appeal outcomes strictly 
confidential. 
9.2 
Records are filed confidentially on the University’s Central Student’s File managed by Student 
Administration. 
10 ADMISSIONS, ENROLMENT AND READMISSION 
 
10.1 An applicant or student who is dissatisfied with a decision with respect to admission and/or 
selection, enrolment, or readmission, or has had their offer and/or enrolment cancelled by 
Student Administration, may appeal the decision to the Academic Registrar. 
10.2 Grounds for appeal:  
10.2.1 For Program admission decisions: An applicant may only appeal on the grounds that the 
Admissions Office failed to follow due process or published selection processes. 
10.2.2 For Course enrolment decisions: A Student may appeal an enrolment refusal or 
cancellation on the grounds that the decision-maker failed to follow due process, failed 
to consider relevant evidence, or can demonstrate based on an error of fact which, if 
rectified, would mean the Student meets the requirements for continued enrolment. 
10.3 Timing for lodging appeal: The applicant or Student must lodge the appeal within 10 Working 
Days of the date the applicant received notice of the decision. The Academic Registrar may 
extend the time for lodging the appeal in exceptional circumstances. 
10.4 Timing for University review of appeal: The Academic Registrar will review and determine the 
appeal within 20 Working Days of receiving the appeal. 
10.5 Notification: The Academic Registrar will advise the applicant or Student, the decision-maker 
and the National Director, Admissions in writing of the determination, in accordance with the 
requirements for notification set out in section 6.5 of this policy. 
10.6 Further appeal: The decision of the Academic Registrar is final and not open to further internal 
appeal. 
11 CREDIT AND RECOGNITION OF PRIOR LEARNING (RPL) 
 
11.1 A Student may appeal the decision of Student Administration to deny an application for credit 
or RPL to the Academic Registrar. 
11.2 Grounds for appeal: The Student may appeal on the grounds that show that Student 
Administration failed to follow due process in accordance with the General Regulations and the 
