14 TERMINATION FOR NON-PAYMENT OF FEES OR CHARGES 
 
14.1 A Student whose enrolment at the University has been terminated by Student Administration 
for non-payment of fees may appeal the decision to the Academic Registrar. 
14.2 Grounds for appeal: The Student may appeal on the grounds which show that Student 
Administration failed to follow due process in accordance with the General Regulations and the 
Policy: Termination for Non Payment. 
14.3 Timing for lodging appeal: The Student must lodge the appeal within 10 Working Days of the 
date the Student received notice of Student Administration’s decision. The Academic Registrar 
may extend the time for lodging the appeal at their absolute discretion. 
14.4 Timing for University review of appeal: The Academic Registrar will review and determine the 
appeal within 20 Working Days of receiving the appeal. 
14.5 Notification: The Academic Registrar will advise the Student in writing of the determination, in 
accordance with the requirements for notification set out in section 6.5 of this policy. 
14.6 Conditions on the decision: If the Academic Registrar permits re-enrolment, the Academic 
Registrar may impose any conditions on the re-enrolment relating to the payment of fees 
and/or charges that the Academic Registrar deems reasonable. 
14.7 Further appeal: The decision of the Academic Registrar is final and not open to further internal 
appeal. 
15 PROGRAM TERMINATION – FAILURE IN A COMPULSORY COURSE 
 
15.1 A Student whose enrolment in a program has been terminated due to a second failure of a 
compulsory Course may appeal a decision to the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic. 
15.2 Grounds for appeal: The Student may appeal on the grounds that the Board of Examiners failed 
to follow due process in accordance with the Procedure: Academic Progress. 
15.3 Timing for lodging appeal: The Student must lodge the appeal within 10 Working Days of the 
date the Student received notice of the National Head of School’s decision. The Deputy Vice 
Chancellor- Academic may extend the time for lodging the appeal in exceptional circumstances. 
15.4 Timing for University review of appeal: The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic will review and 
determine the appeal within 20 Working Days of receiving the appeal. 
15.5 Notification: The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic will advise the Student, the National Head 
of School in writing of the determination, in accordance with the requirements for notification 
set out in section 6.5 of this policy. 
15.6 Further appeal: The decision of the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic is final and not open to 
further internal appeal. 
