16 UNIVERSITY SUSPENSION 
 
16.1 Appeal against Allocation of “University Suspended” Status 
16.2 A Student may appeal the allocation of “University Suspended” status to the Deputy Vice 
Chancellor, Academic. 
16.2.1 Grounds for appeal: The Student may appeal on the following grounds: 
(a) administrative error by the Board of Examiners; or 
(b) a breach of the University's Policies and/or Regulations by the Board of Examiners 
sufficient to cause disadvantage to the Student; or 
(c) grounds deemed acceptable by the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic due to 
exceptional circumstances, except where a Student was afforded Show Cause in 
relation to their University Suspension. 
16.2.2 Timing for lodging appeal: 
(a) Domestic students must lodge the appeal within 10 Working Days of the date the 
Student received notice of the Board of Examiners’ decision. The Deputy Vice 
Chancellor, Academic may extend the time for lodging the appeal in exceptional 
circumstances. 
(b) International students must lodge the appeal within 20 Working Days of the date the 
Student received notice of the Board of Examiners’ decision. The Deputy Vice 
Chancellor, Academic may extend the time for lodging the appeal in exceptional 
circumstances. 
16.2.3 Timing for University review of appeal: The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic will: 
review and determine the appeal within 20 Working Days of receiving the appeal. 
16.2.4 Notification: The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic will advise the Student, the National 
Head of School in writing of the determination, in accordance with the requirements for 
notification set out in section 6.5 of this policy. 
16.2.5 Further appeal: The decision of the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic is final and not 
open to further internal appeal 
17 STUDENT PLACEMENTS 
 
17.1 A Student may appeal a decision of a National Head of School made in accordance with clause 
10.1 of the Procedure: Program and Course Delivery and Management to refuse permission to 
enrol in a Placement Course or to remove the Student from a Placement to the Deputy Vice 
Chancellor, Academic. 
17.2 A Student may not appeal a decision to prevent them from enrolling in a Placement where the 
decision has been made under clause 8.3.2 of this Policy.   
17.3 Grounds for appeal: The Student may appeal on the grounds which show that the National 
Head of School failed to follow due process in accordance with the Procedure: Program and 
Course Delivery and Management (Section 10). 
17.4 Timing for lodging appeal: The Student must lodge the appeal within 10 Working Days of the 
date the Student received notice of the National Head of School’s decision. The Deputy Vice 
Chancellor, Academic may extend the time for lodging the appeal in exceptional circumstances. 
17.5 Timing for University review of appeal: The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic will review and 
