notification set out in section 6.5 of this policy. 
17.7 Further appeal: The decision of the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic is final and not open to 
further internal appeal. 
18 DEFERRED OR IRREGULARLY SCHEDULED EXAMINATION 
 
18.1 Where Student Administration denies an application for a Deferred or Irregularly Scheduled 
Examination, or an extension to a Deferred Examination, the Student may appeal in writing to 
the Academic Registrar. 
18.2 Grounds for appeal: The Student may appeal on the grounds that show that Student 
Administration failed to follow due process in accordance with the General Regulations and the 
Procedure: Assessment and Learning Flexibility. 
18.3 Timing for lodging appeal: The Student must lodge the appeal within 10 Working Days of the 
date the Student received notice of Student Administration’s decision. The Academic Registrar 
may extend the time for lodging the appeal in exceptional circumstances. 
18.4 Timing for University review of appeal: The Academic Registrar will review and determine the 
appeal within 20 Working Days of receiving the appeal. 
18.5 Notification: The Academic Registrar will advise the Student and National Head of School in 
writing of the determination, in accordance with the requirements for notification set out in 
section 6.5 of this policy. 
18.6 Further appeal: The decision of the Academic Registrar is final and not open to further internal 
appeal. 
19 SPECIAL CONSIDERATION 
 
19.1 A Student may appeal the decision of the National Head of School to deny an application for 
Special Consideration to the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic. 
19.2 Grounds for appeal: The Student may appeal on the grounds that show that the National Head 
of School failed to follow due process in accordance with the Procedure: Assessment and 
Learning Flexibility. 
19.3 Timing for lodging appeal: The Student must lodge the appeal within 10 Working Days of the 
date the Student received notice of the National Head of School’s decision. The Deputy Vice 
Chancellor, Academic may extend the time for lodging the appeal in exceptional circumstances. 
19.4 Timing for University review of appeal: The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic will review and 
determine the appeal within 20 Working Days of receiving the appeal. 
19.5 Notification: The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic will advise the Student, National Head of 
School in writing of the determination, in accordance with the requirements for notification set 
out in section 6.5 of this policy. 
19.6 Further appeal: The decision of the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic is final and not open to 
