21.2 Further Appeal to the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic  
21.2.1 A Student may appeal the decision of the National Head of School to deny an appeal 
regarding Final Mark to the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic. 
21.2.2 Grounds for appeal: The Student may appeal on the grounds that show that the National 
Head of School failed to follow due process in the review of the appeal. 
21.2.3 Timing for lodging appeal: The Student must lodge the appeal within five Working Days 
of the date the Student received notice of the National Head of School’s decision. The 
Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic may extend the time for lodging the appeal in 
exceptional circumstances. 
21.2.4 Timing for University review of appeal: The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic will 
review and determine the appeal within 10 Working Days of receiving the appeal. 
21.2.5 Notification: The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic will advise the Student, National 
Head of School and Student Administration in writing of the determination, in 
accordance with the requirements for notification set out in section 6.5 of this policy. 
21.2.6 Further appeal: The decision of the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic is final and not 
open to further internal appeal. 
22 RETROACTIVE WITHDRAWAL 
 
22.1  A Student may appeal a decision by the Director, Student Administration to reject their 
application for retroactive withdrawal or any waiver to the Academic Registrar. 
22.2 Grounds for appeal: The Student may only appeal on the grounds that the Director, Student 
Administration failed to follow due process in accordance with the General Regulations and the 
Policy: Retroactive Withdrawal. 
22.3 Timing for lodging appeal: The Student must lodge the appeal within 20 Working Days of the 
date the Student received notice of Student Administration’s decision. The Academic Registrar 
may extend the time for lodging the appeal in exceptional circumstances. 
22.4 Timing for University review of appeal: The Academic Registrar will review and determine the 
appeal within 20 Working Days of receiving the appeal. 
22.5 Notification: The Academic Registrar will advise the Student and Student Administration in 
writing of the determination, in accordance with the requirements for notification set out in 
section 6.5 of this policy. 
22.6 Further appeal: The decision of the Academic Registrar is final and not open to further internal 
appeal. However, a student who is not satisfied with the outcome of an appeal made against a 
decision to deny the remission or re-crediting of their HELP balance, or repay any tuition fees 
or student contribution amounts may apply to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal 
(https://www.art.gov.au/) within 28 days of being notified of the decision. 
