23.1 A Student may appeal the determination of the National Head of School, relevant Executive 
Director or School Discipline Committee to the University Discipline Committee, except  where 
the decision of the University Discipline Committee is final and there is no further internal right 
of appeal. 
23.2 Grounds for appeal: The Student may appeal on the grounds that show that the National Head 
of School, relevant Executive Director or School Discipline Committee failed to follow due 
process in accordance with the General Regulations, when determining the outcome of 
misconduct. 
23.3 Timing for lodging appeal: The Student must lodge the appeal within 10 Working Days of the 
date the Student received notice of the National Head of School, relevant Executive Director or 
School Discipline Committee decision the Chair, University Discipline Committee. The Chair, 
University Discipline Committee may extend the time for lodging the appeal in exceptional 
circumstances. 
23.4 Timing for University review of appeal: The Chair of the University Discipline Committee must 
convene a hearing of the University Discipline Committee and determine the matter within 20 
Working Days of receipt of the appeal. 
23.5 Notification: The Chair of the University Discipline Committee will advise the Student, National 
Head of School, Student Administration and other staff as required in writing of the 
determination, in accordance with the requirements for notification set out in section 6.5 of 
this policy. 
23.6 Further appeal: The decision of the University Discipline Committee is final and not open to 
further internal appeal. 
24 MISCONDUCT - UNIVERSITY DISCIPLINE COMMITTEE 
 
24.1 A Student may appeal the decision of the University Discipline Committee to the Student 
Misconduct Appeals Committee in accordance with the General Regulations 
24.2 Grounds for appeal: The Student may only appeal on the following grounds: 
24.2.1 the University Discipline Committee failed to comply with Procedural Fairness; 
24.2.2 the Student has evidence relating to the allegation that was not reasonably available at 
the time of the University Discipline Committee hearing and that, if available, may have 
reasonably affected the decision of the University Discipline Committee or the penalty 
imposed; 
24.2.3 the penalty imposed was excessive. 
24.3 Timing for lodging appeal 
24.3.1 Domestic Students: The Student must lodge the appeal within 10 Working Days of the 
date the Student received notice of the University Discipline Committee decision. The 
Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic, may extend the time for lodging the appeal in 
exceptional circumstances. 
24.3.2 International Students: The student must lodge the appeal within 10 Working Days of 
the date the Student received notice of the University Discipline Committee decision. If 
the decision is to defer, suspend or cancel an international student’s enrolment, the 
student must lodge the appeal within 20 working days of the date they received notice 
of the University Discipline Committee decision. The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic, 
