25 OUTCOME OF HIGHER DEGREE BY RESEARCH THESIS EXAMINATION 
 
25.1 A Student may appeal the outcome of a thesis examination. 
25.2 Grounds for appeal: The Student may only appeal against a decision relating to a thesis 
examination on procedural grounds, in accordance with the Procedure: Higher Degree by 
Research Candidature. 
25.3 Timing for lodging appeal: The Student must lodge the appeal within 10 Working Days of the 
25.4 date the Student received written notification of the outcome of their thesis examination. The 
time for lodging the appeal may be extended in exceptional circumstances. 
25.5 Timing for University review of appeal: The appeal will be reviewed and determined within 
20 Working Days of the appeal being received. 
25.6 Notification: The Student, and Director, Research Services will be advised in writing of the 
determination, in accordance with the requirements for notification set out in section 6.5 of 
this policy. 
25.7 Further appeal: The decision is final and not open to further internal appeal. 
26 TERMINATION OF HIGHER DEGREE BY RESEARCH CANDIDATURE 
 
26.1 A Student may appeal the decision to terminate candidature to the Deputy Vice Chancellor, 
Academic. 
26.2 Grounds for appeal: A Student may only appeal a decision to terminate candidature on 
procedural grounds in accordance with the Procedure: Higher Degree by Research Candidature. 
26.3 Timing for lodging appeal: 
26.3.1 Domestic Students must lodge the appeal within 10 Working Days of the date the 
Student received notice of termination of candidature. The Deputy Vice Chancellor, 
Academic may extend the time for lodging the appeal in exceptional circumstances. 
26.3.2 International Students must lodge the appeal within 20 Working Days of the date the 
Student received notice of termination of candidature. The Deputy Vice Chancellor, 
Academic may extend the time for lodging the appeal in exceptional circumstances. 
26.4 Timing for University review of appeal: The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic will review and 
