27 RESEARCH TRAINING PROGRAM (RTP) SCHOLARSHIPS 
 
27.1 A Student may appeal the denial of an RTP scholarship, to the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic. 
27.2 Grounds for an appeal: A Student may only appeal a denial of an RTP scholarship on the 
grounds of failure to follow due process in accordance with the Guideline: Application and 
Assessment Processes for Higher Degree by Research Scholarships. 
27.3 Timing for lodging appeal: The Student must lodge the appeal within 10 Working Days of the 
date the Student received written notification of their RTP scholarship application being 
unsuccessful. The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic may extend the time for lodging the appeal 
in exceptional circumstances. 
27.4 Timing for University review of appeal: The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic  will review and 
determine the appeal within 20 Working Days of receiving the appeal. 
27.5 Notification: The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic will advise the Student, and the Director, 
Research Office in writing of the determination, in accordance with the requirements for 
notification set out in section 6.5 of this policy. 
27.6 Further appeal: The decision of the Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic is final and  not open to 
further internal appeal. 
28 INTERNATIONAL STUDENT TRANSFER 
 
28.1 An International Student may appeal the decision of Student Administration to deny a transfer 
(Letter of Release), to the Academic Registrar. 
28.2 Grounds for appeal: The Student may only appeal on the grounds that Student Administration 
failed to take mitigating circumstances into account. 
28.3 Timing for lodging appeal: The Student must lodge the appeal within 20 Working Days of the 
date the Student received notice of Student Administration’s decision. The Academic Registrar 
may extend the time for lodging the appeal in exceptional circumstances. 
28.4 Timing for University review of appeal: The Academic Registrar will review and determine the 
appeal within 20 Working Days of receiving the appeal. 
28.5 Notification: The Academic Registrar will advise the Student and Student Administration in 
writing of the determination, in accordance with the requirements for notification set out in 
section 6.5 of this policy. 
28.6 Further appeal: The decision of the Academic Registrar is final and not open to further internal 
appeal. 
