29 REASONABLE ADJUSTMENTS FOR STUDENTS WITH A DISABILITY 
 
29.1 A Student with a disability may appeal a decision of Student Administration to deny requested 
reasonable adjustments to the Academic Registrar. 
29.2 Grounds for appeal: The Student may only appeal against the decision of Student 
Administration regarding reasonable adjustments, including the provision of equipment and 
services in accordance with the Procedure: Assessment and Learning Flexibility. 
29.3 Timing for lodging appeal: The Student must lodge the appeal within 10 Working Days of the 
date the Student received notice of Student Administration’s decision. 
29.4 Timing for University review of appeal: The Academic Registrar will review and determine the 
appeal within 20 Working Days of receiving the appeal. 
29.5 Notification: The Academic Registrar will advise the Student and Student Administration in 
writing of the determination, in accordance with the requirements for notification set out in 
section 6.5 of this policy. 
29.6 Further appeal: The decision of the Academic Registrar is final and not open to further internal 
appeal.  
