6 
STANDARDS TO BE OBSERVED 
6.1 
Once a Student enrols in the University, he or she is expected to observe the following 
obligations: 
6.1.1 
Observe and be familiar with all Rules and Regulations concerning  their conduct that 
are in force and may be amended from time to time, in particular any obligations 
placed on them in the following: 
(a) Statutes of the University; 
(b) Rules, Regulations and By-Laws of the University; 
(c) Code of Conduct of the University; 
(d) Policies and Procedures of the University. 
 
6.1.2 
Comply with all laws of the State and Commonwealth including local by-laws. 
 
6.1.3 
Conduct themselves at all times in a manner that is courteous and respects the rights 
and reputations of students, staff and visitors to the University. 
 
6.1.4 
Do not engage in any scandalous behavior. 
 
6.1.5 
Avoid behaviour that could be perceived as harassment, intimidation, discrimination 
on any basis, bullying or threatening in any other way. 
 
6.1.6 
Carry out their academic studies conscientiously and with honesty and diligence and 
maintain satisfactory academic progress. 
 
6.1.7 
Attend classes (lectures, tutorials, seminars and practical work) and examinations. 
 
6.1.8 
Submit original work and abide by deadlines when submitting work for assessment. 
 
6.1.9 
Be familiar with enrolment status and deadlines for withdrawal of subjects and 
payment and liability for enrolment fees. 
 
6.1.10 Conduct themselves in a safe, orderly and proper manner in any class or library or 
other University facility so as not to affect the working environment of others or 
cause injury or harm to any other person. 
 
6.1.11 Not use any form of physical violence or any act which may cause serious personal 
injury to another. 
 
6.1.12 
Use University facilities, resources and information in a proper manner. 
