7.3 
If, upon investigation, those responsible for conducting the investigation form the opinion that 
the allegation was made maliciously or with intent to harm the student to whom the 
allegation was made against or for some other reason was not made in good faith, the 
allegation itself may give rise to a breach of this Code by the student who made the allegation. 
 
7.4 
The University may initiate disciplinary action against any student responsible for making a 
malicious or harmful allegation.  
 
7.5 
If a student or staff member is unsure about how to commence the process for allegations that 
a student has breached the Code of Conduct he or she should contact the Manager, Registrar’s 
