1 
OBJECTS OF THE UNIVERSITY 
 
 
1.1 
The University's Objects are defined in Section 5 of its Act of Parliament: The Objects of the 
University are: 
(a) 
the provision of university education, within a context of Catholic faith and values; and 
(b) 
the provision of an excellent standard of - 
i. 
teaching, scholarship and research; 
ii. 
training for the professions; and 
iii. pastoral care for its students. 
 
2 
INTRODUCTION 
 
 
2.1 
In accordance with s16 and s17 of the University of Notre Dame (UNDA) Act (1989), the Vice 
Chancellor has been delegated certain powers and duties by the Board of Directors. In 
accordance with Statute 22, the Vice Chancellor has further delegated some of these powers 
and duties.  
2.2 
This Policy constitutes the principal instrument through which those powers and duties are 
exercised and recorded. Where required, these have been endorsed by the Board of Directors in 
accordance with s16 of the Act. The Vice Chancellor retains all powers and authorities except 
those expressly delegated. 
2.3 
The delegations in this Policy supersede and revoke all previous delegations to the extent that 
they are inconsistent with those previous delegations, but nothing in this Policy has the effect 
of invalidating past acts validly performed by Delegates under any previous delegations. 
 
3 
PURPOSE 
 
 
3.1 
This Policy: Standing Delegations of Authority is intended to be the primary source of the 
functions, duties and powers which the Vice Chancellor has authorised particular bodies and 
officers of the University to carry out regularly.  
3.2 
This Policy also provides a clear and structured framework for the exercise of delegated 
authority across the University. However, it is not an exclusive statement of all delegated 
authority. Other sources of delegated authority are found in: 
3.2.1 The Statutes of the University; 
3.2.2 The General Regulations of the University; 
3.2.3 Responsibilities listed in Policies, Procedures and Guidelines of the University; 
3.2.4 The Register: Academic Delegations; 
3.2.5 The functions and duties set out in an individual’s Duty Statement or in a Committee’s 
Terms of Reference/Charter; and 
3.2.6 Specific written delegations. 
