3.3 
To the extent of any inconsistency: 
3.3.1 The Statutes prevail over the delegations in this Policy ; 
3.3.2 The General Regulations prevail over the delegations in this Policy ; 
3.3.3 Specific written delegations executed after the date of this Policy  prevail over the 
delegations contained in this Policy. 
 
4 
SCOPE 
 
 
4.1 
This Policy is applicable to all the University’s operations. 
4.2 
This Policy applies to all Staff and to any other person engaged by the University to the extent 
that they are subject to the University’s governance framework. Delegated authority may only 
be exercised by a Staff member or office holder where expressly authorised in writing by the 
Vice Chancellor. 
 
5 
GENERAL PRINCIPLES 
 
 
5.1 
The following principles apply to any delegated authority: 
5.1.1 Delegated authority may not be exercised by a person who is not a staff member of the 
University, unless the instrument of delegation, agreement or contract executed by the 
Vice Chancellor expressly states that such delegation may be exercised by a contractor 
or other person who is not a staff member. 
5.1.2 In exercising any delegation, a Delegate must act in the interests of the University, for 
the purpose delegated and not for any improper purpose. Nothing in this Policy 
authorises a Delegate to do anything which is, or is likely to be, a breach of any applicable 
law, enterprise agreement or of the Employee Code of Conduct and Ethical Behaviour. 
5.1.3 Authority delegated by the Vice Chancellor in this Policy cannot be further delegated 
except with the prior written permission of the Vice Chancellor. Any request for further 
delegation made to the Vice Chancellor must be in writing, must not exceed the scope 
or conditions of the original delegation. 
5.1.4 In exercising any delegation, the Delegate must follow the approved policies, procedures 
and guidelines of the University (where applicable). 
5.1.5 Any delegation which provides a Delegate authority to incur expenditure must be 
exercised within the limits of the relevant approved budget or other approved source of 
funds. 
5.1.6 A Delegate must not exercise a delegation in order to approve a recommendation made 
either wholly or partly by the Delegate. 
5.1.7 A delegation relates to a Delegate’s position, not to the individual occupying the position. 
An authority delegated under these Standing Delegations of Authority extends to: 
5.1.7.1 Any person acting officially in a Delegate’s position on an approved temporary 
basis (unless otherwise specified in the appointment to act); and 
5.1.7.2 The Delegate’s manager or other more senior staff member, where that manager 
or senior staff member has responsibility for the Delegate’s Accountability Area. 
