DEFINITIONS 
 
 
8.1 
For the purpose of this Policy, the following definitions apply: 
8.1.1 Academic Leader/Academic Leadership Position means all positions of Executive Dean, 
National Head of School or Director of an Academic or Research Centre or Institute. 
8.1.2 Academic Staff means academic staff of the University, including teaching staff and 
research academic staff, research focused and teaching focused academic staff and any 
other classes of academic staff as listed in Schedules A, B or E of The University of Notre 
Dame Australia Enterprise Agreement 2022-2026 (the EA), including those staff engaged 
as sessional and casual employees. 
8.1.3 Accountability Area means an organisational unit (such as an Academic school, division, 
department, or office), for which a Delegate is responsible according to a duty statement 
and/or employment contract, or carries fiscal responsibility. 
8.1.4 Adjunct means a title conferred on persons of standing in their profession or field of 
expertise whose association with the University will contribute to the teaching, research, 
scholarship, professional activities, or creative work of the University. 
8.1.5 Admissions Manager means the National Director of Admissions and National Manager 
of Admissions. 
8.1.6 Agreement means a document between one or more parties that creates a legal 
commitment or a legally enforceable agreement. 
8.1.7 Approved Supplier means a supplier who has been pre-approved by the CFO (or 
delegate) to provide goods and/or services under agreed terms and conditions. 
