8.1.8 Assoc DVC A and Acad Reg means Associate Deputy Vice Chancellor Academic and 
Academic Registrar. 
8.1.9 Budget Sums: Funds available for an activity within a project. 
8.1.10 Business Case means the University approved Business Case (form and process). 
8.1.11 Campus Development: means built environment projects (physical infrastructure, 
property and buildings) and does not include IT systems. 
8.1.12 Casual means a professional staff member who is engaged and paid on an hourly rate. 
8.1.13 CFO means Chief Financial Officer.  
8.1.14 CIO means Chief Information Officer.  
8.1.15 COO means Chief Operating Officer.  
8.1.16 CPO means Chief People Officer. 
8.1.17 CPFO means Chief Property and Facilities Officer. 
8.1.18 Contingency Sum: Funds provided within the Project Budget for unforeseen costs 
required to achieve approved project scope. 
8.1.19 Corporate Card Holder means a University representative issued with a University 
corporate credit card. 
8.1.20 DCFO means Deputy Chief Financial Officer 
8.1.21 Delegate means a staff member, or Committee or any other person or entity to whom 
or to which a delegation has been made by the Vice Chancellor in these Delegations of 
Authority. 
8.1.22 Dir means all positions of Director. 
8.1.23 Dir PS means Director, People Services 
8.1.24 Director of Centre or Institute means all Directors of UNDA Research Institutes or 
Centres. 
8.1.25 Policy means the Policy: Standing Delegations of Authority, including Schedules A to F. 
8.1.26 DVC means all positions of Deputy Vice Chancellor. 
8.1.27 DVC RP&I means Deputy Vice Chancellor, Research, Partnerships and International. 
8.1.28 DVC F and COO means Deputy Vice Chancellor, Finance and Chief Operating Officer  
8.1.29 DVC A means Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic 
8.1.30 EA means The University of Notre Dame Australia Enterprise Agreement 2022-2026 (or 
any replacement Agreement). 
8.1.31 ELICOS means component courses offered in accordance with the English Language 
Intensive Courses for Overseas Students (ELICOS) National Standards. 
8.1.32 Enabling Program means a program offered by the University for preparation for 
tertiary study. 
8.1.33 Exempt (non-standard) Staff means staff to whom the EA does not apply, including 
those with positions in Vocational Education and Training. 
8.1.34 FIC means the Finance and Investment Committee of the Board of Directors. 
8.1.35 Gift Register means the University’s Register of Gifts and Bequests. 
8.1.36 Manager means all positions of Manager. 
8.1.37 Memorandum of Understanding means a Memorandum of Understanding, and is a 
document between the University and one or more parties that expresses a common 
purpose or common course of action. It does not create a legal commitment or a legally 
enforceable agreement. 
8.1.38 Operating Budget is a combination of the University’s known expenses, expected future 
costs, and forecast income and expenditure over the course of a year as agreed by the 
Board in respect of each year. It does not include capital expenses. 
