8.1.39 PCG means Project Control Group, being the body appointed by the Board or Vice 
Chancellor to exercise responsibility for overseeing and supervising the delivery of a 
major project. 
8.1.40 Principal Officer has the same meaning as provided in the University Statutes, as 
amended from time to time. 
8.1.41 Professional Staff means employees of the University as defined in The University of 
Notre Dame Australia Enterprise Agreement 2022-2026 (or any replacement Agreement) 
and includes those who are not Academic staff and not Exempt Staff. 
8.1.42 Project Director means an officer, staff member or contractor of the University with 
responsibility for delivering a major capital works project. 
8.1.43 Project Budget: Total Funds committed to project including Contingency Funds. 
8.1.44 Project Design: Architectural design of building includes floor plans, elevations, finishes, 
fixtures and fittings. 
8.1.45 PVC means all positions of Pro Vice Chancellor. 
8.1.46 PVC C&E means Pro Vice Chancellor, Communications and Engagement. 
8.1.47 PVC E means Pro Vice Chancellor, Education. 
8.1.48 PVC En&N means Pro Vice Chancellor, Enabling and Nursing. 
8.1.49 PVC G&L means Pro Vice Chancellor, Governance and Legal and General Counsel. 
8.1.50 PVC I&C means Pro Vice Chancellor, Innovation and Communities. 
8.1.51 PVC R means Pro Vice Chancellor, Research. 
8.1.52 PVC R&M means Pro Vice Chancellor, Recruitment and Marketing. 
8.1.53 RPCI means the UNDA approved Research Project Chief Investigator on an externally 
funded research grant or contract. 
8.1.54 School means an academic organisational unit or equivalent budget unit. 
8.1.55 Senior Leaders means members of the Senior Management Group as amended from 
time to time, and additionally also includes National Director; Director; VET CEO; 
University Librarian and Academic Registrar. 
8.1.56 Sessional means an academic staff member who is engaged and paid on an hourly rate. 
Sponsorship means a commercial relationship between a donor and a recipient through 
which the donor receives a material benefit in return for making a financial or other 
commitment to the recipient. 
8.1.57 Superintendent: means consultant or University employee responsible for supervising a 
project. 
8.1.58 Supervisor/line manager means any person responsible for leading, managing or 
supervising the activities of others. 
8.1.59 University Logo, means the crest, shield and words which together form The University of 
Notre Dame Australia logo. 
8.1.60 University name means the words The University of Notre Dame Australia or Notre 
Dame. 
8.1.61 Uni Sec means the University Secretary. 
8.1.62 Uni Lib means the University Librarian. 
8.1.63 University Website means a website which is either owned or controlled by the 
University or located on a web domain owned or controlled by the University. 
8.1.64 VET means Vocational Education and Training. 
8.1.65 VET CEO means the position nominated to the Australian Skills Quality Authority as the 
Chief Executive Officer for the University’s Registered Training Organisation. 
8.1.66 VC means Vice Chancellor. 
 
