 Page 10 of 29 
 
SCHEDULE A: GENERAL DELEGATIONS 
 
 
GENERAL REQUIREMENTS 
 
 
1. This Schedule forms part of the Policy: Standing Delegations of Authority and must be read in conjunction with 
the Principles, Scope and Definitions applicable to all Schedules. 
2. Where the delegations contained in this Schedule refer to the execution of any contract or MOU, the authority 
to execute is subject to the agreement being first reviewed and approved by the authorised legal, 
procurement (as appropriate) and financial officers of the University, following due diligence processes in 
accordance with relevant policy and procedures. 
3. The delegations listed in this Schedule must be exercised in accordance with relevant legislation, industrial 
agreements, policies, procedures and guidelines and any written directives of the Vice Chancellor. 
4. All delegations listed in this Schedule are subject to the financial tolerances listed in Schedule B. 
5. Where the contract value exceeds the financial delegation of the listed delegate, the agreement must be 
escalated and executed by the next appropriate delegate according to the financial thresholds in Schedule B. 
6. All delegations listed in this Schedule are to be interpreted as the minimum level of delegation required. 
 
RECORDING AND REPORTING REQUIREMENTS 
 
 
1. All executed agreements should be filed with the portfolio of Governance and Legal. 
2. Executed MOUs relating to school or discipline matters must be filed within the relevant Faculty and a copy 
provided to the Associate Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic and Academic Registrar, and also to the Pro Vice 
Chancellor, Research where MOUs cover research matters. 
3. The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Research, Partnerships and International is responsible for providing an annual 
report to the Vice Chancellor in July each year on MOUs executed with any international partners. 
4. Formal policy documents (policies, procedures and guidelines) are stored in the University’s official policy 
repository. 
5. Formal records evidencing delegated actions and decisions, including supporting recommendations and 
advice, should be retained within minutes of relevant meetings and/or stored appropriately. 
 
