SCHEDULE C: ACADEMIC DELEGATIONS 
 
 
 
INTRODUCTION 
 
 
1. This Schedule forms part of the Policy: Standing Delegations of Authority and must be read in conjunction with 
the Principles, Scope and Definitions applicable to all Schedules. 
2. Academic powers, duties and responsibilities are delegated to various officers and committees of the 
University, primarily through two University instruments, namely: 
a. The Statutes of the University; and 
b. The General Regulations of the University. 
3. Underpinning both of these documents are University policies, procedures and guidelines (“policy 
documents”). 
4. This Schedule addresses those academic powers, duties and responsibilities that are not otherwise covered in 
the aforementioned documents. To the extent of any inconsistency, this Schedule will be overwritten by the 
Statutes, General Regulations. 
5. The Register: Academic Delegations provides a more detailed compilation of delegated authorities and 
responsibilities related to academic matters and should be read in conjunction with this Schedule. 
6. All delegations included in this Schedule are to be interpreted as the minimum level of delegation required. 
 
RECORDING AND REPORTING REQUIREMENTS 
 
 
1. Formal records to evidence delegated actions and decisions, including supporting recommendations and advice, 
should be retained within minutes of relevant meetings and/or stored in the appropriate system or file. 
2. Where applicable, outcomes of decisions will be published on the University’s website and in relevant program 
and course publications. 
 
