SCHEDULE E: CAMPUS DEVELOPMENT 
 
 
 
GENERAL REQUIREMENTS 
 
 
1. This Schedule forms part of the Policy: Standing Delegations of Authority and must be read in conjunction 
with the Principles, Scope and Definitions applicable to all Schedules. In addition, terms relating exclusively 
to this Schedule are defined below. 
2. The delegations in this Schedule apply to all capital works projects that are funded by the central Capital 
Budget/Forecast. 
3. Where the delegations contained in this Schedule refer to the execution of any contract, the authority to 
execute is subject to the agreement being first reviewed and approved by the authorised legal and financial 
officers of the University. 
4. The delegations listed in this Schedule must be exercised in accordance with the relevant legislation, policies, 
procedures and guidelines and any directives of the Vice Chancellor. 
5. All delegations listed in this Schedule are to be interpreted as the minimum level of Delegation required. 
 
RECORDING AND REPORTING REQUIREMENTS 
 
 
1. Reports from CPFO or delegate are submitted to the Major Project Group /Operations Group as required to 
ensure effective oversight of implementation of the project (including monitoring of budgets and 
expenditure). 
2. The following information must be reported to the Operations Group: 
a. Project Budget, and any variations, including redirection of sums; 
b. Project Design, and any variations 
c. Project Scope, and any variations; 
d. suspension of works; 
e. management of Program, including extensions of time; 
f. 
Expenditure or commitment of funds;  
g. Contract management and administration, including contract variations, notice of default 
termination, release of guarantee and referral to arbitration; and 
h. Risk and mitigation measures. 
3. In the case of notice of default, suspension of works, referral to arbitration, termination of contract and 
release of guarantee, the CPFO or delegate must immediately notify the Legal Office. 
4. Formal records to evidence delegated actions and decisions, including supporting recommendations and 
meeting minutes of the relevant governance committees for the project must be maintained. 
 
 
 
