4.7 
All identified risks will be assigned an owner (Risk Owner) who is responsible for responding to 
risks in a manner that is appropriate to the nature of the risk, the resources available to manage 
the risk, the broader University objectives and priorities; and the University’s Risk Appetite. 
4.8 
Risks will be reviewed and monitored by the relevant Risk Owner on an ongoing basis. 
4.9 
The University’s assurance activity, including Internal Audit, assist in providing a systematic 
approach to evaluate and improve the effectiveness of the University's risk management, 
control and governance processes. 
5 
ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES 
5.1 
The Risk Management Policy places responsibility on all Staff across the University. 
5.2 
All Staff should: 
5.2.1 Be aware of the need for effective management of risk in the University’s operations 
and have a role to play in the identification and management of the risks",,verified,data\raw\Notre_Dame\Notre_Dame_Merged_Policies.pdf,df5bbc9ff79666d022c57a98bc8df7e52aa34589b98c21fae1873d874226e864
