control and governance processes. 
5 
ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES 
5.1 
The Risk Management Policy places responsibility on all Staff across the University. 
5.2 
All Staff should: 
5.2.1 Be aware of the need for effective management of risk in the University’s operations 
and have a role to play in the identification and management of the risks facing the 
functions and/or activities with which they are involved; and 
5.2.2 Familiarise themselves with the University’s Risk Management Policy and procedures 
that may apply from time to time. 
5.3 
Board of Directors oversees, monitors and approves systems of control, accountability, 
governance, planning and organisation, including policy relating to the assessment and 
managements of risk across the University.1 
5.4 
Audit and Risk Committee, in accordance with its Charter, oversees the University’s Risk 
Management framework having regard to the University’s risk profile describing all material 
risks facing the University and the Risk Appetite set by the Board of Directors. 
5.5 
Academic Council, in accordance with its Charter, oversees risks to the University’s academic 
activities and standards, and the effectiveness of strategies to mitigate identified risks. 
5.6 
Executive Management, under delegation by the Board of Directors, are responsible for: 
5.6.1 Ensuring that Risk Assessments are undertaken for their individual areas of 
responsibility and overall for the University; 
5.6.2 Ensuring Risk Registers reflect identified risks existing controls, proposed Risk 
Treatments and Risk Owners and are kept updated;  
5.6.3 Providing updates on the status of Risk Treatments; 
5.6.4 Championing the roll out of the Risk Management framework into the University’s 
operations; and 
5.6.5 Developing a risk aware culture within their areas of responsibility. 
5.7 
University Academic Quality & Standards Committee, a subcommittee of Academic Council, 
in accordance with its Charter, is responsible for monitoring academic risk management 
processes, including the identification, assessment and evaluation of Academic Risks, and the 
effectiveness of relevant risk controls and Risk Treatments. 
5.8 
Pro Vice Chancellor, Governance and Legal is responsible for overseeing reporting on an 
 
