Communication seeks to support the understanding and awareness of risk.  Consultation 
includes collecting feedback and information to support decision making. 
3.2 
Establishment of Context defines the external and internal operating environment and 
describes how this impacts on the University’s operations. This is the first step in the Risk 
Management process. 
3.3 
Risk Assessment involves identifying risks that may impact on the capacity to achieve the 
University’s Objects and strategic goals (or a particular area’s purpose and priorities); and 
analysing and evaluating the nature and level of those risks. 
3.4 
Risk Treatment - determining the appropriate actions to be taken to mitigate the risk, 
nominating a Risk Owner that is accountable for ensuring that the mitigation actions are 
undertaken, and recording this information together with the monitoring frequency and 
associated responsibility in the relevant Risk Register. 
3.5 
Monitoring and Reviewing entails ongoing monitoring and periodic review of the Risk 
Management process to assure and improve its quality and effectiveness. 
3.6 
Recording and Reporting includes recording the results and outcomes of the Risk Management 
process. Reporting is an important part of the University’s governance and management’s 
accountability to the Audit and Risk Committee, the Executive and key stakeholders. 
4 
ACADEMIC RISK MANAGEMENT 
4.1 
The Academic Risk Assessment is performed on an annual basis by the Deputy Vice Chancellor 
Academic, other members of Executive Management with institutional-level responsibilities for 
academic leadership, the Executive Deans, and the Chairs of Academic Council and Academic 
Council sub-committees. Relevant managers and staff are included as required. 
4.2 
The Academic Risk Assessment involves the identification and analysis of Academic Risks, as 
follows. This process is facilitated with assistance from the Director Risk & Assurance.  
4.2.1 Identification of Academic Risks through consideration of relevant Context (as per 
Section 3.2), and relevant priorities, operations and strategies. This includes 
consideration of: 
4.2.1.1 the Higher Education Standards Framework (Threshold Standards) 2021; 
4.2.1.2 the National Code of Practice for Providers of Education and Training to 
Overseas Students 2018; and 
4.2.1.3 compliance priorities and sector risks identified by the Tertiary Education 
Quality and Standards Agency; 
4.2.2 Identified Risks are profiled to consider each Risk’s potential Causes and Consequences, 
and their existing Controls; 
4.2.3 In view of each Risk’s profile, they are analysed to rate: 
4.2.3.1 The Likelihood/Probability of their occurring, based on the descriptors in 
Appendix A; and 
4.2.3.2 The Consequence/Impact if they were to occur, based on the descriptors in 
Appendix B; 
