4.2.6 The results of the Academic Risk Assessment are documented in the Academic Risk 
Register. 
4.3 
With the support of the Director Quality & Risk, Curriculum and Quality, the Deputy Vice 
Chancellor Academic (or delegate) facilitates the University Academic Quality & Standards 
Committee’s endorsement of the Academic Risk Assessment prior to approval by Academic 
Council.  
4.4 
Risk Owners develop and action Treatment Plans for each Academic Risk as appropriate.  
4.4.1 A Risk Treatment Plan is required for all Academic Risks with a rating of ‘High’ or above. 
4.4.2 Academic Risk Treatment Plans may be incorporated into business or strategic planning 
as appropriate, and monitored accordingly. 
4.4.3 The status of Academic Risk Treatment Plan actions should be monitored by Risk Owners 
on a regular basis. With the support of the Director Quality & Risk, Curriculum and 
Quality, the Deputy Vice Chancellor Academic reports on this to the University Academic 
Quality & Standards Committee. 
4.5 
Results of the Academic Risk Assessment inform the University Material Risks (refer Section 6). 
5 
OPERATIONAL RISK MANAGEMENT 
5.1 
Operational Risk Assessments are performed on an annual basis by each member of Executive 
Management responsible for the University’s operational portfolios, such as Finance, 
Information Technology, Facilities, People & Culture, and Communications. Relevant managers 
and staff are included as required. 
5.2 
Each Operational Risk Assessment involves the identification and analysis of Risks, as follows. 
This process is facilitated with assistance from the Director Risk & Assurance. 
5.2.1 Identification of Risks through consideration of relevant Context (as per Section 3.2), 
and relevant priorities, operations and strategies;  
5.2.2 Identified Risks are profiled to consider each Risk’s potential Causes and Consequences, 
and their existing Controls; 
5.2.3 In view of each Risk’s profile, they are analysed to rate: 
5.2.3.1 The Likelihood/Probability of their occurring, based on the descriptors in 
Appendix A; and 
5.2.3.2 The Consequence/Impact if they were to occur, based on the descriptors 
Appendix B; 
5.2.4 Each Risk receives an overall rating in line with the University’s Risk Matrix, in 
accordance with Appendix C; and 
5.2.5 Each Risk is assigned a Risk Owner, being the person with accountability and authority 
