6 
UNIVERSITY MATERIAL RISK MANAGEMENT 
6.1 
On an annual basis, the University Material Risk Assessment is undertaken by the Vice 
Chancellor, Executive Management and the Audit and Risk Committee on behalf of the Board.  
6.2 
The University Material Risk Assessment involves the identification and analysis of University 
Material Risks, as follows. This process is facilitated with assistance from the Director Risk & 
Assurance. 
6.2.1 Identification of University Material Risks through consideration of relevant Context (as 
per Section 3.2), results of the Academic Risk Assessment, Operational Risk 
Assessments, University priorities, operations and strategies; 
6.2.2 Identified University Material Risks are profiled to consider each University Material 
Risk’s potential Causes and Consequences, and their existing Controls; 
6.2.3 In view of each University Material Risk’s profile, they are analysed to rate: 
6.2.3.1 The Likelihood/Probability of their occurring, based on the descriptors in 
Appendix A; and 
6.2.3.2 The Consequence/Impact if they were to occur, based on the descriptors in 
Appendix B; 
6.2.4 Each University Material Risk receives an overall rating in line with the University’s Risk 
Matrix, in accordance with Appendix C; and 
6.2.5 Each University Material Risk is assigned a Risk Owner, being the Executive with 
accountability and authority to manage the University Material Risk. 
6.2.6 The results of the University Material Risk Assessment are documented in the University 
Material Risk Register. 
6.3 
Input from the Audit and Risk Committee is sought in the finalisation of the University Material 
Risk Assessment.    
6.4 
Risk Owners develop and action Treatment Plans for each University Material Risk as 
appropriate.  
6.4.1 Risk Treatment Plans are required for all University Material Risks with a rating of ‘High’ 
or above. 
6.4.2 University Material Risk Treatment Plans may be incorporated into University business 
