Are student grievances confidential?
Student grievances are treated confidentially by the University. This means that, to the greatest
extent possible, information about your grievance will not be shared with other staff or students.
In some situations, the resolution process may require information about your grievance to be
shared. For example, if you submit a formal grievance involving a staff member, the staff member
will be informed about the grievance in sufficient detail to enable them to properly understand the
grievance and respond.
In general, any information that you provide to the Student Grievance Officer regarding your
grievance will be shared with as few people as possible, depending on the circumstances of your
