PROCESS SUMMARY: (VET) STUDENT APPEALS  
 
Process Step 
Responsibility  
 
 
Lodging an Appeal 
 
• An appeal should be lodged in writing as early as possible after 
notification of the decision, and within 20 working days to the Appeals 
and Conduct Officer. 
• Appeals should include all information required by the Form: (VET) 
Student Appeals, including the grounds for appeal and any relevant 
supporting documentary evidence  
• Advice and assistance on appeals processes is available from the Student 
Appeals and Conduct Officer fremantle.studentappeals@nd.edu.au. 
 
 
Student 
 
 
 
Student 
 
 
 
 
Notification of Appeal Outcome 
 
Notifications of the outcome of an appeal will be provided in writing and 
emailed to the Student’s Notre Dame student email address. 
 
 
Relevant Staff 
Member via 
Student Appeals 
and Conduct 
Officer 
 
 
External Appeals 
Should a Student wish to appeal a decision of the University’s appeals 
process: 
• Submit 
a 
written 
request 
to 
the 
Head 
of 
Campus 
via 
fremantle.studentappeals@nd.edu.au, within 20 working days from the 
date of receiving written notification of the outcome of their internal 
appeal.  
 
• Request acknowledged 
• Request forwarded to the External Reviewer 
• Any recommendations implemented 
• Copy of the decision provided to the Student and the Campus Registrar. 
 
 
 
 
Student 
 
 
 
 
Head of Campus, 
via Student 
Appeals and 
Conduct Officer 
 
 
