Page 4 of 14 
Effective Date: 13/10/2026 
3.2 
This Policy applies to all: 
3.2.1 employees of the University employed under fixed or maximum term contracts of 
employment whether employed on a full time or fractional basis 
3.2.2 sessional or casual employees of the University 
3.2.3 adjunct and visiting appointments 
3.2.4 students enrolled in any program or course at the University, and 
3.2.5 any other person or corporation who under a contract of service with the University is 
employed as a consultant or on secondment to the University. 
3.3 
Unless otherwise agreed by written agreement between the University and a person to who 
this Policy applies, the ownership of any Intellectual Property created by that person will be 
determined by the terms of this Policy 
3.4 
Commitments in an employee’s individual contract or any separate agreement executed 
between employees, students, a third party and the University for the purpose of dealing with 
Intellectual Property ownership will not be altered by any changes to the conditions in the 
Policy without the consent of those parties involved. 
3.5 
An Intellectual Property Agreement (IPA) between the University and any other party will 
govern the ownership and use of any Intellectual Property which may arise if there is an 
inconsistency between the IPA and this Policy. 
3.6 
If necessary for evidential purposes to satisfy third parties, including Intellectual Property 
Offices in Australia and other countries, the University shall execute confirmatory assignments 
of Intellectual Property with employees, students, adjuncts, visitors and Third Party Sponsors. 
4 INDIGENOUS CULTURAL AND INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY 
4.1 
The University acknowledges that Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander communities are the 
owners of their Indigenous Cultural and Intellectual Property (ICIP) and have an interest in 
protecting their ICIP from exploitation that is contrary to their customary laws. 
4.2 
The University will recognise, protect and respect both ICIP and the owners of ICIP.  
4.3 
The University acknowledges that ICIP may be incorporated in Research, Scholarly Works 
and/or Course Material and it will not assert ownership rights in any ICIP incorporated with said 
Research, Scholarly Works and/or Course Materials.   
4.4 
The University will take all reasonable steps, as is appropriate, to ensure that: 
4.4.1 ICIP is used for a purpose permitted by the owners of the ICIP with free, prior and 
informed consent and, if required, continued consent of its owners, on mutually agreed 
terms 
4.4.2 the ownership of the ICIP made available for use in Research or Course Materials is not 
affected by those uses 
4.4.3 ICIP is not used, obtained, appropriated, claimed or Commercialised without the prior 
approval of the ICIP owners, and 
4.4.4 owners of ICIP can expect that activities, projects and research conducted utilising their 
ICIP that contributes to the generation of new IP will be of benefit to Aboriginal and 
Torres Strait Islander communities, and that there is a fair and reasonable sharing, that 
will be negotiated, of any benefits arising from the use of such ICIP. 
