6 
INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY CREATED BY STUDENTS 
6.1 
Students retain ownership of any Intellectual Property they create in the course of their studies 
at the University, except where they have: 
6.1.1 used Substantial University Resources or University owned Intellectual Property in the 
creation of the work 
6.1.2 received project-specific funding from the University or a Third Party Sponsor 
contracted with the University 
6.1.3 used Intellectual Property owned by another employee of the University, 
6.1.4 created Intellectual Property at the request of a Placement Provider for the purposes of 
the Placement Provider during a placement attended by the student, or 
6.1.5 participated in a University Project.  
6.2 
Where a student's supervisor contributes to the student’s creation of Intellectual Property, it 
will be owned jointly by the student and the University, unless the product is a Scholarly Work, 
in which case the Intellectual Property will be owned jointly by the student and their supervisor. 
6.3 
Other than for Intellectual Property created under clause 6.1.4, where any exception under 
clause 6.1 applies to Intellectual Property created by a student in the course of their studies at 
the University the student must enter an IPA with the University that assigns ownership rights 
to any Intellectual Property arising out of a University Project to the University.  
6.4 
Where a student owns the Intellectual Property in a discovery or invention made in the course 
of their studies, the student and the University may agree to enter an IPA to commercially 
exploit that discovery or invention. 
6.5 
Unless otherwise agreed between a student and the University, a student will own the 
copyright in their Thesis. Students will, for research purposes only, make available a full text 
copy of their Thesis to the University Library. 
6.6 
Any Intellectual Property created as a result of a student’s participation in a University Project 
will be owned by the University. 
6.7 
A student involved in a University Project will generally be required to enter an IPA with the 
University before the project commences to assign any ownership rights to any Intellectual 
Property arising out of the University Project to the University. In these circumstances the 
student’s supervisor must ensure the student signs an IPA prior to the commencement of the 
University Project, and that informed consent of the student is obtained before signing the IPA 
6.8 
Where Intellectual Property is created by a student who has participated in a University Project 
and the student did not enter into an IPA prior to the commencement of the University Project 
