University, the provisions of the IPA prevail to the extent of any inconsistency between the IPA 
and this Policy. 
9 
NOTIFICATION OF INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY 
9.1 
Employees and students must notify Research Services in writing of any Intellectual Property 
they create if any of the following circumstances apply: 
9.1.1 ownership or use of the Intellectual Property is governed an IPA or some other third 
party agreement 
9.1.2 the Intellectual Property is a discovery or invention that is capable of patentability or 
some other form of legal protection 
9.1.3 the Intellectual Property may have the potential for commercial application, or 
9.1.4 the Intellectual Property has been created outside their course of employment or 
studies with the University and may be used in their work or studies at the University. 
9.2 
Employees and students must also notify Research Services of any pre-existing Intellectual 
Property that was developed before they commenced with the University and is likely to be 
relevant to their work or studies at the University. Notification of pre-existing Intellectual 
Property to be brought into the University must be made as soon as practicable upon 
commencing with the University. 
9.3 
Notification of Intellectual Property under clauses 9.1 and 9.2 must include as applicable, the 
following information:  
9.3.1 a description of the nature and operation of the Intellectual Property 
9.3.2 the date on which it the Intellectual Property was created 
9.3.3 the person or persons who contributed to creating the Intellectual Property 
9.3.4 details of any pre-existing Intellectual Property used in creating the Intellectual Property 
9.3.5 details of any University facilities or resources used to create the Intellectual Property  
9.3.6 whether any person other than the creator claims any entitlement or interest in the 
Intellectual Property 
9.3.7 details of any known existing use or commercial exploitation of the Intellectual Property 
9.3.8 whether the Intellectual Property is subject to any contract, licensing agreement or third 
party rights, and  
9.3.9 in the case of disclosures of pre-existing Intellectual Property to be brought into the 
University, documentation that establishes ownership of the Intellectual Property. 
9.4 
Employees and students must maintain adequate records and documentation relating to any 
Intellectual Property they create in accordance with Policy: Records Management Framework, 
and to ensure the University can appropriately assess, protect, use and commercialise the 
Intellectual Property.  
9.5 
Employees and students who notify Research Services of Intellectual Property they have 
created must ensure appropriate confidentiality is maintained prior to and during its initial 
assessment (refer to section 10). 
10 ASSESSMENT OF INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY 
10.1 Upon receiving notification from an employee or student about the creation of Intellectual 
Property, Research Services will inform the Deputy Vice Chancellor Research, Partnerships and 
