15 DISPUTE RESOLUTION 
15.1 If a dispute arises between an employee and the University under this Policy, the parties to the 
dispute will try in good faith to settle the dispute with the assistance in accordance with the 
Informal Procedure provided in the Policy: Employee Grievance Resolution. 
15.2 If a dispute arises between a student and the University under this Policy, the parties to the 
dispute will try in good faith to settle the dispute with the assistance in accordance with the 
Informal Procedure provided in the Procedure: Student Grievance. 
15.3 Where the dispute remains unresolved, or an aggrieved party is not an employee of the 
University then that party may seek assistance in resolving the dispute through an external 
agency for Dispute Resolution.  
16 BREACH OF POLICY 
16.1 This Policy applies to all employees and students. A breach of this Policy by employees will be 
considered as misconduct and the University may initiate disciplinary proceedings in 
accordance with the applicable industrial agreement. 
17 RESPONSIBLE OFFICER 
17.1 The Deputy Vice Chancellor Research, Partnerships and International is responsible for the 
