18.10 Policy: Records Management Framework 
19 DEFINITIONS  
For the purpose of this Policy, the following definitions apply: 
19.1 Commercialisation or commercial exploitation means any use or exploitation including, but 
not limited to, sub-licensing, franchising or assignment of Intellectual Property for the purpose 
of generating financial or some other commercial gain. 
19.2 Computer program means any literary work that is incorporated in, or associated with, a 
computer program, and is essential to the effective operation of a function of that computer 
program. 
19.3 Course Material means any material whether electronic, digital, written or any other form of 
media created by an employee specifically for use in, or in connection with a program, subject, 
course or microcredential offered by the University including but not limited to all: 
• lecture notes 
• lecture materials including course outlines, study guides and reading materials 
• audio-visual works 
• on-line material 
• assessment and examination questions, and 
• any other copyright works created by an employee for the purpose of teaching a program 
or course offered at the University.  
19.4 Indigenous Cultural and Intellectual Property or ICIP means Aboriginal and Torres Strait 
Islander peoples’ rights to their knowledge, heritage and culture, including all aspects of 
cultural practices, traditional knowledge and resources and knowledge systems developed by 
those Indigenous people as part of their Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander identity and 
includes:  
• literary, performing and artistic work 
• languages 
• types of knowledge, including spiritual knowledge 
• tangible and intangible cultural property 
• Indigenous ancestral remains and genetic material 
• cultural environmental resources 
• sites of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander significance, and/or 
• documentation of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander heritage. 
19.5  ‘In the course of their employment’ means any such duties of an employee set out in or 
incidental to their contract of employment with the University including involvement in a 
University Project. 
Intellectual Property has the meaning stated in clause 3.1. 
19.6 Intellectual Property Agreement or IPA means any written agreement entered into between 
an employee, student, or third party and the University which relates to the ownership and use 
of any form of Intellectual Property which may arise.  
19.7 Moral Rights has the meaning stated in clause 9.1. 
19.8 Net Revenue has the meaning stated in clause 14.2. 
