4.3.1 Industry standards are agreed-upon requirements and specifications that guide 
practices within a specific industry. These standards aim to improve quality, reduce 
risk, and ensure consistency. There are two main types of standards relevant to 
records management: 
4.3.1.1 
Government Information Standards – these standards are frameworks and 
guidelines that help organisations to manage and protect information 
effectively. It covers various aspects of information management, including 
classification, handling, and disposal of information. The standards and 
retention schedules that include: 
4.3.1.1.1 
State Records Principles and Standards 2002 (WA) 
4.3.1.1.2 
Standards on Records Management – Standard No. 15 (NSW) 
4.3.1.1.3 
Standard on the physical storage of State Records – Standard No. 
14 (NSW)  
