7 
DEFINITIONS  
7.1 
For the purpose of this Policy, the following definitions apply: 
A compliant recordkeeping system is a system that ensures the creation, capture, 
management, and disposal of records adhere to legal, regulatory, and organisational 
requirements throughout their lifecycle. Microsoft Outlook and network drives are not 
considered compliant recordkeeping systems for effectively capturing, storing, and managing 
business records. 
Contracted Supplier means a supplier who been contracted to provide a specific goods and/or 
service for a specified term, with agreed price, terms and conditions. 
Employee means an Academic Employee and/or a Professional Employee, as defined in the 
University of Notre Dame Staff Enterprise Agreement 2022-2026. 
Records are defined as any information, regardless of format, created, received, or 
maintained by the University for business, legal, administrative, or historical purposes. These 
include, but are not limited to, written documents, emails, electronic files, social media posts, 
and any other information that serves as evidence in the University’s business activities. 
 
