4 
GENERAL PRINCIPLES 
4.1 
The University will respond to any Grievance made by a student regarding their dealings with 
the University, the University’s education agents, or any related third party involved in the 
delivery of a program, course, or related services on behalf of the University. 
 
4.2 
Anonymous Grievances, or Grievances made on behalf of another student will not be 
considered.  
 
4.3 
All documentation must be provided to the responsible Grievance Officer by all parties. 
 
4.4 
 All students must be able to seek resolution of a Grievance free from fear of discrimination and 
victimisation. 
 
4.5 
Where possible, Grievances should be resolved informally at the Campus concerned.  However, 
the University may determine that because of the nature of the Grievance or those involved in 
the Grievance, it is more appropriate for the resolution procedure to be conducted at another 
Campus or location.   
 
4.6 
A Grievance may be dismissed or discontinued at any time if found to be frivolous, vexatious or 
result in abuse, harassment or victimisation to any person. 
 
4.7 
The student or any other party to a Grievance may be accompanied at any meeting or hearing 
by a support person. The support person: 
 
 
may not act as advocate; 
 
may not be a person who was, or may be perceived to be involved in, or associated with 
the Grievance; and 
 
must not be a legal practitioner unless permitted in writing by the University.  
 
4.8 
A student may withdraw a Grievance at any stage. 
 
4.9 
The time limits set out in this Procedure are to enable a swift and efficient resolution of 
Grievances. They may altered, varied or changed by the University for the purpose of properly 
considering the Grievance and with the consent of all parties. The Senior Officer or Campus 
Deputy Vice Chancellor may alter, vary or change the time limits on reasonable request from 
the parties or where he or she considers it necessary for the proper consideration of the 
Grievance. 
 
4.10 The Grievance may be suspended by the Senior Officer or Senior Staff member (eg PVC, NHOS, 
Executive Dean) if the Grievance raises an allegation of misconduct against a staff member. 
5 
PRELIMINARY ACTION 
5.1 
A student should first attempt to resolve a Grievance directly with the staff member or 
student concerned and as soon as possible after the Grievance occurs. 
 
