6.8 
If a resolution cannot be reached, the Senior Officer will provide either or both parties with a 
proposed resolution, including reasons for the resolution, in writing. Each party must either 
accept or decline the resolution within 5 working days of receipt. If both parties accept the 
resolution, the agreed course of action will be implemented immediately.  
 
6.9 
If the proposed resolution is not accepted, the Senior Officer will, within 5 working days of 
receiving notification of non-acceptance, notify the parties of the failure to reach a resolution 
and refer the Grievance to the appropriate Senior Staff Member of the relevant Campus. 
 
7 
REFERRING THE GRIEVANCE TO THE PRO VICE CHANCELLOR, STUDENT 
EXPERIENCE 
7.1 
A referral must include all documentation relating to the Grievance including an outline of the 
steps undertaken by the Senior Officer and the time frames in which these steps have been 
taken. 
 
7.2 
Within 5 working days of receiving the referral either the Senior Staff Member or their 
nominated staff member who is at a senior level to the Senior Officer (Nominee) should: 
 
 Notify the student in writing that he/she is considering the Grievance; and 
 Begin an independent review of the Grievance. 
 
7.3 
The Senior Staff Member or Nominee may inspect all the documentation relevant to the 
grievance and the resolution process, take statements and consult with or interview any 
student, staff member or third party that he or she regards as relevant to the resolution of the 
Grievance. 
 
7.4 
The Senior Staff Member or Nominee should complete the review within 20 working days from 
the date of appointment and may take any action to resolve the agreement, including but not 
limited to: 
 
 
referring the Grievance back to the Senior Officer for further action. 
 
making a final determination in respect of the Grievance which is the same or different 
to the determination/resolution proposal made by the Senior Officer. 
 
convening a committee to consider the Grievance and referring the Grievance to the 
Committee for investigation; or  
 
referring the Grievance to the Vice Chancellor. 
 
7.5 
The Senior Staff Member or Nominee should notify the student in writing of the decision and 
details of the reasons for the decision within 5 working days of it being made.  
7.5.1 The notification sent to the student will include the contact details of the appropriate 
complaints handling and external appeals body. (Refer to clause 10.1 of this procedure) 
7.5.2 Any decision in favour of the student will be implemented immediately. 
 
