1 
OBJECTS OF THE UNIVERSITY 
The University's Objects are defined in Section 5 of its Act of Parliament: 
 
The Objects of the University are: 
 
(a) the provision of university education, within a context of Catholic faith and values; and 
(b) the provision of an excellent standard of - 
i. 
teaching, scholarship and research 
ii. 
training for the professions, and 
iii. 
pastoral care for its students. 
2 
PURPOSE  
2.1 
This policy outlines principles and processes for institutional monitoring, review and 
improvement at the University of Notre Dame Australia (the University). 
3 
SCOPE 
3.1 
The scope of this policy includes monitoring, review and improvement of institutional 
performance relating to: 
3.1.1 achievement of the University’s Objects and strategic goals 
3.1.2 corporate and academic governance 
3.1.3 management of operations and service provision in academic areas, including schools, 
faculties, research institutes and centres, functional and professional support areas 
3.1.4 the integrity and quality of teaching, student learning, research, research training, and 
scholarship,  
3.1.5 compliance with standards for higher education and vocational education and training. 
4 
PRINCIPLES 
4.1 
Institutional reviews are a primary mechanism for self-assurance that support: 
4.1.1 a cycle of continuous improvement to the quality of student experiences and education 
and training outcomes, research and other services provided by the University, and 
4.1.2 ongoing compliance with the following: 
4.1.2.1 Higher Education Standards Framework (Threshold Standards) 2021  
4.1.2.2 Australian Qualifications Framework 
4.1.2.3 Australian Code of Conduct for the Responsible Conduct of Research 2018 
4.1.2.4 Education Services for Overseas Students Act 2000 
4.1.2.5 National Code of Practice for Registration Authorities and Providers of 
Education and Training to Overseas Students 
4.1.2.6 Standards for Registered Training Organisations (RTOs) 2015 
4.1.2.7 Higher Education Support Act 2003, and 
4.1.2.8 Higher Education Provider Guidelines 2023, and 
4.1.2.9 other legislative and regulatory obligations documented in the Legislative 
Compliance Register. 
