5.3 
Effective operation of governance committees 
5.3.1 Cyclical self-assessment and review of governance committees in accordance with 
charters. 
5.3.2 External periodic reviews of Board governance and academic governance. 
5.4 
Higher education program and course quality and standards 
5.4.1 Program review and re-accreditation, professional accreditation/registration, program 
monitoring and reporting processes. 
5.4.2 Assessment benchmarking, moderation and review. 
5.4.3 Monitoring and reporting on risks to academic integrity, including academic integrity 
breaches and strategies for risk mitigation. 
5.4.4 Peer review of teaching. 
5.4.5 Collection, reporting and response to student feedback, including student  teaching and 
course experience surveys. 
5.4.6 Collection, reporting and response to alumni, industry and employer feedback. 
5.4.7 Annual review and reporting on third party arrangements, including legal agreements, 
academic quality and student experiences.   
5.4.8 Review and reporting of education agent agreements and performance.  
5.5 
Student cohort outcomes – equity groups, Aboriginal and Torre Strait Islander peoples 
5.5.1 Monitoring and reporting on student participation, success and retention for identified 
cohorts, with respect to key performance indicators and institutional targets. 
5.6 
Student support and well-being 
5.6.1 Cyclical reporting and review of student support services to support student wellbeing 
and safety, including across equity groups. 
5.7 
Vocational education and training quality 
5.7.1 Vocational education and training quality assurance, including assessment validation 
and moderation and VET course review. 
5.7.2 Collection, reporting and response to feedback from students, industry and employers. 
5.8 
Legislative and regulatory compliance 
5.8.1 Internal self-assessments of compliance against the Threshold Standards, culminating in 
annual compliance statements considered by the Board of Directors. 
5.8.2 Annual self-assessments of the Standards for RTOs and Declaration on Compliance. 
5.8.3 Ongoing monitoring of legislative compliance obligations and annual statements 
provided on the management of significant legislative compliance obligations. 
5.9 
Catholic identity and mission 
5.9.1 Periodic external reviews of the University’s Catholic identity and mission. 
6 
ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES 
6.1 
Roles and responsibilities for institutional monitoring and review processes are outlined in the 
relevant policies and procedures, including those listed in clause 7 of this policy. 
