1 OBJECTS OF THE UNIVERSITY 
The University's Objects are defined in Section 5 of its Act of Parliament: 
 
The Objects of the University are: 
(a) the provision of university education, within a context of Catholic faith and values; and 
(b) the provision of an excellent standard of - 
i. 
teaching, scholarship and research; 
ii. 
training for the professions; and 
iii. 
pastoral care for its students. 
2 PURPOSE 
2.1 
The Policy: Academic Governance Framework sets out the broad principles, structures, systems 
and responsibilities for academic governance at the University of Notre Dame Australia (the 
University). 
3 DEFINITION AND ATTRIBUTES  
3.1 
For the purpose of this policy, academic governance refers to the framework of policies, 
processes, structures, delegated responsibilities and relationships that collectively support 
academic decisions and maintain effective oversight for the integrity and quality assurance of 
the University’s core higher education activities of teaching, learning, research (including 
research training) and scholarship. 
3.2 
Attributes of effective academic governance include: 
3.2.1 establishing and maintaining effective academic leadership and academic quality 
assurance 
3.2.2 monitoring compliance with legislative and regulatory obligations that apply to the 
University’s academic activities (refer to clause 4.2 below) 
3.2.3 ensuring the ongoing effectiveness of the University academic policies and procedures 
3.2.4 providing self-assurance for academic and research integrity, mitigation of academic 
risks, and delivering expected outcomes for students 
3.2.5 providing competent advice to the Board of Directors and Senior Management Group 
(SMG) on academic matters, including advice on academic outcomes, policies and 
practices, and 
3.2.6 ensuring that all qualifications awarded reflect the requirements within the Australian 
Qualifications Framework. 
4 ACADEMIC GOVERNANCE INSTRUMENTS 
4.1 
Academic governance takes account of provisions of key governance instruments of the 
University, including the following:  
4.1.1 University of Notre Dame Australia Act 1989  
4.1.2 Trustees Rules  
4.1.3 Board of Directors Governance Statement 
4.1.4 Statutes of The University of Notre Dame Australia (the Statutes) 
