4.2.9 Australian Code for the Responsible Conduct of Research, 2018, and 
4.2.10 external professional accreditation requirements and standards for programs and 
graduates. 
5 PRINCIPLES 
5.1 
The University’s academic governance framework ensures that: 
5.1.1 the requirements in Section 6.3 of the Higher Education Standards Framework 
(Threshold Standards) 2021 are met 
5.1.2 academic governance supports the achievement of the University’s strategic and 
operational objectives 
5.1.3 academic governance contributes to the identification and mitigation of academic risks 
and risks to the safety and wellbeing of students 
5.1.4 academic governance contributes to maintaining an institutional environment in which 
freedom of intellectual inquiry is upheld and protected 
5.1.5 there is effective communication between senior academic leaders and the Academic 
Council based on the collaboration and involvement of University executives and senior 
administrators on Academic Council and its subcommittees 
5.1.6 student voice is valued and students have opportunities to participate in academic 
governance decision making 
5.1.7 committees contributing to academic governance receive adequate support and 
resourcing to operate in accordance with their charters, including secretariat support 
for their operations 
5.1.8 the membership of academic governance committees reflect the diversity of the 
University community 
5.1.9 academic decision making is conducted openly, ethically and transparently in support 
of an inclusive University community  
5.1.10 clearly communicated procedures are followed for making, recording and publishing 
decisions about academic matters and disclosures of conflicts of interest in academic 
decision making 
5.1.11 decisions that require the exercise of academic judgement are made by staff who are 
qualified to make such judgements, and 
5.1.12 any delegation of decision-making authority to a subordinate academic body or 
