6.3 
To ensure institutional self-assurance is embedded in the University’s business-as-usual 
operations:  
6.3.1 roles, responsibilities and accountabilities for institutional monitoring, review and 
improvement of academic activities and requirements for reporting to academic 
governance committees are clearly documented in University policies and procedures, 
and 
6.3.2 Academic Council and Academic Council Sub-committee chairs maintain annual 
workplans that include key academic quality assurance reports and other information 
required for these committees to fulfil the duties and responsibilities as set out in their 
charters.  
6.4 
Ongoing assurance for the effectiveness of academic governance at the University is achieved 
through cyclical self-review and assessment of the performance of Academic Council, Academic 
Council sub-committees and faculty boards. 
6.5 
The University’s academic governance processes will be independently reviewed every five 
years. 
7 ACADEMIC GOVERNANCE COMMITEES OF THE UNIVERSITY 
7.1 
Academic Council 
7.1.1 Academic Council as the primary academic committee of the University (Statutes, S40), 
assists the Board of Directors by providing effective oversight of academic risk, 
monitoring assurance processes and policy to uphold standards, quality and excellence 
in teaching, learning, scholarship, research and research training, and providing 
competent advice to the Board of Directors on academic matters. 
7.2 
Academic Council sub-committees 
7.2.1 Academic Council has established the following Academic Council sub-committees 
under the authority delegated in the Statutes (40.9(i)) and section 3.3 of its Charter: 
7.2.1.1 University Learning and Teaching Committee 
7.2.1.2 University Programs and Courses Committee 
7.2.1.3 University Academic Quality and Standards Committee 
7.2.1.4 University Research Committee. 
7.2.2 Academic Council has oversight for the operation of Academic Council sub-committees 
through: 
7.2.2.1 confirmed minutes of sub-committee meetings tabled as standing agenda 
items for Academic Council meetings, and 
7.2.2.2 standing reports provided by each Academic Council sub-committee chair on 
the committee’s activities. 
7.3 
Academic Council and Academic Council sub-committee charters 
7.3.1 The academic governance functions of Academic Council and its committees are set out 
in their respective charters, including for: 
7.3.1.1 decision-making authority 
7.3.1.2 statement of purpose 
7.3.1.3 duties and responsibilities 
7.3.1.4 committee chair and deputy chair requirements 
7.3.1.5 membership composition and terms of office 
