7.3.1.6 quorum requirements 
7.3.1.7 meeting requirements, including frequency, scheduling, rules for the conduct 
of its business, managing conflicts of interest, and 
7.3.1.8 review requirements, including review of charters, self-review and assessment 
of its performance, and individual member contributions. 
7.3.2 The duties and responsibilities for Academic Council, its sub-committees and faculty 
boards are determined in accordance with each committee’s stated purpose and to 
ensure each committee functions to support the role of Academic Council in maintaining 
effective academic governance. (In accordance with clause 3.2 above.) 
7.4 
Faculty boards 
7.4.1 Faculty boards are established by the Statutes (s55) and their role is to: 
7.4.1.1 provide advice to the Executive Dean and Academic Council on issues relating 
to the faculty’s plans, academic risks and academic standards 
7.4.1.2 monitor, scrutinise and make recommendations on the performance and 
sustainability of the faculty’s profile of academic programs and courses 
7.4.1.3 make recommendations on:  
• 
new programs and courses to be delivered 
• 
matters related to teaching, scholarship and research 
• 
any matters relating to the content, teaching and examination of any of its 
programs and courses, and 
• 
provide advice on any matter referred to it for consideration. 
7.4.2 In accordance with the Statutes (s55.1) and the Faculty Boards Charter, faculty boards 
are responsible to Academic Council through the relevant executive dean. 
7.5 
Other University committees with academic advisory and decision-making authority 
7.5.1 In addition to Academic Council and its sub-committees, the following University 
committees provide academic advice and decision-making as set out in the Statutes 
(references to the Statutes are shown in parentheses), and as delegated in University 
policies and procedures (and recorded the Academic Delegations Register): 
7.5.1.1 Core Curriculum Committee (s39) 
7.5.1.2 Ethics Committee (s42) 
7.5.1.3 Student Board (s43) 
7.5.1.4 Boards of Examiners (ss56,57), and 
7.5.1.5 Faculty and/or School Advisory Boards (s58). 
7.5.2 The University Research Committee has also established the following sub-committees: 
7.5.2.1 Human Research Ethics Committee  
7.5.2.2 Research degree and Scholarships Committee 
7.6 
Refer to Attachment 1 for an overview of the relationships between the different committees 
involved in academic governance at the University. 
