8.2.1 The Vice Chancellor is the chief executive officer and principle academic officer of the 
University with duties set out in the Statutes (s20). 
 
8.3 
Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic 
8.3.1 The Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic, with the support of the Pro Vice Chancellor, 
Education and the Associate Deputy Vice Chancellor, Academic and Academic Registrar, 
provides leadership for the University’s learning and teaching strategy and institutional 
self-assurance and managing risks to quality and standards for: 
8.3.1.1 the design, delivery, accreditation, monitoring, review and improvement of the 
University’s programs, and maintaining academic integrity 
8.3.1.2 learning environments, facilities and resources 
8.3.1.3 student engagement, progression and retention 
8.3.1.4 student attainment, including achievement of learning outcomes and 
outcomes for employment and further study 
8.3.1.5 prevention and responding to threats to student learning and the integrity of 
qualifications awarded by the University due to contract cheating and the 
misuse of artificial intelligence 
8.3.1.6 maintaining student wellbeing and safety 
8.3.1.7 supporting scholarship and ensuring scholarly activities and outcomes inform 
teaching, learning, and professional practice and contribute to the 
advancement and dissemination of knowledge 
8.3.1.8 identifying and implementing good practices and advances in teaching and 
learning, and sharing practice with the higher education sector more broadly 
8.3.1.9 the breadth and depth of academic leadership and expertise to guide teaching, 
learning, and academic governance in the fields of education offered by the 
University, and 
8.3.1.10 engagement with employers, industry, and the professions. 
8.4 
Deputy Vice Chancellor, Research, Partnerships and International 
8.4.1 Deputy Vice Chancellor, Research, Partnerships and International provides leadership 
for institutional self-assurance and managing risks to quality and standards for: 
8.4.1.1 student recruitment and admission practices, including information for 
prospective students, guarding against non-genuine students, sufficiency of 
academic preparation and proficiency in English, credit and recognition of prior 
learning, monitoring student engagement, progression and retention to inform 
recruitment and admission practices 
8.4.1.2 monitoring education agent performance and recruitment practices 
8.4.1.3 partnerships with other providers for the delivery of programs and research 
training, and 
8.4.1.4 collaborative research partnerships. 
8.4.2 With the support of the Pro Vice Chancellor, Research, the Deputy Vice Chancellor, 
Research, Partnerships and International also provides leadership for the University’s 
research strategy and institutional self-assurance and managing risks to quality and 
standards for: 
8.4.2.1 monitoring review improvement of institutional research quality and 
performance, and the quality of research training and supervision 
8.4.2.2 maintaining a culture of research integrity and upholding responsible research 
