8.6 
Deputy Chairs of Academic Council 
8.6.1 Deputy Chairs of Academic Council are elected in accordance with the Academic Council 
Charter (Section 8) and has the following responsibilities: 
8.6.1.1 assisting the Chair of Academic Council in the performance of their functions 
as the Chair determines from time to time, and 
8.6.1.2 acting as the Chair of Academic Council during when the Chair is absent. 
8.7 
Chairs of Academic Council sub-committees 
8.7.1 The responsibilities of the Chair of each Academic Council sub-committee include:  
8.7.1.1 providing leadership to the committee and fostering active involvement of 
members in in the committee's work 
8.7.1.2 planning and chairing committee meetings effectively 
8.7.1.3 maintaining an annual plan of work that identifies key reports and other 
information required by the committee to discharge its duties and 
responsibilities 
8.7.1.4 following up on actions or resolutions of the committee 
8.7.1.5 engaging the committee in assessing and improving its performance 
8.7.1.6 overseeing the induction and development of new committee members, and 
8.7.1.7 reporting to Academic Council on matters relating to committee duties, 
responsibilities, authority and decisions, emerging priorities for the 
committee, and subcommittee performance. 
8.8 
University Secretary 
8.8.1 The responsibilities of the University Secretary, include: 
8.8.1.1 advising the Chair of Academic Council on the requirements of the Academic 
Governance Framework, University regulations, policies and procedures 
pertaining to the functions of Academic Council and its sub-committees 
8.8.1.2 ensuring Academic Council and Academic Council sub-committee business and 
secretariat services are effectively managed, including for the completion and 
distribution of committee agenda, and maintaining meeting records, and 
8.8.1.3 overseeing election processes and acting as the Returning Officer for elected 
academic staff appointments to Academic Council and faculty boards, in 
accordance with the Academic Council Election Regulations. 
8.9 
Other academic leadership roles 
8.9.1 The following academic leadership roles have delegated academic decision-making 
authority set out in academic policies and procedures and recorded in the Academic 
Delegations Register: 
8.9.1.1 Academic Registrar 
8.9.1.2 Executive deans 
8.9.1.3 Associate deans, research 
