ATTACHMENT 1. COMMITTEES INVOLVED IN ACADEMIC GOVERNANCE 
Academic Council, Ethics Committee, Student Board and Core Curriculum Committee are established in the 
Statues (s38) as standing committees of the University. Academic Council, Ethics Committee, and Student 
Board report to the Board of Directors through the Vice Chancellor.  In addition, the Chair of Academic Council 
attends each Board meeting. The Core Curriculum Committee reports to the Board of Trustees through the 
Vice Chancellor. 
Senior Management Group is a standing committee of the University and is responsible to the Vice Chancellor 
(Statutes, s41).   
University Learning and Teaching Committee, University Programs and Courses Committee, University 
Academic Quality and Standards Committee, and University Research Committee are established as Academic 
Council sub-committees by Academic Council under its authority in the Statutes (40.9).  Each sub-committee 
reports on its activities in accordance with their charters to Academic Council. 
Faculty boards are established by the Statutes (s55) and report on their activities in accordance with their 
charters to Academic Council. 
 
 
 
