1 
PURPOSE 
1.1 
This Guideline supports the University’s commitment to excellence in Transformative 
Research: addressing real world challenges, improving the lives of people in our 
communities, and impacting society for the common good.  
1.2 
This Guideline sets out the criteria for authorship, peer review and dissemination of 
research, and processes to be followed in: 
1.2.1 appointing and reporting authors of all research outputs; 
1.2.2 attributing authorship in other documents related to research, including (but not 
limited to) grant applications, contracts, and tenders; 
1.2.3 ensuring appropriate peer review of research outputs; 
1.2.4 publishing and promoting research outputs.  
1.3 
The Guideline applies where research outputs and other research related documents are 
disseminated and/or made publicly available, including but not limited to journal articles, 
book chapters, books, conference papers, research reports, performances or exhibitions, 
project reports, grant applications and curriculum vitae’s. These may be in hardcopy, 
electronic or other form. 
