5 
INFORMATION ABOUT PROGRAMS WITH PROFESSIONAL 
ACCREDITATION REQUIREMENTS 
5.1 
Where a program or program component is accredited by a professional accrediting agency 
this must be clearly and accurately indicated in the program requirements and in any 
information about the program published in online or print formats. 
5.1.1 Where an individual course is accredited by a professional accrediting agency, this 
must be indicated in the Course Outline. 
5.2 
Programs must not be advertised as professionally accredited until accreditation has been 
granted by the accrediting agency. 
5.2.1 Where professional accreditation of a program is in progress, its accreditation status 
may only be advertised as pending when the following conditions have been met: 
5.2.1.1 an application for program accreditation has been submitted to the 
accrediting agency and the accrediting agency has acknowledged they have 
received the application 
5.2.1.2 the accrediting agency has confirmed the program can be advertised with 
professional accreditation pending while the accreditation decision is in 
progress 
5.2.1.3 any conditions or information requirements set by the accrediting agency 
have been met, and 
5.2.1.4 the professional accreditation status is indicated as pending in the program 
requirements and in any program information published in online or print 
formats. 
5.2.2 Where a program or program component is provisionally accredited by a professional 
accrediting agency, this provisional status and the implications of this status must be 
clearly communicated in all information intended for prospective and current students. 
6 
COURSE OUTLINES 
6.1 
A course outline provides the information students enrolled in the course need to complete it 
successfully. 
6.2 
A course coordinator will provide a course outline for each delivery of any course they 
coordinate other than: 
6.2.1 courses in VET programs 
6.2.2 courses to record students’ enrolments in research components of higher degree by 
research programs, and 
6.2.3 courses with no credit points weighting in which students are enrolled for an 
administrative purpose. 
6.3 
When drafting or updating a course outline for any course, the course coordinator will use the 
University’s course outline template and follow the instructions in the template. 
