11.1.5.4 the phrase ‘for example’ or ‘such as’ followed by a single instance or list, the 
instance or list is not exhaustive 
11.1.5.5 the phrases ‘described in’, ‘set out in’, ‘specified in’ or ‘stated in’, it will be 
read as if the words ‘expressly or impliedly’ appeared immediately before 
them; 
11.1.5.6 the singular, it also means the plural, and vice versa 
11.1.5.7 any gender, it includes the other genders, and 
11.1.5.8 a reference to a statute, ordinance, code or other law, it includes regulation, 
by-laws, rules and other statutory instruments under it for the time being in 
force and consolidations, amendments, re-enactments, or replacements of 
any of them. 
11.2 Definitions 
11.2.1 The definitions section of the Policy: Programs and Courses defines many of the terms 
used in this procedure.  
11.2.2 The following additional terms have the meanings stated below. 
11.2.2.1 Hurdle assessment task has the definition stated in the Definitions section 
of the Procedure: Assessment and Examinations. 
11.2.2.2 Inherent requirements mean the tasks and activities a student must be able 
to undertake in a course or a program to achieve its learning outcomes, and 
the abilities a student must have in order to undertake these tasks and 
activities successfully. Reasonable adjustments to enable a student with a 
disability to undertake learning activities or assessment tasks must not 
remove the need for the student to meet inherent requirements. 
 
