 with learning opportunities, guidance and feedback on ethical scholarship;"", ""L021"": ""(d) design assessment tasks that minimise the potential for academic misconduct; and"", ""L022"": ""(e) report suspected violations of Academic Integrity consistently in accordance with this policy."", ""L023"": ""5.3 All students have a responsibility to:"", ""L024"": ""(a) familiarise themselves and act in accordance with this policy and expectations, and those of"", ""L025"": ""relevant programs and courses, by using the information and guidance provided by the University"", ""L026"": ""and staff;"", ""L027"": ""(b) meet any University requirements for students to undertake ethical scholarship training made"", ""L028"": ""available by the University, and seek additional assistance if needed;"", ""L029"": ""(c) submit original work for assessment which meets the requirements of Academic Integrity; and"", ""L030"": ""(d) avoid all intentional and unintentional acts which could be considered or perceived as academic"", ""L031"": ""misconduct."", ""L032"": ""5.4 Unit Coordinators have a responsibility to consider:"", ""L033"": ""(a) designing assessments that minimise opportunities for unfair advantage through breaches of"", ""L034"": ""academic integrity;"", ""L035"": ""(b) designing assessment tasks that minimise opportunities for:"", ""L036"": ""i. contract cheating going undetected; and"", ""L037"": ""ii. misuse of generative artificial intelligence or automated writing tools that replaces"", ""L038"": ""genuine student effort; and"", ""L039"": ""(c) reviewing and redesigning, where practical, assessment items and tasks for each unit to prevent"", ""L040"": ""recurrence of academic integrity breaches. The timing of this activity may occur at the discretion"", ""L041"": ""of the Unit Coordinator."", ""L042"": ""6 Part 3 – Types of Academic Misconduct"", ""L043"": ""Academic Integrity breaches encompass any act that compromises the integrity of the University’s"", ""L044"": ""educational goals, outcomes, process and standards. Types of academic misconduct include, but are not"", ""L045"": ""limited to, the following:"", ""L046"": ""6.1 Plagiarism"", ""L047"": ""(a) Plagiarism occurs when the source of paraphrased material is not cited; quoted material is cited"", ""L048"": ""as if it were paraphrased; and quoted material not cited. Types of plagiarism include, but are not"", ""L049"": ""limited to, the following:"", ""L050"": ""i. using material generated by Artificial Intelligence (AI), including Generative AI and"", ""L051"": ""related tools in assessments;"", ""L052"": ""4""}","Approval Date: 23 September 2026 
 
