Integrity Policy to UWA India 
1.1 
This Schedule supports the application of the Academic Integrity Policy to students and staff 
involved in units, courses, research training or other educational activities delivered through 
UWA India. 
1.2 
Academic integrity expectations, misconduct categories, procedural fairness requirements, 
decision-making authority and penalty frameworks are applied consistently with the Academic 
Integrity Policy. 
1.3 
UWA India may use University-approved local procedures, roles, systems or support services 
to implement this policy, provided they are consistent with the policy unless variation is required 
by applicable local law or regulatory requirements. 
1.4 
References to University academic literacy programmes, support services, Academic Integrity 
Officers, schools, units and University systems include equivalent University-approved local 
arrangements for UWA India, where applicable. 
1.5 
Students at UWA India must be provided with clear information about academic integrity 
expectations, permitted and prohibited use of artificial intelligence, assessment 
acknowledgements, academic misconduct processes, support services and appeal pathways. 
1.6 
Records of academic misconduct matters relating to UWA India must be maintained in 
accordance with University records management, privacy, confidentiality and applicable local 
regulatory requirements. 
1.7 
Any external reporting or review pathway applicable to UWA India may be identified in a 
University-approved local procedure or schedule. 
 
