4.7 
The University may approve local procedures or schedules to support the application of this policy to 
offshore campuses, transnational education arrangements or other approved delivery locations. Any 
local procedure or schedule must be consistent with this policy, unless a variation is required to 
comply with applicable local law or regulatory requirements. 
5 
Eligibility Requirements for EVA 
5.1 
Students may request an EVA under exceptional circumstances provided: 
(a) the disruption is severe or serious in nature (see Table 1 for exceptional circumstances), 
substantially interrupting the student’s assessment performance; and 
(b) the disruption is beyond the student’s control; and 
(c) the disruption: 
i. 
is short-term, whereby the exceptional circumstance is unanticipated/unavoidable to the 
extent the exceptional circumstance has prevented the student from completing or 
attending an assessment on a specific date or due date (e.g. 
Tests/Exams/Laboratories/Practicals); OR 
ii. 
has occurred during a critical study or assessment period and lasted for more than three 
days in a row (for examples, see procedure at Appendix A). 
5.2 
The University does not provide EVA for conditions or circumstances that result from planned activities 
or a student’s actions or inactions. Examples of circumstances that are not eligible grounds for EVA 
include: 
(a) misreading/misunderstanding unit outline, exam timetable or assessment deadline; 
(b) any holiday travel;  
(c) attending social events (e.g. birthdays, concerts), or sporting events (excluding participation in 
University games / elite competitions); 
(d) usual rostered work commitments or professional experience organised independently by the 
student;  
(e) student workloads and stress associated with assessments; 
(f) overloading with additional units in a given teaching period; 
(g) computer and/or IT (Information Technology) failure, unless experienced during an online exam or 
equivalent (e.g. major folio submission) or an unplanned computer update occurs during an online 
assessment;  
(h) volunteering commitments; and 
(i) commencing a unit late.  
5.3 
Students who are identified as having received an excessive number of assessment adjustments 
within a teaching period are required to attend an interview with Student Life. Subsequent EVA 
applications are assessed, but outcomes are not implemented until after the required interview has 
occurred.  
6 
Possible outcomes of EVA 
6.1 
EVA applies to the following types of assessment, except for those referred to in Section 7 of this 
policy: 
(a) in-semester assessments or continuous assessments;  
(b) centrally administered examinations; and 
(c) school-administered examinations 
6.2 
The possible outcomes of an EVA application include the following: 
(a) subject to section 6.5 of this policy, undertaking a deferred examination;  
(b) extension to an assessment deadline; 
(c) provision of a replacement or additional assessment opportunity; 
(d) permission to sit examinations away from the University; 
 
