(e) exemption of assessment and reassignment of marks to other assessments provided the 
exempted assessment is worth more than ten per cent and the unit learning outcomes are met by 
other assessment items. In an event where the reassignment of marks is allocated to a final exam, 
the weighting of the final exam must be aligned to the requirements set out in the University Policy 
on Assessment; 
(f) aggregation or averaging of marks obtained for completed assessment items to achieve a final 
percentage mark for the unit, provided the student has met all the learning outcomes in the unit, 
unless specifically stated otherwise in the LMS (Learning Management System) Unit Outline 
where the unit forms part of an accredited sequence; and 
(g) withdrawal without academic penalty. 
6.3 
In cases where a student can provide appropriate documentation for being absent in an exam or 
unable to continue during an exam they are sitting due to exceptional circumstances, a deferred exam 
may be offered. Students who sit the entirety of the exam are not eligible for EVA. 
6.4 
All deferrals of centrally administered exams are administered in accordance with University exam 
rules unless a School has been approved to opt out of the arrangement.   
6.5 
A student who has been given a deferred exam cannot apply for further deferral of the deferred exam 
via EVA. Only outcome 6.2 (g) may be considered in such a situation.   
6.6 
In cases where a student who is part of a group assessment receives approval for an EVA application, 
the outcome must be considered in consultation with the Unit Coordinator. The possible outcomes 
include: 
(a) extension to an assessment deadline for the whole group; 
(b) provision of alternative assessment for the individual student; and  
i. 
redistribution of the assigned work to the rest of the group members with the possibility 
of an extension to the assessment deadline; and/or 
ii. 
a reduced assessment task for the group 
(c) Reassignment of group mark to other assessments if assessment task/item is weighted 10 per 
cent or less. This may be relevant for in-class group activities such as group presentations. 
(d) Where a group member has a UAAP in place, any approved adjustment may be extended to the 
whole group within reason at the discretion of the UC. 
6.7 
A student who has been granted a supplementary assessment is not eligible for EVA. Where a 
student is unable to undertake the supplementary assessment, the original mark stands.  
7 
Minimum Limitations for EVA 
 
7.1 
Subject to section 8.3 and unless the unit outline provides otherwise in the case where the unit forms 
part of a sequence in a professionally accredited course, application for EVA is not permitted for any 
assessment item that: 
(a) is worth 10 per cent or less; and 
(b) comprises a series of evenly weighted assessment tasks (e.g. weekly quizzes); and 
(c) when the top 80 per cent of marks are used to calculate the overall result for the assessment item.  
7.2 
Where an exceptional circumstance occurs during the 48-hour grace period that is provided in the 
form of a penalty waiver for late submission, as set out in the Assessment Policy, students are 
ineligible for EVA. A penalty waiver does not apply to the following types of summative assessments: 
tests/laboratories/mid-semester and final exams administered centrally or by schools. 
7.3 
Application for EVA is not required for missing attendance of no more than 20 per cent of classes that 
assess participation unless the unit outline specifies a higher threshold of attendance. Any unforeseen 
disruption limiting the student’s capacity to meet the minimum threshold of attendance for classes that 
assess participation may entail submission for an EVA, subject to the student meeting eligibility and 
application requirements, including the requirement set out in section 8.4.  
8 
Application Requirements for EVA 
8.1 
With the exception of applications for examination timetable deviations where the deadlines are 
provided in Schedule B1 of Appendix 3 of the University Policy on Assessment, students applying for 
