(c) be guided by academic integrity, common sense, compassion, cultural sensitivity and logic when 
making decisions under this policy. 
10.2 Where an applicant’s exceptional circumstances are unlikely to change or do not change sufficiently to 
permit them to complete a unit's remaining requirements (i.e., any outstanding assessments) within a 
reasonable period, the appropriate form of EVA is withdrawal without academic penalty. 
10.3 Withdrawal without academic penalty may only be applied in retrospect if applied to a unit undertaken 
in the last academic year. 
10.4 To assist the decision-making process, assessors may: 
(a) seek additional information from the applicant directly;  
(b) verify documentation provided by the applicant with the relevant professionals directly; and 
(c) consult with relevant professionals, subject to the applicant’s consent. 
11 
EVA Decisions 
11.1 An application for EVA may be: 
(a) approved or approved in part, and the assessor may grant form(s) of EVA other than the one(s) 
requested by the applicant, but they must comply with section 6.2; 
(b) not approved with no further action required; or 
(c) ineligible, as a final decision of the University, on the grounds that there is no provision for an 
exception within relevant policy to consider the case for EVA.   
11.2 In extreme cases, an assessor may permit a variation to the deadline for receipt of work for 
assessment that extends beyond the University’s deferred examination period for the teaching period 
in question within a reasonable period as long as the assessment is completed before the 
commencement of the following teaching period. This decision must be made in consultation with the 
Unit Coordinator. An extension granted beyond the examination period in the last period of study may 
delay the student’s graduation. 
11.3 Where practical, assessors as far as possible aim to notify applicants in writing of the outcome of their 
application within three University working days of receipt of all documentation relating to the 
application.  
11.4 Applications and all related material, including outcomes, must be recorded in the University’s 
approved records management system and handled in accordance with applicable confidentiality, 
privacy and information governance requirements. 
11.5 Unless the EVA application is deemed ineligible, a student may request a review of the original 
decision in accordance with the Review and Appeal of Academic Decisions Policy (UP15/1).  
 
