Procedures and Guides – For: 
Administrative Procedures see Appendix A 
Guidance Notes for Students see Appendix B 
Guidance Notes for Academic Staff see Appendix C 
 
Related forms:  
Form 1: EVA Online Application  
Form 2: UWA Verification Form (to be uploaded along with Medical Certificate or other evidentiary support, 
where relevant, when submitting EVA application online) 
 
Table 1: Approved Exceptional Circumstances and Required Evidence 
The table below lists common applicable circumstances and supporting evidence that may be supplied; 
however, this list is not exhaustive. 
 
For students undertaking study through an offshore campus, transnational education arrangement or other 
approved delivery location, references in Table 1 to University support services include equivalent University-
approved local student support, wellbeing, safety or advisory services. 
 
Note: 
1. 
Where medical evidence is produced, it must be based on consultation with a registered health practitioner or on the 
health practitioner’s knowledge of the student’s medical history in the case of a temporary exacerbation of an existing 
medical condition.  
2. 
Students are eligible for UniAccess support if they have an ongoing disability, or physical or mental health condition 
that is diagnosed by a doctor or other qualified health practitioner and affects their studies. UniAccess-registered 
students receive reasonable adjustments via a UniAccess Academic Adjustment Plan (UAAP).  
 
Exceptional Circumstance 
Suggested supporting evidence required  
1. Short-term illness, including emergencies 
• 
Medical Certificate for illness lasting three days or more 
(provided by the health practitioner and completion of the 
relevant section of the EVA Form)  
• 
Medical Certificate for illness lasting seven days or more 
(provided by the health practitioner, a verification form 
and completion of the relevant section of the EVA Form); 
OR 
• 
Hospital Discharge Certificate; OR 
• 
Documentation from UWA Counselling and Wellbeing 
team / Guild Student Assist for short-term mental health 
emergencies 
 
2. Hardship or trauma, including: 
• 
Sudden change in domestic 
arrangements (e.g. eviction, 
homelessness) 
• 
Victims of family or domestic 
violence 
• 
Unexpected serious financial 
difficulties 
• 
Unexpected events/accidents 
• 
Hospitalisation of a family member 
 
• 
Official letter from relevant source/authority; OR 
• 
Police report; OR 
• 
Medical Certificate (provided by the health practitioner 
and completion of the relevant section of the EVA Form); 
OR  
• 
Hospital Discharge Certificate; OR 
• 
Documentation from UWA Counselling and Wellbeing 
team / Guild Student Assist or Safe and Respectful 
Community Team 
 
Where none of the above is available, the evidence may be 
presented in another form as determined by the student.  
 
3. Death of a relative or friend 
• 
Death Notice/Certificate; OR 
• 
Obituary; OR  
• 
Order of service; OR 
• 
Statutory Declaration; OR 
• 
Documentation from UWA Counselling and Wellbeing 
team 
Note: Indigenous students may provide a declaration form 
signed by an approved delegate from within Student Services 
in the School of Indigenous Studies 
 
