Exceptional Variation of Assessment Policy 
1.1 
This Schedule supports the application of the Exceptional Variation of Assessment Policy to 
students undertaking units through UWA India. 
1.2 
EVA applications for UWA India students must be submitted through the University-approved 
EVA application mechanism, or any approved local application mechanism specified for UWA 
India. 
1.3 
Evidence submitted in support of an EVA application may include documentation from a health 
practitioner, government authority, court, hospital, employer, University-approved student 
support service, or other authorised professional or person, provided the evidence satisfies the 
requirements of the policy. 
1.4 
Evidence must be provided in English or accompanied by an English translation from an 
appropriately accredited or recognised translator. 
1.5 
References in the policy to UniAccess, University support services, verification forms, records 
management systems or student support processes include equivalent University-approved 
local processes or services used for UWA India. 
1.6 
The University may adapt administrative processes for EVA applications relating to UWA India 
where required to comply with applicable local law, regulatory requirements or approved local 
operating arrangements. 
1.7 
Any local adaptation must preserve the principles of equity, academic integrity, confidentiality, 
fairness and consistency in decision-making. 
 
