University Policy on Exceptional Variation of Assessment (EVA) 
POLICY PROCEDURES 
Note: See Table 1 of the EVA Policy for list of common relevant circumstances and supporting 
evidence that may be supplied. 
 
A) PREPARATORY STEPS (PRIOR TO SEMESTER/TEACHING PERIOD) 
 
Responsible Person/Area:  
Unit Coordinator 
1. In Unit Outline Builder (UOB) – Prior to Week 1: 
a. Update/confirm EVA accomodations in the assessment section. 
b. Identify units requiring special arrangements associated with the deferred examination 
within the UOB data: 
• 
Identify units with multiple Final Examinations for the one unit. 
• 
Identify units with a final examination shared across multiple units. 
• 
Identify units where a final examination includes multiple components 
across different days (Medicine). 
c. EVA allowances are for staff access only, for use in determining appropriate student 
outcomes, and not for publication. 
Responsible Person/Area:  
AskUWA 
2. Configuration of EVA Portal (AskUWA) 
a. EVA portal configured with details of units, assessment items and allowances to guide 
student applications and assessments. 
 
 
B) ONGOING STEPS (DURING SEMESTER/TEACHING PERIOD) 
Responsible Person/Area:  
Students 
1. Students must observe the EVA Submission Eligibility Check, which provides a self-check 
to ensure they can apply for EVA. This rule applies at three points: before undertaking an 
assessment, during an assessment and post assessment: 
a. (Before undertaking an assessment): Students can apply for EVA, subject to 
satisfying the eligibility requirements. 
b. (During an assessment): If a student feels unwell or is impacted by other 
circumstances to the point that they cannot continue with their timed assessment, they 
must: 
• 
stop working on the assessment, 
• 
tell a staff member immediately that they are unwell (i.e. their Unit 
Coordinator, teaching academic or exam supervisor - they must be advised 
before the end of the timed assessment), and 
• 
apply for EVA within three working days of the assessment date. Their 
supporting evidence must be dated within 24 hours of the assessment date. 
c. (Post assessment): While the general cut off for EVA applications is three days after 
the submission deadline, a student cannot apply for EVA after accessing and/or 
attending a timed assessment. Exceptions may be considered if it is clear that they 
were prevented from making an informed decision. Decisions relating to such 
exceptions cannot be reviewed or appealed.  
 
