No medical certificate will be required for the first 48 hours of an illness for assignment extensions 
as there is a late penalty waiver. 
• 
A new UWA Verification Form for Exceptional Variation of Assessment will be required for any EVA 
request for accommodations totalling seven days or more within a teaching period. 
If EVA is requested frequently within one teaching period, as identified by the university, you will be 
invited to discuss your needs with the Student Life team. This meeting will help us provide you with the 
appropriate support. Approval of additional EVAs will be considered only after this consultation. 
 
Top tips: 
• 
Check your unit outline! 
• 
EVA is only available in exceptional circumstances, where the disruption is severe or serious, short-
term, and beyond the student’s control. See Table 1 of the EVA policy for exceptional circumstances 
and required evidence. 
• 
Self-check EVA Submission Eligibility Check, as set out in the Administrative Procedures (see 
Appendix A of the EVA Policy). 
• 
Keep your documentation (evidence such as medical certificate), even if you don’t need to apply 
for EVA at the time. 
• 
Know where to go for help to meet your deadlines: 
o 
UWA Academic Skills Centre have a range of supports. 
 
 
 
Scenario Examples: 
 
Scenario 1: 
A student misses one of the 10 tutorials in a unit as they have been called for Jury duty. There is a 10 
per cent mark for overall participation based on the student’s contribution across the semester. A 
marking rubric/criterion for assessing participation is provided. 
• 
Old system: They would get letter of attendance after the trial and apply for Special Consideration. 
• 
New system: They would not have to do anything as participation is assessed on the basis of the 
whole semester’s work. Note: if attendance is described as compulsory in the unit outline, students 
must attend 80 per cent of the tutorials unless a higher threshold has been set by the unit 
coordinator.  
 
Scenario 2: 
A student is unwell for one or two days and has an assignment due. 
• 
Old system: They would get a documentation and apply for Special Consideration for the two days. 
• 
New system: As long as the student can submit within 48 hours of the assignment deadline no late 
penalty will be applied. A penalty of 5 per cent per day will accrue throughout, being applied as a 
15 per cent penalty on day 3 and a further 5 per cent per day until day 7, after which the assessment 
will not be accepted. Note: If the student elects to take advantage of the two-day late penalty waiver 
and they fall ill during this two-day period, they are not eligible to apply for EVA because the 
assessment is already late.  
 
 
Scenario 3: 
A student is unwell for more than 7 days and has an assignment due. 
• 
Old System: They would get a medical certificate and apply for Special Consideration for the 
number of days they are sick. 
• 
New system: They visit a health practitioner for a medical certificate and request that the health 
practitioner completes the new UWA Verification Form for Exceptional Variation of Assessment.  
 
 
Scenario 4: 
A student has an online quiz as part of 10 online quizzes (worth 10 per cent) in a unit.  They are unable 
to complete one quiz in the middle of semester due to illness or other circumstance listed in Policy Table 
1.  
• 
Old system: They would get documentation and apply for Special Consideration. 
• 
New System: They should still get documentation or UWA verification form but not apply for EVA 
unless they miss more than 20 per cent of their online quizzes for that unit and can demonstrate 
