 with ongoing challenges that affect their studies should be referred to the relevant UWA"", ""L021"": ""support service rather than being advised to apply for EVA."", ""L022"": ""• The Student Guidance Notes contain detailed information on when students can apply for EVA."", ""L023"": ""• It is students’ responsibility to check their unit schedules at the beginning of each semester and notify"", ""L024"": ""relevant UCs if they will be absent from a class due to e.g. a field trip or test/mid-semester exam in"", ""L025"": ""another unit."", ""L026"": ""• Tests/mid-semester exams in core units in a student’s degree-specific major take precedence over"", ""L027"": ""tests/mid-semester exams and classes in other units."", ""L028"": ""o For example, a test in a core unit scheduled at the same time as a test in another unit is the one"", ""L029"": ""that the student should take with their degree-specific major cohort, and they should speak to the"", ""L030"": ""other UC to make alternative arrangements."", ""L031"": ""o UCs should be proactive about supporting students where clashes are a result of university"", ""L032"": ""scheduling. Students must show evidence of any clashes (e.g. their CAS timetable)."", ""L033"": ""• In the interests of equity, UCs do not have discretion to grant extensions. If a UC is approached for an"", ""L034"": ""extension by a student who has missed the EVA document submission deadline without extenuating"", ""L035"": ""circumstances and is therefore deemed ineligible, the UC must refuse the request and apply the usual"", ""L036"": ""late penalties."", ""L037"": ""************""}","Section 11.2 In extreme cases, an assessor may permit a variation to the deadline for receipt of work for 
assessment that extends beyond the University’s deferred examination period for the teaching period in 
question within a reasonable period as long as the assessment is completed before the commencement 
of the following teaching period. This decision must be made in consultation with the Unit Coordinator. An 
extension granted beyond the examination period in the last period of study may delay the student’s 
graduation.  
• 
UCs should consider how this might be approached in the context of their unit. 
 
 
C. LMS Unit Outline  
• 
UCs are encouraged to consider and plan for how EVA will be managed when designing assessment 
items for their unit(s). 
• 
Under the heading Required Assessments in the LMS Unit Outline Builder, UCs must provide 
information to the Student Offices on EVA outcomes permitted for each assessment item. This 
information is not visible to students.  
• 
Information for students about deadlines should be provided under Required Assessments and may 
also be provided in the Unit Schedule. 
• 
If more detailed information on assessment is made available to students in another section of the 
LMS (e.g. Assessments or Assessment Information) UCs must indicate this clearly in the LMS Unit 
Outline Builder, as per the example below: 
 
 
D. Further guidance 
• 
Students with ongoing challenges that affect their studies should be referred to the relevant UWA 
support service rather than being advised to apply for EVA. 
• 
The Student Guidance Notes contain detailed information on when students can apply for EVA. 
• 
It is students’ responsibility to check their unit schedules at the beginning of each semester and notify 
relevant UCs if they will be absent from a class due to e.g. a field trip or test/mid-semester exam in 
another unit.  
• 
Tests/mid-semester exams in core units in a student’s degree-specific major take precedence over 
tests/mid-semester exams and classes in other units.   
o 
For example, a test in a core unit scheduled at the same time as a test in another unit is the one 
that the student should take with their degree-specific major cohort, and they should speak to the 
other UC to make alternative arrangements.  
o 
UCs should be proactive about supporting students where clashes are a result of university 
scheduling. Students must show evidence of any clashes (e.g. their CAS timetable). 
• 
In the interests of equity, UCs do not have discretion to grant extensions. If a UC is approached for an 
extension by a student who has missed the EVA document submission deadline without extenuating 
circumstances and is therefore deemed ineligible, the UC must refuse the request and apply the usual 
late penalties.  
 
 
 
