Policy No:
UP15/5
Approval Date:
28 August 2024
Assessment Date:
28 August 2027
1
Purpose
1.1
Assessment and feedback are integral to the student learning experience – and form a key part of the 
coursework units that are delivered to students. 
1.2
This policy sets out the principles that govern the approach and management of formal assessment in 
coursework units offered within the University to comply with the Australian Higher Education 
Standards Framework.
1.3
This policy comprises the following parts:

Part 1 – University Standards for Assessment, which deals with key standards for the conduct and 
management of assessment at the University;

Part 2 – Governance of Assessment Standards, which deals with the governance of assessment 
standards, including responsibilities for monitoring assessment standards and ensuring 
consistency with regard to assessment practices and processes across the University;

Part 3 – Academic Provisions for Coursework Units, which sets out the principles that govern the 
delivery of formal assessment for coursework students within the University;

Part 4 – Examinations, which deals with the types of examinations held at the University and sets 
out the principles for ensuring consistency in the conduct and management of examinations;

Part 5 – Grading System, which sets out the formal principles and requirements for the provisions 
of final results for undergraduate and postgraduate coursework units.  It also aims to ensure that 
the amendment of examination results and other academic decisions found to be in error after 
notification to the student, is both equitable, and an accurate record of student achievement
2
Scope
2.1
The scope of this Policy applies to Unit and Course Coordinators, and all students enrolled in 
coursework units.
3
Part 1: University Standards For Assessment
3.1
The University is committed to assessment that is fair, integral, valid and efficient. 
3.2
Assessment must be: 
(1) fair if it:
(a) provides opportunities for all students to demonstrate their learning;
(b) promotes behaviour consistent with the University Charter of student rights and 
responsibilities (UP07/132) and the University Policy on Academic Conduct (UP07/21); and,
(c) is transparent and clearly communicated.
(2) integral to the learning process if it:
(a) is used for formative and summative purposes;
(b) is designed to promote student engagement with course content; and,
(c) is timed to promote effective learning.
(3) valid if it:
(a) evaluates student learning outcomes;
