41"": ""of 50, receives after penalty a mark of 37.5 out of 50 (a mark of 2.5 is deducted per day"", ""L042"": ""as a penalty for each student from the mark obtained). Where there are a number of tasks"", ""L043"": ""within an assessment item, the late penalty may be applied holistically to the assessment"", ""L044"": ""item after all tasks have been completed."", ""L045"": ""__________________________________________________________________________"", ""L046"": ""Effective from Semester 2, 2025 in line with Exceptional Variation of Assessment Policy"", ""L047"": ""A penalty of five per cent of the possible mark allocated for the assessment item is"", ""L048"": ""deducted per day in accordance with the following:"", ""L049"": ""a. A penalty waiver is granted for the first two days (including weekends and public"", ""L050"": ""holidays) following the due date of an assessment. This excludes"", ""L051"": ""tests/laboratories/mid-semester and final exams administered centrally or by"", ""L052"": ""schools*."", ""L053"": ""b. Where a student submits after the first two 24-hour blocks, the penalty is applied per"", ""L054"": ""day from day one to day seven (including weekends and public holidays). For"", ""L055"": ""example, a student, who has submitted a piece of work for an assessment item late"", ""L056"": ""by three days and was awarded a mark of 45 out of a possible mark of 50, receives"", ""L057"": ""after penalty a mark of 37.5 out of 50 (a mark of 2.5 is deducted per day from the"", ""L058"": ""mark obtained). An assessment that is submitted after seven days including the two"", ""L059"": ""days of penalty waiver is not accepted. Each 24-hour block is recorded from the time"", ""L060"": ""the assignment is due*."", ""L061"": ""6""}","(b) Students must declare that the work submitted for assessment is their own work. This 
declaration may be made at the point of submission via LMS or ensure that it accompanies 
the work submitted for assessment via other means. Students are required to retain their own 
copy of all work submitted for summative assessment.
(c) Where practical and possible, all summative assessments are submitted via the Learning 
Management System and are passed through the University’s approved text-matching 
software. A range of programs may be used for checking other forms of assessment items. 
Where a piece of assessment ‘passes’ an automated checking program, this does not in itself 
confirm that academic misconduct has not occurred. Markers may make other checks as 
appropriate.
(d) Preliminary marks for each summative assessment task including the final assessment are to 
be entered into and published via the Learning Management System, which is the University’s 
approved secure repository, in accordance with Section 5.8(5)(a) of this policy. 
(2) Principles of submission and penalty for late submission:
(a) Deadlines for submission must be communicated to students; this communication must be 
clear, explicit and clearly stated via unit outlines. 
(b) Deadlines for submission of an assessment task must not coincide with the pre-examination 
study break.  
(c) For all coursework assessments submitted through LMS, the deadline for submission is 
standardised at 11:59pm AWST, unless otherwise given exemption by the Pro Vice-
Chancellor (Academic Excellence) or nominee.
(d) Where a unit does not include a school or formal University examination it may have an 
assessment task due during the formal University exam period.
(e) Alternate assessments granted as a result of special consideration applications are exempted 
from setting deadlines in accordance with 5.3(2)(a), 5.3(2)(b) and 5.3(2)(c).
(f)
Methods for granting of extensions to the submission deadline for assessed work must ensure 
that all students are treated fairly and consistently. The following circumstances are not 
acceptable grounds for extensions:
(i)
inability to have an assignment word processed by the due date;
(ii) other assignments due on or about the due date;
(iii) computer, printer or internet break-down with the exception of a University system or 
database essential to that assessment item;
(iv) foreseeable work commitments;
(v) holiday travels including overseas. 
(g) The following consequences of late or non-submission must be made clear to students: 
(i)
a penalty of five per cent of the possible mark allocated for the assessment item is 
deducted per day for the first seven days (including weekends and public holidays), after 
which the assigned work is not accepted. Each 24-hour block is recorded from the time 
the assignment is due. For example, a student, who has submitted a piece of work for an 
assessment item late by three days and was scored a mark of 45 out of a possible mark 
of 50, receives after penalty a mark of 37.5 out of 50 (a mark of 2.5 is deducted per day 
as a penalty for each student from the mark obtained). Where there are a number of tasks 
within an assessment item, the late penalty may be applied holistically to the assessment 
item after all tasks have been completed.
__________________________________________________________________________
Effective from Semester 2, 2025 in line with Exceptional Variation of Assessment Policy
A penalty of five per cent of the possible mark allocated for the assessment item is 
deducted per day in accordance with the following: 
a.
A penalty waiver is granted for the first two days (including weekends and public 
holidays) following the due date of an assessment. This excludes 
tests/laboratories/mid-semester and final exams administered centrally or by 
schools*.
b.
Where a student submits after the first two 24-hour blocks, the penalty is applied per 
day from day one to day seven (including weekends and public holidays). For 
example, a student, who has submitted a piece of work for an assessment item late 
by three days and was awarded a mark of 45 out of a possible mark of 50, receives 
after penalty a mark of 37.5 out of 50 (a mark of 2.5 is deducted per day from the 
mark obtained). An assessment that is submitted after seven days including the two 
days of penalty waiver is not accepted. Each 24-hour block is recorded from the time 
the assignment is due*. 
