rements must not exceed 70 per cent of the total assessment for the unit, unless"", ""L021"": ""an exception has been granted in accordance with Part 2 (section 4.10) of this policy."", ""L022"": ""5.6 Alternative assessment and arrangements"", ""L023"": ""(1) Alternative assessment and arrangements may be made for particular students in the following"", ""L024"": ""circumstances:"", ""L025"": ""(a) alternative assessment: may, for example, be necessary if teaching resources such as"", ""L026"": ""prescribed texts are not available at short notice."", ""L027"": ""(b) special individual arrangements: may need to be made for assessment items to be set for"", ""L028"": ""students for whom the carrying out of a specific assessment item, as originally set out, is not"", ""L029"": ""possible (such as unanticipated resource access problems or other matters). These"", ""L030"": ""arrangements are directly negotiated between the student and the unit coordinator with due"", ""L031"": ""consideration given to issues of equity and assessment validity. The agreed arrangements"", ""L032"": ""must be placed on the student file and lodged electronically in the student’s record."", ""L033"": ""5.7 Failure and reassessment"", ""L034"": ""(1) The school may approve re-submission of a failed assessment item."", ""L035"": ""(2) Where re-submission of a failed assessment item is approved, students have up to five University"", ""L036"": ""working days to produce and resubmit their work for reassessment."", ""L037"": ""(3) Where resubmission is approved, the reassessed mark is capped at the assessment pass mark,"", ""L038"": ""unless an application for mitigation is approved in accordance with the University Policy on"", ""L039"": ""Assessment: Special Consideration (UP11/23)."", ""L040"": ""(4) To ensure consistency and fairness, reassessment in a form different from the original form of"", ""L041"": ""assessment to determine marks for borderline students is not permitted, unless an exception has"", ""L042"": ""been granted in accordance with Part 2 (section 4.10) of this policy."", ""L043"": ""(5) Reassessment is not available to improve upon a mark or grading above the pass level required"", ""L044"": ""for an assessment task in a unit."", ""L045"": ""5.8 Student Feedback on Summative Assessment"", ""L046"": ""(1) Students must be provided with feedback on all assessed work."", ""L047"": ""(2) Student feedback needs to be fit for purpose and may:"", ""L048"": ""(a) fulfil a range of purposes, including clarifying, troubleshooting, correcting, encouraging and"", ""L049"": ""explaining;"", ""L050"": ""8""}","(6) To ensure consistency all summative marking processes for an assessment item/task are 
