Part 4: Examinations 
6.1
Administration of examinations
(1) Types of examinations offered to students may include:
(a) formal University examinations held during the official examination period and administered by 
Student Services and Engagement; or
(b) formal University exam timetable deviations administered by Student Services and 
Engagement; or
(c) school examinations held outside the official examination period.
(2) The frequency and nature of examinations must be decided by schools in line with any constraints 
imposed by policies of the University.
(3) Student Services and Engagement, schools and the Albany Campus determine appropriate 
venues where examinations are to be conducted.
(4) In extreme mitigating circumstances, the Deputy Vice-Chancellor’s (Education) delegate 
(Associate Director, Service and Engagement, Student Services) may approve a venue other than 
as in 6.1(3).
