(d) process and issue of final unit results in accordance with Part 5 (Grading System) of this 
policy as soon as possible after completion of the unit; and
(e) provide feedback to heads of schools on matters within the school's control that contribute to 
difficulties in examinations. 
(2) Information about examination times are not given to students over the telephone.
(3) No one other than Student Services and Engagement publishes examination timetable information 
on the web.
(4) Students are responsible for accessing their examination timetable through StudentConnect.
6.7
Invigilation
(1) Invigilation in all central examination venues during the formal University examination periods 
must be carried out by invigilators appointed by the Examinations Office, Student Services and 
Engagement. 
(2) All invigilators must attend a training session prior to their first invigilation session.
(3) During the conduct of an examination, invigilators are required to:
(a) provide instructions immediately prior to commencement regarding the conduct of an 
examination, and making students aware they can take notes and start their answers at any 
time.
(b) accompany to the University Medical Centre, where appropriate, any student who needs to 
leave an examination venue due to illness.
(c) report to the student’s allocated course advising student office, via Student Services and 
Engagement, any student found with unauthorised material.
6.8
Contacting examiners during formal University examination
(1) Students are not able to contact the academic member(s) or staff responsible for writing the 
examination paper or their delegates with knowledge of the paper content during the examination.
(2) A student who has a question or comment on the examination, or would like to alert the Unit 
Coordinator to a perceived error should include a comment in their exam for online exams, or 
complete an Exam Content Query Form for written exams.
(3) If applicable, the comment(s) may be taken into account when marking.  
6.9
Exam rules for students
(1) Any student who commits any breach of the rules set out in this section or is guilty of any 
misconduct in relation to the examination is subject to action under Regulations for Student 
Conduct and Discipline.
