as a form of photographic identification and verification.
(3) Behaviour during an examination:
(a) Students must obey all instructions relating to the conduct of an examination given by an 
examination supervisor or invigilator. Instructions are given prior to the commencement of an 
examination and students must be aware of them, if unclear or unable to hear they may ask 
the supervisor to repeat the instructions.
(b) Students requiring assistance during the examination must raise their arm and wait for an 
invigilator to come to them. 
(c) No communication by word or otherwise between students is allowed in the examination 
room.  Students are subject to disciplinary action if found to be communicating with other 
students in the examination room.
(d) Smoking and, unless authorised, eating is not permitted in any examination venue.
(e) Students may only have authorised materials on their desk in the examination room. All 
unauthorised material must be placed in their closed bag under their chair, under their desk if 
they do not have a bag, or in the designated area. All unauthorised electronic devices 
(including mobile phones) must be switched off and remain in their bag or under their desk. 
Any student with unauthorised material on their desk or chair, in their pocket or on their 
person in the examination room must declare it to the supervisor immediately.
(f)
Where a candidate in an examination has been found to have unauthorised material in 
whatever form, in their pocket, on their person, on their desk or chair, or in their pocket or on 
their person en route to / from the toilets, the matter is reported, via Student Administration, to 
the student’s student advising office and disciplinary action is normally taken against them 
regardless of whether the material has been used at the time it is found. 
(g) A student whose conduct is, in the opinion of the Chief Invigilator, disturbing to other students 
and who persists in such behaviour after receiving a warning from an invigilator may be 
required to end their examination and leave the venue.
(h) In the event of an emergency, students must follow the instructions given by the invigilators 
and during an evacuation must refrain from talking or communicating in any other way to 
anyone except an invigilator. 
(i)
Academic misconduct, including cheating in examinations, is dealt in accordance with the 
Regulations for Student Conduct and Discipline, and the University Policy on Academic 
Conduct (UP07/21).  
(4) Exam booklets and written responses:
(a) Students must not remove pages from answer books or the answer books from the 
examination room. Such action may be treated under Regulations for Student Conduct and 
Discipline.
(b) Students must write their examination answers in biro or ink, unless otherwise instructed. 
(c) Students whose writing is illegible may be required to have the Schools to organise for their 
examination answers typed at their own expense or may be recorded as fail.
(5) Entering and leaving the examination venue:
(a) Students may not enter the examination venue until instructed to do so by the Chief Invigilator.
(b) Students are not permitted to enter the examination room more than one hour after the 
commencement of the exam.
(c) Students are not permitted to leave an exam venue or complete and submit an online exam 
for the duration of the exam (2 hours), except in special circumstances. Comfort breaks are 
not permitted in the first 30 minutes and the last hour of any two-hour examination (taken in-
person or online). Students failing to comply with this requirement are reported to the 
University for appropriate action.
(d) Where the time of a School-based examination is of one hour duration or less no student is 
permitted to leave the venue after the commencement of the examination.
(e) Where a student has been permitted by the Chief Invigilator to leave an examination room due 
to illness, the student is required to seek medical advice on the same day of the exam. 
(f)
Students are advised, ten minutes/ five minutes where applicable, before the end that the 
examination is about to conclude. No student must leave their seat until all question papers / 
answer books have been collected and the announcement is made that students may leave 
the room.
(6) Arriving late for an examination:
(a) Students arriving late for examinations:
