 approved calculator are permitted to sit the examination or test"", ""L044"": ""but are not provided with a calculator."", ""L045"": ""6.11 Online Examinations and acting with integrity"", ""L046"": ""(1) The University is committed to ensuring the integrity of online exams, including tests, and treats"", ""L047"": ""integrity breaches seriously."", ""L048"": ""(2) An online exam and/or test is valid provided students act with integrity."", ""L049"": ""(3) A student may be required to undertake an academic integrity check for an online exam/test, in an"", ""L050"": ""event where:"", ""L051"": ""14""}","(i)
are admitted to the examination hall without question during the first hour of the 
examination period but no additional time is made available to students to complete their 
examination.
(ii) are not permitted to take the exam in its entirety at an alternative time (with the exception 
of students graduating at the end of the semester).
(7) Failure to attend an examination:
(a) Failure to attend an examination may only be excused in the case of serious illness or 
exceptional personal circumstances. Applications for mitigation may be submitted in 
accordance with the University Policy on Assessment: Special Consideration (UP11/23). 
6.10
Permitted materials in formal University examinations – See procedures in Appendix 3
(1) Students are only permitted to have books including dictionaries, papers or electronic aids 
specifically authorised by the school in the examination. No students are permitted to have 
unauthorised material in their pocket, on their person or on their desk or chair during 
examinations.
(2) Students bringing pencils, pens and other such items have the option to carry them in a 
transparent pencil case or bag. Other pencil cases must be left in designated areas. 
(3) Students are not permitted to have any electronic devices including mobile telephones, music 
players, digital watches, smart watches, laptops and tablets in their pocket, on their person or on 
their desk or chair during examinations unless with the prior written permission of the 
Examinations Officer (see section 6.10(5) on use of calculators in Examinations).
(4) No student may bring any food and drink into the examination venue, with the exception of water 
in a transparent bottle from which all labels have been removed.
(5) Use of calculators in examinations:
(a) Calculators with the following capabilities must not be taken into an examination venue:
(i)
programmable;
(ii) able to display graphics; or
(iii) have the capacity to communicate with other devices, including but not limited to 
Bluetooth.
(b) Student Services and Engagement, in consultation with the School of Physics, Mathematics 
and Computing must approve and publish on its website all calculators permitted to be taken 
into examination venues.  
(c) Schools must adhere to the approved list when stipulating calculators for use in examinations. 
(d) Students must be informed whether or not a calculator is permitted in an examination, and 
where permitted, be provided with:
(i)
a list of approved calculators; and
(ii) a link to this policy.
(e) All calculators taken into an examination venue must be approved and identifiable by a non-
removable and non-transferable approved sticker that has been attached by an authorised 
body or position comprising staff from Student Services and Engagement or Course Advising 
Student Office.
(f)
Calculators without an approved sticker taken into any examination or test are removed from 
the student and returned at the end of the examination or test.
(g) Students who do not have an approved calculator are permitted to sit the examination or test 
but are not provided with a calculator.
6.11
Online Examinations and acting with integrity 
(1) The University is committed to ensuring the integrity of online exams, including tests, and treats 
integrity breaches seriously.
(2) An online exam and/or test is valid provided students act with integrity.  
(3) A student may be required to undertake an academic integrity check for an online exam/test, in an 
event where:
