person or online). Students failing to comply with this requirement are reported to the 
University for appropriate action.
(d) Where the time of a School-based examination is of one hour duration or less no student is 
permitted to leave the venue after the commencement of the examination.
(e) Where a student has been permitted by the Chief Invigilator to leave an examination room due 
to illness, the student is required to seek medical advice on the same day of the exam. 
(f)
Students are advised, ten minutes/ five minutes where applicable, before the end that the 
examination is about to conclude. No student must leave their seat until all question papers / 
answer books have been collected and the announcement is made that students may leave 
the room.
(6) Arriving late for an examination:
(a) Students arriving late for examinations:
