Overview of Assessment Model 
The photo essay assignment is a flexible and engaging model that can be adapted across a 
wide array of disciplines. It uses visual storytelling as a powerful medium for conveying complex 
concepts in an accessible way: as students must search some environment (natural, built), the 
assessment allows them to draw in their personal or emerging professional interests while 
attempting to develop and present a narrative that connects these interests with class content. 
This model can be applied to various professional disciplines beyond its motivating discipline of 
health studies. For example, in environmental studies, students could capture and report on 
visual impacts of climate change, while in sociology students might focus on socio-economic 
disparities and their relation to climate change. This model is useful as it fosters critical thinking 
while encouraging students to bring their own interests into the assignment, promoting a deeper 
understanding of theoretical concepts and encouraging students to engage with the subject 
matter in a real-world context.  
Assessment Design 
The assessment involves tow component tasks: a photo essay and an oral presentation on a 
subject chosen by the students within the broad topic relevant to the unit. The photos and the 
presentation together should offer an insightful narrative about the chosen topic, highlighting 
different aspects and perspectives.  
• Student prompt: Students are to select a specific topic within the broader general theme of 
the unit. They should then capture three original photos that explore different aspects of the 
chosen topic. These photos can be presented through PowerPoint slides or through a 
similar/alternative platform, allowing the student to explore and discuss connections with both 
unit content (curriculum) and those personal interests they have integrated within the 
assessment (i.e., as a student-centred approach). The focus should be on the original photos, 
without any additional text or inserted images atop the captured images. Later, during a 
scheduled or recorded session, students are to deliver a three-minute oral presentation 
explaining their photos and their relevance to the chosen topic. Students are reminded to 
adhere to ethical guidelines while capturing and presenting their photos.  
• Aims: The primary aim of this assignment is to foster a deeper understanding of a chosen topic 
within the broader theme of the unit, while encouraging students to identify connections 
between unit content and personal/professional interests. The photo essay encourages 
students to explore different aspects of their selected topic in a creative and visual format. The 
oral presentation enhances their communication skills and provides an opportunity to explain 
their understanding and perspective. The assignment aims to cultivate critical thinking, visual 
literacy, ethical awareness, and communication skills among students.  
• Tasks:  
• Task 1 - Photo Essay Submission: Students select a specific topic or component theme, 
and the natural and/or built environment(s) of interest: they will then capture three 
original photos that represent different aspects of this topic and submit these by the 
nominated deadline using PowerPoint or similar slideware. The photos should be original 
and linked, illustrating different perspectives on the chosen topic. 
• Task 2 - Oral Presentation: Following the submission of the photo essay, students prepare 
and deliver a three-minute oral presentation, either live or recorded depending on class 
size and pedagogy. This presentation should explain each photo and its relation to the 
chosen topic. 
