Generative AI and Other Technology Considerations 
Students may need access to specific equipment or software, relevant to the disciplines in which 
the model is deployed. Instructors should ensure that all students have access to the necessary 
software packages and should provide training or resources to help students use these 
technologies effectively: this could be done through asynchronous training materials made 
available before the class begins, and/or through software demonstrations in the middle of 
semester. Importantly, generative AI can be used to augment and enhance the efficacy of the 
assessment, and as a critical tool to improve the efficiency of the student-centred extension 
approach(es) described above. Chat-based tools could be deployed to help students rapidly 
iterate through potential target questions or data collection methods, and as a vehicle to help 
them quickly bound the open-ended nature of the problem. Further, chat-based AI tools that 
are connected to internet search engines may provide the opportunity for students to quickly 
obtain search through, filter, and refine data relevant to the client and/or project (i.e., from 
public information sources without needing to spend significant time on internet searches). 
