Varying Assessment Elements to Maintain Academic Integrity 
To maximise academic integrity, the specific experiment or analysis that students must conduct 
as part of their field or lab book can be varied each year. This ensures that students cannot 
simply replicate past students' experiments. The effort required to change this element will 
depend on the complexity of the experiment or analysis involved. However, it is expected that 
updating this element will be a part of the regular unit preparation and should not significantly 
increase the workload for academics. 
