reflection (although optional in the assessment structure), and integrating theory with practice. 
By providing a flexible and adaptable framework, this task prepares students for success in a 
diverse range of professional environments. 
• Active engagement with a real organisation: Students are required to conduct 
interviews with practitioners from a real organisation, allowing them to interact with 
professionals and gain insights into organisational challenges. This experience helps 
students develop communication and analytical skills while encouraging them to take 
responsibility for their learning process. 
• Research and information literacy: Students are expected to perform in-depth literature 
reviews and gather secondary data to diagnose and analyse the selected organisation. 
