may be public data available about the organisation or chosen perspective/approach, the use 
of generative AI-based data analytics tools may also be useful for students with limited 
background exposure to these methods (i.e., either in searching for publicly-available data 
using internet-connected AI tools or in identifying trends within obtained public data sets).  
If all cases, lecturers should discuss the clear constraints when using generative AI tools in 
connection with organisations, with specific direction given to any restrictions around 
confidential data/interviews, clear acknowledgement of and reporting on the tools’ use cases, 
and awareness of potential inaccuracies or mistakes that can be introduced by the tools. 
