Overview of Assessment Model 
The assessment model revolves around a field trip report and is an excellent method of 
engaging students with real-world applications of their academic knowledge. In the motivating 
example, the student is required to visit a location (a farm) and then analyse and reflect on the 
practices and techniques being used there in a technical, discipline-specific report. This 
submission must then be linked back to unit concepts and theories, providing an opportunity for 
students to apply their understanding in a practical context. This model is beneficial because it 
encourages critical thinking, observational skills, and the ability to analyse and interpret real-
world scenarios. Furthermore, it fosters independent learning as students must conduct their own 
research and form conclusions based on their observations and findings. 
