Further, chat-based generative AI can play a key role as students receive the assignment 
instructions and before they embark on the field trip experience. Particularly this might represent 
a students’ first experience in the field, chat-based AI systems deployed in a flipped-classroom 
environment could allow students to bound the problem, identify preliminary dimensions of 
enquiry, and to rapidly iterate on their approach to the problem. When combined with informal 
dialogue with lecturers, the use of chat-based AI can provide a more personalised learning and 
planning experience, after which students can engage with formal class resources (e.g., online 
materials or the class textbook) to formalise their strategy for the field trip. In this example, the 
combination of chat-based generative AI and in-class conversations work together as a 
dialogic method to establish academic integrity on a per-student basis.   
