 Encourage Collaboration: Promote a collaborative learning environment, where students can 
learn from each other (accessible when students are not working on joint/shared datasets). 
This can be facilitated through discussion forums, group tasks, or peer review activities. 
Generative AI and Other Technology Considerations 
Technology plays a crucial role in this assessment model. The use of MYOB Essentials, a cloud-
based accounting software, allows students to gain hands-on experience in managing financial 
transactions and reports, providing them with valuable skills for their future careers. However, the 
use of technology also presents several considerations: it requires reliable internet access, which 
may not be available to all students. Further, students may struggle with the technical aspects of 
using the software, requiring additional support; this also underscores concerns around data 
privacy and security, especially when dealing with financial data. When considering extension 
to other disciplines, the use of professional software may carry license restrictions to be used only 
on university computers: in this limiting scenario, the lecturer(s) should trial the use of software 
through UniDesk to ensure it is accessible to students over the appropriate period of time (e.g., if 
running a computational simulation, the UniDesk connection does not time out within the 
expected simulation time frame). 
The use of generative AI tools must be approached with extreme caution for some disciplines, 
including the originating discipline of accounting: although AI tools can be useful, professional 
confidentiality expectations should be mimicked in the classroom. Where the student may have 
access to generative AI tools with enterprise-level security (i.e., that may be deployed within a 
corporation), the use of chat-based tools and extensions to explore trends in analysed or raw 
data can be a useful extension concept, particularly if the discipline does not have a significant 
existing scaffold in data analysis.  
