1. Promote Critical Thinking: The assessment tasks are designed to stimulate critical 
thinking, encouraging students to delve into the intricacies of design and to consider 
various factors and implications in their work. 
2. Encourage Creativity: The tasks aim to foster creativity, providing students with the 
freedom to explore various design ideas and concepts, and to develop their own 
unique design solutions. 
3. Develop Professional Communication: The dialogue-based nature of the model 
encourages students to develop their communication skills, both in terms of 
articulating their design ideas and in terms of receiving and responding to feedback. 
4. Enhance Discipline-Specific Skills: The tasks aim to enhance the students' technical 
skill sets (i.e., those specific to the discipline), providing them with practical experience 
in various aspects of the design process, from initial ideation and concept 
development to final execution and presentation. 
