UWA,N050,"Assessment Model Guide 2024 (pdf, 4 MB)",175,175,"L001, L002, L003, L004, L005, L006, L007, L008, L009, L010, L011, L012, L013, L014, L015, L016, L017, L018, L019, L020, L021, L022, L023, L024, L025, L026, L027, L028, L029, L030, L031, L032, L033, L034, L035, L036, L037, L038, L039, L040, L041, L042, L043, L044, L045, L046, L047, L048","{""L001"": ""1. Promote Critical Thinking: The assessment tasks are designed to stimulate critical"", ""L002"": ""thinking, encouraging students to delve into the intricacies of design and to consider"", ""L003"": ""various factors and implications in their work."", ""L004"": ""2. Encourage Creativity: The tasks aim to foster creativity, providing students with the"", ""L005"": ""freedom to explore various design ideas and concepts, and to develop their own"", ""L006"": ""unique design solutions."", ""L007"": ""3. Develop Professional Communication: The dialogue-based nature of the model"", ""L008"": ""encourages students to develop their communication skills, both in terms of"", ""L009"": ""articulating their design ideas and in terms of receiving and responding to feedback."", ""L010"": ""4. Enhance Discipline-Specific Skills: The tasks aim to enhance the students' technical"", ""L011"": ""skill sets (i.e., those specific to the discipline), providing them with practical experience"", ""L012"": ""in various aspects of the design process, from initial ideation and concept"", ""L013"": ""development to final execution and presentation."", ""L014"": ""5. Foster a Professional Mindset: The model aims to help students foster a professional"", ""L015"": ""mindset (or to help migrate toward the expectation of the professional practitioner),"", ""L016"": ""which is critically developed through continuous engagement and feedback"", ""L017"": ""between students and instructors."", ""L018"": ""• Tasks: The assessment model involves multiple tasks, each designed to help students develop"", ""L019"": ""and demonstrate their design skills. The tasks are sequential, with each one building on the skills"", ""L020"": ""and knowledge gained in the previous task."", ""L021"": ""6. Task 1: Concept Development (30% weighting): Students are asked to develop a"", ""L022"": ""concept in response to the prompt. This involves initial research, ideation, and"", ""L023"": ""concept development. Students are expected to present their initial concept in the"", ""L024"": ""form of a concept board, along with a written explanation of their idea and the"", ""L025"": ""rationale behind it."", ""L026"": ""7. Task 2: Design Development (40% weighting): Based on feedback from Task 1,"", ""L027"": ""students refine their concept and start developing their design. This involves further"", ""L028"": ""research, sketching, prototyping, and testing. Students are expected to present their"", ""L029"": ""design development process in the form of a design development board, along with"", ""L030"": ""a written explanation of the changes they made and the rationale behind them."", ""L031"": ""8. Task 3: Final Design Presentation (30% weighting): Students present their final design,"", ""L032"": ""along with a comprehensive explanation of their design process, the decisions they"", ""L033"": ""made, and the rationale behind them. This can be in the form of a physical model, a"", ""L034"": ""digital rendering, a video presentation, or any other format that effectively"", ""L035"": ""communicates the design."", ""L036"": ""• Feedback serves as a tool for learning and improvement, helping students to refine their work"", ""L037"": ""and hone their design skills. In each stage of development, students receive feedback through"", ""L038"": ""dialogue with lecturer(s) and/or expert(s) in the discipline, focusing on both the process and"", ""L039"": ""the product. The feedback process is designed to be comprehensive and constructive,"", ""L040"": ""providing students with clear guidance on how to improve their work. The feedback focuses"", ""L041"": ""on a variety of areas, including conceptual understanding, creativity, critical thinking,"", ""L042"": ""communication skills, and design skills. It encourages students to reflect on their work, to"", ""L043"": ""consider the feedback received, and to apply this feedback in future tasks. The feedback"", ""L044"": ""process also encourages students to develop their own self-assessment skills, helping them to"", ""L045"": ""become more self-aware and reflective in their design practice. This can be achieved through"", ""L046"": ""the use of self-assessment forms, reflection journals, or other self-assessment tools accessible"", ""L047"": ""within the discipline."", ""L048"": ""pg. 87""}","pg. 87 
 
