3) Facilitate community of inquiry processes. 
The assessment is an opportunity to learn and apply a methodology, so it could be designed 
to any specific area of interest, like a particular sub-theme in bioethics, such as euthanasia, or 
questions on the newgenics of prenatal testing. Philosophical theories on mind, could be 
applied to questions about artificial intelligence, and the ethics of ChatGPT. Or feminist 
theories could be applied to questions about cultural bias and the position of Indigenous 
Australians in contemporary society. Any big question is up for consideration and can be 
applied as theme for the assessment.   
Tasks: As above, outlined in the Student Prompt. This assessment accounts for 40% of a 
complete unit of study via the two tasks: an analysis (15%), and the designing of a CoI prompt 
and discussion (25%).  
