Overview of Assessment Model 
The summative model presented here is a dynamic and immersive assessment system motivated 
by the earth science disciplines, specifically geology. The model leverages the unique 
experiential learning that field trips offer to enrich students' understanding of geological 
structures and systems, honing their observational, interpretative, and practical skills in a real-
world context. The essence of this model lies in its ability to foster a deep level of engagement 
with the natural environment. Students are expected to both observe and interact with the 
environment in question, as active participants in the exploration of technical concepts at the 
field scale. The model encourages students to apply theoretical knowledge practically, drawing 
connections between classroom learning and real-world (field-scale) features. 
Assessment Design 
The model is designed to enhance students' abilities to collect, interpret, and present geological 
