Overview of Assessment Model 
The summative model presented here is a dynamic and immersive assessment system motivated 
by the earth science disciplines, specifically geology. The model leverages the unique 
experiential learning that field trips offer to enrich students' understanding of geological 
structures and systems, honing their observational, interpretative, and practical skills in a real-
world context. The essence of this model lies in its ability to foster a deep level of engagement 
with the natural environment. Students are expected to both observe and interact with the 
environment in question, as active participants in the exploration of technical concepts at the 
field scale. The model encourages students to apply theoretical knowledge practically, drawing 
connections between classroom learning and real-world (field-scale) features. 
Assessment Design 
The model is designed to enhance students' abilities to collect, interpret, and present geological 
data. It involves various tasks, such as making field observations, creating draft and final maps, 
constructing a cross-section, formulating a key, and writing a geological history. The assignment 
culminates in an intensive submission process, with students required to submit their work in a 
handwritten format. This is to reflect the field-based nature of the task and the practical skills 
being honed.  
• Student prompt: The model begins with an intensive field trip experience where students are 
required to observe, examine, and interpret various geological features. Students are 
prompted to make detailed observations (in response to prompting questions), take 
measurements, and note their initial interpretations during this field trip. They are required to 
apply their classroom knowledge to the interpretation of these real-world geological 
phenomena (or, conversely, a field-scale application in another discipline). The observations 
and interpretations made during the field trip form the basis of the tasks to be completed 
during the assignment. In the motivating assessment, students are required to create a draft 
map during the field trip nights, drawing upon their daily observations and interpretations. This 
draft map is then transformed into a final map, a cross-section, a key, and a detailed 
geological history (all exemplars of professional disciplinary practice), completed in a 
handwritten format to maintain the authenticity of the field-based learning experience. 
Students are challenged to not only present their observations and interpretations but also to 
weave these into a narrative that tells the geological history of the area studied. Through this, 
they are prompted to demonstrate their understanding of geological concepts and processes 
and their ability to apply this understanding in a practical, real-world context. 
• Aims: The primary aim of the model is to facilitate an experiential learning environment that 
encourages students to immerse themselves in practical fieldwork and apply their theoretical 
knowledge to real-world contexts (geology, in the motivating assessment). The goal is to 
enable students to understand the fundamental aspects of the discipline and to develop 
essential skills in observation, interpretation, data collection, and data presentation. The 
assignment aims to cultivate students' abilities to connect their classroom knowledge with their 
field observations, helping them to better comprehend the complexity and dynamism of real-
world applications or systems. Further, the assessment approach fosters independent thinking 
and problem-solving skills, as students must rationalise their interpretations and ensure that they 
are backed by their collected data. Additionally, the assignment aims to enhance students' 
abilities to communicate their findings effectively. The requirement to produce a final map, a 
cross-section, a key, and a detailed geological history encourages students to develop their 
scientific communication skills, particularly in terms of presenting complex geological data in a 
clear, concise, and comprehensive manner.  
