• Tasks are sequenced to ensure students receive and can act on feedback from instructors at 
multiple (five, in this design) instances before submitting their final professional task. 
 
Field Observations and Measurements (20% of assessment mark): Students should 
document all observations and measurements in a field notebook, noting any initial 
interpretations of the observed geological features. 
Draft Map Creation (15% of assessment mark): Every night during the field trip, students 
should update their draft map with the day's observations and interpretations. 
Final Map Creation (20% of assessment mark): After returning from the field trip, students 
should refine their draft map into a final map, ensuring it accurately reflects their field 
observations and interpretations. 
Cross-Section Construction (15% of assessment mark): Using their final map as a 
