take ownership of their learning. By presenting students with complex, real-world problems to 
solve, the model motivates students to engage deeply with the material and seek out additional 
resources as needed. This promotes a sense of autonomy and self-efficacy, essential skills for 
lifelong learning. Moreover, feedback/consultation during the semester provides the opportunity 
for students to emphasise their personal interests and career aspirations, allowing the academic 
