Overview of Assessment Model 
This assessment model considers a comprehensive, problem-oriented project assignment that 
requires the application of scientific principles, technical judgment, and relevant literature to 
address a complex, real-world environmental problem (with the motivating assessment focussed 
on geotechnics). This model is designed to mimic the conditions and challenges professionals 
face in the field, encouraging students to employ critical thinking, technical skills, and sound 
judgment. This model is based on the principle of 'authentic assessment', whereby students are 
assessed on their ability to apply the skills and knowledge they have acquired to realistic 
scenarios, rather than being tested purely on theoretical knowledge. The assignment is designed 
to enable the development and assessment of a range of skills, including problem-solving, data 
interpretation, report writing, and decision-making.  
Assessment Design 
