Generative AI and Other Technology Considerations 
The MSPA can be implemented in various learning environments, including face-to-face and via 
remote online settings (e.g. Microsoft Teams or Zoom). For online settings, it is crucial to have the 
necessary technology and resources, such as a stable internet connection, a webcam for 
remote invigilation, and a platform for hosting the MSPA. Proctoring software may also be 
necessary to ensure academic integrity in online settings. This software can monitor students 
during the assessment, preventing cheating or plagiarism: it should be noted that the motivating 
assessment requires in-person participation, so in-discipline quality assurance and/or peer review 
should be considered if adapting this model to an online-only environment.  
Generative AI, in all its forms, is generally excluded from relevance in the MSPA, as the 
assessment is performed individually between academics and each student on a timed basis.  
