Overview of Assessment Model 
The model is an in-depth, comprehensive learning approach that requires students to apply 
theoretical knowledge to practical situations. It offers a way to assess students' ability to 
understand, interpret, and apply concepts from a unit to a real-life scenario. The model is 
designed for individual work, encouraging students to think critically and make informed 
decisions based on their knowledge and understanding of the subject. The assignment is divided 
into multiple parts, each designed to evaluate different aspects of a student's understanding 
and analytical skills. The first part typically focuses on diagnosing and formulating a case based 
on a given scenario, with the second part centred around proposing interventions and 
reflecting on their potential outcomes. Students are prompted to apply their knowledge of the 
subject matter, such as diagnostic frameworks and intervention strategies, in their responses. 
