 to students at the beginning of the unit."", ""L039"": "" Provide resources: Provide students with resources and support to help them understand the"", ""L040"": ""grant application process and how to develop a project proposal."", ""L041"": "" Regular feedback: Provide regular and constructive feedback at each task stage to help"", ""L042"": ""students improve their work and enhance their learning."", ""L043"": ""pg. 155""}","pg. 155 
 
basis, instead of relying on the automated detection of violations. The requirement for students 
to reflect on their learning and their approach to the task also enhances academic integrity, as 
it encourages students to engage authentically with the assignment. The marking criteria should 
also emphasise the originality and creativity of the project proposal, further discouraging 
plagiarism and encouraging students to develop unique ideas. 
Varying Assessment Elements to Maintain Academic Integrity 
To maintain academic integrity, it's essential to vary certain elements of the assignment each 
year. The main aspects that can be changed include the funding body’s strategic goals, the 
application form template, the criteria for project selection, and the specifics of the budget and 
timeline requirements. In terms of effort, varying these elements requires some preparation at the 
beginning of each academic year. However, the effort is minimal compared to the benefits of 
maintaining academic integrity and ensuring that students engage authentically with the 
assignment.  
Student-Focussed Learning Design within the Model    
The model offers students the opportunity to select a project that aligns with their personal 
interests and career aspirations, thereby enhancing engagement and relevance. This model 
allows students to explore areas of personal interest within the broader framework of their 
discipline. For example, a student interested in environmental conservation might choose a 
project that involves monitoring local biodiversity, while a student interested in public health 
might choose a project that involves community health data analysis and recommendations. 
The project-based nature of this model also allows students to gain practical experience in areas 
that are relevant to their career aspirations, such as project management, budgeting, and grant 
application writing. Given students are generating and developing their own research ideas, 
consideration should be given to withholding student submissions from a repository associated 
with assessment submission software, such as Turnitin.  Students might wish to pursue their 
proposed research project through the data collection and analysis phases as part of an 
Honours or Masters research project. 
Equity, Diversity and Accessibility Support by the Model  
The flexibility of the model allows it to be adapted to meet a variety of learning needs and 
preferences. The model's focus on individual work also ensures that each student's work is 
assessed on its own merits, while the ability for students to choose projects that reflect their 
personal and emerging professional interests. As this assessment seeks to foster independent 
research strategies in students, providing early consultation to ensure each student has a 
strategy for both time/workload management and support is crucial.  
Best Practices for Successful Implementation 
For successful implementation of the model, consider the following best practices: 
 Clear communication: Ensure that the assignment requirements, deadlines, and marking 
criteria are clearly communicated to students at the beginning of the unit. 
 Provide resources: Provide students with resources and support to help them understand the 
grant application process and how to develop a project proposal. 
 Regular feedback: Provide regular and constructive feedback at each task stage to help 
students improve their work and enhance their learning. 
