• Aims:  
o 
Define a research problem and develop a research question: Students must identify a 
significant problem related to their chosen geographic location and craft a research 
question to guide their investigation. 
o 
Develop a methodology: Students should demonstrate their ability to design a 
comprehensive methodology that can adequately address their research question. This 
includes the selection and processing of appropriate data, the application of relevant 
methods and techniques, and the use of GIS (in the motivating discipline). 
o 
Implement the methodology and analyse the results: The assessment tests students' skills 
in implementing their methodology, interpreting the results, and critically evaluating their 
approach. They are expected to process the data, apply their methodology within a 
GIS, and discuss the outputs critically. 
