The feedback covers both the technical aspects of the work (e.g., the accuracy and 
appropriateness of calculations and designs) and the presentation aspects (e.g., clarity, 
organisation, referencing). Feedback is also provided on group dynamics and collaboration, 
where additional consultation and dialogue may be necessary for groups demonstrating early 
signs of unprofessional conduct. The comprehensive feedback strategy in this assessment helps 
students understand their strengths and weaknesses in the context of teamwork, and provides 
guidance on how to improve their collaboration skills.  
