In this assessment you need to produce a record of your control and instrumentation. It will include a 
specification of each control loop and a detailed P and ID for each section. The control loops will also be 
evaluated between and across all the sections to ensure that they do not conflict in any way. 
The foregoing are all individual tasks.  
 
Submission should be in the following form: 
Each group should submit only one complete document as before. It should include a SHORT 
introduction/summary followed by each person’s individual section. This should be clearly labelled who 
did the work per section. It must include an up to date and correctly labelled PFD and stream tables. The 
document should look professional and be coherently put together. 
 
 
Section Title: Control Summary and Instrumentation Scheme 
Section Weighting: 0.25 (25%) 
Description: A summary of the control and instrumentation scheme for each individual’s section including: 
• What is to be controlled and why for each unit operation included 
• What is to be manipulated to achieve control 
• What measurements need to be made 
• How control loops are to be configured 
• What sensors are used and why (level etc) 
Marking Criteria: 
Creative design of control systems 
Sensible design and implementation of safety systems 
Justification for choice of each control systems 
Demonstration of consideration of lags and delays in chosen control 
 
Section Title: Safety and Maintenance in Control 
Section Weighting: 0.20 (20%) 
Description: A summary of the safety and maintenance implementation in your control and instrumentation 
scheme for each individual’s section including: 
• What safety items are included (alarms, trips and/or interlocks) and their justification  
• Ability of the control system to adapt to change (flow, temperature, composition etc) 
• Implementation of redundancy of equipment when required 
• Isolation valves, drains, bypasses etc. 
• LOPA analysis and proven adequate SILS 
Marking Criteria: 
Implementation of safety devices on the PID diagram 
Discussion and justification for the choice of safety equipment (PSV, Vents, Fail positions of valves etc) 
Discussion on how the PID can cope with change with process parameters without endangering the system 
Design of the PID (and relevant discussion) to allow for maintenance on equipment 
Adequacy and justification of the LOPA and SILS 
 
 
Section Title: Start-up and Shutdown 
Section Weighting: 0.10 (10%) 
Description: Discussion of the operation of start-up, planned shutdown and emergency shutdown for each 
individual’s section including: 
•  Logical start-up and shutdown procedures taking into account requirements of other services, lag times (heat 
etc) and other considerations deemed relevant 
• How your section influences and is influenced by shutdowns/start-ups in other sections 
Marking Criteria: 
Logical start-up and planned Shutdown procedures 
How the system is designed for emergency shutdown 
Discussion on how your section is influenced and influences other sections during the start-up and shutdown 
procedures. 
 
