Description: Your report needs to contain section(s) on safety. This should cover the following suggested areas, 
chemical safety and exposure limits, physical hazards present in the plant, risks the plant poses to surrounding 
infrastructure populations, Explosion and fire risks  and their impact and mitigation, a HAZOP (on nominated 
area), and other safety/risk information that the group deems important to discuss. 
Marking Criteria: 
HAZOP – correct formatting, sensible actions items 
Applicability of discussion on chemical safety to current project 
Applicability of chemical exposure information and consistency to other project data 
Relevancy and completeness of discussion and on physical hazards and their mitigation strategies 
Justification of fire/explosion risks and consistency of discussion to plant layout 
Relevance and applicability to mitigation plans discussed 
 
Section Title: Environmental Impact Assessment 
Section Weighting: 0.15 (15%) 
Description: Environmental assessments are very important to get any proposal approved. The report should 
discuss the environmental impacts of your proposed plant. Areas covered should include (but not limited to) 
waste streams and management/minimisation – both planned and unplanned. Effects on surrounding areas –
communities, effects of increased transport of feed/products etc. 
Marking Criteria: 
Demonstration of completeness of the plume analysis 
Breadth of environmental issues discussed (both planned and unplanned releases) 
Quality of discussion of impact to wider community beyond plant boundaries 
Consideration of environmental issues throughout the whole plant lifecycle 
Applicability of mitigation procedures discussed (from engineering and economic standpoints) 
Use of government regulations in framing the impact statement 
 
Section Title: Plant Location/Layout 
Section Weighting: 0.15 (15%) 
Description: The location and layout of the proposed plant must be discussed. The layout should take into 
account safety, environmental impact, access to feedstock/markets/labour etc. The layout needs to consider safe 
distances between various types of equipment and occupied areas, flaring, firefighting emergency evacuation 
etc. 
Marking Criteria: 
Justification for location of plant based on criteria stated above and others 
Demonstration of applicability of plant layout in respect to required safe distances and safe operation of the plant. 
Use of references to set out layout of the plant. 
Application and consistency of issues raised in safety and environmental sections on plant layout. 
 
Section Title: Economics 
Section Weighting: 0.20 (20%) 
Description: This section should contain detailed economics on the proposed plant. This should include cost and 
time of construction, operating costs, return on investment, sensitivity analysis, historical and future projections of 
relevant process of feed and products. Marks are not awarded on profitability but on correctness and justification 
of the analysis. 
Marking Criteria: 
Appropriate pricing of equipment based on quality of available data used 
Sensible OPEX and CAPEX approximations and their justification. 
Degree of heat integration and its effect on plant economics through the three scenarios 
Breadth and justification of sensitivity analysis parameters and variations 
Justification for predicted trends in costs and demand of product 
 
Section Title: Risk and Threat Analysis 
Section Weighting: 0.15 (15%) 
