UWA,N052,"Appendix 2 Assessment Policy Academic Referencing (doc, 35 KB)",296,296,"L001, L002, L003, L004, L005, L006, L007, L008, L009, L010, L011, L012, L013, L014, L015, L016, L017, L018, L019, L020, L021, L022, L023","{""L001"": ""Appendix 2: University Policy on: Assessment"", ""L002"": ""Academic Referencing – as approved by Academic Council on 4 December 2019 (R61/19)"", ""L003"": ""1. The following range of footnote, author-date and numeric referencing styles are permitted to be"", ""L004"": ""used at UWA in coursework academic courses:"", ""L005"": ""a) Australian Guide to Legal Citation (AGLC)"", ""L006"": ""b) American Psychological Association (APA) referencing style (author-date style)"", ""L007"": ""c) Chicago Style Guide (footnote and author-date style)"", ""L008"": ""d) Institute of Electrical and Electronic Engineers (IEEE) style (author-date style)"", ""L009"": ""e) Vancouver referencing and citation style (numeric style)"", ""L010"": ""f) MLA (author-page style of in-text citation)"", ""L011"": ""2. No individual academic customised styles are to be used in coursework academic courses"", ""L012"": ""(Harvard referencing is not included in the list of styles because although it is known as the"", ""L013"": ""\""author date\"" style (that is, you must cite both the author and publication date), there is no"", ""L014"": ""definitive version of Harvard available)."", ""L015"": ""3. The requirements for referencing, including any prescribed referencing style, and links to"", ""L016"": ""relevant support materials, must be made clear in the unit outline in support of the University"", ""L017"": ""Policy on Assessment Section 10.41."", ""L018"": ""4. The library may provide online guides, EndNote styles and support for the prescribed"", ""L019"": ""coursework (undergraduate and postgraduate) referencing styles."", ""L020"": ""5. Potential exceptions to the above requirements for courses at honours and master’s level may"", ""L021"": ""be considered on the following grounds:"", ""L022"": ""a) the course of study is committed to a single referencing style"", ""L023"": ""b) external factor/reasons (such as accreditation/professional requirements)""}","Appendix 2: University Policy on: Assessment 
Academic Referencing – as approved by Academic Council on 4 December 2019 (R61/19)
1.
The following range of footnote, author-date and numeric referencing styles are permitted to be 
used at UWA in coursework academic courses: 
a)
Australian Guide to Legal Citation (AGLC) 
b)
American Psychological Association (APA) referencing style (author-date style) 
c)
Chicago Style Guide (footnote and author-date style) 
d)
Institute of Electrical and Electronic Engineers (IEEE) style (author-date style) 
e)
Vancouver referencing and citation style (numeric style) 
f)
MLA (author-page style of in-text citation)
2.
No individual academic customised styles are to be used in coursework academic courses 
(Harvard referencing is not included in the list of styles because although it is known as the 
""author date"" style (that is, you must cite both the author and publication date), there is no 
definitive version of Harvard available).
3.
The requirements for referencing, including any prescribed referencing style, and links to 
relevant support materials, must be made clear in the unit outline in support of the University 
Policy on Assessment Section 10.41.
4.
The library may provide online guides, EndNote styles and support for the prescribed 
coursework (undergraduate and postgraduate) referencing styles. 
5.
Potential exceptions to the above requirements for courses at honours and master’s level may 
be considered on the following grounds:
a)
the course of study is committed to a single referencing style
b)
external factor/reasons (such as accreditation/professional requirements)
