UWA,N054,"Appendix 4 Assessment Policy Expectations of Major Coordinator (docx, 71 KB)",302,302,"L001, L002, L003, L004, L005, L006, L007, L008, L009, L010, L011, L012, L013, L014, L015, L016, L017, L018, L019, L020, L021, L022, L023, L024, L025, L026, L027, L028, L029, L030, L031, L032, L033, L034, L035, L036, L037, L038, L039, L040, L041, L042, L043, L044, L045, L046, L047, L048, L049, L050, L051, L052","{""L001"": ""Expectations of Major or Course Coordinator (Tasks and Responsibilities)"", ""L002"": ""Definition"", ""L003"": ""A Major/Course Coordinator has subject matter expertise in the relevant discipline area and is a point"", ""L004"": ""of"", ""L005"": ""contact for the School to manage education matters within its governance arrangements. A Major/Course"", ""L006"": ""Coordinator manages and oversees the undergraduate/postgraduate content and integration within/across"", ""L007"": ""Expectations of Major or Course Coordinator"", ""L008"": ""A Major/Course Coordinator is an advocate for their course of study. They provide leadership in"", ""L009"": ""developing and implementing a high standard of teaching, research, creative, and service activities, by"", ""L010"": ""encouraging collegiate engagement, participation, and innovation. A Coordinator leads the shaping and"", ""L011"": ""implementation of Major/Course curriculum and cohesion, manages policy compliance, fosters collegiate"", ""L012"": ""decision-making, and ensures that staff teaching into the major/course understand their"", ""L013"": ""roles and contribute to the discipline, School and University."", ""L014"": ""A Major/Course Coordinator is expected to meet the qualifications set out in Section 3.2.3 of the"", ""L015"": ""Higher Education Standards Framework for the availability, skills and knowledge of teaching staff. a"", ""L016"": ""Note: a Major Coordinator can act as coordinator for associated Minors, where appropriate."", ""L017"": ""No ti ng t he d iversity in School oper a tions, a M ajor or C o urse C o ordinator should u s ua lly o versee"", ""L018"": ""or und ert ake t he f o ll ow i ng : b"", ""L019"": ""Major or Course Promotion"", ""L020"": ""Maintain and circulate accurate course related information to promote the Major/Course priorities and"", ""L021"": ""objectives."", ""L022"": ""Contribute to student recruitment through marketing strategies and activities."", ""L023"": ""Encourage cohort-building within the Major/Course, including contributing to prize/award selection"", ""L024"": ""and presentation, where applicable."", ""L025"": ""Be available to meet with staff and current or prospective students and make considered"", ""L026"": ""recommendations relating to transition arrangements, entry, cross-institutional enrolment, and"", ""L027"": ""recognition of prior learning."", ""L028"": ""Manage partnerships and relationships with key stakeholders and communities to strengthen and"", ""L029"": ""support the ongoing development of the Major/Course."", ""L030"": ""Major or Course Management"", ""L031"": ""Ensure compliance with and lead translation of UWA, School and external body processes and policies"", ""L032"": ""within the Major/Course, including professional standards and accreditation, where applicable."", ""L033"": ""Lead Major/Course development and documentation, ensuring learning and teaching is consistent with"", ""L034"": ""requirements (for example, updating manuals/handbooks, contributing to accreditation processes,"", ""L035"": ""where applicable)."", ""L036"": ""Monitor and advise on the suitability of units as core and/or elective."", ""L037"": ""Consider and approve units for Study Abroad/Exchange."", ""L038"": ""Manage Major/Course quality and currency through annual/biennial review, and liaise with key staff,"", ""L039"": ""regarding curricula, assessments, and pedagogy, with due consideration of student feedback."", ""L040"": ""Manage the integration of units within a Major/Course. This includes appraising the appropriateness of:"", ""L041"": ""content duplication; knowledge scaffolding and learning outcomes, whilst accounting for cross-"", ""L042"": ""discipline content; and ensuring discipline experts are delivering content."", ""L043"": ""Evaluate the appropriateness of assessments between units and across levels, including responsibility"", ""L044"": ""for review of all substantial unit assessments (as a guide >30% of unit grade)."", ""L045"": ""Review the timing of assessments across the academic teaching periods, giving consideration to"", ""L046"": ""student workload."", ""L047"": ""Review and fulfil curriculum change process requirements, in accordance with the University Policy on"", ""L048"": ""Coursework Units (4.6, 4.7)."", ""L049"": ""Participate in School level student result validation meetings to provide oversight and/or Board of"", ""L050"": ""Examiner meetings to consider progression."", ""L051"": ""aTEQSA Higher Educaton Standards are listed in Appendix 1, University Policy on Assessment."", ""L052"": ""bTasks and responsibilities are undertaken with appropriate support (e.g., from Head of Discipline), as determined by the School.""}","Expectations of Major or Course Coordinator (Tasks and Responsibilities)
Definition
A Major/Course Coordinator has subject matter expertise in the relevant discipline area and is a point 
of
contact for the School to manage education matters within its governance arrangements. A Major/Course 
Coordinator manages and oversees the undergraduate/postgraduate content and integration within/across 
Expectations of Major or Course Coordinator
A Major/Course Coordinator is an advocate for their course of study. They provide leadership in 
developing and implementing a high standard of teaching, research, creative, and service activities, by 
encouraging collegiate engagement, participation, and innovation. A Coordinator leads the shaping and 
implementation of Major/Course curriculum and cohesion, manages policy compliance, fosters collegiate 
decision-making, and ensures that staff teaching into the major/course understand their
roles and contribute to the discipline, School and University.
A Major/Course Coordinator is expected to meet the qualifications set out in Section 3.2.3 of the 
Higher Education Standards Framework for the availability, skills and knowledge of teaching staff. a 
Note: a Major Coordinator can act as coordinator for associated Minors, where appropriate.
