Maintain and circulate accurate course related information to promote the Major/Course priorities and
objectives.
Contribute to student recruitment through marketing strategies and activities.
Encourage cohort-building within the Major/Course, including contributing to prize/award selection
and presentation, where applicable.
Be available to meet with staff and current or prospective students and make considered
recommendations relating to transition arrangements, entry, cross-institutional enrolment, and 
recognition of prior learning.
Manage partnerships and relationships with key stakeholders and communities to strengthen and
support the ongoing development of the Major/Course.
Major or Course Management
Ensure compliance with and lead translation of UWA, School and external body processes and policies
within the Major/Course, including professional standards and accreditation, where applicable.
Lead Major/Course development and documentation, ensuring learning and teaching is consistent with
requirements (for example, updating manuals/handbooks, contributing to accreditation processes, 
where applicable).
Monitor and advise on the suitability of units as core and/or elective.
Consider and approve units for Study Abroad/Exchange.
Manage Major/Course quality and currency through annual/biennial review, and liaise with key staff,
regarding curricula, assessments, and pedagogy, with due consideration of student feedback.
Manage the integration of units within a Major/Course. This includes appraising the appropriateness of:
content duplication; knowledge scaffolding and learning outcomes, whilst accounting for cross- 
discipline content; and ensuring discipline experts are delivering content.
Evaluate the appropriateness of assessments between units and across levels, including responsibility
for review of all substantial unit assessments (as a guide >30% of unit grade).
Review the timing of assessments across the academic teaching periods, giving consideration to
student workload.
Review and fulfil curriculum change process requirements, in accordance with the University Policy on
Coursework Units (4.6, 4.7).
Participate in School level student result validation meetings to provide oversight and/or Board of
Examiner meetings to consider progression.
aTEQSA Higher Educaton Standards are listed in Appendix 1, University Policy on Assessment.
bTasks and responsibilities are undertaken with appropriate support (e.g., from Head of Discipline), as determined by the School.
