(A).
Author means a Researcher who has made significant intellectual or scholarly contribution to 
the research described in the research output, and is willing to be accountable for their 
contribution, and agree to be listed as an Author.
(B).
Authorship will be based on substantial intellectual involvement.
(C).
All Authors must be collectively accountable for the whole Research output.
(D).
Authorship requires substantial contributions to Research output and must include one and 
should include two or more of the following —
(1).
conception and design of the project;
