, ""L022"": ""(3). conduct or collaborate in a clinical trial at the discretion of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor"", ""L023"": ""(Research) who will take advice from Risk and Legal and Research support managers;"", ""L024"": ""(4). upon request, consider accepting the role of GCP Sponsor of a clinical trial and respond"", ""L025"": ""in writing with the outcome of its decision;"", ""L026"": ""(5). commit to GCP as defined by Therapeutic Goods Administration note for guidance"", ""L027"": ""when responsible for clinical trials administration; and"", ""L028"": ""(6). expect Researchers involved in clinical trials to understand and comply with the"", ""L029"": ""Guidelines for Good Clinical Practice."", ""L030"": ""(B). Researchers will —"", ""L031"": ""(1). obtain written acceptance from the University before nominating the University as a"", ""L032"": ""The University of Western uwa.edu.au/policy 13"", ""L033"": ""Australia"", ""L034"": ""Code of Conduct Integrity Academic""}","12.2 Collaboration potentially involving researchers or organisations 
supporting the Unethical Organ Transplant Industry
(A).
The University must not engage in any Research collaboration with Researchers and/or an 
organisation that engages directly in any activity that is part of the Unethical Organ 
Transplant Industry.
(B).
Unethical Organ Transplant Industry means any organisation involved in unethical human 
organ harvesting, human organ trafficking and/or unethical human organ transplantation.
(C).
The University must not engage in any Research collaboration that would directly support or 
facilitate the Unethical Organ Transplant Industry.
(D).
The University may engage in Research collaboration with an organisation that is peripherally 
involved in the Unethical Organ Transplant Industry if, in the option of the Vice-Chancellor —
(1).
the primary business of that organisation is unrelated to the Unethical Organ 
Transplant Industry; and
(2).
the proposed collaboration cannot be perceived to support the Unethical Organ 
Transplant Industry or its activities.
13
Clinical Trials
(A).
The University will —
(1).
support clinical trial Research by providing ethical review, clinical expertise, Research 
infrastructure, and funds administration;
(2).
promote collaborative agreements with medical Research institutes, and public 
hospitals for the conduct of clinical trials where responsibilities are shared;
(3).
conduct or collaborate in a clinical trial at the discretion of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor 
(Research) who will take advice from Risk and Legal and Research support managers;
(4).
upon request, consider accepting the role of GCP Sponsor of a clinical trial and respond 
in writing with the outcome of its decision;
(5).
commit to GCP as defined by Therapeutic Goods Administration note for guidance 
when responsible for clinical trials administration; and
(6).
expect Researchers involved in clinical trials to understand and comply with the 
Guidelines for Good Clinical Practice.
(B).
Researchers will —
(1).
obtain written acceptance from the University before nominating the University as a 
