Breaches
(A).
The Guide to Managing and Investigating Potential Breaches of the Australian Code for the 
Responsible Conduct of Research, 2018 (the Investigation Guide) forms a critical part of 
Australia’s framework for research integrity, established by the Australian Code for the 
Responsible Conduct of Research, 2018 (the 2018 Code).
(B).
The Investigation Guide assists the University to manage, investigate and resolve complaints 
about potential breaches of the 2018 Code by outlining a preferred model that can be 
implemented by institutions engaged in research, regardless of the size or type.
(C).
Developed jointly by the National Health and Medical Research Council, the Australian 
Research Council and Universities Australia, the Investigation Guide has broad applicability 
across all research disciplines.
(D).
The Investigation Guide should be read alongside the Research Code —
https://nhmrc.gov.au/about-us/publications/guide-managing-and-investigating-potential-
