1
Related to UP20/6
Research Integrity
Academic
Research Integrity
Advisors
Guideline
1
Intent
(A).
The University has appointed Research Integrity Advisors (RIAs) to assist Researchers in 
addressing ethical and procedural issues in the design and conduct of their Research.
(B).
The intention of the Research Integrity Advisors (RIAs) Guideline (this Guideline) is to provide 
advice on how to obtain ethical review, publication and dissemination of research findings, 
authorship, conflicts of interest, and management of research data and primary materials. 
(C).
Research Integrity Advisors can also advise about questionable research practices and the 
process of making an allegation of a breach of the codes of ethics and conduct. 
(D).
In essence, the RIAs are to —
(1).
provide advice to those with concerns around research conduct and potential 
complainants about the appropriate way forward;
(2).
provide guidance on relevant University processes and procedures; 
(3).
advise on issues relating to activities external to the University e.g. authorship on 
research papers.
(4).
promote good research practice rather than react to concerns; and
(5).
understand that the role of RIA is advisory, not investigatory or compliance oriented.
Approval Date 
16 September 2020
Assessment Date 16 September 2020
Administrators
AD Research Operations
Academic Secretary 
