: No AI"", ""L018"": ""The assessment is completed entirely without AI assistance."", ""L019"": ""Example 1: AI-assisted idea generation and structuring"", ""L020"": ""Students are permitted to use generative AI tools, software or"", ""L021"": ""services to generate initial ideas, structures, or outlines, but must"", ""L022"": ""complete the work themselves."", ""L023"": ""Example 2: AI-assisted editing"", ""L024"": ""AI can be used to make improvements to the clarity or quality of"", ""L025"": ""student-created work to improve the final output, but no new"", ""L026"": ""TIER 2: AI assistance or collaboration"", ""L027"": ""content can be created using AI."", ""L028"": ""AI is used before or after human input as an aid. Assessment"", ""L029"": ""might be to assure learning, or to develop learning. Some"", ""L030"": ""examples are given here but note there may be others."", ""L031"": ""Example 3: AI task completion, human evaluation"", ""L032"": ""Please pay careful attention to the instructions given."", ""L033"": ""AI is used to complete certain elements of the task, with students"", ""L034"": ""providing critical analysis on the AI generated content. This level"", ""L035"": ""requires critical engagement with AI generated content and"", ""L036"": ""evaluating its output."", ""L037"": ""AI is embedded throughout the assignment, allowing for a"", ""L038"": ""collaborative approach with AI. There is no assessment security"", ""L039"": ""present, and the main objective is to develop learning and skills,"", ""L040"": ""not for assurance of learning (unless the use of AI tools is itself the"", ""L041"": ""learning outcome)"", ""L042"": ""TIER 3: Full Embedded AI""}","UWA wants students to explore the range of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and generative AI (GenAI) tools available to you 
throughout your teaching and learning experience, and where suitable, to use in your assessments. Your UC will 
determine which tier of AI usage is most suitable for the specific assignment you have been set, and you are encouraged 
to use tools to help you in your work as specified in the assignment brief, in accordance with one or more tier. If no 
specific tools have been recommended by your UC, you can use any tool. You will be asked to reference how/where you 
used AI and may be asked to state which tool/s you used (please refer to the second table for help in this). Please 
remember that AI tools store any data or entry that you put into it, so keep yourself and others safe and do not upload 
any private, personal or identifying information into any AI tool! Unless you have been given permission to do so, you 
should not upload any lecture slides or unit materials. For more information on using AI, check out this page. 
 
AI Tiers that may be applied to assessment tasks by your lecturer 
 
TIER 1: No AI 
The assessment is completed entirely without AI assistance.  
Assessment must be secured and is essential for assurance of 
learning 
 
 
 
TIER 2: AI assistance or collaboration 
AI is used before or after human input as an aid. Assessment 
might be to assure learning, or to develop learning. Some 
examples are given here but note there may be others. 
Please pay careful attention to the instructions given. 
 
 
Example 1: AI-assisted idea generation and structuring 
Students are permitted to use generative AI tools, software or 
services to generate initial ideas, structures, or outlines, but must 
complete the work themselves. 
Example 2: AI-assisted editing  
AI can be used to make improvements to the clarity or quality of 
student-created work to improve the final output, but no new 
content can be created using AI. 
Example 3: AI task completion, human evaluation  
AI is used to complete certain elements of the task, with students 
providing critical analysis on the AI generated content. This level 
requires critical engagement with AI generated content and 
evaluating its output. 
 
 
 
 
 
TIER 3: Full Embedded AI 
AI is embedded throughout the assignment, allowing for a 
collaborative approach with AI. There is no assessment security 
present, and the main objective is to develop learning and skills, 
not for assurance of learning (unless the use of AI tools is itself the 
learning outcome) 
 
AI use in assessments 
This is a guide for how you can use AI in your assessment task. Your assignment will 
have been categorised against one of these tiers, the tables below show you 
how/when you should use AI and how you reference what you did. 
