"L025"": ""All work must include standard disciplinary citations."", ""L026"": ""Additionally, any use of generative AI tools must be clearly"", ""L027"": ""indicated, with the specific tool referenced. You may be"", ""L028"": ""required to provide both pre- and post-AI submissions,"", ""L029"": ""including prompts and outputs from AI tools. Some word"", ""L030"": ""processing tools may require auto-rewriting functions to be"", ""L031"": ""disabled. A reflective component may also be required,"", ""L032"": ""explaining how AI-generated ideas were used or disregarded."", ""L033"": ""You may use AI throughout your assessment to support your"", ""L034"": ""own work, although AI should not be used to complete the"", ""L035"": ""entire task. It should always be used collaboratively. You may"", ""L036"": ""be asked to specify which content is AI generated."", ""L037"": ""Referencing"", ""L038"": ""Normal citation for any non-AI work; you may be requested to"", ""L039"": ""TIER 3: Full Embedded AI"", ""L040"": ""show which tools completed which elements of the task or"", ""L041"": ""show the series of prompts you used to produce the work.""}","Assessment completion and use of AI by tier 
Tier 
Guidelines for student 
 
 
TIER 1: No AI 
The assessment is completed entirely without AI assistance.  
AI must not be used at any point during the assessment, there 
may be controls in place to detect the use of AI. 
 
Referencing  
Normal citation of all work in accordance with disciplinary 
conventions, 
 
 
TIER 2: AI assistance or collaboration 
AI is used before or after human input as an aid. Assessment 
might be to assure learning, or to develop learning. Some 
examples are given here but note there may be others. 
Please pay careful attention to the instructions given. 
 
 
Example 1: AI-assisted idea generation and structuring 
No AI-generated content is allowed in the final submission, you 
may be asked to show the prompts and outputs from the AI 
tool you used to get ideas. No AI-generated content to be 
included in your submission. 
Example 2: AI-assisted editing  
AI can be used, but your original work should have been 
completed before asking AI to make improvements. You may 
be required to provide your original work and the AI output. No 
AI-generated content to be included in your submission. 
Example 3: AI task completion, human evaluation  
You will use AI to complete specified tasks in your assessment. 
Any AI created content must be cited as specified in your 
assignment brief. 
Referencing 
All work must include standard disciplinary citations. 
Additionally, any use of generative AI tools must be clearly 
indicated, with the specific tool referenced. You may be 
required to provide both pre- and post-AI submissions, 
including prompts and outputs from AI tools. Some word 
processing tools may require auto-rewriting functions to be 
disabled. A reflective component may also be required, 
explaining how AI-generated ideas were used or disregarded. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
TIER 3: Full Embedded AI 
 
You may use AI throughout your assessment to support your 
own work, although AI should not be used to complete the 
entire task. It should always be used collaboratively. You may 
be asked to specify which content is AI generated. 
 
Referencing 
Normal citation for any non-AI work; you may be requested to 
show which tools completed which elements of the task or 
show the series of prompts you used to produce the work. 
 
