UWA Document (Public)
This is a UWA Official document authorised or intended for public access.
 
 
 
 
Information Privacy Policy  
Policy UP 14/10 
 
Approver 
Senate 
Sponsor 
Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Operations) 
Owner 
Chief Risk Officer 
Secretary 
Corporate Secretary 
Policy Type 
Institutional 
Policy Category 
Corporate Governance 
 
1. 
Purpose 
The University respects the privacy of individuals and is committed to protecting the Personal 
Information it collects, uses and manages. 
1.1 
The purpose of this Policy is to — 
(a) Set out the principles and requirements that govern how the University manages Personal 
Information to ensure it is handled lawfully, fairly and responsibly in accordance with the 
University’s legislative obligations and expectations; and 
(b) Protect individuals from misuse, unauthorised access or disclosure of their information; and 
(c) Ensure the principles align with the Privacy and Responsible Information Sharing Act 2024 (WA) 
(the PRIS Act) and where applicable the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth.). 
 
1.2 
This Policy is to be read in conjunction with the following — 
(a) Information Privacy Guidelines, 
(b) Information Breach Policy,  
(c) Information Protection Policy, 
(d) Information Retention Policy, 
(e) Acceptable Use of Information Technology Policy,  
(f) Cyber Security Policy, 
(g) UWA Code of Conduct, and; 
(h) Supporting guidelines. 
 
2. 
Definitions 
 
Term 
Definition 
Health Information1  
Sensitive Personal Information that relates to: 
•  the health (at any time) or disability (at any time) of an individual 
•  a health service provided or to be provided to an individual; 
•  an individual’s expressed wishes about future provision of health services, or  
•  any other personal information collected to provide a health service. 
Information Users 
A member of the University Community that creates, captures, receives or uses 
University Information. 
