This is a UWA Official document authorised or intended for public access.
Personal Information1 
Information or opinion, (whether true or not, and whether recorded in a material 
form or not), that relates to an individual (living or deceased), whose identity is 
apparent, or can reasonably be ascertained from the information or opinion. This 
is a broad definition and can include: 
• a name or pseudonym, date of birth, address or other contact information 
• a unique or online identifier, such as a driver’s licence number or IP address 
• information that relates to an individual’s location 
• technical or behavioural information regarding activities, preferences or 
identity 
• inferred information, or predictions about behaviour or preferences 
• profiles generated from aggregated information 
• information specific to one or more of an individual’s physical, physiological, 
genetic, mental, behavioural, economic, cultural or social identity. 
Privacy Collection 
Notice 
A privacy collection notice is the information provided to a person when their 
personal information is collected so they understand: 
• who is collecting it, 
• why it is being collected, 
• what law or authority allows or requires the collection (if applicable), 
• what happens if they do not provide it (if relevant), 
• who it may be disclosed to, and 
• how they can access or correct their information. 
Privacy Impact 
Assessment 
A Privacy Impact Assessment (PIA) is a formal documented assessment 
conducted to identify privacy risks, assess impacts and mitigate privacy risks 
associated with a function or activity. 
Sensitive Personal 
Information1 
Sensitive personal information is Personal Information relating to an individual’s: 
•  health information (see also definition for Health Information) 
•  racial or ethnic origin 
•  gender identity, where that does not correspond with their designated sex at 
birth 
•  sexual orientation or practices 
•  political opinions or membership of a political association 
•  religious beliefs or affiliations 
•  philosophical beliefs 
•  membership of a professional or trade association, or a trade union 
•  criminal record 
•  genetic or genomic information 
•  biometric information, or 
•  any information as above that can reasonably be inferred. 
Significant Decision  
Under the PRIS Act, a Significant Decision is one that affects an individual’s 
rights, entitlements, interests or liabilities, or otherwise has a significant effect on 
an individual’s life, circumstances, opportunities, behaviours or wellbeing. 
University 
The University as defined in Part 1 section 2 of the University of Western Australia Act 
1911 (WA) 
University Community 
All individuals who engage in University activity and/or use University property. 
University Executive 
Any of the following positions: 
• Vice-Chancellor 
• Senior Deputy Vice-Chancellor 
• Deputy Vice-Chancellors 
• Chief Financial Officer. 
University Information 
All data, records and information created, captured, processed, stored, shared 
and/or disposed of by the University Community or on behalf of the University 
relating to University business in any format or medium.  
University Officer 
University Officer means any individual employed, appointed, engaged or 
otherwise authorised by the University to perform duties or exercise functions on 
behalf of the University, including, but not limited to: 
(a) Senate Members and Senate committee members; 
(b) Employees (full-time, part-time, fixed term and casual); 
 
1 For the purposes of this Policy is taken as defined in Part 1 section 4 of the PRIS Act and includes 
Sensitive Personal information, unless otherwise differentiated.  
 
