3 
Scope 
3.1 
This policy applies to all University Officers as well as affiliates, volunteers, students and other third 
parties when acting for, on behalf of, or under the control or direction of the University when collecting, 
holding, accessing, utilising, sharing, retaining or disclosing Personal Information and Sensitive 
Personal Information as part of a University activity. 
3.2 
This Policy applies to all University activities conducted on or off campus, in Australia or overseas, 
including activities undertaken by or through entities controlled by the University.  
3.3 
Compliance with this Policy and any supporting guidance or subordinate documentation issued under 
it is mandatory. 
 
4 
Information Privacy Principles 
4.1 
Collection 
a) The University must only collect Personal Information when the information is necessary for one or 
more of its functions and activities such as, but not limited to, the provision of educational services, 
research in varying disciplines, as an employer or when providing services to the wider community. 
b) Before collecting Personal Information, a University Officer must document why it is being collected 
and how it must be used or disclosed. 
c) The University must only collect Sensitive Personal Information if the information is necessary and 
the individual consents to the collection of information, it is required by law, or the collection is 
necessary to prevent a serious threat of harm. 
d) The University must, where it collects Personal Information, provide individuals with a Privacy 
Collection Notice, or a reference to where the notice can be accessed, explaining the purpose for 
collecting, using, disclosing and retaining the information. 
e) The University must collect Personal Information by lawful, fair and transparent means, limited to 
what is reasonably required for University activities by various means, including but not limited to:  
i. 
direct contact in the course of providing services or administration of a University activity 
and/or University business; 
ii. 
enrolment, registration or subscription process 
iii. 
forms that are submitted by individuals (including via online portals); 
iv. 
from CCTV cameras on University Property; 
v. 
from cookies set from web browsers visiting the University’s websites; 
vi. 
from Google applications including AdWords; 
vii. 
from public health databases where the relevant consent processes described in the 
national research and ethics codes are reviewed and approved; 
viii. 
from an individual’s usage of University’s IT Assets and IT Services; 
ix. 
from third parties with which the University collaborates; and 
x. 
when undertaking research. 
f) 
The University must, where Personal Information about an individual is collected from a third party, 
seek to ensure the information was collected lawfully, and the individual is made aware of its 
collection and intended use and disclosure of the information from the third party, except in 
circumstances required by law.  
 
4.2 
Use and Disclosure  
