2 
 
4.6 
A review/appeal of a decision may lead to no change or to either a less favorable or more favorable 
outcome for the candidate. 
4.7 
The following circumstances are not grounds for review/appeal of HDR decisions: 
(a) a candidate’s disagreement with academic judgement; 
(b) a candidate’s disagreement with a University rule, policy or procedure. 
4.8 
A completed review must precede a request for an appeal to the University Appeals Committee, which 
is a committee of the Academic Board.  
4.9 
A request for a review may be declined by the Graduate Research School in the following 
circumstances: 
(a) where the review request is not submitted within the stated period as prescribed in Schedule A; 
(b) where the review request is made on grounds other than those specified in Schedule A. 
4.10 A decision to decline the request for a review/appeal in circumstances referred to in 4.9 is final. 
 
