4.10 A decision to decline the request for a review/appeal in circumstances referred to in 4.9 is final. 
 
5 
Specific principles – Management of HDR Candidature 
5.1 
A candidate may request a review of their candidature relating to: 
(a) management of enrolment and candidature status; 
(b) a decision to not Confirm Candidature; 
(c) a determination of unsatisfactory progress. 
5.2 
For a progress status to be amended following a review, the Board or the University Appeals 
Committee must be satisfied that:  
(a) the relevant rule, policy or process was not followed; or  
(b) the decision reached was unfair; or  
(c) additional information has become available that merits a different decision; and  
(d) the request by the candidate can be accommodated, including, for example, that appropriate 
supervision and resources are available. 
 
6 
Specific principles – Thesis classification and examination 
6.1 
A candidate whose thesis and/or other research output has been classified by the HDRCC may 
request a review of their classification if they are of the view that the examination and classification 
were conducted other than according to the relevant rules, policies and procedures or were otherwise 
unfair. 
6.2 
The following circumstances are not considered grounds for review for thesis classification and 
examination: 
(a) perceived shortcomings in supervision or support, or any other matters not directly related to the 
examination and classification process;  
(b) matters of academic judgement of examiners, the HDRCC or the Board, including the candidate’s 
view that the classification unfairly reflects the merit of their work or demonstrated ability. 
 
7 
Specific Principles - Award and management of scholarships 
7.1 
An applicant may only request a review of or appeal against a decision by the Higher Degree by 
Research Scholarships Committee to not award a scholarship on the grounds that the Committee's 
procedures for the assessment of the application have not been observed.  A review/appeal based on 
any other grounds, including the quality of the application or the academic record of the applicant, is 
not considered. 
7.2 
A candidate may only request a review of or appeal against a decision by the Graduate Research 
School to suspend or terminate a scholarship on the grounds that the decision to suspend or terminate 
was not consistent with the Conditions of the scholarship. 
