4.19 In applying for an appeal of an academic decision, the student must identify the appropriate ground on 
which they believe the review decision was unreasonable and provide all relevant evidence from the 
review process, including where relevant any informal resolution attempt. Reproducing the same 
paperwork already considered in a Review or not providing evidence to demonstrate the ground for 
appealing against the Review decision may result in the case being summarily dismissed.   
