Part 7: Freedom of Expression Panel   
7.1. 
There shall be a Freedom of Expression Panel to provide advice to the Vice-Chancellor on 
whether the University’s facilities should be made available for use by a visiting speaker. 
7.2. 
The Freedom of Expression Panel will provide such advice on the request of the Vice-
Chancellor or on the request of 15 or more members of the University staff and/or students.  
7.3. 
In providing such advice the Freedom of Expression Panel will have regard to the Principles of 
this Code, and may advise as to any conditions under which the proposed use of the 
University’s facilities should be permitted.  
7.4. 
The Freedom of Expression Panel will consist of: 
(a) Nominee of the Vice-Chancellor as Chair; 
(b) The Chair of Academic Board or nominee; 
(c) Guild President or nominee; and 
(d) Two members of senior academic and senior professional staff appointed by the Vice-
Chancellor for the provision of relevant expertise and inclusivity. 
 
 
