Delegations Framework 
Policy UP22/7 
 
Approver 
Senate 
Sponsor 
Vice-Chancellor 
Owner 
University Secretary 
Secretary 
Corporate Secretary 
Policy Type 
Institutional 
Policy Category 
Corporate Governance 
 
1 
Purpose 
1.1 
The purpose of this Policy is to — 
(a) establish the Delegations Framework, consisting of this Policy and all Instruments of Delegation; 
(b) express the practices and behaviour expected in relation to Delegation and the exercise of 
Delegations;  
(c) ensure Delegations are properly governed, recorded and accessible, as is appropriate; and 
(d) facilitate institutional effectiveness, efficiency and accountability. 
1.2 
This Policy is to be read in conjunction with the following — 
(a) Matters Retained by the Senate. 
(b) The relevant Instrument of Delegation, including: 
i. 
Delegation of Financial Authority; 
ii. 
Delegation of Signing Authority; 
iii. 
Delegation of People and Culture Authority; and 
iv. 
Delegation of Academic Authority. 
2 
Definitions 
 
Term 
Definition 
Business Unit 
Any academic or administrative area of the University with its own 
University cost centre. 
Delegate 
A person or persons invested with the authority to carry out the powers, 
authorities, duties, functions or commitments. 
Delegation 
The formal assignment of powers, authorities, duties, functions or 
commitments, to enter into official and legitimate commitments on behalf of 
the University. 
Delegations Framework 
The Delegations Framework means (as they may be amended from time to 
time) — 
(a) the University of Western Australia Act 1911 (WA) 
(b) other relevant legislation including the University of Western 
Australia Statute (2020), University regulations and by-laws; 
(c) Matters Retained by the Senate; 
(d) Instruments of Delegation; and  
(e) other formal instruments including enterprise agreements and 
employment contracts. 
Responsibility for developing and managing elements of the framework are 
set out in section 7 (as may be amended from time to time and approved by 
the Vice-Chancellor). 
