Term 
Definition 
Delegations Guidelines or 
Procedures 
A relevant internal document or documents that provides additional 
explanatory information or step-by-step instruction about the particular 
Delegation and relevant Policies, that may be updated frequently. 
Employee 
An individual employed by the University. 
Financial Commitment 
Expenditure, assets and attractive items acquisition and disposal, contract 
authorisations, quotations waivers, tender waivers, and related variations or 
adjustments. 
Instrument of Delegation 
The approved document (as it may be amended from time to time) used to 
express the powers, authorities, duties, functions or commitments an 
individual (or entity) is authorised to carry out on behalf of the Senate or 
Vice-Chancellor and includes — 
(a) University Committee constitutions; 
(b) Matters Delegated to the Vice-Chancellor; 
(c) University Policies; and 
(d) Other instruments of delegation such as power of attorney 
Matters Retained by the 
Senate 
The Matters Retained by Senate as approved by the Senate on 2 
December 2024 and updated from time to time.   
Senate 
The governing body of the University, as defined in the University of 
Western Australia Act 1911 (WA). 
Senate Committee 
A committee of the Senate to which the Senate has delegated 
responsibilities under section 16G of the UWA Act. 
Senate Member 
Defined in Part 4 section 8 of the University of Western Australia Act 1911 
(WA). 
University 
The University of Western Australia established under the University of 
Western Australia Act 1911 (WA) 
University Committee 
A committee of the Senate and Academic Board including their sub-
committees and AdHoc Committees established by Senate from time to 
time. 
University Community 
All individuals who engage in University activity and/or use University 
property. 
University Executive 
A member of the Executive as appointed by the Chancellor’s Committee 
including each of the following;  
(a) Vice-Chancellor 
(b) Senior Deputy Vice-Chancellor 
(c) Deputy Vice-Chancellors 
(d) Chief Financial Officer. 
University Officer 
means any individual employed, appointed, engaged or otherwise 
authorised by the University to perform duties or exercise functions on 
behalf of the University, including, but not limited to:  
(a) Senate Members and Senate committee members;  
(b) Employees (full-time, part-time, fixed term and casual);  
(c) Contractors;  
(d) holders of honorary, adjunct or clinical appointments; and  
(e) holders of the title Emeritus or Emerita. 
3 
Scope 
3.1 
The scope of this Policy applies to the entire University and its Officers. 
 
