Step 6: Monitoring and Reporting (ongoing) 
(A).
Monitoring and review is integral to successful risk management as risks change over 
time. Monitoring should occur at the required frequency per the University’s risk matrix 
and per the below table, and/or based on a trigger event or changing circumstances.
(B).
The risk management process should be well documented and shared in order to 
improve risk management activities and inform planning and decision making.
(C).
Monitoring and reporting processes should be incorporated into all aspects of the risk 
management process and it should be taken into consideration whether —
(1).
Controls are effective; 
(2).
Treatment plans are being implemented and are managing the risks; 
(3).
Lessons from events (near misses), changes, trends, successes and failures are 
being learned; 
(4).
Changes in the external and internal environment are being detected; 
(5).
Emerging risks are being identified; 
(6).
Risks and risk treatments are monitored and reported per table below; and 
(7).
UWA Strategic Assurance will report strategic risks and significant Business 
Unit risks to the Audit and Risk Committee and Senate 
(D).
Key things to remember are —
(1).
each business unit’s operational risk register should be updated annually (at a 
minimum) and sent to UWA Strategic Assurance. 
(2).
consideration of risks and treatment plans should be embedded into business 
unit planning processes. 
