Step 7: Communication and Consultation (ongoing) 
(A).
Communication and consultation needs to take place throughout all stages of the risk 
management process. Effective external and internal communication and consultation 
ensures that those who are accountable for implementing the risk management 
process share with stakeholders the basis on which decisions are being made and the 
reasons that particular actions are required. 
(B).
This may be achieved through —
(1).
Business Unit leadership team meetings; 
(2).
Cross-business unit engagement; 
(3).
Formal business planning processes; and 
(4).
Executive Leadership Team meetings.
(C).
Since the views of external stakeholders can have a significant impact on the decisions 
made it is important that their perceptions of risk are identified and integrated into the 
decision-making process. External stakeholders include community organisations, 
students, partners, suppliers, other Universities, other institutions, industry bodies e.g. 
Go8, Government and Media. 
(D).
The advantages of a consultative team approach include —
(1).
Establishing the context appropriately; 
(2).
Ensuring that the interests of stakeholders are understood and considered; 
(3).
Helping to ensure that risks are adequately identified; 
(4).
Bringing together different areas of expertise; 
(5).
Ensuring that different views are considered; and 
(6).
Assisting in securing endorsement and support for treatment action plans.
4
