 Complainant means an individual, group of individuals or an organisation, who has made a"", ""L027"": ""Complaint to the University."", ""L028"": ""(B). A Complainant will —"", ""L029"": ""University of Western Australia"", ""L030"": ""uwa.edu.au/policy"", ""L031"": ""3""}","3
Complaints
(A).
Complaint means an expression of dissatisfaction in relation to the University or its 
Complaints handling process where a response or resolution is explicitly or implicitly 
expected and where the matter does not relate to the employment or enrolment of the 
Complainant at the University.
(B).
The University will accept all Complaints —
(1).
regarding matters within the University’s authority to do so; and
(2).
that are made in good faith. 
(C).
The University will formally acknowledge a Complaint within five days of receiving one.
(D).
The University will handle Complaints —
(1).
without bias;
(2).
fairly; and 
(3).
in a timely manner. 
4
Making a Complaint
(A).
Anyone may make a Complaint to the University.
(B).
Before accepting a Complaint, a complainant is encouraged to seek to resolve their concern 
informally with the relevant area of the University.
(C).
Complaints must be submitted using the University’s Complaint Lodgement System.
(D).
Complaints about possible wrongdoing by the University may be made under the protection 
of the Public Interest Disclosure Act in accordance with the University’s Public Interest 
Disclosure Policy.
(E).
Anonymous Complaints can be made to the University using the —
(1).
University’s Complaint Lodgement System; or
(2).
University’s external ‘whistleblower’ service, Stopline. 
5
Complainants
(A).
Complainant means an individual, group of individuals or an organisation, who has made a 
Complaint to the University.
(B).
A Complainant will —
