Part 1 – Preliminary 
 
Purposes of these regulations 
These regulations have the following purposes — 
(a) to inform students of behaviour that the University regards as misconduct,  
(b) to implement fair and just procedures for dealing with cases of possible misconduct;  
(c) to provide for the imposition of penalties for misconduct; and 
(d) to constitute, and regulate the conduct of, the Board of Discipline. 
 
These regulations are to be read in conjunction with the Academic Integrity Policy. 
1 
What misconduct is 
(1) In these regulations misconduct means — 
(a) an act or omission of a student which is prohibited by the Statute or a 
University regulation, rule, by-law, Code of Conduct or policy or Senate 
Resolution, or by an order made under, or Code of Conduct adopted by, the 
