from time to time and approved by the Vice-Chancellor).
5
Delegation Principles
(A).
Delegations must be formally recorded, and be transparent and accessible to Senate, 
University Committees, and relevant University Officers. 
(B).
Delegations must —
(1).
reflect the organisational and hierarchical structure of the University; and
(2).
be in writing in accordance with the relevant Delegations Procedure.
(C).
Persons and entities engaged by the University who are not Employees of the University 
cannot exercise delegated authority on behalf of the University.
