4
Risk
(A).
Risk means the “effect” of uncertainty on objectives as defined by Standards Australia 
(AS/NZS ISO 31000: 2018; Risk Management – Guidelines) and —
(1).
is expressed by reference to a potential event occurring; 
(2).
is measured in terms of a combination of the likelihood of an event occurring and 
the consequence if that event was to occur; and
(3).
represents a deviation from the expected and can be positive, negative or both and 
may address, create or result in opportunities and threats.
5 Risk Type
(A).
The University will manage Risks differently according to the following types —
(1).
Strategic Risk means Risk that may impact the University’s strategic objectives;
(2).
Operational Risk means Risk that may impact Business Units’ performance 
targets and delivery of outcomes;
(3).
Compliance Risk means Risk that may impact the University’s ability to meet 
obligations, including but not limited to those required by law, industry 
standards, codes of good governance and community commitments; and
(4).
Project Risk means Risk that may impact Business Units change initiative or 
project deliverables, timelines, milestones, activities, budgets and output 
quality. 
(B).
The University will manage Risks in accordance with the Risk Management Framework.
