6 Risk Appetite
(A).
Risk Appetite means the degree of Risk that the University is willing to accept in pursuit 
of its strategic and operational objectives. 
(B).
University Officers must consider the Risk Appetite Statement during University planning 
and decision-making, to enable decisions that reflect the University’s position on Risks 
that are acceptable and necessary in pursuing strategic and operational objectives. 
(C).
Senate will approve the University’s Risk Appetite Statement, which will be available on 
the Staff Intranet.
(D).
UWA Strategic Assurance will facilitate annual reviews of the Risk Appetite Statement.
7 Risk Owners
(A).
The Vice-Chancellor will assign an Executive Member as an owner for each Risk listed in 
the University Strategic Risk Register.
(B).
Heads of Business Units or project sponsors, as appropriate, will assign an owner to each 
Risk listed in a local Business Unit Risk register or Project Risk register.
8 Risk Assessment
(A).
Risk Assessment means the process of identification, analysis and evaluation of Risks to 
strategic and operational outcomes.
(B).
Business Units must perform a Risk Assessment at least once a year in accordance with 
the Risk Management Framework, which includes —
(1).
identifying, analysing and evaluating Risks;
(2).
developing and implementing Risk treatment strategies; and
(3).
monitoring and reviewing the effectiveness of strategies.
(C).
University Officers must conduct Risk Assessments prior to undertaking or planning new 
projects or activities.
