12 Business Continuity Management 
(A).
Business Continuity Management is the capability of an organisation to manage its 
response to and continue the delivery of products and services following a disruptive 
event. 
(B).
The University will manage the University’s Business Continuity Management System in 
accordance with ISO 22301:2022, Security and Resilience – Business Continuity 
Management Systems – Requirements.
