Scope
(A)
This Policy applies to:
(1).
All Staff, Researchers and Students.
(2).
Visitors, Honorary, Adjunct, Clinical Adjunct and Emeritus Appointments as if they are 
Employees during the period of any visit or appointment by the University.
(B)
This Policy includes the Intellectual Property Commercialisation Guidelines.
4
Definitions
Commercialise means to obtain commercial benefit from IP including exercise of all rights owned by 
the University and ‘Commercialisation’ has a like meaning.
Contributor means any individual, other than an Originator, who contributes to the creation 
of IP.
Computer Program means a computer program as defined by the Copyright Act, 1968 (Cth).
Copyright means any work or thing in which Copyright may subsist including, but not limited to 
—
(1).
artistic work;
(2).
literary work;
(3).
Computer Programs;
(4).
dramatic work;
(5).
musical work;
(6).
sound recording;
(7).
cinematograph film;
(8).
television broadcast;
