(6).
Patent;
(7).
Plant Variety;
(8).
Trade Mark; and/or
(9).
Rights of a related nature.
Originator means any individual who creates IP that vests in the University.
Patent means a patent as defined by the Patents Act, 1990 (Cth).
Plant Variety means a plant variety as defined by Plant Breeders' Rights Act, 1994 (Cth).
Student is defined in the Policy Framework Policy.
Teaching Materials means Copyright works created in any medium (other than a Computer 
Program) by an Employee under a contract of service to the University to instruct or assist in 
instruction in a University Course, subject or Unit.
Thesis is defined in the Admission: Coursework Policy.
Trade Mark means a trade mark as defined by the Trade Marks Act, 1995 (Cth).
Unit is defined in the Coding System for Courses, Unit Sets and Units. University is defined in the 
University of Western Australia Act 1911 (WA). 
