7
IP created with third parties including Centres, Institutes 
and other Research Collaborations
(A).
The ownership of IP in projects involving a third party will be determined by the terms of the 
agreement between the University and that third party.
(B).
Employees and Students employed by or participating in the research activities of Centres, 
Institutes and similar research collaborations will be subject to the policies and contractual 
obligations of that research activity which may require, as a condition of participation, 
confidentiality undertakings and assignment of IP rights.
(C).
Employees and Students who participate in teaching, work experience and other 
collaborations with third parties will be subject to the policies and contractual obligations of 
that collaboration including confidentiality undertakings and assignment of IP rights.
