Use of University IP
(A).
Employees and Students must protect the University’s interests in its IP and not act in any way 
inconsistent with those interests including not benefiting at the University’s expense.
(B).
Employees and Students should consider the implications of disclosing University 
Information or trade secrets that may affect patentability or registrability of IP rights.
13
IP Disputes
(A).
If a dispute arises as to the operation of this Policy, a Deputy Vice-Chancellor may use 
their discretion to:
(1).
resolve the dispute themselves;
(2).
make an agreement for mediation and appoint an agreed mediator; and/or
(3).
make an agreement for arbitration and appoint an agreed arbitrator.
