Commercialisation
Guidelines
1
Purpose
(A).
The University supports the development and translation of Intellectual Property and aims to 
maximise the value of Intellectual Property for the benefit of the University Community.
(B).
Originators are encouraged to engage the University in the early stages of Intellectual 
Property development. Early engagement can assist with the evaluation of disclosure and 
pathways to maximise Intellectual Property value.
(C).
These Guidelines provide support and direction on:
(1).
the Commercialisation of Intellectual Property;
(2).
the sharing of Net Proceeds from Commercialisation;
(3).
Spinouts; and
(4).
Directorships with companies with rights to University Intellectual Property.
(D).
The University will proactively manage the Net Proceeds of Commercialisation including any 
equity portfolio in a manner consistent with the Intellectual Property Policy and these 
Guidelines.
