Definitions
Commercialise means to obtain commercial benefit from IP including exercise of all rights
owned by the University and ‘Commercialisation’ has a like meaning.
Contributor means any individual, other than an Originator, who contributes to the creation 
of IP.
Computer Program means a computer program as defined by the Copyright Act, 1968 (Cth).
Copyright means any work or thing in which Copyright may subsist including, but not limited to:
(1).
artistic work;
(2).
literary work;
(3).
Computer Programs;
(4).
dramatic work;
(5).
musical work;
(6).
sound recording;
(7).
cinematograph film;
(8).
television broadcast;
(9).
sound broadcast;
(10).
published edition of work; and/or
(11).
photographs.
Design means a design as defined by the Designs Act, 2003 (Cth).
Equity means a share in a company as payment or consideration for using IP.
Intellectual Property (IP) means without limitation, all rights in relation to any:
(1).
circuit layout or eligible layout as defined by the Circuit Layouts Act, 1989 (Cth);
(2).
privileged information of any kind which, because of its characteristics, is capable of 
protection by contractual or equitable means, and includes information of a valuable 
