1
Purpose
1.1
Coursework units are key components of a plan of study which takes the form of a course, 
undergraduate major, and minor. As part of this plan of study, coursework units are designed as 
discrete entities but also designed to complement other units to form a coherent plan of study that 
leads to the learning outcomes of an award course. 
1.2
This policy sets out principles for the creation, management, and approval of coursework units offered 
in undergraduate and postgraduate coursework courses. 
1.3
The policy addresses the following aspects of a coursework unit:
Part 1 – General principles;
Part 2 – Creation of coursework units;
Part 3 – Changes to coursework units; and
Part 4 – Selection of teaching modes.
2
Scope
2.1
The scope of this Policy applies to all curriculum developers, professional staff members supporting 
curriculum development, and committees responsible for endorsing or approving curriculum.
3
Part 1: General Principles
3.1
Within the context of maintaining the University’s reputation as a university of the highest international 
standing, the University is committed to:
(1) providing a high-quality learning experience for all of its students;
(2) providing teaching at the highest international standards of quality;
(3) embedding and fostering the relationship between teaching and research across the range of its 
disciplines; 
(4) providing opportunities for experiential learning which is an integral part of the University’s 
courses; and
(5) the effective and efficient use of scarce resources.
3.2
A coursework unit:
(1) has a credit point value assigned by the University;
(2) is designed to deliver a set of learning outcomes, which may in turn be part of delivering the 
overall objectives of an undergraduate major or a postgraduate coursework course;
(3) is designed with a view to minimising duplication of unit content (see Part 2);
(4) is coded in accordance with the University Policy on: Coding System for Courses: Unit Sets and 
Units;
(5) is assessed in accordance with the University Policy on: Assessment; 
(6) is pedagogically sound and delivered effectively using the most appropriate teaching mode or 
modes (see Part 4 on Teaching Modes);
(7) is offered in accordance with the University Policy on: Teaching Periods; and
(8) may have quotas set in accordance with this policy.
4
Part 2: Creation of Coursework Unit
4.1
A coursework unit may function as a/an:
(1) core, where it is compulsory to be undertaken by a student; 
(2) option, where it is chosen from among a range of given options in a unit set; 
