4.8
Where duplication of units is identified within a school, the Head of the School must consult with the 
disciplines concerned to resolve any issue(s). Where duplication of units is identified between schools, 
the Heads of Schools are encouraged to resolve inter-school disputes without recourse to intervention 
by the University. Intra-school or inter-school consultations must occur within the context of the 
University's academic and resource policies and processes (See Procedure 3 in Appendix A).
