(a) The Head of School or delegate may approve a change to the title of a unit in situations 
where:
(i)
a new unit title is necessary to reflect minor changes to the content (but no changes to 
outcomes), and does not warrant it being classified as a new unit;
(ii) a new unit title is necessary to avoid confusion with another unit title; or 
(iii) a new unit title better reflects the academic objectives of the unit. 
(b) The Head of School may approve a change to the title of a unit in other circumstances on a 
case-by-case basis; 
(4) Changing the responsible organisational entity 
(a) The Head of School or delegate may approve a change to the responsible organisational 
entity for the unit, which may occur in, but not limited to, the following circumstances: 
(i)
where changes have been made or will be made to the academic content of the unit 
which requires a change in the teaching responsibilities of the unit; or
(ii) to accommodate organisational realignment, subject to appropriate consultation.
(5) Changing teaching responsibility
(a) Teaching responsibilities can be split between schools but in any change schools must ensure 
that 100% of the teaching is accounted for (refer to sections 4.6 – 4.8 for Unit Duplication). 
Schools may approve a change in teaching responsibility where: 
(i)
there has been a change in the academic content of the unit which is collaboratively 
taught; or 
(ii) staffing or administrative reasons necessitate the change. 
(b) Any change in teaching responsibilities must not adversely impact the standard of teaching 
nor compromise the learning outcomes.
5.4
The following changes, depending upon their impact on the course, require either consultation and 
approval by relevant board(s) through the University Committee system (for changes that have an 
impact on a course), or approval through a 'Fast Track' approval process with limited consultation (for 
nil impact) (to be determined by the School when submitting a change via CAIDi):
(1) Changing unit rules
(a) The relevant board(s) may approve a change to a unit pre-requisite / co-requisite where: 
(i)
there are proposed structural changes to an undergraduate major or a postgraduate 
course; 
(ii) the academic content of the unit requiring the pre-requisite / co-requisite is being 
changed; 
(iii) the learning outcomes of the pre-requisite / co-requisite has changed; or 
(iv) a pre-requisite / co-requisite is unavailable in a teaching period. Any change to a pre-
requisite / co-requisite within an undergraduate major or a postgraduate course must: 

ensure that the basis of the proposed change is academically sound;

ensure sequential building of academic knowledge within the structure of an 
undergraduate major or postgraduate course; 

provide learning progression and academic coherence; and 

be in accordance with the approved structures for an undergraduate major or 
postgraduate course.
(2) Changing unit incompatibility
(a) The relevant board(s) may approve a change to unit incompatibility where the content of one 
or more units that were considered incompatible has changed such that the units concerned 
are no longer considered incompatible or vice-versa.
(3) Changing the teaching period
(a) The relevant board(s) may approve a change to the teaching period where the change is 
necessary due to: 
(i)
the availability of teaching staff or other resources;  
(ii) the projected number of students enrolled in the unit; or 
(iii) to facilitate student study planning and progression through the unit sequence.
(b) The relevant board(s) may approve a change to the teaching period of a unit where the 
change could prevent or delay students from completing their course or otherwise adversely 
impact on students, providing it is satisfied with the arrangements that have been made to 
address these issues. All proposals to change unit offerings to teaching periods that do not 
