Definitions – 
Commonly defined terms are in the UWA Policy Library Glossary. 
In this policy and any associated procedures, 
the University means The University of Western Australia
an active unit is an approved unit that is available on an ongoing basis.
an area of knowledge is a group of proximal disciplinary fields that delineate broadening units. There are 
five areas of knowledge as follows: Design and Creative areas is the study of the design and construction of 
structures and landscapes and the creative and performing arts including music, dance, and drama; Life, 
Health and Natural Sciences is the study of living organisms and maintaining and restoring the physical health 
and well-being of humans; Mathematical and Physical Sciences is the study of inanimate natural and human-
constructed objects and phenomena and mathematical quantity, structure, space, and change; Management 
and Commerce is the study of the human, material and natural resources of private and public organisations 
and institutions; Society and Culture is the study of the physical, social and cultural organisation of human 
society
broadening means the structure through which degrees deliver the requirement of broad-based knowledge 
and skills.  It is satisfied by taking 24 credit points (normally four units) of study from outside the unit 
sequence of the degree-specific major.  Foundational units and bridging units do not count towards 
Broadening
