Bundle page 498 | N203 | source page 8 | line numbers at left","service teaching occurs when a unit or part unit is taught by a school that is normally or primarily 
responsible for teaching units in the course/major concerned.
teaching mode is the delivery technique or means through which students are taught.
teaching period is a scheduled duration, within an academic year, in which a unit of study is offered and 
includes approved non-teaching study breaks, pre-examination study breaks, and examination periods.
teaching responsibility refers to the schools through which the unit is taught.
unit quota is an upper limit imposed on the number of enrolments in a particular unit.
