1 
 
 
Lecture Capture and Student Access 
Policy  UP10/9 (F22828) 
 
Approver 
Academic Board 
Sponsor 
Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Education and Student Experience) 
Owner 
Pro Vice-Chancellor Academic 
Secretary 
Academic Secretary 
Policy Type 
Academic 
Policy Category 
Academic Governance 
 
1 
Purpose 
1.1 
This policy sets out the general principles associated with the recording of lectures and teaching 
activities  at all of the University campuses, and the conditions under which students may access the 
substance of these recordings.  
1.2 
Recording educational activities and developing multi-media learning resources is an important part of 
the University’s vision to enhance the quality of the student experience.  
1.3 
The University's Lecture Capture System (LCS) is designed to enhance the institution's commitment 
to flexible modes of learning and teaching. The educational benefits to capturing lectures include: 
(a) flexible learning – providing flexibility to students to access learning materials anytime and 
anywhere at the learners’ own pace  
(b) multi-mode learning – providing learning materials in multiple formats to suit individual learning 
preferences  
(c) deep learning – providing learners with the opportunity to contextualise and evaluate learning 
materials over time 
(d) reflective learning – providing students with the opportunity to review and reflect on the specific 
aspects of the taught content  
(e) accessibility – particularly useful for students with a range of special educational needs or 
students whose first language is not English  
(f) pedagogical innovation – providing opportunities to explore and experiment new pedagogic 
approaches as well as the development of blended learning approaches 
1.4 
This Policy is to be read in conjunction with the following: 
(a) University Policy on Timetabling UP10/6; 
(b) University Policy on Intellectual Property UP07/49; 
(c) University Policy on Consultantcy UP07/204; 
(d) University Policy on Coursework Units UP21/5 – Part 4 (Selecting Teaching Modes); 
(e) University Code of Conduct and Annexure B; 
(f) University Policy on Teaching Periods UP14/12; and 
(g) University Policy on the Acceptable Use of IT UP19/1. 
(h) Regulations for Student Conduct and Discipline 
 
2 
Definitions 
In this policy and any associated procedures 
Learning Management System (LMS) means the University approved technology for delivering online learning 
materials to students. 
Lecture means a teaching activity where the primary focus is on the lecturer’s presentation, explanation and 
analysis of key academic content. 
Lecture Capture means the recording of a lecture.  
Record(ing) means audio and/or visual recording of teaching using University-approved technologies unless a 
different type of recording is specifically identified. 
The University means The University of Western Australia. 
