Authorship Disputes
Procedure
Important Information
(A).
If you have a potential, perceived or actual authorship dispute follow the Research Authorship 
and Authorship Dispute Procedure.
(B).
This Procedure has 2 processes —
(1).
Process 1 – Authorship Agreement Process
(2).
Process 2 – Resolving Disputes Between Authors
(C).
This Procedure should be read in conjunction with the Research Integrity Policy, Research 
Integrity Guideline and Research Integrity Advisors Guideline.
(D).
Good authorship practice is expected of all individuals at UWA.  These procedures set out the 
requirements of determining authorship on publications and outlines the process for dealing 
with disputes between authors of publications where one or more of the authors are 
Employees or Students. 
(E).
Authorship disputes may include a disagreement about the inclusion, exclusion or order of 
authors, and should be as much as possible resolved at the local level.
