This is a UWA Official document authorised or intended for public access.
 
(b) Contracts between the University and third parties must include obligations requiring the third 
party to act in a manner that supports and enables the University to comply with these 
identification and reporting requirements, including by promptly notifying the University of any 
actual or suspected information breach and complying with directions given by the University’s 
nominated contract representative. 
 
4.3 
University Officers and Information Users must comply with the Information Breach Response 
Procedure and follow guidance and instructions provided by the Privacy Office. 
4.4 
All information breaches must be assessed in a consistent, documented and timely manner to 
determine their nature, scope and potential impact, including whether the breach constitutes a 
Notifiable Information Breach under applicable legislation. 
4.5 
The University must take proportionate action to contain information breaches, mitigate harm to 
affected individuals, and reduce the likelihood of recurrence. 
4.6 
Where required or mandated by law, authorised University Officers must notify affected individuals 
and relevant regulatory authorities such as, but not limited to, the Office of the Information 
Commissioner (WA) and may provide notification in other circumstances where appropriate to 
mitigate risk or support transparency. 
4.7 
Information breaches must be recorded in a mandatory breach register maintained by the University 
to support oversight and required reporting to regulatory authorities. 
4.8 
Responsibility for oversight, coordination and assurance of information breach management is 
assigned to the University’s designated Privacy Officer, supported by defined roles across the 
University as per the Privacy Policy. 
4.9 
Information breach management activities and decisions must be documented and used to inform 
assurance, audit, and continuous improvement of the University’s information governance 
framework. 
5 
Breaches and Consequences 
 
Breaches of this Policy or supporting guidance or subordinate documents issued under this Policy 
may result in action under applicable University policies, enterprise agreements, contracts or 
legislation, including disciplinary or contractual action, where appropriate. 
 
 
Legislative Context 
Relevant Legislation or Regulations 
University of Western Australia Act 1911 (WA) 
University of Western Australia Statute (2020) 
Privacy and Responsible Information Sharing Act 2024 (WA) 
Information Commissioners Act 2024 (WA) 
Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) 
Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 (part 3.3) 
Tertiary Education Quality and Standards Agency Act 2011 (Cth) 
 
End 
